{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:01:28.400Z","session":"acfb2b14-97e1-47c7-9b97-8b6f6c60576e","event":"tool.end","callId":"3c1adf2e-f333-47dc-86bd-9748bb7320db","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2321,"result":[{"title":"Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing ...","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/infosys-appoints-salil-s-parekh-as-ceo-and-managing-director-661468303.html","content":"Infosys announced today that its Board of Directors has appointed Salil S. Parekh as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director (CEO & MD) of the Company effective January 2, 2018.\n\n     (Logo:  ) [...] Mr. U B Pravin Rao will step down as the interim CEO and Managing Director effective January 2, 2018 and will continue as Chief Operating Officer and a whole-time Director of the Company.\n\nAbout Infosys [...] Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation\n\n# Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing Director\n\n- India - English\n\nInfosys Logo (PRNewsfoto/Infosys)\")\n\n## News provided by\n\n Infosys \n\nDec 02, 2017, 05:45 ET\n\n## Share this article\n\nShare toX\n\nShare this article\n\nShare toX\n\nBANGALORE, India, December 2, 2017 /PRNewswire/ --","score":0.8936907},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] Parekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others. He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[edit] [...] 4. ↑ \"A Gujarati appointed as CEO and MD of Infosys\". DeshGujarat. 2 December 2017. Retrieved 14 July 2025.\n5. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". mint. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n6. ↑ Shivapriya, N. \"Salil Parekh: The man who played a pivotal role in building Capgemini's India operations\". The Economic Times. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n7. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". LiveMint. Retrieved 3 January 2018.","score":0.8512743},{"title":"Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as Salil Parekh Prepares to Step Down - INDIA New England News","url":"https://indianewengland.com/infosys-names-ashiss-kumar-dash-ceo-designate-as-salil-parekh-prepares-to-step-down","content":"Parekh will leave the role effective April 1, 2027, following the completion of his second term. He joined Infosys in January 2018 and is the longest-serving non-founder CEO in the company’s history.\n\nDash will become CEO and Managing Director on April 1, 2027, subject to the completion of statutory requirements, Infosys said in a regulatory filing. [...] Nilekani also praised Parekh for strengthening Infosys during his tenure.\n\n“On behalf of the Board, I also thank Salil for his outstanding leadership over 9 years. Under his stewardship, Infosys has strengthened its market position, expanded its capabilities, delivered significant value to shareholders, and built a strong platform for future growth,” he said.\n\nParekh’s current five-year term is scheduled to end March 31, 2027, allowing Dash to take over the following day. (Source: IANS) [...] INDIA New England News\n\n Search for\n\nBusiness\n\n# Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as Salil Parekh Prepares to Step Down\n\nJuly 23, 2026\n\n1,138  1 minute read\n\nFacebook   X   LinkedIn   Tumblr   Pinterest   Reddit   VKontakte   Odnoklassniki   Pocket\n\n\n\nBengaluru–Infosys announced Thursday that CEO and Managing Director Salil Parekh will step down after nine years at the helm, with Ashiss Kumar Dash appointed as his successor.","score":0.8170061},{"title":"Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...","url":"https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors","content":"Home\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] ## More Topics\n\n### TTM TECHNOLOGIES EXPANDS WORKFORCE IN CONNECTICUT\n\nMay 6 2024\n\nStafford, Connecticut, May 6, 2024 – AdvanceCT today announced that TTM Technologies Inc. (TTM), a global manufacturer of technology solutions including radio frequency (“RF”) components, RF microwave/microelectronic assemblies, and advanced printed circuit boards (“PCBs”), is expanding its workforce in its two Stafford locations.TTM was looking to invest in modernization and...Continue Reading [...] ### Danbury, Bridgeport Ranked In Top 15 Most Diverse Cities in US\n\nApr 29 2024 \n\nAmerica is undergoing an extreme makeover, thanks to rapid demographic diversification. For example, the percentage of people in the U.S. who are multiracial increased from 2.9% in 2010 to 10.2% in 2020, according to data compiled by the website WalletHub.Not only have waves of immigration changed the face of the...Continue Reading\n\n### Report: CT a top destination for relocating remote workers\n\nApr 23 2024","score":0.75312227},{"title":"World Economic Forum 2025 | Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/wef/2025/salil-parekh.html","content":"# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer & Managing Director, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh [...] Salil Parekh\n\nSalil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic\ndirection for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team\nto drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services\nindustry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing\nbusiness turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions. [...] Salil was also Partner at Ernst & Young and widely credited for bringing scale and value to the\nIndian operations of the consultancy firm.\n\nHe holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell\nUniversity, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian\nInstitute of Technology, Bombay.\n\nSubsidiaries\n\nPrograms\n\nCompany\n\nSupport\n\nCopyright © 2026 Infosys Limited\n\nLoading","score":0.38581482}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:01:28.411Z","session":"acfb2b14-97e1-47c7-9b97-8b6f6c60576e","event":"tool.end","callId":"6528b435-66cd-47d7-8300-ab44a7997aeb","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2330,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] [edit]\n\nSalil Parekh is born into a Gujarati family. He is a graduate from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay (IIT Bombay) in Aeronautical Engineering. Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University.\n\nParekh was member of the group management board at Capgemini, where he had worked since 2000, after Ernst & Young's consultancy division, where he had been working before, was merged into the company. [...] Print/export\n\n Download as PDF\n Printable version\n\nIn other projects\n\n Wikimedia Commons\n Wikidata item\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian businessman, current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n\n| Born | (1964-06-05) 5 June 1964 (age 62) |\n| Education | IIT Bombay (BTech) Cornell University (MS) |\n| Occupations | CEO & MD of Infosys |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh |","score":0.83678174},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/salil-parekh","content":"### CEO, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys Limited, one of India’s leading global IT services companies. Parekh graduated with a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Bombay in 1986. He then pursued higher studies at Cornell University, earning Master of Engineering degrees in both Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering in 1988.","score":0.81979275},{"title":"Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay","url":"https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh","content":"Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988. [...] Mr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Prior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.”","score":0.7487387},{"title":"Salil Parekh - Managing Director and CEO, Infosys","url":"https://usispf.org/board-of-directors/salil-parekh","content":"Salil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic direction for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team to drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services industry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing business turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions. He is a member of the National Council of the [...] Capgemini’s North America Executive Council. He was the architect of the North America growth and turnaround strategy, and was instrumental in setting up their offshoring capabilities. [...] Salil was also Partner at Ernst & Young and widely credited for bringing scale and value to the Indian operations of the consultancy firm.\n\nHe holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.\n\n###### Subscribe to our\n\n Daily Newsletter   Weekly Newsletter","score":0.71040785},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html","content":"+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] Salil is on the board of Advance CT, an organization that supports business and innovation in the state of Connecticut. Salil is on the Board of the US-India Strategic Partnership Forum (USISPF) an organization that works towards strengthening the US-India relationship and promoting collaboration in various sectors, including technology.\n\nSalil Parekh is also an Executive Officer for Infosys.\n\n## Request for services [...] Salil holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.","score":0.6721816}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:01:28.612Z","session":"acfb2b14-97e1-47c7-9b97-8b6f6c60576e","event":"tool.end","callId":"ddb9a3d6-5bb7-497d-9dfa-c44345f39847","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2538,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] 1. 1 2 3 \"Infosys gets a new boss in Salil Parekh today but can he keep Narayana Murthy happy?\". economictimes.indiatimes.com. 2 January 2018. Retrieved 2 January 2018.\n2. ↑ Ishwarbharath B, Sai; Suresh, Haripriya (23 July 2026). \"Infosys names insider Ashiss Kumar Dash next CEO, trims growth forecast\". Reuters. Retrieved 25 July 2026.`{{cite news}}`: CS1 maint: url-status (link)\n3. ↑ Admin. \"Member List\". The Business Council. Retrieved 11 July 2025. [...] 11. ↑ Iyengar, Rishi (22 October 2019). \"Indian tech group Infosys rocked by whistleblower claims against CEO Salil Parekh | CNN Business\". CNN. Retrieved 11 July 2025.\n12. ↑ \"Infosys' audit committee finds no wrongdoing, SEC investigation continues\". The Economic Times. Retrieved 23 October 2020.","score":0.8342047},{"title":"World Economic Forum 2025 | Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/wef/2025/salil-parekh.html","content":"# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer & Managing Director, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh [...] Salil Parekh\n\nSalil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic\ndirection for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team\nto drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services\nindustry with a 