{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:01:29.081Z","session":"acfb2b14-97e1-47c7-9b97-8b6f6c60576e","event":"llm.start","callId":"d86bd953-45b2-4833-b8fa-0aacd8458cef","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence, as {\"name\", \"type\", \"data\": {key facts}}.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"data\": object}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: Who is the current CEO of Infosys and when did they take the role?\nSub-questions to cover:\n- Who is the current Chief Executive Officer of Infosys?\n- On what exact date did the current CEO of Infosys take office?\n- Has there been any recent change in the CEO position at Infosys?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Salil Parekh\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh\nSalil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] 1. 1 2 3 \"Infosys gets a new boss in Salil Parekh today but can he keep Narayana Murthy happy?\". economictimes.indiatimes.com. 2 January 2018. Retrieved 2 January 2018.\n2. ↑ Ishwarbharath B, Sai; Suresh, Haripriya (23 July 2026). \"Infosys names insider Ashiss Kumar Dash next CEO, trims growth forecast\". Reuters. Retrieved 25 July 2026.`{{cite news}}`: CS1 maint: url-status (link)\n3. ↑ Admin. \"Member List\". The Business Council. Retrieved 11 July 2025. [...] 11. ↑ Iyengar, Rishi (22 October 2019). \"Indian tech group Infosys rocked by whistleblower claims against CEO Salil Parekh | CNN Business\". CNN. Retrieved 11 July 2025.\n12. ↑ \"Infosys' audit committee finds no wrongdoing, SEC investigation continues\". The Economic Times. Retrieved 23 October 2020.\n\n[S2] World Economic Forum 2025 | Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/wef/2025/salil-parekh.html\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer & Managing Director, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh [...] Salil Parekh\n\nSalil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic\ndirection for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team\nto drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services\nindustry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing\nbusiness turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions. [...] Salil was also Partner at Ernst & Young and widely credited for bringing scale and value to the\nIndian operations of the consultancy firm.\n\nHe holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell\nUniversity, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian\nInstitute of Technology, Bombay.\n\nSubsidiaries\n\nPrograms\n\nCompany\n\nSupport\n\nCopyright © 2026 Infosys Limited\n\nLoading\n\n[S3] Infosys Board Appoints Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO ...\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/newsroom/press-releases/2026/board-appoints-ceo-designate.html\nvalue. Infosys begins this next phase from a position of enormous strength—with a clearly articulated AI strategy, exceptional talent, deep client relationships, and values that have earned the trust of customers globally. My commitment is to build on those strengths while accelerating innovation, expanding our capabilities and helping our clients succeed in an increasingly AI-driven world. Together with the outstanding leadership team, all my colleagues, customers and partners, I look forward [...] Infosys (NSE, BSE, NYSE: INFY) is a global leader in AI first business consulting and technology services. Over 325,000 of our people work to amplify human potential and create the next opportunity for people, businesses, and communities. As navigators of enterprise transformation, we enable businesses in 59 countries to unlock AI value at scale. With over four decades of experience in managing the systems and workings of global enterprises, we accelerate business transformation through our [...] Infosys (NSE, BSE, NYSE: INFY), a global leader in AI-first business consulting and technology services, today announced the appointment of Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO Designate. This appointment is based on the recommendation of the Nomination and Remuneration Committee of the Infosys Board, and is for a period of five years, subject to the approval of shareholders.\n\n[S4] Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html\n+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] ### Experience\n\n  + Infosys Aster\n  + Digital Marketing\n  + Digital Commerce\n  + Digital Interactions\n  + Digital Workplace Services\n  + Digital Experience\n  + Infosys Metaverse Foundry\n\n  + Application Development and Maintenance\n  + Business Process Management\n  + Consulting Services\n  + Incubating Emerging Offerings\n ### Platforms\n\n  + EdgeVerve\n  + Infosys Finacle\n  + Infosys Live Enterprise Suite\n  + Infosys Cortex\n  + Infosys Meridian [...] + Healthcare\n  + High Technology\n  + Industrial Manufacturing\n  + Information Services & Publishing\n  + Insurance\n  + Life Sciences\n  + Logistics & Distribution\n  + Media and Entertainment\n  + Mining\n  + Retail\n  + Semiconductor\n  + Travel and Hospitality\n  + Utilities\n  + Waste Management\n ## Services\n\n  ### Insights\n\n  + Infosys Topaz\n  + Applied AI\n  + Infosys Generative AI\n  + Infosys Sustainability Services\n\n  ### Innovate\n\n[S5] Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay\nURL: https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh\nMr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988.\n\n[S6] Ashiss Kumar Dash named Infosys CEO designate, to take charge in April 2027\nURL: https://www.peoplematters.in/news/appointments/ashiss-kumar-dash-named-infosys-ceo-designate-to-take-charge-in-april-2027-51021\nInfosys has appointed company veteran Ashiss Kumar Dash as its CEO-designate, setting the stage for a planned leadership transition as the IT services major sharpens its focus on AI-led growth.\n\n  \n\nAccording to media reports, the board approved Dash's appointment on the recommendation of the Nomination and Remuneration Committee. He will serve as CEO-designate until 31 March 2027 and take over as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director on 1 April 2027, subject to statutory approvals. [...] ### Appointments\n\n# Ashiss Kumar Dash named Infosys CEO designate, to take charge in April 2027\n\n\n\nRia Duneja•Join UsGoogle News\n\nLinkedIn|\n\nJoin UsGoogle News\n\nArticle cover image\n\nDash will succeed Salil Parekh, who will step down after completing his second five-year term. Parekh will remain CEO until 31 March 2027 to ensure a smooth handover. [...] Infosys Chairman Nandan Nilekani said Dash was well placed to lead the company through the industry's next phase.\n\n  \n\n\"The Board is delighted to appoint Dash as CEO-designate. Our industry is entering a period of considerable change. The Board was clear that our next CEO needed to combine the ability to drive bold transformation with the judgment to preserve the values and customer trust that have always distinguished Infosys,” he said.\n\n[S7] Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing ...\nURL: https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/infosys-appoints-salil-s-parekh-as-ceo-and-managing-director-661468303.html\nInfosys announced today that its Board of Directors has appointed Salil S. Parekh as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director (CEO & MD) of the Company effective January 2, 2018.\n\n     (Logo:  ) [...] Mr. U B Pravin Rao will step down as the interim CEO and Managing Director effective January 2, 2018 and will continue as Chief Operating Officer and a whole-time Director of the Company.\n\nAbout Infosys [...] Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation\n\n# Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing Director\n\n- India - English\n\nInfosys Logo (PRNewsfoto/Infosys)\")\n\n## News provided by\n\n Infosys \n\nDec 02, 2017, 05:45 ET\n\n## Share this article\n\nShare toX\n\nShare this article\n\nShare toX\n\nBANGALORE, India, December 2, 2017 /PRNewswire/ --\n\n[S8] [Solved]  Who is appointed as the CEO of Infosys in place of Vis\nURL: https://testbook.com/question-answer/who-is-appointed-as-the-ceo-of-infosys-in-pl--5f61b12098b643c504e19a37\nThe correct answer is Salil Parekh.\n\n Salil Parekh was appointed as the CEO & MD of Infosys in place of Vishal Sikka on 2nd January 2018.\n Prior to this, he was a member of the Group Executive Board at Capgemini.\n\nImportant Points [...] | N.R. Narayanmurthi |  He is the founder of Infosys.  He has been awarded Padma Shri (2000) and Padma Vibhushan (2008) by Government of India. | [...] | Nandan Nilekani |  He was the co-founder and co-chairman of Infosys  He was also the chairman of the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) in the rank of a Cabinet Minister.  He was awarded Padma Bhusan in 2006.  He is also the author of “Imagining India” and co- authored his second book with Viral Shah, “Rebooting India: Realizing a Billion Aspirations”. |\n\n[S9] Salil Parekh: Infosys appoints Capgemini’s Salil Parekh as MD & CEO - Times of India\nURL: https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/infosys-appoints-capgeminis-salil-parekh-as-md-ceo/articleshow/61893756.cms\nBENGALURU: Infosys has appointed Salil Parekh chief executive officer (CEO) and managing director (MD) of the company with effect from January 2 next year, culminating the search of a CEO which began since the departure of Vishal Sikka in August due to a spat with the founders over various issues. [...] Infosys appoints Capgemini’s Salil Parekh as MD and CEO\n\nInfosys' newly appointed MD & CEO Salil Parekh (Image Source: Twitter)\n\nKey Highlights\n\n Infosys has appointed Salil Parekh MD & CEO of the company with effect from January 2\n He joins from French IT and consulting company Capgemini where he is the CEO of financial services across Europe\n Infosys will hope that Parekh’s background in financial services gets them to garner more deals [...] The appointment marks the end of the intense CEO search Infosys embarked in August, after a protracted public spat with the company’s founding executives, led by Narayana Murthy led to Sikka’s resignation, over alleged corporate governance lapses.\n\n[S10] Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as Salil Parekh Prepares to Step Down - INDIA New England News\nURL: https://indianewengland.com/infosys-names-ashiss-kumar-dash-ceo-designate-as-salil-parekh-prepares-to-step-down\nParekh will leave the role effective April 1, 2027, following the completion of his second term. He joined Infosys in January 2018 and is the longest-serving non-founder CEO in the company’s history.\n\nDash will become CEO and Managing Director on April 1, 2027, subject to the completion of statutory requirements, Infosys said in a regulatory filing. [...] Nilekani also praised Parekh for strengthening Infosys during his tenure.\n\n“On behalf of the Board, I also thank Salil for his outstanding leadership over 9 years. Under his stewardship, Infosys has strengthened its market position, expanded its capabilities, delivered significant value to shareholders, and built a strong platform for future growth,” he said.\n\nParekh’s current five-year term is scheduled to end March 31, 2027, allowing Dash to take over the following day. (Source: IANS) [...] INDIA New England News\n\n Search for\n\nBusiness\n\n# Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as Salil Parekh Prepares to Step Down\n\nJuly 23, 2026\n\n1,138  1 minute read\n\nFacebook   X   LinkedIn   Tumblr   Pinterest   Reddit   VKontakte   Odnoklassniki   Pocket\n\n\n\nBengaluru–Infosys announced Thursday that CEO and Managing Director Salil Parekh will step down after nine years at the helm, with Ashiss Kumar Dash appointed as his successor.\n\n[S11] Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...\nURL: https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors\nHome\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] ## More Topics\n\n### TTM TECHNOLOGIES EXPANDS WORKFORCE IN CONNECTICUT\n\nMay 6 2024\n\nStafford, Connecticut, May 6, 2024 – AdvanceCT today announced that TTM Technologies Inc. (TTM), a global manufacturer of technology solutions including radio frequency (“RF”) components, RF microwave/microelectronic assemblies, and advanced printed circuit boards (“PCBs”), is expanding its workforce in its two Stafford locations.TTM was looking to invest in modernization and...Continue Reading [...] ### Danbury, Bridgeport Ranked In Top 15 Most Diverse Cities in US\n\nApr 29 2024 \n\nAmerica is undergoing an extreme makeover, thanks to rapid demographic diversification. For example, the percentage of people in the U.S. who are multiracial increased from 2.9% in 2010 to 10.2% in 2020, according to data compiled by the website WalletHub.Not only have waves of immigration changed the face of the...Continue Reading\n\n### Report: CT a top destination for relocating remote workers\n\nApr 23 2024\n\n[S12] Infosys | Company Overview & News\nURL: https://www.forbes.com/companies/infosys\nInfosys Ltd. is a digital services and consulting company, which engages in the provision of end-to-end business solutions. It operates through the following segments: Financial Services, Retail, Communication; Energy, Utilities, Resources, and Services; Manufacturing, Hi-Tech, Life Sciences, and All Other. The company was founded by Dinesh Krishnan Swamy, Senapathy Gopalakrishnan, Narayana Ramarao Nagavara Murthy, Raghavan N. S., Ashok Arora, Nandan M. Nil