{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:02:14.479Z","session":"763ca2d6-3a8f-4dea-9e91-2eb27389dcdd","event":"tool.end","callId":"12451d97-6e53-40a2-92d7-da0352045990","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2426,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] Parekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others. He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[edit] [...] 4. ↑ \"A Gujarati appointed as CEO and MD of Infosys\". DeshGujarat. 2 December 2017. Retrieved 14 July 2025.\n5. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". mint. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n6. ↑ Shivapriya, N. \"Salil Parekh: The man who played a pivotal role in building Capgemini's India operations\". The Economic Times. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n7. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". LiveMint. Retrieved 3 January 2018.","score":0.91137725},{"title":"Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay","url":"https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh","content":"Mr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988. [...] Prior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.”","score":0.8763069},{"title":"Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...","url":"https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors","content":"Home\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] Apr 23 2024 \n\nConnecticut was a top 10 destination for remote workers who relocated in 2022, according to a new study.Yardi Kube, a coworking management platform, released the results of its study in February in a report titled, “Remote Workers Leading the Migration Across State Lines.”The study, which is based on data from...Continue Reading\n\n## Contact Us\n\nBen Dwyer headshot\n\nBen Dwyer  \nDirector, Marketing [...] ## More Topics\n\n### TTM TECHNOLOGIES EXPANDS WORKFORCE IN CONNECTICUT\n\nMay 6 2024\n\nStafford, Connecticut, May 6, 2024 – AdvanceCT today announced that TTM Technologies Inc. (TTM), a global manufacturer of technology solutions including radio frequency (“RF”) components, RF microwave/microelectronic assemblies, and advanced printed circuit boards (“PCBs”), is expanding its workforce in its two Stafford locations.TTM was looking to invest in modernization and...Continue Reading","score":0.8194462},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html","content":"+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] Prior to Infosys, Salil was a member of the management board at Capgemini and a partner at consulting practice Ernst & Young LLP prior to its acquisition by Capgemini. He had different leadership roles there across US, UK, Europe, Asia, over a span of 25 years.\n\nSalil has received several awards as a leading CEO.","score":0.77261686},{"title":"Why Salil Parekh didn't seek a third term at Infosys; praises CEO-designate Ashiss Dash","url":"https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/information-technology/whats-next-for-salil-parekh-outgoing-infosys-ceo-on-life-after-infosys-and-nandan-nilekani-13990109.html","content":"Parekh, whose tenure ends on March 31, 2027, took charge at a turbulent time for Infosys following a leadership crisis. During his tenure, the company doubled annual revenue from $10 billion to $20 billion, expanded its workforce from around 200,000 to more than 300,000 employees, strengthened its large deals business and pivoted from digital transformation to artificial intelligence services.\n\n## Related Stories [...] Responding to questions on why he did not seek a third term despite being eligible for another extension, Parekh stopped short of giving a direct reason but said Infosys had achieved the transformation he envisioned when he took over in January 2018. [...] Also read: You need companies like Infosys to make AI work in enterprises, says CEO Parekh\n\nBacks Ashiss Dash\n\nParekh also strongly endorsed CEO-designate Ashiss Dash, who was named last week to succeed him from April 1, 2027.\n\nCalling Dash ‘a very good friend’ and ‘a great leader’, Parekh said the two would work closely over the coming months to ensure a smooth leadership transition.","score":0.71496695}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:02:14.623Z","session":"763ca2d6-3a8f-4dea-9e91-2eb27389dcdd","event":"tool.end","callId":"0bb08f6d-e586-4d2a-8365-7adb12353a76","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2571,"result":[{"title":"Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing ...","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/infosys-appoints-salil-s-parekh-as-ceo-and-managing-director-661468303.html","content":"Infosys announced today that its Board of Directors has appointed Salil S. Parekh as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director (CEO & MD) of the Company effective January 2, 2018.\n\n     (Logo:  ) [...] Mr. U B Pravin Rao will step down as the interim CEO and Managing Director effective January 2, 2018 and will continue as Chief Operating Officer and a whole-time Director of the Company.\n\nAbout Infosys [...] Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation\n\n# Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing Director\n\n- India - English\n\nInfosys Logo (PRNewsfoto/Infosys)\")\n\n## News provided by\n\n Infosys \n\nDec 02, 2017, 05:45 ET\n\n## Share this article\n\nShare toX\n\nShare this article\n\nShare toX\n\nBANGALORE, India, December 2, 2017 /PRNewswire/ --","score":0.89324445},{"title":"Infosys Board Appoints Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO ...","url":"https://www.infosys.com/newsroom/press-releases/2026/board-appoints-ceo-designate.html","content":"Playback Speed\n\n# Infosys Board Appoints Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO Designate\n\nLeadership transition to be effective April 1, 2027\n\nBengaluru, India – July 23, 2026 [...] Dash is currently the global head of a diverse business portfolio comprising multiple industry verticals and is planned to succeed Salil Parekh as Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer on April 1, 2027, following the completion of Salil’s second term, after over 9 years. [...] 31, 2027, and work closely with Dash to ensure a seamless leadership transition.\"","score":0.8684817},{"title":"[Solved] Who is appointed as the CEO of Infosys in place ...","url":"https://testbook.com/question-answer/who-is-appointed-as-the-ceo-of-infosys-in-pl--5f61b12098b643c504e19a37","content":"The correct answer is Salil Parekh.\n\n Salil Parekh was appointed as the CEO & MD of Infosys in place of Vishal Sikka on 2nd January 2018.\n Prior to this, he was a member of the Group Executive Board at Capgemini.\n\nImportant Points [...] | N.R. Narayanmurthi |  He is the founder of Infosys.  He has been awarded Padma Shri (2000) and Padma Vibhushan (2008) by Government of India. | [...] Q8.Which Indian political leader was appointed as the central observer for the Bharatiya Janata Party’s legislative-party-leader selection in Bihar in Nov 2025?\n\nQ9.Which body’s Chairperson was appointed on 1 September 2025, with Ajay Seth taking over the role?\n\nQ10.In September 2024, who has been appointed as Chief of the National Crime Records Bureau?\n\n## More Appointments and Resignations Questions","score":0.8619225},{"title":"Infosys names insider Ashiss Kumar Dash next CEO, trims growth forecast | Reuters","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/india/indias-infosys-misses-quarterly-revenue-view-names-ceo-designate-2026-07-23","content":"Sign up here.\n\nDash, who ​heads the company's energy and utilities business, will take over in April 2027 for a five-year term ​after Salil Parekh steps down at the end of his tenure in March, the ⁠company said.\n\nThe appointment comes as India's $315 billion IT sector wrestles with the impact of AI on technology spending ​and traditional outsourcing models. [...] BENGALURU, July 23 (Reuters) - Infosys (INFY.NS) named company veteran Ashiss Kumar Dash as its next ‌CEO on Thursday, tapping a three-decade insider to lead India's No. 2 IT firm through an AI-driven upheaval reshaping the technology services industry.\n\nThe succession plan was announced alongside a cut to the company's annual revenue growth forecast, sending its U.S.-listed shares down 5% in early trading.\n\nSign up here.","score":0.796562},{"title":"Infosys updates board with independent director move | INFY SEC Filing - Form 6-K","url":"https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/INFY/6-k-infosys-ltd-current-report-foreign-issuer-7c9deca6e2e4.html","content":"## FAQ\n\nAI-generated questions and answers. How Rhea-AI works. Not financial advice.\n\n \n\n### What did Infosys (INFY) disclose in its April 2026 Form 6-K?\n\nInfosys disclosed that it notified stock exchanges on April 18, 2026 about the appointment or re-appointment of an independent director. The detailed intimation to exchanges is included as Exhibit 99.1 to the Form 6-K filing.\n\n  \n\n### What is the main purpose of this Infosys (INFY) Form 6-K filing? [...] Infosys Limited submitted a Form 6-K as a foreign private issuer to report a board change. On April 18, 2026, the company notified stock exchanges about the appointment or re-appointment of an independent director. The formal intimation sent to the exchanges is attached as Exhibit 99.1, titled “Appointment/Re-appointment of Independent Director's.” The information is furnished, not filed, meaning it is not automatically incorporated into other U.S. securities law filings unless specifically [...] On April 18, 2026, the Company notified the stock exchanges regarding an Appointment/Re-appointment of Independent Director's. A copy of the intimation as disseminated by Infosys Limited to the stock exchanges in this regard is attached to this Form 6-K as Exhibit 99.1.\n\nSIGNATURES\n\nPursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned, thereunto duly authorized.","score":0.6682966}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:02:14.639Z","session":"763ca2d6-3a8f-4dea-9e91-2eb27389dcdd","event":"tool.end","callId":"5b0b2e2c-7964-43a4-9c3a-835f813dbb6c","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2584,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] [edit]\n\nSalil Parekh is born into a Gujarati family. He is a graduate from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay (IIT Bombay) in Aeronautical Engineering. Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University.\n\nParekh was member of the group management board at Capgemini, where he had worked since 2000, after Ernst & Young's consultancy division, where he had been working before, was merged into the company. [...] Print/export\n\n Download as PDF\n Printable version\n\nIn other projects\n\n Wikimedia Commons\n Wikidata item\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian businessman, current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n\n| Born | (1964-06-05) 5 June 1964 (age 62) |\n| Education | IIT Bombay (BTech) Cornell University (MS) |\n| Occupations | CEO & MD of Infosys |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh |","score":0.83678174},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/salil-parekh","content":"### CEO, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys Limited, one of India’s leading global IT services companies. Parekh graduated with a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian In