executive officer and managing director of Infosys\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n\n| Born | (1964-06-05) 5 June 1964 (age 62) |\n| Education | IIT Bombay (BTech) Cornell University (MS) |\n| Occupations | CEO & MD of Infosys |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh | [...] 1. 1 2 3 \"Infosys gets a new boss in Salil Parekh today but can he keep Narayana Murthy happy?\". economictimes.indiatimes.com. 2 January 2018. Retrieved 2 January 2018.\n2. ↑ Ishwarbharath B, Sai; Suresh, Haripriya (23 July 2026). \"Infosys names insider Ashiss Kumar Dash next CEO, trims growth forecast\". Reuters. Retrieved 25 July 2026.`{{cite news}}`: CS1 maint: url-status (link)\n3. ↑ Admin. \"Member List\". The Business Council. Retrieved 11 July 2025.\n\n[S2] Infosys Board Appoints Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO ...\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/newsroom/press-releases/2026/board-appoints-ceo-designate.html\nInfosys (NSE, BSE, NYSE: INFY), a global leader in AI-first business consulting and technology services, today announced the appointment of Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO Designate. This appointment is based on the recommendation of the Nomination and Remuneration Committee of the Infosys Board, and is for a period of five years, subject to the approval of shareholders. [...] Infosys (NSE, BSE, NYSE: INFY) is a global leader in AI first business consulting and technology services. Over 325,000 of our people work to amplify human potential and create the next opportunity for people, businesses, and communities. As navigators of enterprise transformation, we enable businesses in 59 countries to unlock AI value at scale. With over four decades of experience in managing the systems and workings of global enterprises, we accelerate business transformation through our [...] Ashiss Kumar Dash, CEO Designate, Infosys said, \"I am honoured by the confidence that the Board has placed in me and excited about the opportunity to lead Infosys into its next chapter. I would also like to thank Salil for his mentorship, guidance, and the countless opportunities for growth over the years. I look forward to collaborating with him to ensure a seamless transition. Technology is entering a new era, with AI fundamentally reshaping how businesses operate and create value. Infosys\n\n[S3] Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay\nURL: https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh\nMr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988. [...] Prior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.”\n\n[S4] Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html\n+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] Salil has helped transform Infosys into a leading digital, cloud, and AI company. Salil helps set the strategy and nurture a leadership team to drive its execution. Infosys is in the top decile of shareholder return during his tenure, leading in client satisfaction results, and leading in employee engagement scores.\n\nSalil has a strong track record of driving transformations, executing business turnarounds, and managing successful acquisitions. [...] ### Experience\n\n  + Infosys Aster\n  + Digital Marketing\n  + Digital Commerce\n  + Digital Interactions\n  + Digital Workplace Services\n  + Digital Experience\n  + Infosys Metaverse Foundry\n\n  + Application Development and Maintenance\n  + Business Process Management\n  + Consulting Services\n  + Incubating Emerging Offerings\n ### Platforms\n\n  + EdgeVerve\n  + Infosys Finacle\n  + Infosys Live Enterprise Suite\n  + Infosys Cortex\n  + Infosys Meridian\n\n[S5] Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...\nURL: https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors\nHome\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] Based in India, Parekh brings over three decades of experience in the global IT services industry. Parekh holds a Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay. [...] “I am delighted and honored to be inducted to the board of AdvanceCT and express my sincere thanks to the state of Connecticut. I look forward to working with my fellow board members and with the state’s leadership to further deepen collaboration between government and business,” said Mr. Parekh.\n\nInfosys has a Technology and Innovation Hub in Hartford and employs over 900 people in Connecticut.\n\n[S6] Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing ...\nURL: https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/infosys-appoints-salil-s-parekh-as-ceo-and-managing-director-661468303.html\nInfosys announced today that its Board of Directors has appointed Salil S. Parekh as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director (CEO & MD) of the Company effective January 2, 2018.\n\n     (Logo:  ) [...] Mr. U B Pravin Rao will step down as the interim CEO and Managing Director effective January 2, 2018 and will continue as Chief Operating Officer and a whole-time Director of the Company.\n\nAbout Infosys [...] Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation\n\n# Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing Director\n\n- India - English\n\nInfosys Logo (PRNewsfoto/Infosys)\")\n\n## News provided by\n\n Infosys \n\nDec 02, 2017, 05:45 ET\n\n## Share this article\n\nShare toX\n\nShare this article\n\nShare toX\n\nBANGALORE, India, December 2, 2017 /PRNewswire/ --\n\n[S7] [Solved] Who is appointed as the CEO of Infosys in place ...\nURL: https://testbook.com/question-answer/who-is-appointed-as-the-ceo-of-infosys-in-pl--5f61b12098b643c504e19a37\nThe correct answer is Salil Parekh.\n\n Salil Parekh was appointed as the CEO & MD of Infosys in place of Vishal Sikka on 2nd January 2018.\n Prior to this, he was a member of the Group Executive Board at Capgemini.\n\nImportant Points [...] | N.R. Narayanmurthi |  He is the founder of Infosys.  He has been awarded Padma Shri (2000) and Padma Vibhushan (2008) by Government 