pendent Director |\n| Michael Nelson Gibbs | Non Executive Independent Director |\n| Sundaram Damodarannair | Non Executive Independent Director |\n| Suryanarayana Anur Gurugopala Raju Manikantha | Company Secretary & Compliance Officer |\n\n[S2] Nandan Nilekani - Wikipedia\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nandan_Nilekani\nNandan Mohanrao Nilekani is an Indian entrepreneur. He co-founded Infosys and is the non-executive chairman of Infosys replacing R Seshasayee and Ravi Venkatesan, who were the co-chairs of the board, on 24 August 2017. After the exit of Vishal Sikka, Nilekani was appointed non-executive chairman of the board effective 24 August 2017. [...] In 2017 he returned to Infosys after the exit of CEO Vishal Sikka to become a chairman. Upon his return he changed power centre from California back to its Bengaluru headquarters.\nAlso, such people as R. Seshasayee (a chairman and board director), Ravi Venkatesan (a co-chairman), Sikka (executive vice chairman and director), and Jeffrey Lehman and John Etchemendy (directors) resigned from their posts.\n\n### Bureaucracy [...] |  v  t  e  Infosys | |\n --- |\n| People (list) | |  |  |  --- | | Founders |  N. R. Narayana Murthy  Nandan Nilekani  N. S. Raghavan  S. Gopalakrishnan  S. D. Shibulal  K. Dinesh  Ashok Arora | | Board of directors |  Salil Parekh (CEO & MD)  U. B. Pravin Rao (COO)  Carol M. Browner  John Etchemendy  Jeffrey S. Lehman  Kiran Mazumdar-Shaw  Ravi Venkatesan | |\n| Divisions |  Infosys BPM  Infosys Consulting  EdgeVerve Systems |\n| Products |  Finacle  Panaya |\n\n[S3] Salil Parekh\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh\nSalil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] Print/export\n\n Download as PDF\n Printable version\n\nIn other projects\n\n Wikimedia Commons\n Wikidata item\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian businessman, current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n\n| Born | (1964-06-05) 5 June 1964 (age 62) |\n| Education | IIT Bombay (BTech) Cornell University (MS) |\n| Occupations | CEO & MD of Infosys |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh | [...] 1. 1 2 3 \"Infosys gets a new boss in Salil Parekh today but can he keep Narayana Murthy happy?\". economictimes.indiatimes.com. 2 January 2018. Retrieved 2 January 2018.\n2. ↑ Ishwarbharath B, Sai; Suresh, Haripriya (23 July 2026). \"Infosys names insider Ashiss Kumar Dash next CEO, trims growth forecast\". Reuters. Retrieved 25 July 2026.`{{cite news}}`: CS1 maint: url-status (link)\n3. ↑ Admin. \"Member List\". The Business Council. Retrieved 11 July 2025.\n\n[S4] Infosys - Nandan M. Nilekani: Co-founder and Chairman of the Board | Management Profiles\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/nandan-nilekani.html\nNandan Nilekani is the Co-Founder and Chairman of Infosys Limited. He was the Founding Chairman of the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) in the rank of a Cabinet Minister from 2009-2014. Nandan has co-founded and is the Chairman of EkStep Foundation, a not-for-profit effort to create a learner centric, technology-based platform to improve basic literacy and numeracy for millions of children. In January 2023, he was appointed as the co-chair of the “G20 Task Force on Digital [...] for Economic & Business Innovation 2017. He was inducted as International Honorary Member of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences in 2019. Business Standard Annual awards 2022 conferred “The Lifetime Achievement Award.” TIME Magazine has featured him among 100 Most Influential People in AI-2024. [...] + Healthcare\n  + High Technology\n  + Industrial Manufacturing\n  + Information Services & Publishing\n  + Insurance\n  + Life Sciences\n  + Logistics & Distribution\n  + Media and Entertainment\n  + Mining\n  + Retail\n  + Semiconductor\n  + Travel and Hospitality\n  + Utilities\n  + Waste Management\n ## Services\n\n  ### Insights\n\n  + Infosys Topaz\n  + Applied AI\n  + Infosys Generative AI\n  + Infosys Sustainability Services\n\n  ### Innovate\n\n[S5] Infosys Board Appoints Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO ...\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/newsroom/press-releases/2026/board-appoints-ceo-designate.html\nNandan Nilekani, Chairman of the Board, Infosys said, “The Board is delighted to appoint Dash as CEO Designate. Our industry is entering a period of considerable change. The Board was clear that our next CEO needed to combine the ability to drive bold transformation with the judgment to preserve the values and customer trust that have always distinguished Infosys. It gives me great pleasure that we have an internal leader as our next CEO. On behalf of the Board, I also thank Salil for his [...] Infosys (NSE, BSE, NYSE: INFY), a global leader in AI-first business consulting and technology services, today announced the appointment of Ashiss Kumar Dash as CEO Designate. This appointment is based on the recommendation of the Nomination and Remuneration Committee of the Infosys Board, and is for a period of five years, subject to the approval of shareholders. [...] Infosys (NSE, BSE, NYSE: INFY) is a global leader in AI first business consulting and technology services. Over 325,000 of our people work to amplify human potential and create the next opportunity for people, businesses, and communities. As navigators of enterprise transformation, we enable businesses in 59 countries to unlock AI value at scale. With over four decades of experience in managing the systems and workings of global enterprises, we accelerate business transformation through our\n\n[S6] Salil Parekh to step down as Infosys CEO in March 2027 ...\nURL: https://www.peoplematters.in/news/leadership/salil-parekh-to-step-down-as-infosys-ceo-in-march-2027-after-nine-year-tenure-51169\nSalil Parekh will step down as Chief Executive Officer of Infosys on March 31, 2027, bringing to a close a nine-year tenure that began during one of the most turbulent periods in the company's history. His successor, Ashiss Kumar Dash, will assume the role from April 1, 2027, following a planned leadership transition. [...] ### Leadership\n\n# Salil Parekh to step down as Infosys CEO in March 2027 after nine-year tenure\n\n\n\nSamriddhi Srivastava•Join UsGoogle News\n\nLinkedIn|\n\nJoin UsGoogle News\n\nArticle cover image\n\nThe outgoing chief executive says Infosys is well positioned for the AI era after doubling revenue, expanding its workforce and strengthening the company's large deals business. [...] He also said Infosys has maintained pricing discipline on large contracts, choosing not to pursue deals where commercial terms did not align with the company's expectations.\n\n## Preparing the next generation of leadership\n\nParekh expressed confidence in Ashiss Kumar Dash, who will begin working alongside him during the transition period before formally taking over as CEO in April 2027.\n\n[S7] Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as ...\nURL: https://indianewengland.com/infosys-names-ashiss-kumar-dash-ceo-designate-as-salil-parekh-prepares-to-step-down\nINDIA New England News\n\n Search for\n\nBusiness\n\n# Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as Salil Parekh Prepares to Step Down\n\nJuly 23, 2026\n\n1,138  1 minute read\n\nFacebook   X   LinkedIn   Tumblr   Pinterest   Reddit   VKontakte   Odnoklassniki   Pocket\n\n\n\nBengaluru–Infosys announced Thursday that CEO and Managing Director Salil Parekh will step down after nine years at the helm, with Ashiss Kumar Dash appointed as his successor. [...] Parekh will leave the role effective April 1, 2027, following the completion of his second term. He joined Infosys in January 2018 and is the longest-serving non-founder CEO in the company’s history.\n\nDash will become CEO and Managing Director on April 1, 2027, subject to the completion of statutory requirements, Infosys said in a regulatory filing. [...] Nilekani also praised Parekh for strengthening Infosys during his tenure.\n\n“On behalf of the Board, I also thank Salil for his outstanding leadership over 9 years. Under his stewardship, Infosys has strengthened its market position, expanded its capabilities, delivered significant value to shareholders, and built a strong platform for future growth,” he said.\n\nParekh’s current five-year term is scheduled to end March 31, 2027, allowing Dash to take over the following day. (Source: IANS)\n\n[S8] What's next for Salil Parekh? Outgoing Infosys CEO on life ...\nURL: https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/information-technology/whats-next-for-salil-parekh-outgoing-infosys-ceo-on-life-after-infosys-and-nandan-nilekani-13990109.html\nAlso read: You need companies like Infosys to make AI work in enterprises, says CEO Parekh\n\nBacks Ashiss Dash\n\nParekh also strongly endorsed CEO-designate Ashiss Dash, who was named last week to succeed him from April 1, 2027.\n\nCalling Dash ‘a very good friend’ and ‘a great leader’, Parekh said the two would work closely over the coming months to ensure a smooth leadership transition. [...] \"I've worked with him for so many years. Since I started, we put him in this role and he's done a very good job,\" Parekh said. \"He's great with people, he's great with clients and he's built a nice portfolio of the business, both in terms of growth and the way the economics work.\"\n\nFrom October, Parekh will mentor Dash to help broaden his exposure across businesses outside the verticals he currently oversees. [...] Chandra R Srikanth\n\nDiscover the latest Business News, Sensex, and Nifty updates. Obtain Personal Finance insights, tax queries, and expert opinions on Moneycontrol or download the Moneycontrol App to stay updated!\n\n## Watch\n\n## Subscribe to Tech Newsletters\n\nFind the best of Al News in one place, specially curated for you every\nweekend.\n\nStay on top of the latest tech trends and biggest startup news.\n\n### Trending news\n\n[S9] Infosys names insider Ashiss Kumar Dash next CEO, trims ...\nURL: https://www.reuters.com/world/india/indias-infosys-misses-quarterly-revenue-view-names-ceo-designate-2026-07-23\nSign up here.\n\nDash, who ​heads the company's energy and utilities business, will take over in April 2027 for a five-year term ​after Salil Parekh steps down at the end of his tenure in March, the ⁠company said.\n\nThe appointment comes as India's $315 billion IT sector wrestles with the impact of AI on technology spending ​and traditional outsourcing models. [...] The Bengaluru-based firm narrowed its fiscal 2027 revenue growth forecast to 1.5%-3.0% from 1.5%-3.5%, citing cautious client spending amid AI-driven disruption. Analysts had expected growth of 2.5%-4.5%.\n\nParekh said the forecast's upper end reflected expectations of a stronger ​macroeconomic environment, which have ​yet to materialise.\n\nStoxBox analyst Sagar ⁠Shetty said the forecast downgrade likely reflects a more pressuring environment going forward. [...] BENGALURU, July 23 (Reuters) - Infosys (INFY.NS) named company veteran Ashiss Kumar Dash as its next ‌CEO on Thursday, tapping a three-decade insider to lead India's No. 2 IT firm through an AI-driven upheaval reshaping the technology services industry.\n\nThe succession plan was announced alongside a cut to the company's annual revenue growth forecast, sending its U.S.-listed shares down 5% in early trading.\n\nSign up here.\n\n[S10] Infosys Begins Next CEO Hunt 'Quietly': Who’s Next Still Remain Unanswered – Outlook Business\nURL: https://www.outlookbusiness.com/corporate/infosys-begins-next-ceo-hunt-quietly-whos-next-still-remain-unanswered\nInfosys has quietly initiated a CEO succession process, even as current chief Salil Parekh continues in the role.\n The board is likely to consider only a short extension (around 2 years) for Parekh to ensure a smooth, planned leadership transition.\n While internal and external candidates are being evaluated, no clear successor has emerged yet, keeping the leadership question open. [...] The board of Infosys is expected to take up the question of leadership succession at its meeting as its incumbent CEO Salil Parekh, 61, is unlikely to receive a full third five-year term, given that the normal retirement age at the firm is 60.\n\nParekh's current term ends in March 2027. Rather than a full extension, he is expected to receive a two-year continuation, which would be used to oversee and manage an orderly succession process, according to a report by the Economic Times.\n\n[S11] Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html\n+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] + Healthcare\n  + High Technology\n  + Industrial Manufacturing\n  + Information Services & Publishing\n  + Insurance\n  + Life Sciences\n  + Logistics & Distribution\n  + Media and Entertainment\n  + Mining\n  + Retail\n  + Semiconductor\n  + Travel and Hospitality\n  + Utilities\n  + Waste Management\n ## Services\n\n  ### Insights\n\n  + Infosys Topaz\n  + Applied AI\n  + Infosys Generative AI\n  + Infosys Sustainability Services\n\n  ### Innovate [...] Salil has helped transform Infosys into a leading digital, cloud, and AI company. Salil helps set the strategy and nurture a leadership team to drive its execution. Infosys is in the top decile of shareholder return during his tenure, leading in client satisfaction results, and leading in employee engagement scores.\n\nSalil has a strong track record of driving transformations, executing business turnarounds, and managing successful acquisitions.\n\n[S12] Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...\nURL: https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors\nHome\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] Based in India, Parekh brings over three decades of experience in the global IT services industry. Parekh holds a Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay. [...] “I am delighted and honored to be inducted to the board of AdvanceCT and express my sincere thanks to the state of Connecticut. I look forward to working with my fellow board members and with the state’s leadership to further deepen collaboration between government and business,” said Mr. Parekh.\n\nInfosys has a Technology and Innovation Hub in Hartford and employs over 900 people in Connecticut.\n\n[S13] World Economic Forum 2025 | Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/wef/2025/salil-parekh.html\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer & Managing Director, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh\n\n[S14] Infosys (Organization, from memory)\nURL: memory:Infosys\n{\"current_ceo\":\"Salil Parekh\",\"ceo_designate\":\"Ashiss Kumar Dash\"}\n\n[S15] Salil Parekh (Person, from memory)\nURL: memory:Salil Parekh\n{\"role\":\"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys\",\"start_date\":\"January 2, 2018\",\"tenure_end_date\":\"March 31, 2027\",\"predecessor\":\"U. B. Pravin Rao (interim CEO)\"}",{"json":true}]}
