{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:03:12.153Z","session":"45ff7e02-8dd8-4f23-905f-fa7c992e0eb1","event":"tool.end","callId":"d42e06a5-003e-40b3-a5f2-61d7ab18b174","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2316,"result":[{"title":"Zerodha FY25 revenue drops 11.5% to Rs 8,847 crore","url":"https://theheadandtale.com/fintech-news/zerodha-fy25-revenue-drops-11-5--to-rs-8847-crore","content":"Zerodha's net profit narrowed to Rs 4,237 crore in FY25 from Rs 5,496 crore in the previous fiscal.\n\nBy Team Head&Tale • Nov 24, 2025 • 01:42 PM\n\n1 min read\n\nZerodha FY25 revenue drops 11.5% to Rs 8,847 crore  1 min read\n\nShare\n\nAdd as preferred source on Google\n\nZerodha recorded an 11.5% drop in revenue from operations to Rs 8,847 crore in the fiscal ended March 31, 2025 from Rs 9,993 crore in the previous fiscal. [...] Zerodha's net profit narrowed to Rs 4,237 crore in FY25 from Rs 5,496 crore in the previous fiscal, according to consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies.\n\nTotal expenses of the stock broking company grew to Rs 3,238 crore during the fiscal as compared to Rs 3,119 crore in FY24. [...] In its first filing since getting listed, Groww last week said that its revenue from operations dropped 9.5% in the second quarter ended September to Rs 1,018.74 from Rs 1,125.38 crore in the same period in FY25. Its net profit, however, jumped 12% to Rs 471 crore during the quarter from Rs 420 crore in the same period in the previous fiscal.\n\nRelated Topics & Keywords\n\n#Financials#Net Profit#Operating Revenue#Pampl#Revenue#Revenue From Operations#Total Expenditure#Zerodha","score":0.96469927},{"title":"Zerodha Revenue Falls In FY25, Profit Drops 23% - BW Disrupt","url":"https://www.bwdisrupt.com/article/zerodha-revenue-falls-in-fy25-profit-drops-23-580874","content":"Zerodha reported a decline in revenue and profit for FY25 as regulatory changes, reduced trading activity and a fall in active users affected performance. The company posted revenue of Rs 8,868.2 crore, down from Rs 9,994.5 crore in FY24, an 11.2 per cent drop. Net profit declined 23 per cent to Rs 4,236.7 crore, according to Tracxn data, as per media reports. [...] logo\n\nSunday | Sep 20 2026 | 02:23:10 PM\n\n# Zerodha Revenue Falls In FY25, Profit Drops 23%\n\nBW Online Bureau;)   Nov 24, 2025\n\n # Zerodha\n # Revenue\n\nZerodha’s FY25 revenue slips to Rs 8,868 crore and profit falls 23 per cent as regulatory pressure, lower trading activity and user decline weigh on performance [...] For the September quarter, Groww reported net profit of Rs 471.33 crore, a 12 per cent rise, even as revenue fell to Rs 1,018.7 crore, a 9.5 per cent decline.\n\nZerodha holds a 15.8 per cent market share with 7.26 million users. Brokerage income remains its primary revenue driver, supported by investment management fees, software services and interest income.","score":0.94761914},{"title":"Zerodha's revenue drops to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25, market share remains strong | KaroStartup posted on the topic | LinkedIn","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/karo-startup_zerodhas-revenue-from-operations-decreased-activity-7397935828779532288-EbM-","content":"Zerodha’s revenue from operations decreased to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25 from Rs 9,993 crore in FY24, according to its consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies (RoC) show. According to the latest National Stock Exchange data, Zerodha has 7.26 million users and holds a 15.8% market share. Brokerage income continues to be its primary revenue stream, while investment management fees, software services, and interest income also contribute to its overall operating [...] overall operating revenue. [...] Muthuraman Kasimani   1mo \n\n Report this comment","score":0.88372874},{"title":"Zerodha revenue and profit remain flat in FY 26; reports net profit of Rs 4,300 crore","url":"https://www.moneycontrol.com/technology/zerodha-revenue-and-profit-remain-flat-in-fy-26-reports-net-profit-of-rs-4-300-crore-article-14016247.html","content":"According to a blog post by co-founder and CEO Nithin Kamath, the company has reported around Rs 8,500 crore in revenue, while net profits stood at around Rs 4,300 crore, similar to FY 25 figures.\n\n“The last couple of years have been mixed for brokers. We had to take revenue hits because of regulatory changes, and then the Indian market peaked in September 2024. Volumes steadily declined after that, and growth has been muted,” Kamath said in the post. [...] Zerodha does not disclose absolute numbers, but shares a bar graph with indicative numbers.\n\nKamath had warned last year that FY 26 could be worse than FY 25, citing an increase in STT (securities transaction tax)on options and the reduction of expiries to two weekly contracts on options.\n\n## Related Stories\n\nMTF to the rescue","score":0.84858394},{"title":"Zerodha - Products, Competitors, Financials, Employees, Headquarters Locations","url":"https://www.cbinsights.com/company/zerodha","content":"almost flat in FY26 versus ₹8,847 Cr a fiscal year ago. Despite the revenue squeeze, Zerodha kept its bottom line largely intact, with profit rising marginally to ₹4,283 Cr in FY26 from ₹4,231 Cr in FY25. So, with its core revenue engine slowing, what is keeping Zerodha's profits afloat? The answer: Zerodha is increasingly making money from sources other than brokerage. Interest income (₹2,269 Cr): The discount broker earns interest on its cash balances and other interest-generating assets. [...] Zerodha's core business is no longer growing. Regulatory curbs and changing investor behaviour are cooling trading activity and squeezing brokerage revenue. Broking revenue fell 10.4% from ₹3,066 Cr in FY25 to ₹2,738 Cr in FY26. Net transaction charges (income earned from exchange-related transaction fee rebates) also fell to zero from ₹400 Cr in FY25 due to SEBI's true-to-label norm framework. In a blog post, CEO Nithin Kamath hinted that its overall top line remained almost flat in FY26 [...] revenue. The financials show the change clearly. Delayed payment charges and MTF generated ₹448 Cr in FY26, compared with ₹22 Cr in FY25. The reason this matters is simple: Brokerage revenue depends heavily on customers trading. MTF allows Zerodha to earn interest from customers who borrow to invest, creating a revenue stream that is less dependent on the number of trades. The bigger issue is that MTF is being built against a business that remains heavily exposed to derivatives. Avinash","score":0.8201387}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:03:12.283Z","session":"45ff7e02-8dd8-4f23-905f-fa7c992e0eb1","event":"tool.end","callId":"821dcebf-97b5-42eb-89c2-015dbc2a6bf7","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2442,"result":[{"title":"Zerodha - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zerodha","content":"Decrease\nDecrease\n\nZerodha Broking Ltd is an Indian brokerage and financial services company, based in Bengaluru. It offers an online trading platform that facilitates institutional and retail trading of stocks, derivatives \"Derivative (finance)\"), currencies, commodities, mutual funds, and bonds \"Bond (finance)\"). It is a member of the National Stock Exchange of India (NSE), Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE), and the Multi Commodity Exchange (MCX). [...] ## History\n\nZerodha was founded in August 2010 by brothers Nithin Kamath and Nikhil Kamath as a discount brokerage firm. The name Zerodha was a combination of words for the company's ideals: zero and rodha, the Sanskrit word for 'barrier'. The company started with six employees and ₹2 crore in seed money drawn from Nithin Kamath's personal savings and contributions from a Singapore-based friend. [...] Zerodha was founded and bootstrapped \"Bootstrapping (business)\") by brothers Nithin and Nikhil Kamath. As of May 2024, it has 7.5 million active customers registered with the NSE, making it the second-largest stockbroker in India.\n\n## History","score":0.9159971},{"title":"Zerodha Information","url":"https://rocketreach.co/zerodha-profile_b5e6e10bf42e5993","content":"Zerodha is an Indian financial services company (member of NSE, BSE, MCX) that offers brokerage-free equity investments, retail, institutional broking, currencies, and commodities trading. Zerodha Broking Limited | SEBI Registration No.: INZ000031633 [...] Website\nRevenue$88.9 million\nEmployees2,870  (1,407 on RocketReach)\nFounded2010\nAddressJ.p Nagar 4th Phase, Bengaluru, Karnataka 560078, IN\nPhone+91 80 4913 2020\nTechnologiesJavaScript , HTML , PHP+52 more(view full list)\nIndustryFinancial Services, Finance, Finance General, Online Trading, Financial Networking & Knowledge Center, Stock Exchanges, Stock Trading, Lending and Investments, Commodity Trading, Currency Trading, Discount Broking, Fintech\nWeb Rank2552\nWeb Visits13 Million","score":0.8980626},{"title":"Zerodha - Welcome to Zerodha, your friendly neighbourhood brokerage.","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/zerodha","content":"# Zerodha\nWelcome to Zerodha, your friendly neighbourhood brokerage.\nFinancial Services • Bangalore, Karnataka • 608,778 followers • 501-1,000 employees\n\n## Overview\nZerodha is an Indian financial services company (member of NSE, BSE, MCX) that offers brokerage-free equity investments, retail, institutional broking, currencies, and commodities trading. Zerodha Broking Limited | SEBI Registration No.: INZ000031633\n\n### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\nN/A\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nFinancial Services [...] ### Company Size\n501-1,000 employees  \n2864 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed Zerodha as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\n2010\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: N/A\nLast Round Type: N/A\nTotal Rounds: N/A\nLast Round Raised: N/A\n\n### Investors\nN/A\n\n### Specialties\nOnline Trading, Financial Networking & Knowledge Center, Stock Trading, Commodity Trading, Currency Trading, Discount Broking, and Fintech [...] Additional jobs info: Analyst (3,898 open jobs). Engineer (4,853 open jobs). Developer (6,419 open jobs). Marketing Manager (727 open jobs). Software Engineer (4,254 open jobs). Scientist (246 open jobs). Finance Intern (37 open jobs). Writer (158 open jobs). Sales Manager (1,306 open jobs). Human Resources Intern (19 open jobs). Project Manager (1,811 open jobs). Associate Product Manager (335 open jobs). Python Developer (1,429 open jobs). Business Development Associate (365 open jobs).","score":0.8488849},{"title":"Zerodha Portfolio Investments, Zerodha Funds, Zerodha Exits","url":"https://www.cbinsights.com/investor/zerodha","content":"## About Zerodha\n\nZerodha is a zero brokerage firm and an Indian financial service company that offers low brokerage equity investments, retail and institutional broking, currencies and commodities trading, and mutual funds.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\n#153/154, 4th Cross, Dollars Colony, Opp. Clarence Public School, J.P Nagar 4th Phase\n\nBengaluru, 560078,\n\nIndia\n\n+91 80 4040 2020\n\nAre you an investor?\n\nSubmit your portfolio details now to be considered in our investor rankings. [...] K\n\nKarvy\n\nKarvy is a provider of integrated financial services in India. The company provides financial services including stock broking, depository participants, distribution of financial products like mutual funds and bonds, merchant banking and corporate finance, insurance broking, commodities broking, realty services, personal finance advisory services, placement of equity, IPOs, and others.\n\nLoading... [...] Kotak Securities\n\nKotak Securities is a company that focuses on providing opportunities in the capital markets, operating within the financial services industry. The company offers a range of services including online trading in the stock market, investment in futures and options, exchange traded funds, commodities, and mutual funds, among others. It primarily serves individuals and businesses interested in the financial markets. It was founded in 1994 and is based in Mumbai, India.\n\nU\n\nUpstox","score":0.8124067},{"title":"Our company, history, and the people behind it","url":"https://zerodha.com/about","content":"## We pioneered the discount broking model in India. Now, we are breaking ground with our technology.\n\nWe kick-started operations on the 15th of August, 2010 with the goal of breaking all barriers that traders and investors face in India in terms of cost, support, and technology. We named the company Zerodha, a combination of Zero and \"Rodha\", the Sanskrit word for barrier.\n\nToday, our disruptive pricing models and in-house technology have made us the biggest stock broker in India. [...] And yet, we are always up to something new every day. Catch up on the latest updates on our blog or see what the media is saying about us or learn more about our business and product philosophies.\n\n## People\n\n##### Nithin Kamath\n\nFounder, CEO\n\nNithin bootstrapped and founded Zerodha in 2010 to overcome the hurdles he faced during his decade long stint as a trader. Today, Zerodha has changed the landscape of the Indian broking industry. [...] COO\n\nBio\n\nVenu is the backbone of Zerodha taking care of operations and ensuring that we are compliant to rules and regulations. He has over a dozen certifications in financial markets and is also proficient in technical analysis. Workouts, cycling, and adventuring is what he does outside of Zerodha.\n\n  \n  \n\n##### Seema Patil\n\nDirector\n\nBio\n\nSeema who has lead the quality team since the beginning of Zerodha, is now a director. She is an extremely disciplined fitness enthusiast.","score":0.7539928}]}
