{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:03:12.415Z","session":"45ff7e02-8dd8-4f23-905f-fa7c992e0eb1","event":"llm.start","callId":"e66231e2-a98e-40c4-a2a5-1735c35b77ca","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence, as {\"name\", \"type\", \"data\": {key facts}}.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"data\": object}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: What was Zerodha's revenue and net profit in FY2025, and how many employees does it have?\nSub-questions to cover:\n- What was Zerodha's total revenue for financial year 2024-2025 (FY2025)?\n- What was Zerodha's net profit after tax for financial year 2024-2025 (FY2025)?\n- How many employees does Zerodha currently employ?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Zerodha FY25 revenue drops 11.5% to Rs 8,847 crore\nURL: https://theheadandtale.com/fintech-news/zerodha-fy25-revenue-drops-11-5--to-rs-8847-crore\nZerodha's net profit narrowed to Rs 4,237 crore in FY25 from Rs 5,496 crore in the previous fiscal.\n\nBy Team Head&Tale • Nov 24, 2025 • 01:42 PM\n\n1 min read\n\nZerodha FY25 revenue drops 11.5% to Rs 8,847 crore  1 min read\n\nShare\n\nAdd as preferred source on Google\n\nZerodha recorded an 11.5% drop in revenue from operations to Rs 8,847 crore in the fiscal ended March 31, 2025 from Rs 9,993 crore in the previous fiscal. [...] Zerodha's net profit narrowed to Rs 4,237 crore in FY25 from Rs 5,496 crore in the previous fiscal, according to consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies.\n\nTotal expenses of the stock broking company grew to Rs 3,238 crore during the fiscal as compared to Rs 3,119 crore in FY24. [...] In its first filing since getting listed, Groww last week said that its revenue from operations dropped 9.5% in the second quarter ended September to Rs 1,018.74 from Rs 1,125.38 crore in the same period in FY25. Its net profit, however, jumped 12% to Rs 471 crore during the quarter from Rs 420 crore in the same period in the previous fiscal.\n\nRelated Topics & Keywords\n\n#Financials#Net Profit#Operating Revenue#Pampl#Revenue#Revenue From Operations#Total Expenditure#Zerodha\n\n[S2] Zerodha Revenue Falls In FY25, Profit Drops 23% - BW Disrupt\nURL: https://www.bwdisrupt.com/article/zerodha-revenue-falls-in-fy25-profit-drops-23-580874\nZerodha reported a decline in revenue and profit for FY25 as regulatory changes, reduced trading activity and a fall in active users affected performance. The company posted revenue of Rs 8,868.2 crore, down from Rs 9,994.5 crore in FY24, an 11.2 per cent drop. Net profit declined 23 per cent to Rs 4,236.7 crore, according to Tracxn data, as per media reports. [...] logo\n\nSunday | Sep 20 2026 | 02:23:10 PM\n\n# Zerodha Revenue Falls In FY25, Profit Drops 23%\n\nBW Online Bureau;)   Nov 24, 2025\n\n # Zerodha\n # Revenue\n\nZerodha’s FY25 revenue slips to Rs 8,868 crore and profit falls 23 per cent as regulatory pressure, lower trading activity and user decline weigh on performance [...] For the September quarter, Groww reported net profit of Rs 471.33 crore, a 12 per cent rise, even as revenue fell to Rs 1,018.7 crore, a 9.5 per cent decline.\n\nZerodha holds a 15.8 per cent market share with 7.26 million users. Brokerage income remains its primary revenue driver, supported by investment management fees, software services and interest income.\n\n[S3] Zerodha's revenue drops to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25, market share remains strong | KaroStartup posted on the topic | LinkedIn\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/karo-startup_zerodhas-revenue-from-operations-decreased-activity-7397935828779532288-EbM-\nZerodha’s revenue from operations decreased to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25 from Rs 9,993 crore in FY24, according to its consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies (RoC) show. According to the latest National Stock Exchange data, Zerodha has 7.26 million users and holds a 15.8% market share. Brokerage income continues to be its primary revenue stream, while investment management fees, software services, and interest income also contribute to its overall operating [...] overall operating revenue. [...] Muthuraman Kasimani   1mo \n\n Report this comment\n\n[S4] Zerodha revenue and profit remain flat in FY 26; reports net profit of Rs 4,300 crore\nURL: https://www.moneycontrol.com/technology/zerodha-revenue-and-profit-remain-flat-in-fy-26-reports-net-profit-of-rs-4-300-crore-article-14016247.html\nAccording to a blog post by co-founder and CEO Nithin Kamath, the company has reported around Rs 8,500 crore in revenue, while net profits stood at around Rs 4,300 crore, similar to FY 25 figures.\n\n“The last couple of years have been mixed for brokers. We had to take revenue hits because of regulatory changes, and then the Indian market peaked in September 2024. Volumes steadily declined after that, and growth has been muted,” Kamath said in the post. [...] Zerodha does not disclose absolute numbers, but shares a bar graph with indicative numbers.\n\nKamath had warned last year that FY 26 could be worse than FY 25, citing an increase in STT (securities transaction tax)on options and the reduction of expiries to two weekly contracts on options.\n\n## Related Stories\n\nMTF to the rescue\n\n[S5] Zerodha - Products, Competitors, Financials, Employees, Headquarters Locations\nURL: https://www.cbinsights.com/company/zerodha\nalmost flat in FY26 versus ₹8,847 Cr a fiscal year ago. Despite the revenue squeeze, Zerodha kept its bottom line largely intact, with profit rising marginally to ₹4,283 Cr in FY26 from ₹4,231 Cr in FY25. So, with its core revenue engine slowing, what is keeping Zerodha's profits afloat? The answer: Zerodha is increasingly making money from sources other than brokerage. Interest income (₹2,269 Cr): The discount broker earns interest on its cash balances and other interest-generating assets. [...] Zerodha's core business is no longer growing. Regulatory curbs and changing investor behaviour are cooling trading activity and squeezing brokerage revenue. Broking revenue fell 10.4% from ₹3,066 Cr in FY25 to ₹2,738 Cr in FY26. Net transaction charges (income earned from exchange-related transaction fee rebates) also fell to zero from ₹400 Cr in FY25 due to SEBI's true-to-label norm framework. In a blog post, CEO Nithin Kamath hinted that its overall top line remained almost flat in FY26 [...] revenue. The financials show the change clearly. Delayed payment charges and MTF generated ₹448 Cr in FY26, compared with ₹22 Cr in FY25. The reason this matters is simple: Brokerage revenue depends heavily on customers trading. MTF allows Zerodha to earn interest from customers who borrow to invest, creating a revenue stream that is less dependent on the number of trades. The bigger issue is that MTF is being built against a business that remains heavily exposed to derivatives. Avinash\n\n[S6] Annual Report 2024-25.pdf\nURL: https://zerodhacapital.com/static/disclosures/report/Annual%20Report%202024-25.pdf\nSpencer Plaza, Anna Salai, Chennai-600002 Website: zerodhacapital.com Email id: nbfc@zerodha.com Phone No: 080-4716-6888 DIRECTOR’S REPORT To the Members, The Board of Directors have the pleasure in presenting the 12th Board’s Report of Zerodha Capital Private Limited (“Company”/” Zerodha Capital”) together with the Audited Financial Statements for the Financial Year ended on March 31, 2025. 1. FINANCIAL SUMMARY AND HIGHLIGHTS The Financial Statements of the Company for the year ended March 31, [...] Email id: nbfc@zerodha.com Phone No: 080-4716-6888 7. (a) Amount spent on CSR Projects (both Ongoing Project and other than Ongoing Project): 9,95,000/- (b) Amount spent on Administrative Overheads: NIL (c) Amount spent on Impact Assessment, if applicable. NIL (d) Total amount spent for the Financial Year [(a)+(b)+(c)]. 9,95,000/- (e) CSR amount spent or unspent for the financial year: Total Amount Spent for the Financial Year. Amount Unspent Total Amount transferred to Unspent CSR Account as [...] appointed M/s TARAI & CO (FRN: 022166S) as Statutory Auditors of the Company for a term of Five years CIN: U67100KA2014PTC073653 Registered Office: No. 680, 15th Cross, J.P Nagar 2nd Phase Bangalore 560078 Branch office: No.172/1F/12A, (old Door No.769-1F-12A), Spencer Plaza, Anna Salai, Chennai-600002 Website: zerodhacapital.com Email id: nbfc@zerodha.com Phone No: 080-4716-6888 i.e., till the conclusion of the 13th Annual General Meeting of the Company to be held for Financial Year 2\n\n[S7] Annual Report of Trustees - 2024-25.pdf\nURL: https://assets.zerodhafundhouse.com/statutory-reports/disclosures/Annual%20Report%20of%20Trustees%20-%202024-25.pdf\nKarnataka. Zerodha Trustee Private Limited 1 TO THE MEMBERS Your Directors present the Board Report and the Audited Financial Statements of the Zerodha Trustee Private Limited (“the Company”) for the Financial Year ended March 31, 2025 together with the reports of the Auditors thereon. FINANCIAL RESULTS: The Financial Statement of the Company for the year ended March 31, 2025 has been prepared in accordance with the Indian Accounting Standards notified under Section 133 and Schedule III to the [...] Sd/- Swapnil Kale Partner Membership Number: 117812 UDIN: 25117812BMNUUP5645 Mumbai June 27, 2025 Zerodha Trustee Private Limited Balance sheet as at March 31, 2025 (All amount in ₹'000, unless stated otherwise) Notes As at March 31, 2025 As at March 31, 2024 Assets Non-current assets Right of use asset 3 199.50 313.49 Financial assets Other financial assets 4 220.45 205.18 Deferred tax assets (Net) 5 - - Total non-current assets 419.94 518.67 Current assets Financial assets Trade Receivables 6 [...] of even date to the Members of Zerodha Trustee Private Limited on the Financial Statements for the year ended March 31, 2025 Report on the Internal Financial Controls under Clause (i) of Sub-section 3 of Section 143 of the Companies Act, 2013 (“the Act”) We have audited the internal financial controls with reference to financial statements of Zerodha Trustee Private Limited (“the Company”) as of March 31, 2025 in conjunction with our audit of the financial statements of the Company fo\n\n[S8] 2025 Report\nURL: https://zerodha.com/open-source/2025-report\n# 2025 Report\n\n15 Dec 2025\n\n  \n  \n\nAt Zerodha, our commitment to Free (libre) and Open Source Software (FOSS) remains strong. Last year, we joined the Open Source Pledge and committed to sharing annual reports of our financial contributions. This is our 2025 report.\n\nThe Open Source Pledge encourages companies to contribute at least $2,000 per full-time developer annually to the open source projects they depend on. We continue to exceed this baseline significantly.\n\n  \n\n### Past 12 months [...] At Zerodha, our commitment to the open source community extends beyond financial contributions. We have actively engaged in initiatives that foster the sustainability of FOSS. We co-founded the FOSS United Foundation to bolster the open source ecosystem in India. We also support TinkerHub, a hub for FOSS tinkering and innovation. Additionally, we continue to maintain several open source projects that originated from our work at Zerodha.\n\n  \n\nOpen source initiatives\n\n[S9] ZERODHA BROKING LIMITED - 2026 Company Profile & Financials - Tracxn\nURL: https://tracxn.com/d/legal-entities/india/zerodha-broking-limited/__v553aNZpzCj2Bvf4xhnL-tRmJFFZ-TN4gXVbm8w0W1Y\nZERODHA BROKING LIMITED's last Annual General Meeting (AGM) was held on Sep 22, 2025 as per records from Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA). ZERODHA BROKING LIMITED's authorised share capital is ₹112Cr and its paid up capital is ₹73.5Cr. The current board of directors of ZERODHA BROKING LIMITED comprises Nikhil Kamath, Venu Madhav kota Subramanya and 5 more.\n\nZERODHA BROKING LIMITED generated more than ₹1,000 Cr in revenue for the financial year ending on Mar 31, 2025. [...] | Main Activity Group Code | Description of Main Activity | Business Activity Code | Description of Business Activity | Turnover Percentage |\n ---  --- \n| K | Financial and insurance activities | 64 | Financial service activities, except insurance and pension funding | tjb |\n| K | Financial and insurance activities | 66 | Activities auxiliary to financial service and insurance activities | d{j |\n\n## Documents of ZERODHA BROKING LIMITEDFY 25 Available15 mins\n\n### Filing Summary [...] | Vasanth kumar Jayapal | Director | Current | Oct 21, 2021 | 4 Years 10 Months |\n| Santosh Tirumal Hegde | Director | Current | May 02, 2025 | 1 Year 3 Months |\n| Karthik Rangappa | Additional Director | Current | Dec 24, 2025 | 8 Months |\n\n[S10] Zerodha Broking Number of Employees 2026 | Employee Count & Headcount Data | Revelio Labs\nURL: https://www.reveliolabs.com/companies/zerodha-broking/employees\nZerodha Broking had 2,183 employees in 2026, a 5.8% decline (-138) from 2025.\n Zerodha Broking had 2,199 employees in 2025, a 5.5% decline (-156) from 2024.\n Zerodha Broking had 2,355 employees in 2024, a 1.9% increase (+83) from 2023.\n Zerodha Broking had 2,272 employees in 2023, a 2.8% increase (+73) from 2022.\n\nZerodha Broking's total workforce has declined from 2,231 employees in 2023 to 2,183 in 2026. Zerodha Broking's headcount peaked at 2,355 in 2024. [...] How fast is Zerodha Broking growing?\n:   In 2026, Zerodha Broking's headcount shrank 5.8% to 2,183 employees, down from 2,321 in 2025.\n:   See the full headcount history\n\nWhere are Zerodha Broking employees located?\n:   Most Zerodha Broking employees are based in South Asia (97.0% of headcount), followed by North America and Arab States.\n:   Explore where the workforce is based [...] | Year | Qtr | Employees | YoY Change | YoY % |\n ---  --- \n| 2026 | Q1 | 2,183 | -138 | -5.8% |\n| 2025 | Q4 | 2,199 | -156 | -5.5% |\n| 2025 | Q3 | 2,283 | -27 | -1.8% |\n| 2025 | Q2 | 2,310 | +10 | -1.0% |\n| 2025 | Q1 | 2,321 | +30 | +1.0% |\n| 2024 | Q4 | 2,355 | +83 | +1.9% |\n| 2024 | Q3 | 2,310 | +44 | +1.3% |\n| 2024 | Q2 | 2,300 | +69 | +3.9% |\n| 2024 | Q1 | 2,291 | +72 | +2.3% |\n| 2023 | Q4 | 2,272 | +73 | +2.8% |\n| 2023 | Q3 | 2,266 | +40 | +2.7% |\n| 2023 | Q2 | 2,231 | -21 | +0.7% |\n\n[S11] Zerodha - Wikipedia\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zerodha\nZerodha was founded and bootstrapped \"Bootstrapping (business)\") by brothers Nithin and Nikhil Kamath. As of May 2024, it has 7.5 million active customers registered with the NSE, making it the second-largest stockbroker in India.\n\n## History\n\n[S12] Zerodha Employee Directory, Headcount & Staff | LeadIQ\nURL: https://leadiq.com/c/zerodha/5a1d7c7f2400002400564787/employee-directory\nLeadIQ logo\n\nLearn more at LeadIQ.com\n\nZerodha logo\n\n# Zerodha Employee Directory\n\nFinancial ServicesKarnataka, India1001-5000 Employees [...] LinkedIn logo\n\n## Zerodha Global Highlights\n\n### \n\nMinus sign iconPlus sign icon\n\n 1.7K\n United Arab Emirates\n Philippines\n\n  2\n Indonesia\n\n  1\n Saudi Arabia\n\n  1\n Iraq\n\n  1\n Qatar\n\n  1\n Russian Federation\n\n  1\n Jordan\n\n  1\n Bahrain\n\n  1\n\n### North America 71\n\nMinus sign iconPlus sign icon\n\n United States Of America\n\n  66\n Canada\n\n  3\n Honduras\n\n  1\n Mexico\n\n  1\n\n### Europe 24\n\nMinus sign iconPlus sign icon\n\n United Kingdom Of Great Britain And Northern Ireland\n\n  6\n Poland\n\n  5\n Italy [...] M