{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:04:17.002Z","session":"312e9bed-9d34-49fe-9a8e-df084d79301b","event":"llm.start","callId":"76f8f9da-05f5-4c09-886e-3856c5f78984","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence, as {\"name\", \"type\", \"data\": {key facts}}.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"data\": object}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: What was Zerodha's revenue and net profit in FY2025, and how many employees does it have?\nSub-questions to cover:\n- What was Zerodha's total revenue for financial year 2024-25 (FY2025)?\n- What was Zerodha's net profit for financial year 2024-25 (FY2025)?\n- What is Zerodha's current total employee headcount?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Zerodha FY25 revenue drops 11.5% to Rs 8847 crore\nURL: https://theheadandtale.com/fintech-news/zerodha-fy25-revenue-drops-11-5--to-rs-8847-crore\nZerodha's net profit narrowed to Rs 4,237 crore in FY25 from Rs 5,496 crore in the previous fiscal, according to consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies.\n\nTotal expenses of the stock broking company grew to Rs 3,238 crore during the fiscal as compared to Rs 3,119 crore in FY24. [...] Zerodha's net profit narrowed to Rs 4,237 crore in FY25 from Rs 5,496 crore in the previous fiscal.\n\nBy Team Head&Tale • Nov 24, 2025 • 01:42 PM\n\n1 min read\n\nZerodha FY25 revenue drops 11.5% to Rs 8,847 crore  1 min read\n\nShare\n\nAdd as preferred source on Google\n\nZerodha recorded an 11.5% drop in revenue from operations to Rs 8,847 crore in the fiscal ended March 31, 2025 from Rs 9,993 crore in the previous fiscal. [...] In its first filing since getting listed, Groww last week said that its revenue from operations dropped 9.5% in the second quarter ended September to Rs 1,018.74 from Rs 1,125.38 crore in the same period in FY25. Its net profit, however, jumped 12% to Rs 471 crore during the quarter from Rs 420 crore in the same period in the previous fiscal.\n\nRelated Topics & Keywords\n\n#Financials#Net Profit#Operating Revenue#Pampl#Revenue#Revenue From Operations#Total Expenditure#Zerodha\n\n[S2] Zerodha cash reserve stands at Rs 22,679 Cr in FY25\nURL: https://entrackr.com/fintrackr/zerodha-cash-reserve-stands-at-rs-22679-cr-in-fy25-10799921\nWith scale declining 11%, Zerodha’s profits fell 22.9% to Rs 4,237 crore in FY25 from Rs 5,496 crore in FY24. Despite the drop, the company still paid Rs 1,395 crore in taxes during the year. Its ROCE and EBITDA margins also softened and recorded at 32% and 63.78% respectively. [...] Zerodha’s revenue from operations decreased to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25 from Rs 9,993 crore in FY24, according to its consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies (RoC) show. [...] ## Zerodha’s revenue from operations decreased to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25 from Rs 9,993 crore in FY24, according to its consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies (RoC) show.\n\nauthor-image/entrackr/media/member_avatars/2024/10/21/2024-10-21t083822584z-kunal-circle-png-768x768.png )\n\nKunal Manchanada\n\n Follow Us\n\nNew Update\n\n[S3] Zerodha's revenue drops to Rs 8847 crore in FY25, market ...\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/karo-startup_zerodhas-revenue-from-operations-decreased-activity-7397935828779532288-EbM-\nZerodha’s revenue from operations decreased to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25 from Rs 9,993 crore in FY24, according to its consolidated financial statements sourced from the Registrar of Companies (RoC) show. According to the latest National Stock Exchange data, Zerodha has 7.26 million users and holds a 15.8% market share. Brokerage income continues to be its primary revenue stream, while investment management fees, software services, and interest income also contribute to its overall operating [...] overall operating revenue. [...] # Zerodha's revenue drops to Rs 8,847 crore in FY25, market share remains strong\n\nThis title was summarized by AI from the post below.\n\n246,296 followers\n\n Report this post\n\n[S4] Zerodha revenue and profit remain flat in FY 26; reports net ...\nURL: https://www.moneycontrol.com/technology/zerodha-revenue-and-profit-remain-flat-in-fy-26-reports-net-profit-of-rs-4-300-crore-article-14016247.html\nAccording to a blog post by co-founder and CEO Nithin Kamath, the company has reported around Rs 8,500 crore in revenue, while net profits stood at around Rs 4,300 crore, similar to FY 25 figures.\n\n“The last couple of years have been mixed for brokers. We had to take revenue hits because of regulatory changes, and then the Indian market peaked in September 2024. Volumes steadily declined after that, and growth has been muted,” Kamath said in the post. [...] Bengaluru-based Groww reported a revenue of Rs 4,645 crore, and a net profit of over Rs 2,083 crore for FY 26. While these figures represent roughly half of Zerodha's financial performance, the firm is narrowing the margin at a rapid pace.\n\nMumbai-based Angel One reported revenue of Rs 5,136 crore and Rs 913 crore net profit in FY 26.\n\nDAILY-EVENING\n\nDAILY-EVENING [...] appreciate\n\nInvest in Apple, Nvidia, Microsoft, Tesla and 9,000+ U.S. stocks & ETFs. Start from just ₹1.\n\nInvest Now\n\n## Get Instant Loan\n\n### Check eligibility in just 5 mins\n\nUp to ₹50 lakhs | Starts at 9.99%\n\nNeed Urgent Cash\nNeed Urgent Cash\n\n# Zerodha revenue and profit remain flat in FY 26; reports net profit of Rs 4,300 crore\n\njoin Us On WhatsApp\nFollow Us On Google\nAdd as a Preferred Source on Google\n\nSnapshot AI\nread AI Shorts\nspeaker profile\n\nMarket Mastery\n\n[S5] Zerodha - Products, Competitors, Financials, Employees, Headquarters Locations\nURL: https://www.cbinsights.com/company/zerodha\nalmost flat in FY26 versus ₹8,847 Cr a fiscal year ago. Despite the revenue squeeze, Zerodha kept its bottom line largely intact, with profit rising marginally to ₹4,283 Cr in FY26 from ₹4,231 Cr in FY25. So, with its core revenue engine slowing, what is keeping Zerodha's profits afloat? The answer: Zerodha is increasingly making money from sources other than brokerage. Interest income (₹2,269 Cr): The discount broker earns interest on its cash balances and other interest-generating assets. [...] Zerodha's core business is no longer growing. Regulatory curbs and changing investor behaviour are cooling trading activity and squeezing brokerage revenue. Broking revenue fell 10.4% from ₹3,066 Cr in FY25 to ₹2,738 Cr in FY26. Net transaction charges (income earned from exchange-related transaction fee rebates) also fell to zero from ₹400 Cr in FY25 due to SEBI's true-to-label norm framework. In a blog post, CEO Nithin Kamath hinted that its overall top line remained almost flat in FY26 [...] revenue. The financials show the change clearly. Delayed payment charges and MTF generated ₹448 Cr in FY26, compared with ₹22 Cr in FY25. The reason this matters is simple: Brokerage revenue depends heavily on customers trading. MTF allows Zerodha to earn interest from customers who borrow to invest, creating a revenue stream that is less dependent on the number of trades. The bigger issue is that MTF is being built against a business that remains heavily exposed to derivatives. Avinash\n\n[S6] Annual Report of Trustees - 2024-25.pdf\nURL: https://assets.zerodhafundhouse.com/statutory-reports/disclosures/Annual%20