{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:05:34.162Z","session":"5a4c4c23-4a75-4f1b-bd54-29047608f8bf","event":"tool.end","callId":"19cea888-a7a3-42de-a87d-8bc993ad1778","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2581,"result":[{"title":"The Moon is made of green cheese","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Moon_is_made_of_green_cheese","content":"Wikipedia\nThe Free Encyclopedia\n\n## Contents\n\n# The Moon is made of green cheese\n\nPage semi-protected\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| icon | This article needs more citations. Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced material may be challenged and removed. Find sources: \"The Moon is made of green cheese\" – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR (December 2025) (Learn how and when to remove this message) |\n\nicon [...] of the said cheese will leave you unmoved.\" [...] \"The Moon is made of green cheese\" is a statement referring to a fanciful belief that the Moon is composed of cheese. In its original formulation as a proverb and metaphor for credulity with roots in fable, this refers to the perception of a simpleton who sees a reflection of the Moon in water and mistakes it for a round cheese wheel. It is widespread as a folkloric motif \"Morphology (folkloristics)\") among many of the world's cultures, and the notion has also found its way into children's","score":0.80442166},{"title":"Is the moon made of green cheese?","url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/thedullclub/posts/3485571914981236","content":"There was never an actual historical popular belief that the Moon is made of green cheese (cf. Flat Earth and the myth of the Flat Earth).","score":0.65146625},{"title":"The Moon, is it really made of cheese? - ESA's blogs","url":"https://blogs.esa.int/orion/2022/11/18/the-moon-is-it-really-made-of-cheese","content":"Paolo Marovino Posted on 6 Dec 2022 at 06:52\n\n  Fontina d’Aosta\n\n  Reply\n subdirectory\\_arrow\\_right\n\n  \n\n  Le Gall Michèle Posted on 8 Dec 2022 at 11:38\n\n  Je pense que ce pourrait être une meule d’émental, voire de comté savoyard ?\n\n  Reply\n subdirectory\\_arrow\\_right\n\n  \n\n  Carmen Posted on 9 Dec 2022 at 17:11\n\n  I think the moon is made of delicious Leerdammer cheese, Ñam Ñam!\n\n  Reply\n subdirectory\\_arrow\\_right\n\n  \n\n  Luke Posted on 16 Dec 2022 at 00:30 [...] It is often said that the Moon is made of cheese, and when inventor Wallace and his trusty canine companion Gromit, visited the Moon in their first adventure ‘A Grand Day Out’, they tasted the Moon and concluded it was like no other cheese they’d tasted before!\n\n \n\nWallace and Gromit tasting the Moon. Credits: Aardman\n\n \n\nWe’re pretty sure the Moon isn’t made of cheese, but obviously more investigations need to be done – one of the objectives for Shaun the Sheep on his Artemis I mission. [...] Reply\n subdirectory\\_arrow\\_right\n\n  \n\n  Marques Paulo Posted on 4 Dec 2022 at 21:20\n\n  Ok\n\n  Reply\n subdirectory\\_arrow\\_right\n\n  \n\n  Sandrine Le clouerec Posted on 4 Dec 2022 at 22:03\n\n  I thing they are a mixe of cheese l’île gouda cheddar roblochon comte etc..\n\n  Reply\n subdirectory\\_arrow\\_right\n\n  \n\n  Ricardo Posted on 4 Dec 2022 at 22:39\n\n  Serra da Estrela cheese, made in the mountainous region of Serra da Estrela in Portugal. It is sooo high that almost touches the moon.","score":0.5057865},{"title":"Earth's Moon","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/moon","content":"September 19, 2026\n\n### Artemis II Science\n\nLunar science, space weather, astronaut health, and more.\n\n## Moon Composition & Structure\n\nLike Earth, the Moon consists of three main layers: a crust, a mantle, and a core. [...] 6 Min Read\n\nNASA, IBM Launch AI Foundation Model for Lunar Science\n\n3 Min Read\n\nWhat’s Up: September 2026 Skywatching Tips from NASA\n\nArticle5 Min Read\n\nHuman-Related Microbes May Survive Moon’s South Pole, NASA Finds\n\nArticle3 Min Read\n\nNASA’s LRO Images Falcon 9 Crater on Moon, Learns New Details\n\nArticle1 Min Read\n\n2026 Total Solar Eclipse in Spain\n\nImage Article\n\n### EXPLORATION X Science\n\n## The Science of Artemis [...] Billions of years ago, the Moon was a molten world. As it solidified, the heaviest materials (metals like iron) sank down into the Moon’s center, and the lighter materials (lower density rocks) rose towards the surface. The result is a structure a bit like a chocolate-dipped cherry – solid core, mostly solid/partly liquid mantle, and thin outer crust.\n\nGo\n\n## Does the Moon Have an Atmosphere?\n\nYes, but just barely.","score":0.124649465},{"title":"Moon Water and Ices - NASA Science","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/moon/moon-water-and-ices","content":"In 2020, NASA scientists confirmed the presence of water on the Moon.\n\n## Latest News\n\nMore Moon News & Features\n\nArticle\n\n6 Min Read\n\nNASA’s Moon Orbiter Spots New, ‘Once-in-Century’ Moon Crater\n\nArticle\n\n3 Min Read\n\nNASA Will Attempt to Observe Rocket Part’s Lunar Impact\n\n63 Min Read\n\nArtemis II Lunar Science4 Min Read\n\nJohnson’s Cindy Evans Prepares Artemis Teams for Lunar Science\n\nArticle2 Min Read\n\nArtemis II Flight Day 7: Crew Makes Long‑Distance Call, Begins Return\n\nKeep Exploring [...] article  12 hours ago NASA’s Machines for Mars Make Beer Bubbly \n\n3 min read\n\n### NASA’s Machines for Mars Make Beer Bubbly\n\narticle  23 hours ago Cloudy Cloak Over the Northwest\n\n2 min read\n\n### Cloudy Cloak Over the Northwest\n\narticle  1 day ago\n\n### Highlights\n\nNASA Astronaut to Answer Questions from New Hampshire Students\n\n2 min read\n\n### NASA Astronaut to Answer Questions from New Hampshire Students [...] ### Science\n\n Earth Science\n Planetary Science\n Astrophysics & Space Science\n The Sun & Heliophysics\n Biological & Physical Sciences\n Lunar Science\n Citizen Science\n Astromaterials\n Aeronautics Research\n Human Space Travel Research\n\n### Aeronautics\n\n Science in the Air\n NASA Aircraft\n Flight Innovation\n Supersonic Flight\n Air Traffic Solutions\n Green Aviation Tech\n Drones & You\n\n### Technology","score":0.08914505}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:05:34.166Z","session":"5a4c4c23-4a75-4f1b-bd54-29047608f8bf","event":"tool.end","callId":"8df82abf-a8b5-4bdc-b8fd-f519c133c377","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2586,"result":[{"title":"History of Infosys - Origin, Timeline and Subsidiaries","url":"https://www.bajajfinserv.in/history-of-infosys","content":"Infosys was established in 1981 in Pune by seven engineers, including N.R. Narayana Murthy, with an initial capital of just US$250. The company's humble beginnings were marked by a vision to provide world-class IT services from India. In 1983, Infosys relocated its headquarters to Bengaluru, positioning itself in what would become India's Silicon Valley. Over the years, Infosys has grown exponentially, becoming a global leader in IT services and consulting. The company's journey from a small [...] 1981: Infosys is founded in Pune, India.  \n   \n 1983: Headquarters relocated to Bengaluru.  \n   \n 1993: Infosys goes public in India.  \n   \n 1999: Becomes the first Indian company to be listed on NASDAQ.  \n   \n 2002: Launches Progeon, its BPO subsidiary (later renamed Infosys BPM).  \n   \n 2004: Establishes Infosys Consulting Inc. in the USA.  \n   \n 2010: British Prime Minister David Cameron visits Infosys headquarters.  \n   \n 2011: Company renamed to Infosys Limited. [...] ## Frequently asked questions\n\nWho are the 7 founders of Infosys?\n\nInfosys was founded in 1981 by seven visionary engineers: N.R. Narayana Murthy, Nandan Nilekani, Kris Gopalakrishnan, S.D. Shibulal, K. Dinesh, N.S. Raghavan, and Ashok Arora. These individuals laid the foundation of one of India's most successful IT companies with a shared investment of US$250 and a strong vision for global excellence in software services.\n\nWhat is the future outlook for Infosys?","score":0.93309647},{"title":"Instagram","url":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DX1ju4fgPTj","content":"In 1981, Narayana Murthy, along with six other engineers, founded Infosys in a small flat in Pune with a modest ₹10,000 borrowed from Murthy’s wife, Sudha Murthy. Back then, India’s IT sector was in its infancy, and the global market wasn’t aware of the capabilities of Indian tech professionals. [...] In 1993, Infosys made its historic debut on the NASDAQ, becoming the first Indian company to be listed there. The stock market success brought not only credibility but also access to global resources, which fueled the company’s rapid growth. Today, Infosys is a $100 billion IT services giant with a presence in over 50 countries, employing over 250,000 professionals.","score":0.91288006},{"title":"Infosys Revenue, Marketcap, Net Worth, Competitors 2026","url":"https://www.companieshistory.com/infosys","content":"Bengaluru, India\n\nInfosys Ltd. stands as India’s second-largest IT services company and a global leader in consulting, technology, and outsourcing. Seven engineers founded the company in Pune in 1981 with just $250 in capital. The company relocated to Bangalore in 1983 and has since grown into a multinational corporation serving clients across financial services, manufacturing, retail, and communications sectors. [...] N. R. Narayana Murthy and six engineers founded Infosys on July 2, 1981, in Pune, India. The seven co-founders started with just $250 in initial capital.\n\n### What services does Infosys provide?\n\nInfosys provides IT consulting, digital transformation, application development, cloud services, data analytics, AI solutions, and business process outsourcing to global clients.\n\n### How many employees work at Infosys? [...] The company operates 94 sales and marketing offices and 139 development centers worldwide. North America generates approximately 61% of Infosys revenue, followed by Europe at 25%. Infosys became the first Indian company listed on NASDAQ in 1999 and achieved a $100 billion market capitalization milestone in August 2021.\n\n## Infosys History\n\n1981\n\nN. R. Narayana Murthy and six engineers founded Infosys Consultants Private Limited in Pune with an initial capital of $250.\n\n1983","score":0.88420963},{"title":"Company History & Defining Milestones | About Us","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/history.html","content":"### 1981\n\n Infosys is established by N. R. Narayana Murthy and six engineers in Pune, India, with an initial capital of US$250\n Signs up its first client, Data Basics Corporation, in New York\n\n## Request for services\n\nFind out more about how we can help your organization navigate its next. Let us know your areas of interest so that we can serve you better.\n\nLoading [...] Established in 1981, Infosys is a NYSE listed global consulting and IT services company with more than 328K employees. From a capital of US$250, we have grown to become a US$ 20.3 billion (LTM Q1 FY27 revenues) company with a market capitalization of US$ 43 billion. [...] 1981\n\n### 2026\n\n Infosys ranked in the Top 3 IT services brands in the world for the fifth year in a row by Brand Finance; Fastest CAGR in brand value, in IT services industry, over 6 years, in its Global 500 2026 report.\n Infosys has won multiple awards from FinanceAsia, including Best CFO, Best Investor Relations and Best Large Cap Company.\n Recognized as one of the World’s Most Ethical Companies in 2026 for sixth consecutive year by Ethisphere\n\n### 2025","score":0.8443195},{"title":"Infosys - N.R. Narayana Murthy: Founder | Management Profiles","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/narayana-murthy.html","content":"# N.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nFounder\n\nN.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nMr. Murthy founded Infosys in 1981. Infosys is, today, a highly innovative software services global\ncompany listed on NYSE in the US and on the Bombay Stock Exchange in Mumbai. [...] published in March 2015. He is the first Indian winner of Ernst and Young’s World Entrepreneur\nof the Year award. [...] In 2014, Mr. Murthy was ranked 13th among CNBC’s 25 global business leaders and listed among the\n‘12 greatest entrepreneurs of our time’, by Fortune in 2012. He has received\nLegion d’honneur from France, CBE from Britain, and Padma Vibhushan from India. The\nEconomist ranked him among the 10 most-admired global business leaders in 2005. Mr. Murthy\nis ranked among the top 10 Financial Times’ list of “Business pioneers in technology”,","score":0.80735475}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:05:34.882Z","session":"5a4c4c23-4a75-4f1b-bd54-29047608f8bf","event":"tool.end","callId":"edf7f483-fd22-4bc5-8c82-aa5e4f10107c","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":3337,"result":[{"title":"Zerodha's FY24 revenue tops $1bn - Times of India","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/zerodhas-fy24-revenue-tops-1bn/articleshow/116416977.cms","content":"BENGALURU: Online brokerage platform Zerodha has seen its revenue surpass $1 billion in FY24. The company's topline increased by 37% to Rs 9,372 crore from Rs 6,833 crore, according to data sourced from business intelligence platform Tofler. The net profit saw a rise of 89%, reaching Rs 5,496 crore in the same period. The company reduced employee costs by 24% to Rs 474 crore from Rs 623 crore. [...] Top stocks today\n\nUS stock market today\n\nTesla robotaxi\n\nGold Price Prediction\n\nTrump gold card\n\nGold Rate Today\n\nStock market today\n\nThis story is from December 18, 2024\n\n# Zerodha's FY24 revenue tops $1bn\n\nTNN / Updated: Dec 18, 2024, 07:25 IST\n\nShare\n\nAA\n\nText Size\n\n Small\n Medium\n Large [...] Trending Topics","score":0.9492242},{"title":"Zerodha crosses $1B in revenue in FY24; profit up 89%","url":"https://www.facebook.com/yourstorycom/posts/-zerodha-crosses-1b-in-revenue-in-fy24-profit-up-89zerodha-hits-a-milestone-cros/1008078288020812","content":"In FY24, revenue rose 37% to ₹9,372 crore, with net profit reaching ₹5,496 crore. Read more: https://yourstory.com/2024/12/zerodha- crosses-1b","score":0.94796705},{"title":"Zerodha Capital clocks Rs 12.5 Cr profit in FY25","url":"https://entrackr.com/fintrackr/zerodha-capital-clocks-rs-125-cr-profit-in-fy25-9320024","content":"Founded in 2021, Zerodha Capital aims to deepen its credit play within the securities ecosystem. However, its future performance remains tethered to market sentiment and regulatory shifts, especially as retail F&O activity—the group’s mainstay—faces tightening norms.\n\nZerodha Capital’s parent company, Zerodha Broking Limited, has reported a net profit of Rs 5,496 crore in FY24, with a return on net worth of 56% during the same period.\n\nDisclaimer: [...] ## Zerodha Capital, the lending arm of stockbroker Zerodha, posted a net profit of Rs 12.5 crore in the previous fiscal year ending March 2025 from Rs 7.2 crore in FY24.\n\nauthor-image/entrackr/media/member_avatars/2024/10/21/2024-10-21t083822584z-kunal-circle-png-768x768.png )\n\n Follow Us\n\nzerodha capital/entrackr/media/media_files/2025/05/30/ggRIKfXDKowCG24cy7S1.jpg) [...] Zerodha Capital, the lending arm of stockbroker Zerodha, posted a net profit of Rs 12.5 crore in the previous fiscal year ending March 2025 from Rs 7.2 crore in FY24. \n\nAccording to an ET report, the firm doubled its income to Rs 36 crore in FY25 from Rs 17 crore in FY24.\n\nAs per ICRA, this rise in profit was driven by a 3.2X jump in its loan book, which grew to Rs 381 crore in the first nine months of the last fiscal year or 9M FY25.","score":0.9407083},{"title":"Zerodha Revenue Flat in FY26, Rs 4300 Crore Net Profit","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/moneycontrol_zerodha-revenue-and-profit-remain-flat-in-activity-7498393899355242496-jvRu","content":"#Business | Zerodha revenue and profit remain flat in FY 26; reports net profit of Rs 4,300 crore - Zerodha's FY26 revenue and profit were","score":0.44825777},{"title":"Zerodha’s brokerage fees slumped 40% in June quarter: Nithin Kamath | The Arc","url":"https://www.thearcweb.com/article/zerodha-fy25-brokerage-fees-nithin-kamath-groww-qillXxBUJdcznfFz","content":"© 2024 The Arc Web\n\nTerms of Use [...] Our coverage is driven by accurate company facts and data — unbiased and objective.\n\nExplore Companies\n\ninsider-view-illustration\n\n##### Crisp and short\n\nWe value your time. Our reporting and analysis focus on what’s important.\n\nRead Bulletin\n\n[](\n\nArcweb logo\n\n#### Mapping the arc of high-growth companies\n\n##### Explore\n\nBulletinIn-depthComp