e [h]\")\n\nGeneral\n\n* [What links here](/wiki/Special:WhatLinksHere/Salil_Parekh \"List of \n[…]\nall English Wikipedia pages containing links to this page [j]\")\n* [Related changes](/wiki/Special:RecentChangesLinked/Salil_Parekh \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n* [Upload file](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:File_Upload_Wizard \"Upload files [u]\")\n* [Permanent link](/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&oldid=1372553589 \"Permanent link to this revision of this page\")\n* [Page information](/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&action=info \"More information about this page\")\n* [Cite this page](/w/index.php?title=Special:CiteThisPage&page=Salil_Parekh&id=1372553589&wpFormIdentifier=titleform \"Information on how to cite this page\")\n* [Get shortened URL](/w/index.php?title=Special:UrlShortener&url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FSalil_Parekh)\n* [Switch to legacy parser](/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&useparsoid=0)\n\nPrint/export\n\n* [Download as PDF](/w/index.php?title=Special:DownloadAsPdf&page=Salil_Parekh&action=show-download-screen \"Download this page as a PDF file\")\n* [Printable version](/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&printable=yes \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n\nIn other projects\n\n* [Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Salil_Parekh)\n* [Wikidata item](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Special:EntityPage/Q47087171 \"Structured data on this page hosted by Wikidata [g]\")\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian businessman, current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n| --- |\n[…]\n\n| Born | (1964-06-05) 5 June 1964 (age 62) |\n| Education | [IIT Bombay](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IIT_Bombay \"IIT Bombay\") ([BTech](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BTech \"BTech\")) [Cornell University](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornell_University \"Cornell University\") ([MS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M.S. \"M.S.\")) |\n| Occupations | CEO & MD of [Infosys](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infosys \"Infosys\") |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh |\n\n**Salil Parekh** (born 5 June 1964) is the current [chief executive officer](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_executive_officer \"Chief executive officer\") and managing director of [Infosys](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infosys \"Infosys\"). Parekh took over from interim CEO [U. B. Pravin Rao](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U._B._Pravin_Rao \"U. B. Pravin Rao\") on 2 January 2018 for a five year term.[[1]](#cite_note-indiatimes2jan-1) The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027[[2]](#cite_note-2).\n\nParekh is a member of [The Business Council](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Business_Council \"The Business Council\").[[3]](#cite_note-3)\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Early life and education\")]\n\nSalil Parekh is born into a [Gujarati](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gujarati_people \"Gujarati people\") family.[[4]](#cite_note-4) He is a graduate from the [Indian Institute of Technology, Bomba\n[…]\ny](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Institute_of_Technology_Bombay \"Indian Institute of Technology Bombay\") (IIT Bombay) in Aeronautical Engineering. Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from [Cornell University](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornell_University \"Cornell University\").[[1]](#cite_note-indiatimes2jan-1)\n\nParekh was member of the group management board at [Capgemini](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capgemini \"Capgemini\"), where he had worked since 2000, after [Ernst & Young](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernst_&_Young \"Ernst & Young\")'s consultancy division, where he had been working before, was merged into the company.[[5]](#cite_note-5)[[6]](#cite_note-6)\n\nParekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015.[[7]](#cite_note-7) He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others.[[8]](#cite_note-fortune-8)[[1]](#cite_note-indiatimes2jan-1) He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.[[9]](#cite_note-9)\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&action=edit&section=2 \"Edit section: Whistleblower allegations\")]\n\nIn 2019, a board member of Infosys received two anonymous whistleblower complaints of unethical practices at Infosys that also accused Salil Parekh.[[\n[…]\n10]](#cite_note-10)[[11]](#cite_note-11) Audit Committee of the Board of Directors conducted independent investigation into the allegations contained in the anonymous whistleblower complaints and determined that the allegations are substantially without merit. The Audit Committee conducted a thorough investigation with the assistance of independent legal counsel Shardul Amarchand Mangaldas & Co. and PricewaterhouseCoopers Private Ltd.[[12]](#cite_note-12)\n\n## References\n\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&action=edit&section=3 \"Edit section: References\")]\n\n1. [1](#cite_ref-indiatimes2jan_1-0) [2](#cite_ref-indiatimes2jan_1-1) [3](#cite_ref-indiatimes2jan_1-2) [\"Infosys gets a new boss in Salil Parekh today but can he keep Narayana Murthy happy?\"](https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/ites/infosys-gets-a-new-boss-in-salil-parekh-but-can-he-keep-narayana-murthy-happy/articleshow/62333962.cms). *economictimes.indiatimes.com*. 2 January 2018. Retrieved 2 January 2018.\n2. [↑](#cite_ref-2) Ishwarbharath B, Sai; Suresh, Haripriya (23 July 2026). [\"Infosys names insider Ashiss Kumar Dash next CEO, trims growth forecast\"](https://www.reuters.com/world/india/indias-infosys-misses-quarterly-revenue-view-names-ceo-designate-2026-07-23/). *[Reuters](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuters \"Reuters\")*. Retrieved 25 July 2026.`{{cite news}}`: CS1 maint: url-status ([link](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:CS1_maint:_url-status \"Category:CS1 maint: url-status\"))\n3. [↑](#cite_ref-\n[…]\n3) Admin. [\"Member List\"](https://businesscouncil.com/member-list/). *The Business Council*. Retrieved 11 July 2025.\n4. [↑](#cite_ref-4) [\"A Gujarati appointed as CEO and MD of Infosys\"](https://deshgujarat.com/2017/12/03/a-gujarati-appointed-as-ceo-and-md-of-infosys/). *DeshGujarat*. 2 December 2017. Retrieved 14 July 2025.\n5. [↑](#cite_ref-5) D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). [\"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\"](https://www.livemint.com/Companies/vOG72f5bDhhRRLgNuCmMYL/Capgemini-names-Salil-Parekh-deputy-CEO.html). *mint*. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n6. [↑](#cite_ref-6) Shivapriya, N. [\"Salil Parekh: The man who played a pivotal role in building Capgemini's India operations\"](https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/ites/salil-parekh-the-man-who-played-a-pivotal-role-in-building-capgeminis-india-operations/articleshow/47182483.cms). *The Economic Times*. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n7. [↑](#cite_ref-7) D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). [\"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\"](http://www.livemint.com/Companies/vOG72f5bDhhRRLgNuCmMYL/Capgemini-names-Salil-Parekh-deputy-CEO.html). *[LiveMint](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LiveMint \"LiveMint\")*. Retrieved 3 January 2018.\n8. [↑](#cite_ref-fortune_8-0) [\"Infosys Turns to Capgemini's Parekh to Juggle Problems with Founders and U.S. Immigration Reform\"](http://fortune.com/2017/12/04/infosys-ceo-parekh-immigration-founders/). *[Fortune](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortune_(magazine) \"Fortune (magazine)\")*. [Time Inc.](https://en\n[…]\n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Inc. \"Time Inc.\") [Reuters](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuters \"Reuters\"). 4 December 2017. Retrieved 3 January 2018.\n9. [↑](#cite_ref-9) Parekh, Salil (January 2018). [\"About Us Management profiles Salil Parekh Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director\"](https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html).\n10. [↑](#cite_ref-10) Bahree, Megha. [\"Indian Tech Giant Infosys Shaken By Whistleblower Complaints\"](https://www.forbes.com/sites/meghabahree/2019/10/25/indian-tech-giant-infosys-shaken-by--whistleblower-complaints/). *Forbes*. Retrieved 11 July 2025.\n11. [↑](#cite_ref-11) Iyengar, Rishi (22 October 2019). [\"Indian tech group Infosys rocked by whistleblower claims against CEO Salil Parekh | CNN Business\"](https://www.cnn.com/2019/10/22/tech/infosys-india-investigation-salil-parekh). *CNN*. Retrieved 11 July 2025.\n12. [↑](#cite_ref-12) [\"Infosys' audit committee finds no wrongdoing, SEC investigation continues\"](https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/ites/infosys-internal-audit-finds-no-merit-in-whistleblower-allegations-of-wrongdoing/articleshow/73188208.cms). *The Economic Times*. Retrieved 23 October 2020.\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| [India](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India \"India\") | This Indian business-related biographical article is a [stub](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Stub \"Wikipedia:Stub\"). You can help Wikipedia by [adding missing information](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Salil_Parekh&a\n\"\"\"",{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"verdict":{"type":"string","format":"enum","enum":["supported","unsupported","contradicted"]},"evidenceQuote":{"type":"string"},"reasoning":{"type":"string"}},"required":["verdict","evidenceQuote","reasoning"]}}]}
