4263905},{"title":"Quick Commerce India: Funding Hits $40.4M in 2025 After $1.4B Record in 2024","url":"https://www.deccanherald.com/business/with-87-companies-in-indias-quick-commerce-segment-raises-404-million-in-2025-3684626","content":"Features\n\nHealth\n\nEducation\n\nTechnology\n\nDH Brandspot\n\nSubscribe\n\nMenu\n\nGo Ad Lite\n\nAdvertisement.\n\nStory continues below. Go Ad Lite\n\nHomebusiness\n\n# With 87 companies in India's quick commerce, segment raises $40.4 million in 2025\n\nAccording to market intelligence firm Tracxn, there are 87 companies in the quick commerce space in India and in 2025 alone.\n\nUma Kannan\n\nLast Updated : 17 August 2025, 11:32IST\n\nStory continues below. Go Ad Lite\n\nJoin Us\n\nPrefer\n\nComments\n\nAdvertisement. Go Ad Lite [...] Published 17 August 2025, 11:32IST\n\nBusiness NewsSwiggyBlinkitOnline shopping\n\n## Follow us on :\n\n## Follow Us","score":0.89121616},{"title":"Quick Commerce - 2026 Market & Investments Trends - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/trending-business-models/startups-in-quick-commerce/__8Em61CsQQeo5EmPsP-wGXgDzh5yotwlRuXpxOVdqw6Y","content":"| Year | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| 2026 | $507M |\n| 2025 | $2.06B |\n| 2024 | $2B |\n| 2023 | $1.08B |\n| 2022 | $3.28B |\n| 2021 | $11.9B |\n| 2020 | $3.64B |\n| 2019 | $3.84B |\n| 2018 | $4.79B |\n| 2017 | $1.79B |\n\n### Total funding across countries in Quick Commerce\n\nIn the last 10 years, Quick Commerce startups in United States have recieved the highest funding among all countries - $10B. India follows with $8.9B and Germany with $2.8B. [...] | Country | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| United States | $10B |\n| India | $8.9B |\n| Germany | $2.8B |\n| United Kingdom | $1.76B |\n| Saudi Arabia | $286M |\n| Indonesia | $148M |\n| Australia | $23M |\n| Philippines | $21.1M |\n| Canada | $9.1M |\n| Italy | $3M |\n\n### Total funding amount raised by stage in Quick Commerce\n\nOver the last 10 years, Quick Commerce have seen $242M into Seed Stage funding rounds, $4.24B into Early Stage funding rounds and $26.2B go into Late Stage funding rounds. [...] | Company Stage | No. of companies |\n --- |\n| Founded | 256 |\n| Funded | 105 |\n| Series A+ | 55 |\n| Series B+ | 41 |\n| Series C+ | 35 |\n\n## Funding Trends in Quick Commerce\n\n### Total funding year-on-year in Quick Commerce\n\nQuick Commerce saw a total funding of more than $34.9B in the last 10 years. The most amount of funding was in 2021 at more than $11.9B. There has been a total funding of $507M in 2026 till date.","score":0.86413884},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/27/indias-zepto-files-for-ipo-as-quick-commerce-race-heats-up.html","content":"Walmart-owned Flipkart also launched its quick commerce service in 2024. Indian food delivery companies, Swiggy and Eternal, which owns Zomato and Blinkit, were among the first movers in this space.\n\nOver the last three to five years, several companies have entered the quick commerce market in India and are \" indulging in a price war\" as firms chase a large total addressable market, Taurani said. [...] Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details. [...] Quick commerce, which promises deliveries in as little as 10 minutes, has become one of India's most competitive consumer internet sectors.\n\nWhile e-commerce giant Amazon has long offered same-day delivery services in India through \"Amazon Fresh\", the launch of its 15-minute \"Amazon Now\" service in June marked an aggressive shift into a crowded space.\n\nThe Jeff Bezos-owned U.S. company has started its quick commerce operations across Indian's three major cities—Mumbai, Delhi and Bengaluru.","score":0.86080295},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/27/indias-zepto-files-for-ipo-as-quick-commerce-race-heats-up.html?msockid=0c2f936e68336de43ee685be69e56c05","content":"Walmart-owned Flipkart also launched its quick commerce service in 2024. Indian food delivery companies, Swiggy and Eternal, which owns Zomato and Blinkit, were among the first movers in this space.\n\nOver the last three to five years, several companies have entered the quick commerce market in India and are \" indulging in a price war\" as firms chase a large total addressable market, Taurani said. [...] Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details. [...] Quick commerce, which promises deliveries in as little as 10 minutes, has become one of India's most competitive consumer internet sectors.\n\nWhile e-commerce giant Amazon has long offered same-day delivery services in India through \"Amazon Fresh\", the launch of its 15-minute \"Amazon Now\" service in June marked an aggressive shift into a crowded space.\n\nThe Jeff Bezos-owned U.S. company has started its quick commerce operations across Indian's three major cities—Mumbai, Delhi and Bengaluru.","score":0.86080295}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:35:05.654Z","session":"c47cae16-279d-41a2-b401-3efa2780e299","event":"tool.end","callId":"40dc0372-1da8-4388-b5af-d93c87237d18","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2687,"result":[{"title":"The second wave of quick commerce is here | Anuj Suvarna","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/anuj-suvarna_the-second-wave-of-quick-commerce-is-here-activity-7369230316722405378-J7cd","content":"The second wave of quick commerce is here FirstClub has raised $23 million in Series A funding at a valuation of about $120 million, less than three months after launch. The round was led by Accel and RTP Global, with participation from Blume Founders Fund, 2am VC, Paramark Ventures, and Aditya Birla Ventures. Founded by Ayyappan R (ex-Flipkart, Myntra, and former CEO of Cleartrip), FirstClub calls itself India’s first “quality-first” quick commerce platform — a sharp contrast to Blinkit, [...] Partners. Fashion: Slikk, Knot, and Zulu Club raised capital to deliver clothing and accessories within an hour. Food: WAAYU ($2M) is building a zero-commission delivery platform; Zing is betting on ultra-fast fresh meals. Healthcare: Farmako raised funds to deliver medicines in under 30 minutes. Infrastructure: Kuik is building shared dark stores for brands, with a $3–4M round in the works. The message is clear: Quick commerce in India is evolving from “anything in 10 minutes” to vertical-led [...] less than three months since its inception.AccelandRTP Globalled the round, with participation from Blume Founders Fund, 2am VC,Paramark Ventures, andAditya Birla Ventures. Read More: \n\nImage 11: FirstClub Raises $23 Million To Fuel Quality-Led Quick Commerce Expansion FirstClub Raises $23 Million To Fuel Quality-Led Quick Commerce Expansion startup.siliconindia.com\n\nImage 12Image 13 291 Comment\n\nLikeComment\n\n Share \n       Copy\n       LinkedIn\n       Facebook\n       X","score":0.8627572},{"title":"Quick Commerce - 2026 Market & Investments Trends - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/trending-business-models/startups-in-quick-commerce/__8Em61CsQQeo5EmPsP-wGXgDzh5yotwlRuXpxOVdqw6Y","content":"| Country | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| United States | $10B |\n| India | $8.9B |\n| Germany | $2.8B |\n| United Kingdom | $1.76B |\n| Saudi Arabia | $286M |\n| Indonesia | $148M |\n| Australia | $23M |\n| Philippines | $21.1M |\n| Canada | $9.1M |\n| Italy | $3M |\n\n### Total funding amount raised by stage in Quick Commerce\n\nOver the last 10 years, Quick Commerce have seen $242M into Seed Stage funding rounds, $4.24B into Early Stage funding rounds and $26.2B go into Late Stage funding rounds. [...] | Company Stage | No. of companies |\n --- |\n| Founded | 256 |\n| Funded | 105 |\n| Series A+ | 55 |\n| Series B+ | 41 |\n| Series C+ | 35 |\n\n## Funding Trends in Quick Commerce\n\n### Total funding year-on-year in Quick Commerce\n\nQuick Commerce saw a total funding of more than $34.9B in the last 10 years. The most amount of funding was in 2021 at more than $11.9B. There has been a total funding of $507M in 2026 till date. [...] | Year | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| 2026 | $507M |\n| 2025 | $2.06B |\n| 2024 | $2B |\n| 2023 | $1.08B |\n| 2022 | $3.28B |\n| 2021 | $11.9B |\n| 2020 | $3.64B |\n| 2019 | $3.84B |\n| 2018 | $4.79B |\n| 2017 | $1.79B |\n\n### Total funding across countries in Quick Commerce\n\nIn the last 10 years, Quick Commerce startups in United States have recieved the highest funding among all countries - $10B. India follows with $8.9B and Germany with $2.8B.","score":0.8506799},{"title":"Quick-commerce FirstClub doubles valuation to $255M in 9 months | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/03/firstclub-doubles-valuation-to-255m-in-nine-months-on-quality-first-grocery-bet","content":"The Bengaluru-based startup has raised $55 million in a Series B round co-led by Peak XV Partners and Sofina, valuing the company at $255 million after the investment. That’s up from $120 million when it last raised capital in September 2025. Existing investors Accel, RTP Global, and Paramark Ventures also participated. The latest financing brings FirstClub’s total funding to $86 million. [...] In a quick-commerce market obsessed with speed, Indian startup FirstClub has convinced investors that quality may be a fresh opportunity, helping to double its valuation just nine months after its last funding round. [...] As grocery shopping increasingly moves online, India’s quick-commerce market has expanded rapidly, growing from about $6.2 billion in FY25 to an estimated $11 billion to $12 billion in FY26, according to a recent ICICI Securities report. Leading players have popularized online grocery shopping through ever-faster deliveries. However, FirstClub is wagering that a growing segment of consumers will prioritize quality and product curation over receiving orders as quickly as possible.","score":0.7797419},{"title":"Quick Commerce CAN'T SURVIVE Like This - Indian Startups News 291","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vC0p8AHIvKQ","content":"In our Quick Updates, we cover:\nUnacademy admitting an 85% valuation drop and exploring M&A,\nVirat Kohli selling One8 to Agilitas Sports while joining as co-founder,\nUber launching Uber Direct with ONDC to enter B2B logistics,\nand strong IPO debuts from Meesho and Aequs.\n\nFinally, in our Weekly Funding News, we break down the $86 million raised this week — including rounds for Fibe, Smart Joules, Elecbits, Dr. Paws, and NeoSapien. [...] [9:34] brain for you. This device basically listens to you the entire day and that helps you recall, organize, and make better decisions. And they have raised\n[9:42] $2 million in their seed round. All right, that's all the startup news I have for you this week. Thank you so much for watching and I'll see you in the next [...] Then, we look at a major development in India’s innovation ecosystem: IIT Bombay launching a ₹250 crore venture fund dedicated entirely to deep-tech. From semiconductors and robotics to biotech, AI, and new materials, this fund could become a crucial link between research and commercialization—taking India one step closer to building globally competitive deep-tech companies.","score":0.7413937},{"title":"Amazon pilots quick-commerce service in India","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/amazon-pilots-quick-commerce-india-091232017.html","content":"Title: Amazon pilots quick-commerce service in India\n2. Best 0% APR cards. 3. Best balance transfer cards. 2. Best high-yield savings accounts. 3. Best money market accounts. # Amazon pilots quick-commerce service in India. Amazon pilots quick-commerce service in India · TechCrunch. Amazon on Tuesday said it is piloting a quick commerce service in India that will see the U.S. tech giant delivering grocery and other items in 15 minutes or less. The firm is the sixth major entrant in India's quick-commerce market, which is currently clocking more than $6 billion in annual sales. Amazon said it is initially piloting the service in Bengaluru. \"Our strategy has always focused on 'Selection, Value and Convenience' and our vision is to build a large profitable business in India,\" said Samir Kumar, the new country manager of Amazon India, in a statement. \"So, while we focus on implementing our strategy to offer the largest selection at fastest speeds and greatest value to customers in every single pin-code across the country, we are excited to start a pilot to give our customers a choice to get their everyday essentials in 15 min or less.\". The quick-commerce model — delivering items to customers within 10 to 15 minutes — hasn't worked in most parts of the world, but it's increasingly finding success in India, where a range of retailers and internet firms, from food delivery giant Swiggy to online cosmetics platform Nykaa, are gearing up their supply chain ecosystems to accommodate for faster deliveries. Myntra, the top fashion e-commerce retailer in India, launched its own pilot of its quick commerce offering in Bengaluru last week. And Flipkart, Amazon's biggest rival in India, launched its own quick-commerce service in August. India is the only market where Amazon is testing the quick-commerce offering. Amazon entered the Indian market a decade ago, investing more than $7.5 billion to build and scale its e-commerce offering. Quick commerce in India is expected to show exponential growth, with projections from investment firm CLSA indicating a sixfold increase between FY24 and FY27, reaching a total addressable market of $27 billion. Currently representing 3% of the grocery and 1% of the retail market, this segment is expected to expand to 5% and 2%, respectively, within a decade, CLSA said in a report on Tuesday.","score":0.6522641}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:35:05.770Z","session":"c47cae16-279d-41a2-b401-3efa2780e299","event":"tool.end","callId":"63909c81-3916-47dc-9476-a647fdb55333","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2798,"result":[{"title":"Blinkit - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blinkit","content":"Blinkit is an Indian quick-commerce company owned by Eternal Limited. It was founded in December 2013 and is based in Gurgaon.\n\nCustomers of the company use a mobile app to order groceries and essentials online, which are sourced from the company's dark stores and delivered in 10 minutes. Blinkit operates in 153 cities in India, as of March 2025.\n\nIn 2022, Zomato Limited (now Eternal) acquired Blinkit for US$568 million in an all-stock deal.\n\n## History\n\n[edit] [...] Blinkit\n\n| Formerly | Grofers (2013–2021) |\n| Type | Subsidiary |\n| Industry | Q-commerce |\n| Founded | December 2013; 12 years ago (2013-12) |\n| Founders | Albinder Dhindsa Saurabh Kumar |\n| Headquarters | Gurgaon, Haryana, India |\n| Area served | India |\n| Key people | Albinder Dhindsa (CEO) |\n| Products | Bistro |\n| Services | Online grocer |\n| Revenue | Increase ₹5,206 crore (US$540 million) (FY25) |\n| Parent | Eternal Limited |\n| Website | blinkit.com | [...] In June 2022, a Bengaluru-based web development company called Blinkhit filed a trademark infringement lawsuit against Blinkit.\n\nIn April 2023, hundreds of Blinkit delivery partners in Delhi NCR, where about half of the company's dark stores were located, went on strike after a revision in payout structure resulted in lower earnings for them. This led to a temporary closure of many dark stores.","score":0.92125154},{"title":"Blinkit Foods Limited - 2026 Company Profile - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/legal-entities/india/blinkit-foods-limited/__djKNSolKqqiifOhCQSY8wrP4ba7ttguUwe7MUea3s2U","content":"Blinkit Foods Limited is a Public Limited Company and was incorporated on Aug 18, 2025 in India. It is registered at Registrar of Companies, ROC Delhi I. Its registered address is T-19, Basement, Green Park Main, Green Park, South West Delhi, New Delhi, Delhi, India, 110016.  Its corporate identification number is (CIN) U47222DL2025PLC453320 and its current status is Active. Its industry classification as per MCA is retail sale of non-alcoholic beverages including icecream not for consumption [...] | Name | Short Description | Founded Year | Location | Current Stage |\n ---  --- \n| Logo for Blinkit Blinkit | Online retailer of groceries, personal care, and household essential products | 2013 | India | Acquired |\n\nLogo for Blinkit\n\n## Documents of Blinkit Foods Limited15 mins\n\n### Latest Financials, Share Allotment and Annual Report\n\nThe latest filed financial documents, annual reports, and share allotment filings are shown below:\n\n### Recent Filings [...] Blinkit Foods Limited's authorised share capital is ₹1Cr and its paid up capital is ₹27.5L. The current board of directors of Blinkit Foods Limited comprises Deepak Ahluwalia, Ali Kausar Siddiqui and 1 more.\n\n## Contact Details for Blinkit Foods Limited\n\n## Brands associated with Blinkit Foods Limited","score":0.87139857},{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://www.zoominfo.com/c/blinkit/359515698","content":"# Blinkit\n\nBlink Commerce Private Limited, d/b/a Blinkit and formerly Grofers, is an Indian instant delivery service. Customers of the company use a mobile application to order groceries and essentials online. Blinkit's employees then secure the items from their warehouse and deliver the items to the consumer within 10 minutes. In 2022, Zomato acquired Blinki... \n\n## Leadership [...] ## Leadership\n\n- Khevender Daga — Quick Commerce Finance Controller (Blinkit & ...\n- Sanchit Bhasin — City Chief Executive Officer - Gujarat\n- Simran Shrivastav — Co-Chief Executive Officer\n\n## Company Details\n\n- Website: \n- Revenue: $94.2 Million\n- Employees: 1K - 5K\n- Industries: Freight & Logistics Services; Retail; Transportation; Grocery Retail\n- Headquarters: Golf Course Road Vipul Tech Sector-43 Sq Fl 4, Gurgaon, Haryana, 122001, India\n\n## Social Media\n\n- \n- \n- \n\n## Tech Stack [...] - blinkit cfo vipin kapooria has exited the quick commerce startup after more than a year moneycontrol reported kapooria could likely rejoin flipkart where he had worked for around seven years in two separate stints he was blinkits first fulltime designated cfo since amit sachdeva who worked at the startup as cfo between 2019 and 2022 left the firm\n- Blinkit-AI, an advanced artificial intelligence-driven platform, has raised $1.2 million in its seed funding round from Foliflex Cables (India).","score":0.84707206},{"title":"Blinkit - India's Last Minute App ✨ Sell your products on Blinkit via seller.blinkit.com","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/letsblinkit","content":"## Overview\nBlinkit (An Eternal Company) is a grocery and e-commerce platform. We pioneered the doorstep delivery model in India with over 10 million Indians shopping on Blinkit, for everything from grocery staples and vegetables to emergency supplies and electronics, and much more. If our mission interests you, send your CV to future@blinkit.com\n\n### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\nN/A\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nTechnology, Information and Internet [...] ### Company Size\n1,001-5,000 employees  \n29232 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed Blinkit as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\n2013\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: N/A\nLast Round Type: N/A\nTotal Rounds: N/A\nLast Round Raised: N/A\n\n### Investors\nN/A\n\n### Specialties\nN/A\n\n## Locations\nPioneer Square, Sector 62, Golf Course Extension, Blinkit Headquarters, Gurgaon, Haryana 122001, IN\n\n### Get Directions\nDirections [...] ## Similar Companies","score":0.8194462},{"title":"Blinkit | Eternal","url":"https://eternal.com/our-businesses/blinkit","content":"Eternal\n\nInstant commerce indistinguishable from magic\n\nLaunched with the ambition of making everyday essentials available at your doorstep, Blinkit has revolutionized how India shops.  \n  \nIt has now evolved into a full-fledged quick commerce company, delivering thousands of products including grocery and daily essentials, electronics, beauty & personal care items, stationery, and emergency supplies.\n\n# Leading the quick commerce evolution [...] Blinkit is powered by a dynamic network of customers, store partners, and delivery partners working together seamlessly.\n\n31 million+ customers use our app monthly\n\n2,400+ stores across 300+ cities\n\n500,000+ delivery partners delivering at your doorstep\n\n# Beyond essentials\n\nBlinkit is constantly innovating to serve the evolving customer needs, the latest being in:\n\nBeauty & personal care\n\nBeauty & personal care [...] Sports\n\nSports\n\nFor training, playing, or just starting out, you can get the right gear delivered to your doorstep.\n\nToys\n\nToys\n\nBrain-boosting games, cuddly companions, and everything in between — toys to match every age and every mood.\n\n# Download the app now\n\nEverything you need, delivered to your doorstep on the Blinkit app.\n\nApp Download LogoApp Download Logo\n\nScan the QR code to download the app\n\ndownload app\n\n# Our other businesses\n\nBringing the world closer, one meal at a time","score":0.78493005}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:35:05.839Z","session":"c47cae16-279d-41a2-b401-3efa2780e299","event":"tool.end","callId":"9545dee0-6590-4f40-b03d-d906fa19589e","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2870,"result":[{"title":"Indian quick commerce raises Rs 335.32 Crore in 2025, market value to reach Rs 29,300 crore | Debonkar Roy posted on the topic | LinkedIn","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/debonkar-roymarketing_debcreates-india-strategy-activity-7363066691586592769-L8yk","content":"unit economics by leading players. -Expansion beyond metro cities. - Diversification into new product categories. Despite the funding crunch globally, India's venture capital market rebounded in 2024, hitting Rs 1,15,000 crore in funding. Blinkit, Instamart, Zepto, bigbasket, and Dunzo Daily are the major companies operating in this market. With 50+ quick commerce startups, India leads globally, followed by the US with 15 startups, and the UK with 13. The presence of 87 companies in the funding [...] 87 Indian companies have raised Rs 335.32 Crore in 2025 so far for quick commerce! In 2024, quick commerce secured Rs 11,620 crore in funding. The sector is evolving beyond food and grocery delivery, expanding into electronics, household services, and ultra-fast fulfillment promises ranging from 10 minutes to 1 hour. Here are 5 facts about the Indian quick commerce market: 1. Current market value is expected to reach Rs 29,300 crore in 2025. 2. Projected growth for quick commerce space is >4.5% [...] space is >4.5% CAGR to reach Rs 36,500 crore by 2030. 3. It is projected to grow by 16.07% (2025-2029) resulting in a market volume of Rs 8,20,000 crore in 2029. 4. According to Redseer, industry experts predict a 40-45% GMV CAGR for the next 3 years. 5. According to Bain, India's quick commerce market will surge over 40% annually until 2030. The quick commerce sector witnessed a funding boom since 2024 due to: - Investor confidence in the ultra-fast delivery model. - Proven unit economics by","score":0.9202254},{"title":"Quick Commerce - 2026 Market & Investments Trends - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/trending-business-models/startups-in-quick-commerce/__8Em61CsQQeo5EmPsP-wGXgDzh5yotwlRuXpxOVdqw6Y","content":"| Year | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| 2026 | $507M |\n| 2025 | $2.06B |\n| 2024 | $2B |\n| 2023 | $1.08B |\n| 2022 | $3.28B |\n| 2021 | $11.9B |\n| 2020 | $3.64B |\n| 2019 | $3.84B |\n| 2018 | $4.79B |\n| 2017 | $1.79B |\n\n### Total funding across countries in Quick Commerce\n\nIn the last 10 years, Quick Commerce startups in United States have recieved the highest funding among all countries - $10B. India follows with $8.9B and Germany with $2.8B. [...] | Country | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| United States | $10B |\n| India | $8.9B |\n| Germany | $2.8B |\n| United Kingdom | $1.76B |\n| Saudi Arabia | $286M |\n| Indonesia | $148M |\n| Australia | $23M |\n| Philippines | $21.1M |\n| Canada | $9.1M |\n| Italy | $3M |\n\n### Total funding amount raised by stage in Quick Commerce\n\nOver the last 10 years, Quick Commerce have seen $242M into Seed Stage funding rounds, $4.24B into Early Stage funding rounds and $26.2B go into Late Stage funding rounds.","score":0.89121616},{"title":"Deccan Herald - According to #market intelligence firm...","url":"https://www.facebook.com/deccanherald/posts/according-to-market-intelligence-firm-tracxn-there-are-87-companies-in-the-quick/1241701744664887","content":"Quick Commerce India: Funding Hits $40.4M in 2025 After $1.4B Record in 2024","score":0.88564163},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/29/zepto-confidential-ipo-filing-india-quick-commerce-instamart-swiggy-blinkit-zomato-eternal-flipkart-amazon.html?msockid=204eacd0836e69a202fdba03820968af","content":"Walmart-owned Flipkart also launched its quick commerce service in 2024. Indian food delivery companies, Swiggy and Eternal, which owns Zomato and Blinkit, were among the first movers in this space.\n\nOver the last three to five years, several companies have entered the quick commerce market in India and are \" indulging in a price war\" as firms chase a large total addressable market, Taurani said. [...] Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details. [...] Quick commerce, which promises deliveries in as little as 10 minutes, has become one of India's most competitive consumer internet sectors.\n\nWhile e-commerce giant Amazon has long offered same-day delivery services in India through \"Amazon Fresh\", the launch of its 15-minute \"Amazon Now\" service in June marked an aggressive shift into a crowded space.\n\nThe Jeff Bezos-owned U.S. company has started its quick commerce operations across Indian's three major cities—Mumbai, Delhi and Bengaluru.","score":0.8729662},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/29/zepto-confidential-ipo-filing-india-quick-commerce-instamart-swiggy-blinkit-zomato-eternal-flipkart-amazon.html?msockid=0a78734812516d9520186599135b6c8a","content":"Walmart-owned Flipkart also launched its quick commerce service in 2024. Indian food delivery companies, Swiggy and Eternal, which owns Zomato and Blinkit, were among the first movers in this space.\n\nOver the last three to five years, several companies have entered the quick commerce market in India and are \" indulging in a price war\" as firms chase a large total addressable market, Taurani said. [...] Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details. [...] Quick commerce, which promises deliveries in as little as 10 minutes, has become one of India's most competitive consumer internet sectors.\n\nWhile e-commerce giant Amazon has long offered same-day delivery services in India through \"Amazon Fresh\", the launch of its 15-minute \"Amazon Now\" service in June marked an aggressive shift into a crowded space.\n\nThe Jeff Bezos-owned U.S. company has started its quick commerce operations across Indian's three major cities—Mumbai, Delhi and Bengaluru.","score":0.8729662}]}
