{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:35:12.903Z","session":"c47cae16-279d-41a2-b401-3efa2780e299","event":"tool.end","callId":"6066c42f-fb27-4f88-8773-6b931905f088","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2862,"result":[{"title":"FirstClub raises $23M, triples valuation to $120M | Entrepreneur Media India posted on the topic | LinkedIn","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/entrepreneur-media-india_eiupdates-firstclub-quickcommerce-activity-7369330938515771394-dTUX","content":"in its Series A funding, co-led by Accel and RTP Global, valuing the company at $120 million (INR 1,050 crore). Existing investors Blume, 2am VC, Paramark Ventures, and Aditya Birla Ventures also participated. FirstClub aims to use the funds for expansion, adding 35 dark stores in six months, and launching new fulfilment formats like cafés and subscriptions. Hiring will increase across various departments, and the startup plans to introduce new product categories, including kids’ food and pet [...] LinkedIn© 2026\n   About\n   Accessibility\n   User Agreement\n   Privacy Policy\n   Your California Privacy Choices\n   Cookie Policy\n   Copyright Policy\n   Brand Policy\n   Guest Controls\n   Community Guidelines\n   \n        العربية (Arabic) \n        বাংলা (Bangla) \n        Čeština (Czech) \n        Dansk (Danish) \n        Deutsch (German) \n        Ελληνικά (Greek) \n       English (English)\n        Español (Spanish) \n        فارسی (Persian) \n        Suomi (Finnish) \n        Français (French) [...] #EIUpdates Quick-commerce platform FirstClub has secured $23 million in a Series A funding round led by Accel and RTP Global. The investment triples the company's valuation to $120 million just months after its seed round. Founded in June 2025 by former Flipkart executive Ayyappan R, the Bengaluru-based startup is a new player in the competitive quick-commerce market. FirstClub plans to use the new capital to expand its operations from four to 35 dark stores within six months. The company","score":0.86632514},{"title":"FirstClub bucks India’s speed obsession, quickly triples valuation to $120M with premium approach","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/firstclub-bucks-india-speed-obsession-202108490.html","content":"At a post-money valuation of $120 million, the Bengaluru-based startup has raised $23 million in a Series A round (comprising more than 90% equity and the rest in debt) co-led by returning investors Accel and RTP Global. The round also saw participation from Blume Founders Fund, 2am VC, Paramark Ventures, and Aditya Birla Ventures. This new funding comes just eight months after FirstClub raised its $8 million seed round at a $40 million valuation in December. [...] The founder hit the ground running with experience under his belt. Before founding FirstClub in December, Ayyappan spent over a decade at Flipkart, India's largest homegrown e-commerce company, where he led teams at its subsidiaries Myntra (a fashion e-commerce site) and Cleartrip (a travel booking site). He was previously part of the team at Indian consumer goods giant ITC, focusing on strategies to expand grocery market and outlet coverage. Those experiences helped him quickly turn FirstClub [...] \"Based the last three months' data, it's quite clear that consumers are happy to wait if they are getting a very differentiated selection, a good quality of products, a differentiated service, and a very hand-holding sort of an experience,\" said Ayyappan R, founder and CEO of FirstClub, in an interview.","score":0.86024034},{"title":"Former Flipkart exec’s quick comm startup FirstClub raises $23 million; valuation jumps to $120 million - The Economic Times","url":"https://m.economictimes.com/tech/funding/firstclub-raises-23-million-in-a-funding-round-led-by-accel-and-rtp-global/articleshow/123682574.cms","content":"Quick commerce startup FirstClub has raised $23 million in a funding round led by venture capital firms Accel and RTP Global, who had also co-led the previous round. Following this funding round, which was about 90% equity and the rest debt, the company’s valuation now stands at $120 million.  \n  \nExisting investors Blume Ventures and 2am VC doubled down in this round, which also drew new backers Paramark Ventures and Aditya Birla Ventures. [...] BenchmarksLIVE\n\nNifty23,530.50-104.60\n\nBenchmarksLIVE\n\nSensex75,088.89-488.69\n\nBSE Gainer-Large Cap\n\nAdani Ent.3,127.50174.41\n\nBSE Loser-Large Cap\n\nCoforge1,862.80-87.21\n\nPrecious Metal\n\nGold (MCX) (Rs/10g.) (Rs/10g.)\")1,52,875.00296.00\n\nPrecious Metal\n\nUSD/INR95.160.33\n\nThe Economic Timessection logo\n\n| \n\nToday's ePaper\n\nAI\n\nIT\n\nTech & Internet\n\nFunding\n\nStartups\n\nTech Bytes\n\nNewsletters\n\nFull Stack\n\nTech Top 5\n\nMorning Dispatch\n\nUnwrapped\n\nBlogs & Opinion\n\nET AI Awards 2027\n\nET AI-Ready [...] The company plans to deploy the funds towards opening new dark stores in Bengaluru, rolling out formats like cafes and daily subscriptions, expanding into new categories, hiring talent, and investing in brand building.  \n  \nThe company raised $8 million in December last year.","score":0.8593928},{"title":"FirstClub bucks India's speed obsession, quickly triples valuation to $120M with premium approach | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2025/09/03/firstclub-bucks-indias-speed-obsession-quickly-triples-valuation-to-120m-with-premium-approach","content":"At a post-money valuation of $120 million, the Bengaluru-based startup has raised $23 million in a Series A round (comprising more than 90% equity and the rest in debt) co-led by returning investors Accel and RTP Global. The round also saw participation from Blume Founders Fund, 2am VC, Paramark Ventures, and Aditya Birla Ventures. This new funding comes just eight months after FirstClub raised its $8 million seed round at a $40 million valuation in December. [...] The founder hit the ground running with experience under his belt. Before founding FirstClub in December, Ayyappan spent over a decade at Flipkart, India’s largest homegrown e-commerce company, where he led teams at its subsidiaries Myntra (a fashion e-commerce site) and Cleartrip (a travel booking site). He was previously part of the team at Indian consumer goods giant ITC, focusing on strategies to expand grocery market and outlet coverage. Those experiences helped him quickly turn FirstClub [...] “Based the last three months’ data, it’s quite clear that consumers are happy to wait if they are getting a very differentiated selection, a good quality of products, a differentiated service, and a very hand-holding sort of an experience,” said Ayyappan R, founder and CEO of FirstClub, in an interview.","score":0.8467682},{"title":"FirstClub - 2026 Company Profile, Team, Funding, Competitors & Financials - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/firstclub/__mdh2vRqOLmJ-ypn60h21QXYugegx_b8hc8Zk7LHlLWo","content":"| 8th | Logo for LoveLocal  LoveLocal 2015, Mumbai  (India), Series A | Platform offering e-commerce platform connecting consumers with local retailers | $25.7M | Chiratae Ventures, Vulcan Capital  & 63 others | 69/100 |\n| 9th | Logo for DealShare  DealShare 2018, Bengaluru  (India), Series E | Retailer of groceries and household goods through an online platform | $387M | Alpha Wave Global, WestBridge Capital  & 66 others | 66/100 | [...] | Shareholders Name | Post Round Holding % | Net worth | Cumulative Investment | Realised Returns | Unrealised Returns | Return Multiple |\n ---  ---  --- \n| Founder | 39.05% | 919Cr | 3843223 | 5679100 | 2567927 | 1753090 |\n| Ayyappan Rajagopal | 5307009 | 8071430 | 3508259 | 1385427 | 8281566 | 2016943 |\n| Fund | 47.32% | 1,110Cr | 1922069 | 3113621 | 1228733 | 5330764 |\n| Accel | 1476890 | 3869561 | 3932386 | 4689678 | 5348282 | 9120701 | [...] | Peak XV Partners | 5531312 | 2678609 | 2060042 | 1245652 | 5513591 | 6496637 |\n| Sofina | 7065088 | 6837792 | 6645008 | 4839704 | 8802985 | 2142477 |\n| RTP Global | 825439 | 421836 | 983966 | 148190 | 990607 |