{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:35:13.848Z","session":"c47cae16-279d-41a2-b401-3efa2780e299","event":"tool.end","callId":"ebd9087d-3cdb-4f13-a14a-817e3cec189f","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":3805,"result":[{"title":"FirstClub raises $55 million from Peak XV, Sofina and others nine months after $22 million Series A round","url":"https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/funding/firstclub-raises-55-million-from-peak-xv-sofina-and-others-9-months-after-22-million-series-a-round-13940632.html","content":"Bengaluru-based premium grocery and quick commerce startup FirstClub has raised $55 million in a Series B funding round co-led by Peak XV Partners and Sofina, valuing the company at $255 million post-investment.\n\nMoneycontrol was the first to report, in March, that FirstClub was in talks to raise $50-60 million (around Rs 450-550 crore) from Peak XV Partners, Sofina Ventures and others at a valuation of about $250 million (around Rs 2,250 crore). [...] Existing investors Accel, RTP Global and Paramark Ventures also participated in the round. The latest financing takes FirstClub's total funding to $86 million.\n\nThe company said it will use the fresh capital to expand beyond Bengaluru, where it currently operates 21 stores, deepen its presence in Hyderabad, where it recently launched with three locations, and continue investing in its supply chain, technology and category expansion initiatives. [...] The company currently operates through a network of stores in Bengaluru and Hyderabad and plans to expand its footprint further as it scales operations. FirstClub is also looking to broaden its assortment across categories including home products, kids' food, pet care and gifting, while exploring adjacent offerings such as subscription-based services and experiential retail formats.","score":0.93952066},{"title":"FirstClub raises $55 million to deepen quality-first premium quick commerce play | Company Business News","url":"https://www.livemint.com/companies/news/firstclub-quick-commerce-series-b-funding-peak-xv-partners-sofina-ventures-supply-chain-category-expansion-11780479760093.html","content":"FirstClub, a premium quick commerce startup, has raised $55 million in its Series B round of funding from investors led by Peak XV Partners and Sofina Ventures, the company’s top executive said. Existing investors Accel, RTP Global and Paramark Ventures doubled down in the new round. [...] The largest share of the fresh capital will be directed at supply chain infrastructure. The company is building out its third, larger warehouse in Bengaluru. It has one warehouse in Hyderabad, a city it entered a few weeks ago.\n\nBeyond physical infrastructure, the company plans to invest in cold-chain integrity, quality testing protocols and demand forecasting — processes that it expects will distinguish its model from conventional dark-store operators. [...] \"Most of the investment is focused on maintaining quality across the supply chain right from sourcing into warehouses, through to the middle mile,\" Ayyappan said.\n\nWhile Bangalore has 21 ‘clubhouses,’ FirstClub's name for dark stores, Hyderabad has three. In the next six months, the startup plans to open 50 such clubhouses across both cities.\n\n## New product offerings","score":0.8868231},{"title":"FirstClub Raises $55M in Series B Led by Peak XV, Sofina - Ventureburn","url":"https://ventureburn.com/firstclub-raises-55m-in-series-b-led-by-peak-xv-sofina","content":"## Roadmap for Strategic Scale\n\nFirstClub has handled its physical expansion with a conservative footprint relative to standard multi-city operators. The startup currently manages 24 specialised fulfilment hubs, which it designates as clubhouses. Twenty-one of these fulfilment centres are located within its home base of Bengaluru, covering roughly 85% of high-density zip codes. The company recently opened the remaining three hubs to seed a presence in Hyderabad. [...] Editor's Choice\n\n Cryptocurrency\n 4 months ago\n\nBinance Alpha Sealcoin (QAIT) Airdrop To Launch on May 28. How To Claim QAIT Tokens?\n\n Cryptocurrency\n 4 months ago\n\n10 Best Crypto Mining App Options in 2026 (Free & Legit)\n\n Exchanges\n 3 weeks ago\n\n10 Best Decentralized Crypto Exchanges (DEXs) in 2026\n\n Exchanges\n 3 weeks ago\n\nBest Crypto Staking Platforms With Highest APY September 2026\n\n Exchanges\n 2 weeks ago\n\n10 Best Crypto Portfolio Tracker Apps in 2026 (Free & Paid)\n\nTable of Contents [...] The company will channel the newly acquired $55 million toward warehouse infrastructure, fulfilment technology, and expanding clubhouses to 35 centres by year-end. Beyond structural expansion, FirstClub plans a significant category push into non-grocery sectors. Over the next quarter, the application will introduce dedicated verticals for beauty and personal care, domestic essentials, kitchenware, and pet care supplies.\n\nEkemini\n\nEkemini","score":0.7703443},{"title":"Peak XV Partners - 2026 Investor Profile, Portfolio, Team & Investment Trends - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/venture-capital/peak-xv-partners/__KWw3XbsFlXlo-Z5eRJu5pASu9j-uOs_VA1GbauLuLOE","content":"lock\n\n| Date | Company | Location | Round Details | Round Amount | Co-Investors |\n ---  ---  --- |\n| Sep 07, 2026 | Nua | India | Series C | 1913 | Filter Capital   [+2] |\n| Sep 05, 2026 | Mokobara | India | Series C | 1696 | Sauce   [+3] |\n| Aug 31, 2026 | Agrani Labs | India | Seed | 9890 \n| Aug 21, 2026 | Arintra | United States | Series B | 7008 | Define Ventures   [+6] |\n| Aug 17, 2026 | Wispr Flow | United States | Series B | 7957 | Menlo Ventures   [+10] | [...] | Tracxn Score | Company | Short Description | Founded year | Sector | Location | Company Stage | First Investment/ Acquisition Details |\n ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| 75 | Sarvam | Developer of a full-stack generative AI platform designed to build sovereign AI ecosystems for enterprises and governments | 2023 | High Tech ( | Bengaluru | Series B | zgnlfiy |\n| 54 | Alpaca Sec