AI Summit 2026\n\n15th – 18th June, 2026 | Moscone Center, San Francisco, Booth 203\n\nInfosys is participating as a Legend Sponsor at Databricks Data + AI Summit 2026, Databricks’ flagship global conference and the world’s largest gathering of the data and AI community.\n\nRead More\n\nAgentic commerce: How to build agent-aware digital ecosystems for AI-powered retail\n\nInsights","score":0.54782754}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:39:26.273Z","session":"13e27e25-8c9f-4fb2-9419-8b36029615ad","event":"tool.end","callId":"6bdc3198-9fce-4499-858e-8c8be445f9a2","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2537,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] Parekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others. He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[edit] [...] 4. ↑ \"A Gujarati appointed as CEO and MD of Infosys\". DeshGujarat. 2 December 2017. Retrieved 14 July 2025.\n5. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". mint. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n6. ↑ Shivapriya, N. \"Salil Parekh: The man who played a pivotal role in building Capgemini's India operations\". The Economic Times. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n7. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". LiveMint. Retrieved 3 January 2018.","score":0.91137725},{"title":"Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay","url":"https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh","content":"Mr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988. [...] Prior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.”","score":0.8763069},{"title":"Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...","url":"https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors","content":"Home\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] Apr 23 2024 \n\nConnecticut was a top 10 destination for remote workers who relocated in 2022, according to a new study.Yardi Kube, a coworking management platform, released the results of its study in February in a report titled, “Remote Workers Leading the Migration Across State Lines.”The study, which is based on data from...Continue Reading\n\n## Contact Us\n\nBen Dwyer headshot\n\nBen Dwyer  \nDirector, Marketing [...] ## More Topics\n\n### TTM TECHNOLOGIES EXPANDS WORKFORCE IN CONNECTICUT\n\nMay 6 2024\n\nStafford, Connecticut, May 6, 2024 – AdvanceCT today announced that TTM Technologies Inc. (TTM), a global manufacturer of technology solutions including radio frequency (“RF”) components, RF microwave/microelectronic assemblies, and advanced printed circuit boards (“PCBs”), is expanding its workforce in its two Stafford locations.TTM was looking to invest in modernization and...Continue Reading","score":0.8194462},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html","content":"+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] Prior to Infosys, Salil was a member of the management board at Capgemini and a partner at consulting practice Ernst & Young LLP prior to its acquisition by Capgemini. He had different leadership roles there across US, UK, Europe, Asia, over a span of 25 years.\n\nSalil has received several awards as a leading CEO.","score":0.77261686},{"title":"What's next for Salil Parekh? Outgoing Infosys CEO on life ...","url":"https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/information-technology/whats-next-for-salil-parekh-outgoing-infosys-ceo-on-life-after-infosys-and-nandan-nilekani-13990109.html","content":"Responding to questions on why he did not seek a third term despite being eligible for another extension, Parekh stopped short of giving a direct reason but said Infosys had achieved the transformation he envisioned when he took over in January 2018. [...] Parekh, whose tenure ends on March 31, 2027, took charge at a turbulent time for Infosys following a leadership crisis. During his tenure, the company doubled annual revenue from $10 billion to $20 billion, expanded its workforce from around 200,000 to more than 300,000 employees, strengthened its large deals business and pivoted from digital transformation to artificial intelligence services.\n\n## Related Stories [...] Also read: You need companies like Infosys to make AI work in enterprises, says CEO Parekh\n\nBacks Ashiss Dash\n\nParekh also strongly endorsed CEO-designate Ashiss Dash, who was named last week to succeed him from April 1, 2027.\n\nCalling Dash ‘a very good friend’ and ‘a great leader’, Parekh said the two would work closely over the coming months to ensure a smooth leadership transition.","score":0.7409441}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:39:26.289Z","session":"13e27e25-8c9f-4fb2-9419-8b36029615ad","event":"tool.end","callId":"5fffcf78-3df5-4a02-8a78-ff2e1fa5df93","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2549,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] [edit]\n\nSalil Parekh is born into a Gujarati family. He is a graduate from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay (IIT Bombay) in Aeronautical Engineering. Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University.\n\nParekh was member of the group management board at Capgemini, where he had worked since 2000, after Ernst & Young's consultancy division, where he had been working before, was merged into the company. [...] Print/export\n\n Download as PDF\n Printable version\n\nIn other projects\n\n Wikimedia Commons\n Wikidata item\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian businessman, current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n\n| Born | (1964-06-05) 5 June 1964 (age 62) |\n| Education | IIT Bombay (BTech) Cornell University (MS) |\n| Occupations | CEO & MD of Infosys |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh |","score":0.83678174},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/salil-parekh","content":"### CEO, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys Limited, one of India’s leading global IT services companies. Parekh graduated with a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Bombay in 1986. He then pursued higher studies at Cornell University, earning Master of Engineering degrees in both Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering in 1988.","score":0.81979275},{"title":"Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay","url":"https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh","content":"Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988. [...] Mr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Prior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.”","score":0.7487387},{"title":"Salil Parekh - Managing Director and CEO, Infosys","url":"https://usispf.org/board-of-directors/salil-parekh","content":"Salil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic direction for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team to drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services industry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing business turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions. He is a member of the National Council of the [...] Capgemini’s North America Executive Council. He was the architect of the North America growth and turnaround strategy, and was instrumental in setting up their offshoring capabilities. [...] Salil was also Partner at Ernst & Young and widely credited for bringing scale and value to the Indian operations of the consultancy firm.\n\nHe holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.\n\n###### Subscribe to our\n\n Daily Newsletter   Weekly Newsletter","score":0.71040785},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html","content":"+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] Salil is on the board of Advance CT, an organization that supports business and innovation in the state of Connecticut. Salil is on the Board of the US-India Strategic Partnership Forum (USISPF) an organization that works towards strengthening the US-India relationship and promoting collaboration in various sectors, including technology.\n\nSalil Parekh is also an Executive Officer for Infosys.\n\n## Request for services [...] Salil holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.","score":0.6721816}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:39:26.298Z","session":"13e27e25-8c9f-4fb2-9419-8b36029615ad","event":"tool.end","callId":"a36d2d2e-9978-4275-8399-811ff6c7b57b","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2561,"result":[{"title":"History of Infosys - Origin, Timeline and Subsidiaries","url":"https://www.bajajfinserv.in/history-of-infosys","content":"## Frequently asked questions\n\nWho are the 7 founders of Infosys?\n\nInfosys was founded in 1981 by seven visionary engineers: N.R. Narayana Murthy, Nandan Nilekani, Kris Gopalakrishnan, S.D. Shibulal, K. Dinesh, N.S. Raghavan, and Ashok Arora. These individuals laid the foundation of one of India's most successful IT companies with a shared investment of US$250 and a strong vision for global excellence in software services.\n\nWhat is the future outlook for Infosys? [...] |  |  |\n --- |\n| Aspect | Details |\n| Founded | 1981 |\n| Founders | N.R. Narayana Murthy and six others |\n| Headquarters | Bengaluru, Karnataka, India |\n| Revenue (FY25) | US$19.3 billion |\n| Market Capitalisation | US$75.8 billion |\n| Employees | Over 323,000 |\n| Global Presence | Operations in more than 50 countries |\n| Stock Listings | NSE: INFY, BSE: 500209, NYSE: INFY |\n| Core Services | IT consulting, software development, business process outsourcing | [...] Infosys was established in 1981 in Pune by seven engineers, including N.R. Narayana Murthy, with an initial capital of just US$250. The company's humble beginnings were marked by a vision to provide world-class IT services from India. In 1983, Infosys relocated its headquarters to Bengaluru, positioning itself in what would become India's Silicon Valley. Over the years, Infosys has grown exponentially, becoming a global leader in IT services and consulting. The company's journey from a small","score":0.92700076},{"title":"N. R. Narayana Murthy - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N._R._Narayana_Murthy","content":"In this Indian name, the name Nagavara Ramarao is a patronymic, and the person should be referred to by the given name, Narayana Murthy.\n\nNagavara Ramarao Narayana Murthy (born 20 August 1946) is an Indian billionaire businessman. He is the founder of Infosys, and was the chairman, chief executive officer (CEO), president and chief mentor of the company before retiring and becoming chairman emeritus. As of January 2025, his net worth was estimated at US$5.0 billion, according to Forbes. [...] |  v  t  e |\n\n| People (list) | |  |  |  --- | | Founders |  N. R. Narayana Murthy  Nandan Nilekani  N. S. Raghavan  S. Gopalakrishnan  S. D. Shibulal  K. Dinesh  Ashok Arora | | Board of directors |  Salil Parekh (CEO & MD)  U. B. Pravin Rao (COO)  Carol M. Browner  John Etchemendy  Jeffrey S. Lehman  Kiran Mazumdar-Shaw  Ravi Venkatesan | |\n| Divisions |  Infosys BPM  Infosys Consulting  EdgeVerve Systems |\n| Products |  Finacle  Panaya |\n| Other |  Infosys Foundation  Infosys Prize | [...] Murthy mentions that being arrested and expelled for no good reason during the communist era 1974 in a border town near the Yugoslav-Bulgarian border, turned him into a \"compassionate capitalist\" from a \"confused leftist/communist\". In 1981 he, with six software professionals, founded Infosys with an initial capital investment of Rs 10,000, which was provided by his wife Sudha Murty. Murthy was the CEO of Infosys for 21 years from 1981 to 2002 and was succeeded by co-founder Nandan Nilekani. At","score":0.85825616},{"title":"Infosys – Founders of the Company | Management Profiles","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/founders.html","content":"# Founders\n\n## Founder\n\nN.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nN.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nFounder\n\n## Co-founders\n\nNandan M. Nilekani\n\nNandan M. Nilekani\n\nCo-founder\n\nS. Gopalakrishnan\n\nS. Gopalakrishnan\n\nCo-founder\n\nS.D. Shibulal\n\nS.D. Shibulal\n\nCo-founder\n\nK. Dinesh\n\nK. Dinesh\n\nCo-founder\n\nN.S. Raghavan\n\nN.S. Raghavan\n\nCo-founder\n\nAshok Arora\n\nAshok Arora\n\nCo-founder\n\