rvices, and Sogeti (Technology & Engineering Services Division). He was responsible for the strategy and execution of these businesses – setting direction and enabling rapid client adoption. He was also the Chairman of Capgemini’s\n\n[S3] Salil Parekh, Infosys, topped the IT services ...\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/infosys_salil-parekh-infosys-topped-the-it-services-activity-7153321981889662978-cEHf\nImage 1: Infosys\n\nInfosys\n\n10,370,681 followers\n\n 1y \n\n   Report this post\n\nSalil Parekh, Infosys, topped the IT services ranking in Brand Finance's Brand Guardianship Index (BGI) 2024 for the role of CEO as brand custodian and steward of long-term shareholder value. Read more. bit.ly/4aWIBB5\n\n   Image 2: No alternative text description for this image\n\nImage 3Image 4Image 5 2,46242 Comments\n\nLikeComment\n\n Share \n   Copy\n   LinkedIn\n   Facebook\n   Twitter\n\nImage 6: Shantha Pillay, graphic [...] Salil Parekh, Infosys, topped the IT services ranking in Brand Finance's Brand Guardianship Index (BGI) 2024 for the role of CEO as brand custodian and steward of long-term shareholder value. Read… | Infosys | 42 comments\n\nAgree & Join LinkedIn\n\nBy clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement, Privacy Policy, and Cookie Policy.\n\nSkip to main contentLinkedIn\n   Top Content\n   People\n   Learning\n   Jobs\n   Games\n\nJoin nowSign in\n\nInfosys’ Post\n\nImage 1: Infosys [...] Image 14: Shantishesh Warty, graphic\n\nShantishesh Warty\nCEO & MD & Member of Board of Directors / Adviser --- Electrical Reforms in India . Adviser ..... Make in India movement of PM Member ...... India Energy WEEK held in Bengaluru 2023 .\n\n 1y \n\n   Report this comment\n\nVery True , he is a very cool ,humble person with lot of knowledge and skill sets .\n\nLikeReply 1 Reaction \n\nImage 15: Amit Sapkal, graphic\n\nAmit Sapkal\nPrincipal Consultant - Cyber Security at Infosys Limited, Pune\n\n 1y\n\n[S4] World Economic Forum 2024 | Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/wef/2024/salil-parekh.html\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh [...] Salil Parekh\n\nSalil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic\ndirection for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team\nto drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services\nindustry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing\nbusiness turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions.\n\n[S5] Infosys Integrated Annual Report 2024-25\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/investors/reports-filings/annual-report/annual/documents/infosys-ar-25.pdf\nDate of first appointment to the Board, last drawn remuneration and number of Board meetings attended: Salil was first appointed to the Board on January 2, 2018, as CEO & MD, and reappointed on July 1, 2022, as CEO & MD. The details pertaining to his appointment, remuneration, and number of meetings attended are provided in the Corporate governance report section of the Integrated Annual Report 2024-25. Additional information on directors recommended for appointment / reappointment as required [...] and managing successful acquisitions. Salil topped the IT services ranking in Brand Finance’s Brand Guardianship Index (BGI) 2024 for the role of CEO as brand custodian and steward of long-term shareholder value. Over the years Salil has won several CEO leadership awards. Earlier, Salil was a member of the Group Executive Board at Capgemini, where he held several leadership positions for 25 years. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services (North [...] Regulatory orders \n\nThere were no material regulatory orders pertaining to the Company for fiscal 2025, except for the Settlement order dated June 26, 2024 in respect of Settlement Application filed by Salil Parekh, CEO & MD of the Company. The details of the order are disclosed at  company-statement-sebi-27jun2024.pdf. \n\nCEO and CFO certification \n\nAs required by the Listing Regulations, the CEO and CFO certification is provided in this Integrated Annual Report. \n\nCode of Conduct and Ethics\n\n[S6] Salil Parekh\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh\nSalil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] Parekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others. He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[edit] [...] 4. ↑ \"A Gujarati appointed as CEO and MD of Infosys\". DeshGujarat. 2 December 2017. Retrieved 14 July 2025.\n5. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". mint. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n6. ↑ Shivapriya, N. \"Salil Parekh: The man who played a pivotal role in building Capgemini's India operations\". The Economic Times. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n7. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". LiveMint. Retrieved 3 January 2018.\n\n[S7] Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay\nURL: https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh\nMr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988. [...] Prior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.”\n\n[S8] Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html\n+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] Prior to Infosys, Salil was a member of the management board at Capgemini and a partner at consulting practice Ernst & Young LLP prior to its acquisition by Capgemini. He had different leadership roles there across US, UK, Europe, Asia, over a span of 25 years.\n\nSalil has received several awards as a leading CEO.\n\n[S9] What's next for Salil Parekh? Outgoing Infosys CEO on life ...\nURL: https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/information-technology/whats-next-for-salil-parekh-outgoing-infosys-ceo-on-life-after-infosys-and-nandan-nilekani-13990109.html\nResponding to questions on why he did not seek a third term despite being eligible for another extension, Parekh stopped short of giving a direct reason but said Infosys had achieved the transformation he envisioned when he took over in January 2018. [...] Parekh, whose tenure ends on March 31, 2027, took charge at a turbulent time for Infosys following a leadership crisis. During his tenure, the company doubled annual revenue from $10 billion to $20 billion, expanded its workforce from around 200,000 to more than 300,000 employees, strengthened its large deals business and pivoted from digital transformation to artificial intelligence services.\n\n## Related Stories [...] Also read: You need companies like Infosys to make AI work in enterprises, says CEO Parekh\n\nBacks Ashiss Dash\n\nParekh also strongly endorsed CEO-designate Ashiss Dash, who was named last week to succeed him from April 1, 2027.\n\nCalling Dash ‘a very good friend’ and ‘a great leader’, Parekh said the two would work closely over the coming months to ensure a smooth leadership transition.\n\n[S10] History of Infosys - Origin, Timeline and Subsidiaries\nURL: https://www.bajajfinserv.in/history-of-infosys\n## Frequently asked questions\n\nWho are the 7 founders of Infosys?\n\nInfosys was founded in 1981 by seven visionary engineers: N.R. Narayana Murthy, Nandan Nilekani, Kris Gopalakrishnan, S.D. Shibulal, K. Dinesh, N.S. Raghavan, and Ashok Arora. These individuals laid the foundation of one of India's most successful IT companies with a shared investment of US$250 and a strong vision for global excellence in software services.\n\nWhat is the future outlook for Infosys? [...] Infosys was established in 1981 in Pune by seven engineers, including N.R. Narayana Murthy, with an initial capital of just US$250. The company's humble beginnings were marked by a vision to provide world-class IT services from India. In 1983, Infosys relocated its headquarters to Bengaluru, positioning itself in what would become India's Silicon Valley. Over the years, Infosys has grown exponentially, becoming a global leader in IT services and consulting. The company's journey from a small [...] |  |  |\n --- |\n| Aspect | Details |\n| Founded | 1981 |\n| Founders | N.R. Narayana Murthy and six others |\n| Headquarters | Bengaluru, Karnataka, India |\n| Revenue (FY25) | US$19.3 billion |\n| Market Capitalisation | US$75.8 billion |\n| Employees | Over 323,000 |\n| Global Presence | Operations in more than 50 countries |\n| Stock Listings | NSE: INFY, BSE: 500209, NYSE: INFY |\n| Core Services | IT consulting, software development, business process outsourcing |\n\n[S11] Mr. Narayana Murthy and Infosys | Asia Society\nURL: https://asiasociety.org/mr-narayana-murthy-and-infosys\nIn 1981, Narayana Murthy founded Infosys Technologies along with six of his friends. None of them had the money to start the company, but luckily his wife Sudha Murthy, who was an engineer with Tata Industries, had saved 10,000 rupees (Rs)--about 250 U.S. dollars--that she donated to start the company. [...] After India abandoned its planned economy in 1991 and embraced global capitalism, many new technology companies sprang up all over the country, especially in the Bangalore area. One of the most successful of these start-up companies was Infosys, an information technology company launched by Mr. Narayana Murthy and six of his friends in 1981 with the support of Mrs. Sudha Murthy. In 2000 Infosys, the first Indian company to be traded on NASDQ, was worth about U.S. $27 billion. This case study\n\n[S12] N.R. Narayana Murthy: Founder | Management Profiles\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/narayana-murthy.html\n# N.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nFounder\n\nN.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nMr. Murthy founded Infosys in 1981. Infosys is, today, a highly innovative software services global\ncompany listed on NYSE in the US and on the Bombay Stock Exchange in Mumbai. [...] Under Mr. Murthy’s leadership, Infosys became the leader in innovation - in technical, managerial and\nleadership training, software technology, quality, productivity, customer focus, employee\nsatisfaction, and physical and technological infrastructure. [...] Thank you for connecting with us. We will respond\nto you shortly.\n\nSubsidiaries\n\nPrograms\n\nCompany\n\nSupport\n\nCopyright © 2026 Infosys Limited\n\nLoading\n\n[S13] N. R. Narayana Murthy\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N._R._Narayana_Murthy\nIn this Indian name, the name Nagavara Ramarao is a patronymic, and the person should be referred to by the given name, Narayana Murthy.\n\nNagavara Ramarao Narayana Murthy (born 20 August 1946) is an Indian billionaire businessman. He is the founder of Infosys, and was the chairman, chief executive officer (CEO), president and chief mentor of the company before retiring and becoming chairman emeritus. As of January 2025, his net worth was estimated at US$5.0 billion, according to Forbes. [...] Murthy mentions that being arrested and expelled for no good reason during the communist era 1974 in a border town near the Yugoslav-Bulgarian border, turned him into a \"compassionate capitalist\" from a \"confused leftist/communist\". In 1981 he, with six software professionals, founded Infosys with an initial capital investment of Rs 10,000, which was provided by his wife Sudha Murty. Murthy was the CEO of Infosys for 21 years from 1981 to 2002 and was succeeded by co-founder Nandan Nilekani. At [...] Murthy was born and raised in Sidlaghatta, Karnataka. He first worked at the Indian Institute of Management Ahmedabad, as chief systems programmer, and Patni Computer Systems in Pune, Maharashtra. He founded Infosys in 1981 and was the CEO from 1981 to 2002, as well as the chairman from 2002 to 2011. In 2011, he stepped down from the board and became the chairman emeritus. In June 2013, Murthy was appointed as the executive chairman for a period of five years.\n\n[S14] Company History & Defining Milestones | About Us\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/history.html\n### 1981\n\n Infosys is established by N. R. Narayana Murthy and six engineers in Pune, India, with an initial capital of US$250\n Signs up its first client, Data Basics Corporation, in New York\n\n## Request for services\n\nFind out more about how we can help your organization navigate its next. Let us know your areas of interest so that we can serve you better.\n\nLoading [...] ### 2002\n\n Touches revenues of US$500 million\n Nandan M. Nilekani takes over as CEO from N.R. Narayana Murthy, who is appointed Chairman and Chief Mentor\n Opens offices in the Netherlands, Singapore and Switzerland\n Infosys and the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania set up The Wharton Infosys Business Transformation Awards (WIBTA)\n Launches Progeon, offering business process outsourcing services\n\n### 2001\n\n[S15] Infosys | Company Overview & News\nURL: https://www.forbes.com/companies/infosys\nInfosys Ltd. is a digital services and consulting company, which engages in the provision of end-to-end business solutions. It operates through the following segments: Financial Services, Retail, Communication; Energy, Utilities, Resources, and Services; Manufacturing, Hi-Tech, Life Sciences, and All Other. The company was founded by Dinesh Krishnan Swamy, Senapathy Gopalakrishnan, Narayana Ramarao Nagavara Murthy, Raghavan N. S., Ashok Arora, Nandan M. Nilekani, and S. D. Shibulal on July 2, [...] Shibulal on July 2, 1981 and is headquartered in Bangalore, India. [...] The consulting companies recognized on this year's list span 31 countries and offer expertise in a wide range of industries including IT, retail, pharmaceuticals and more.\n\n[S16] (INFY.P) | Stock Price & Latest News | Reuters\nURL: https://www.reuters.com/markets/companies/INFY.P\nInfosys Limited is an India-based company which provides digital services and consulting. The Company enables clients in approximately 63 countries to navigate their digital transformation powered by cloud and artificial intelligence (AI). Its segments include Financial Services; Retail; Communication; Energy, Utilities, Resources and Services; Manufacturing; Hi-Tech; Life Sciences, and All other segments. The Company's solutions have been primarily classified as digital and core. Its digital [...] ## About Infosys Limited (INFY.P)\n\n### Company Information [...] core. Its digital solutions include experience, insight, innovate, accelerate, and assure. Its experience solutions include Infosys Aster, Digital Marketing, Digital Commerce and Infosys Metaverse Foundry. Its insight solutions include Infosys Topaz, Infosys Generative AI Labs, Data Analytics and AI, Infosys Sustainability Services and Applied AI. Its core solutions include application management services, proprietary application development services, traditional enterprise application\n\n[S17] Infosys - LinkedIn\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/company/infosys\nInfosys is a global leader in next-generation digital services and consulting. We enable clients in more than 50 countries to navigate their digital transformation. With over three decades of experience in managing the systems and workings of global enterprises, we expertly steer our clients through their digital journey. We do it by enabling the enterprise with an AI-powered core that helps prioritize the execution of change. We also empower the business with agile digital at scale to deliver [...] at scale to deliver unprecedented levels of performance and customer delight. Our always-on learning agenda drives their continuous improvement through building and transferring digital skills, expertise, and ideas from our innovation ecosystem. Visit www.infosys.com to see how Infosys (NYSE: INFY) can help your enterprise navigate your next. [...] # Infosys\nTransforming Enterprises To Become A Thriving Live Enterprise. AI-Powered. Digital Agility At Scale. Always-On Learning.\nIT Services and IT Consulting • Bangalore, Karnataka • 11,408,183 followers • 10,001+ employees\n\n[S18] Infosys\nURL: https://www.zoominfo.com/c/infosys-ltd/58804259\n# Infosys\n\nInfosys is a global provider of next-generation digital services and consulting services. Infosys provides information technology and digital marketing services such as AI and automation, Agile and DevOps, Salesforce, cyber security, data analytics, engineering services, and much more. Infosys is headquartered in Bengaluru, India.... \n\n## Leadership [...] - [On August 18, Infosys (NYSE:INFY) announced a long-term deal to manage the enterprise software behind Knorr-Bremse AG, a maker of braking systems for rail and commercial vehicles. The work stretches from ERP and data platforms to engineering and product lifecycle tools, and it runs on Infosys Topaz, the company’s AI offering. It is a nice […]](\n- The Palo Alto startup says it has landed multiple seven-figure enterprise contracts within months of launch. [...] ## Leadership\n\n- Kiran Umakanth — Senior Principal - Chief Information Officer ...\n- Vijayanush Narasimh... — Chief Financial Officer, (India & South Asia)\n- Raktim Singh — Chief Technology Officer, Office\n\n## Company Details\n\n- Website: \n- Revenue: $18.8 Billion\n- Stock Symbol:  INFY\n- Employees: 10K+\n- Industries: Business Services; Software Testing\n- Headquarters: 44 Infosys Avenue Hosur Electronics City Rd, Bengaluru, Karnātaka, 560100, India\n- Phone: +91 8028520261\n\n## Social Media\n\n- \n-\n\n[S19] [Infosys India Competitors](/infosys-india-competitors_b7f66710c2adef45 \"Infosys India Competitors\")\nURL: https://rocketreach.co/infosys-india-competitors_b7f66710c2adef45\nWipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO) is a leading AI-powered technology services and consulting company focused on building innovative solutions that address clients’ most complex digital transformation needs. Leveraging our consulting-led approach and the Wipro Intelligence™ unified suite of AI-powered platforms, solutions and transformative offerings, we help clients realize their boldest ambitions to build intelligent and sustainable businesses. The Wipro Innovation Network –\n\n[S20] Salil Parekh - Managing Director and CEO, Infosys\nURL: https://usispf.org/board-of-directors/salil-parekh\nSalil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic direction for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team to drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services industry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing business turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions. He is a member of the National Council of the [...] Capgemini’s North America Executive Council. He was the architect of the North America growth and turnaround strategy, and was instrumental in setting up their offshoring capabilities. [...] Salil was also Partner at Ernst & Young and widely credited for bringing scale and value to the Indian operations of the consultancy firm.\n\nHe holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.\n\n###### Subscribe to our\n\n Daily Newsletter   Weekly Newsletter\n\n[S21] Salil Parekh - India | Professional Profile\nURL: https://in.linkedin.com/in/salilparekh\n## People Also Viewed\n- Saroj Rana (LEXIPHORIA) - \n- Rishi Aurora (IBM) - \n- Jaideep Kapur CPA (US) (Alphamoneta Inc.) - \n- Krishnan R V (Waybeo Inc) - \n- Sreelakshmi Suresh (eDesign Technologies) - \n- usha rani (Self-employed) - \n- Srikanth Mallarapu (Kastech Software Solutions Group) - \n- Adv. Suresh Kumar N (Self-employed) - \n- Sunil Kumar (SoftElixir InfoTech (P) Ltd) - \n- Venkatramana Nagabandi (Palate Networks) - \n- Mohit Thakur (Brain Star Technologies) - [...] # Salil Parekh\n\nIndia, IN  \n424 connections, 13500 followers\n\n## About\nNone\n\n## Experience\nN/A\n\n## Education\nN/A\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nN/A\n\n## Certifications\nN/A\n\n## Volunteering\nN/A\n\n## Languages\nN/A\n\n## Organizations\nN/A\n\n## Activity\n- Age is an issue of mind over matter If you don't mind, it doesn't matter  \nLiked by Salil Parekh  \nView Post  \nActivity Image [...] - Todo listo para la presentación del nuevo libro de nuestro CEO Paulo Morgado en IE Business School el próximo martes 14 noviembre #strategy…  \nLiked by Salil Parekh  \nView Post  \nActivity Image\n\n[S22] N.R. Narayana Murthy\nURL: https://www.forbes.com/profile/nr-narayana-murthy\nN.R. Narayana Murthy is the legendary cofounder and retired chairman of Indian tech giant Infosys, in which he continues to hold a minority stake.\n\nMurthy stepped down as chairman in 2011 after 30 years with the company but returned in 2013 to hand over management to a professional CEO in 2014.\n\nIn 2017, Murthy was in the news for raising concerns over alleged corporate governance lapses at Infosys, which the company denied. [...] Banker Kundapur Vaman Kamath, 63, was recently named chairman of Infosys Technologies, the $6 billion (revenues) Indian software services giant in Bangalore. He will be the first non-founder to occupy that position, albeit in a non-executive role, after N.R. Narayana Murthy, the company’s iconic billionaire founder steps down in August. [...] [...] Infosys was long defined by the charisma and values of its iconic founder-chairman, N.R. Narayana Murthy. With his innings coming to an end, the company begins its quest for longevity in an era of change.\n\n[S23] Narayana Murthy | Indian IT Pioneer, Infosys Founder | Britannica Money\nURL: https://www.britannica.com/money/Narayana-Murthy\nAzim Premji\n\nAzim Premji\nBill Gates smiling and wearing glasses, a dark suit, a pale shirt, and a patterned tie.\n\nBill Gates\nMukesh Ambani\n\nMukesh Ambani\n\nin full:\n:   Nagavara Ramarao Narayana Murthy\n\nborn:\n:   Aug. 20, 1946, Kolar, Karnataka state, India (age 80)\n\nNarayana Murthy (born Aug. 20, 1946, Kolar, Karnataka state, India) is an Indian software entrepreneur who cofounded Infosys Technologies Ltd., the first Indian company to be listed on an American stock exchange. [...] becoming the first Indian company to be listed on an American stock exchange. The following year Asiaweek included Murthy in its Power 50, the magazine’s annual list of the most powerful people in the region. In addition, BusinessWeek named him one of its “Stars of Asia” for three consecutive years (1998–2000), and he was Fortune magazine’s 2003 Asian Businessman of the Year. [...] Entertainment & Pop Culture\n Literature\n Sports & Recreation\n Visual Arts\n\nImage Galleries\nPodcasts\nSummaries\nTop Questions\nBritannica Kids\n\nBritannica Money\n\nRead More\n\nAzim Premji\n\nAzim Premji\nBill Gates smiling and wearing glasses, a dark suit, a pale shirt, and a patterned tie.\n\nBill Gates\nMukesh Ambani\n\nMukesh Ambani\n\n# Narayana Murthy\n\nIndian businessman\n\nWritten by\n\nSherman Hollar\n\nSherman Hollar\n\nSherman Hollar is a senior editor at Encyclopædia Britannica.\n\nFact-checked by\n\n[S24] N R Narayana Murthy at 80: A life that helped shape India's IT industry\nURL: https://www.exchange4media.com/media-others-news/n-r-narayana-murthy-at-80-a-life-that-helped-shape-indias-it-industry-157502.html\nN R Narayana Murthy, born on August 20, 1946, in Karnataka, is celebrated as the father of India's IT services industry, marking his 80th birthday today.\n He co-founded Infosys in 1981 with a seed investment of ₹10,000, which grew into a global technology leader and the first Indian company to list on NASDAQ in 1999.\n Murthy is recognized for promoting transparency and ethical governance in business, stepping down as executive chairman in 2006 in adherence to Infosys's retirement policy. [...] N R Narayana Murthy, the man widely regarded as the father of India's IT services industry, turns 80 today. Born on August 20, 1946, in Sidlaghatta, Karnataka, into a modest, education-focused family, Murthy's journey from a government school in Mysuru to becoming one of the most respected business leaders in the world remains one of Indian industry's most enduring stories. [...] e4m Staff\n\n# N R Narayana Murthy at 80: A life that helped shape India's IT industry\n\n## As the Co-Founder of Infosys marks eight decades, a look back at the quiet revolution he built out of ₹10,000 and an unshakeable belief in Indian talent\n\ne4m by   e4m Staff     \n Published: Aug 20, 2026 1:29 PM  | 2 min read\n\nGoogle News Icon Follow Us\n\nN R Narayana Murthy\n\n e4m Twitter",{"json":true,"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"claims":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"citedUrl":{"type":"string"},"supportingUrls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["text","citedUrl","supportingUrls"]}},"entitiesLearned":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"},"facts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fact":{"type":"string"},"sourceUrl":{"type":"string"}},"required":["fact","sourceUrl"]}}},"required":["name","type","facts"]}},"unableToFind":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["answer","claims","entitiesLearned","unableToFind"]}}]}
