{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:40:13.714Z","session":"5119a7f0-0a98-4e22-b9e3-5f5265af0c19","event":"tool.end","callId":"3bbcef07-550e-4f3c-8e63-c7b7ebd3e943","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":1358,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] Print/export\n\n Download as PDF\n Printable version\n\nIn other projects\n\n Wikimedia Commons\n Wikidata item\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian businessman, current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n\n| Born | (1964-06-05) 5 June 1964 (age 62) |\n| Education | IIT Bombay (BTech) Cornell University (MS) |\n| Occupations | CEO & MD of Infosys |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh | [...] Parekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others. He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[edit]","score":0.96960473},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/salil-parekh","content":"### CEO, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys Limited, one of India’s leading global IT services companies. Parekh graduated with a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Bombay in 1986. He then pursued higher studies at Cornell University, earning Master of Engineering degrees in both Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering in 1988. [...] In May 2022, Parekh was reappointed as CEO and Managing Director for a five-year term ending March 2027, reflecting the board’s confidence in his leadership abilities. Parekh has received several awards as a leading CEO in the technology sector. He is a member of The Business Council, where he contributes his expertise to business leadership discussions. His strategic vision have earned him recognition as one of the prominent figures in the global IT services industry. Parekh’s vision for the [...] Before joining Infosys, Parekh had a distinguished 25-year career at Capgemini, where he held several key leadership positions. He began his career at Ernst & Young in 1992 when the consultancy arm later merged with Capgemini. During his tenure at Capgemini, he served as a member of the group management board and held leadership roles in Cloud Infrastructure Services and various business clusters, including Application Services. Since taking the helm at Infosys in 2018, Parekh has led the","score":0.93309647},{"title":"Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay","url":"https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh","content":"Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988. [...] Mr. Parekh has been the CEO of Infosys since January 2018 and has helped strategize the company’s focus on digital transformation and cloud services, and driven its execution. Mr. Parekh works with several client leaders directly to help them put in place and execute their digital transformation programmes. Examples include a leading global automotive company, a leading mutual fund company, and a leading telecommunication company, amongst others. Over the years, he has helped build, grow, and [...] Prior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.”","score":0.92074},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html","content":"+ Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018. [...] Salil has helped transform Infosys into a leading digital, cloud, and AI company. Salil helps set the strategy and nurture a leadership team to drive its execution. Infosys is in the top decile of shareholder return during his tenure, leading in client satisfaction results, and leading in employee engagement scores.\n\nSalil has a strong track record of driving transformations, executing business turnarounds, and managing successful acquisitions. [...] Prior to Infosys, Salil was a member of the management board at Capgemini and a partner at consulting practice Ernst & Young LLP prior to its acquisition by Capgemini. He had different leadership roles there across US, UK, Europe, Asia, over a span of 25 years.\n\nSalil has received several awards as a leading CEO.","score":0.8997663},{"title":"Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...","url":"https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors","content":"Home\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] Based in India, Parekh brings over three decades of experience in the global IT services industry. Parekh holds a Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay. [...] “We are very fortunate to have someone of Salil’s caliber as one of our board of directors,” said John Bourdeaux, President and CEO of AdvanceCT. “He is an experienced global business leader who will be able to provide valuable guidance and counsel to our organization and to Connecticut. I am also happy to report that Salil knows Connecticut and cares deeply about what we do. He lived in Westport and, so he has first-hand knowledge of what our state has to offer.”","score":0.8752871}]}
