{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:40:27.633Z","session":"690c1958-498c-4c54-adff-1d9cbab4a284","event":"tool.end","callId":"d2cc8458-3086-4793-909c-e57c0c7aff2a","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2389,"result":[{"title":"N. R. Narayana Murthy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N._R._Narayana_Murthy","content":"|  v  t  e |\n\n| People (list) | |  |  |  --- | | Founders |  N. R. Narayana Murthy  Nandan Nilekani  N. S. Raghavan  S. Gopalakrishnan  S. D. Shibulal  K. Dinesh  Ashok Arora | | Board of directors |  Salil Parekh (CEO & MD)  U. B. Pravin Rao (COO)  Carol M. Browner  John Etchemendy  Jeffrey S. Lehman  Kiran Mazumdar-Shaw  Ravi Venkatesan | |\n| Divisions |  Infosys BPM  Infosys Consulting  EdgeVerve Systems |\n| Products |  Finacle  Panaya |\n| Other |  Infosys Foundation  Infosys Prize | [...] In this Indian name, the name Nagavara Ramarao is a patronymic, and the person should be referred to by the given name, Narayana Murthy.\n\nNagavara Ramarao Narayana Murthy (born 20 August 1946) is an Indian billionaire businessman. He is the founder of Infosys, and was the chairman, chief executive officer (CEO), president and chief mentor of the company before retiring and becoming chairman emeritus. As of January 2025, his net worth was estimated at US$5.0 billion, according to Forbes. [...] Murthy mentions that being arrested and expelled for no good reason during the communist era 1974 in a border town near the Yugoslav-Bulgarian border, turned him into a \"compassionate capitalist\" from a \"confused leftist/communist\". In 1981 he, with six software professionals, founded Infosys with an initial capital investment of Rs 10,000, which was provided by his wife Sudha Murty. Murthy was the CEO of Infosys for 21 years from 1981 to 2002 and was succeeded by co-founder Nandan Nilekani. At","score":0.8266142},{"title":"N.R. Narayana Murthy: Founder | Management Profiles","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/narayana-murthy.html","content":"# N.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nFounder\n\nN.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nMr. Murthy founded Infosys in 1981. Infosys is, today, a highly innovative software services global\ncompany listed on NYSE in the US and on the Bombay Stock Exchange in Mumbai. [...] Under Mr. Murthy’s leadership, Infosys became the leader in innovation - in technical, managerial and\nleadership training, software technology, quality, productivity, customer focus, employee\nsatisfaction, and physical and technological infrastructure. [...] ##### Chat\n\nChat Expand Icon\n\n## Recent\n\nSearch AI icon\n\n##### Ask Leon\n\nSpecial characters are not allowed. Maximum length: 1000 characters.\n\nContent is generated with AI\nassistance\n\nSearch with voice\n\n## Navigate your next\n\nUnlock AI Value\n\nKnow\nMore\n\nTales\nof\ntransformation\n\nKnow\nMore\n\n## Industries\n\n## Services\n\n### Insights\n\n### Innovate\n\n### Assure\n\n### Accelerate\n\n### Experience\n\n### Platforms\n\n### Infosys Knowledge Institute\n\n### Learn\n\n### About Us\n\n### Flagship Brand Partnerships","score":0.818055},{"title":"Infosys - Nandan M. Nilekani: Co-founder and Chairman of the Board | Management Profiles","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/nandan-nilekani.html","content":"Nandan Nilekani is the Co-Founder and Chairman of Infosys Limited. He was the Founding Chairman of the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) in the rank of a Cabinet Minister from 2009-2014. Nandan has co-founded and is the Chairman of EkStep Foundation, a not-for-profit effort to create a learner centric, technology-based platform to improve basic literacy and numeracy for millions of children. In January 2023, he was appointed as the co-chair of the “G20 Task Force on Digital [...] ### Experience\n\n  + Infosys Aster\n  + Digital Marketing\n  + Digital Commerce\n  + Digital Interactions\n  + Digital Workplace Services\n  + Digital Experience\n  + Infosys Metaverse Foundry\n\n  + Application Development and Maintenance\n  + Business Process Management\n  + Consulting Services\n  + Incubating Emerging Offerings\n ### Platforms\n\n  + EdgeVerve\n  + Infosys Finacle\n  + Infosys Live Enterprise Suite\n  + Infosys Cortex\n  + Infosys Meridian [...] + Healthcare\n  + High Technology\n  + Industrial Manufacturing\n  + Information Services & Publishing\n  + Insurance\n  + Life Sciences\n  + Logistics & Distribution\n  + Media and Entertainment\n  + Mining\n  + Retail\n  + Semiconductor\n  + Travel and Hospitality\n  + Utilities\n  + Waste Management\n ## Services\n\n  ### Insights\n\n  + Infosys Topaz\n  + Applied AI\n  + Infosys Generative AI\n  + Infosys Sustainability Services\n\n  ### Innovate","score":0.70871735},{"title":"Infosys Foundation | Our Trustees - List and Profiles","url":"https://www.infosys.com/infosys-foundation/about/trustees.html","content":"Sumit is Executive Chairman of Edgeverve, a wholly owned subsidiary of Infosys that accelerates enterprise transformation with digital platforms. Additionally, he serves on the Board of WongDoody – Infosys’ experience design company. Forbes has ranked Sumit among the top 50 most influential chief marketing officers globally for three consecutive years, most recently in 2025. CNBC Storyboard 18 also recognised him as a global marketing visionary in 2024.\n\nSunil Kumar Dhareshwar [...] Infosys Foundation\n\n# About Us\n\n## \n\n### Trustees\n\nSalil Parekh\n\n##### Salil Parekh\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chairman of Infosys Foundation. [...] Shaji has over 31 years of experience in Infosys. Prior to his current role, he was Infosys’ global head of delivery for Financial Services, Insurance, Healthcare and Life Sciences. Over the years, he has played various leadership roles in delivery, as also in managing client relationships, commercials, solutioning, and people management across the US, Europe, and Asia Pacific. He has been actively steering the company’s efforts to create a more inclusive and diverse workforce. He is also a","score":0.683948},{"