2, 2018 and will continue as Chief Operating Officer and a whole-time Director of the Company.\n\nAbout Infosys [...] Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation\n\n# Infosys Appoints Salil S. Parekh as CEO and Managing Director\n\n- India - English\n\nInfosys Logo (PRNewsfoto/Infosys)\")\n\n## News provided by\n\n Infosys \n\nDec 02, 2017, 05:45 ET\n\n## Share this article\n\nShare toX\n\nShare this article\n\nShare toX\n\nBANGALORE, India, December 2, 2017 /PRNewswire/ --\n\n[S2] Infosys appoints Capgemini's Salil Parekh as MD & CEO\nURL: https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/infosys-appoints-capgeminis-salil-parekh-as-md-ceo/articleshow/61893756.cms\nBENGALURU: Infosys has appointed Salil Parekh chief executive officer (CEO) and managing director (MD) of the company with effect from January 2 next year, culminating the search of a CEO which began since the departure of Vishal Sikka in August due to a spat with the founders over various issues. [...] Infosys appoints Capgemini’s Salil Parekh as MD and CEO\n\nInfosys' newly appointed MD & CEO Salil Parekh (Image Source: Twitter)\n\nKey Highlights\n\n Infosys has appointed Salil Parekh MD & CEO of the company with effect from January 2\n He joins from French IT and consulting company Capgemini where he is the CEO of financial services across Europe\n Infosys will hope that Parekh’s background in financial services gets them to garner more deals [...] As part of the appointment, interim CEO and MD Pravin Rao, a company veteran, will step down from his role but continue as the chief operating officer and a whole time director till August 2022 “The board is also grateful to Pravin for his leadership during this period of transition,” Nilekani added.\n\n[S3] Salil Parekh\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh\nSalil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit] [...] Parekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others. He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[edit] [...] 4. ↑ \"A Gujarati appointed as CEO and MD of Infosys\". DeshGujarat. 2 December 2017. Retrieved 14 July 2025.\n5. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". mint. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n6. ↑ Shivapriya, N. \"Salil Parekh: The man who played a pivotal role in building Capgemini's India operations\". The Economic Times. Retrieved 20 April 2021.\n7. ↑ D'Monte, Leslie (31 March 2015). \"Capgemini names Salil Parekh deputy CEO\". LiveMint. Retrieved 3 January 2018.\n\n[S4] Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as ...\nURL: https://indianewengland.com/infosys-names-ashiss-kumar-dash-ceo-designate-as-salil-parekh-prepares-to-step-down\nINDIA New England News\n\n Search for\n\nBusiness\n\n# Infosys Names Ashiss Kumar Dash CEO-Designate as Salil Parekh Prepares to Step Down\n\nJuly 23, 2026\n\n1,138  1 minute read\n\nFacebook   X   LinkedIn   Tumblr   Pinterest   Reddit   VKontakte   Odnoklassniki   Pocket\n\n\n\nBengaluru–Infosys announced Thursday that CEO and Managing Director Salil Parekh will step down after nine years at the helm, with Ashiss Kumar Dash appointed as his successor. [...] Parekh will leave the role effective April 1, 2027, following the completion of his second term. He joined Infosys in January 2018 and is the longest-serving non-founder CEO in the company’s history.\n\nDash will become CEO and Managing Director on April 1, 2027, subject to the completion of statutory requirements, Infosys said in a regulatory filing. [...] Nilekani also praised Parekh for strengthening Infosys during his tenure.\n\n“On behalf of the Board, I also thank Salil for his outstanding leadership over 9 years. Under his stewardship, Infosys has strengthened its market position, expanded its capabilities, delivered significant value to shareholders, and built a strong platform for future growth,” he said.\n\nParekh’s current five-year term is scheduled to end March 31, 2027, allowing Dash to take over the following day. (Source: IANS)\n\n[S5] Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of ...\nURL: https://www.advancect.org/news-and-media/p/item/57410/infosys-ceo-salil-parekh-joins-advancects-board-of-directors\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Salil Parekh: Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys\n\nHome\n\nLatest News.png)\n\n# Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh, Joins AdvanceCT's Board of Directors\n\n8 May 2024\n\n  \n\nPress Release, News\n\nNew Haven, Connecticut, May 8, 2024 – Today, AdvanceCT announced that Salil Parekh, the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, will be joining our Board of Directors. [...] ## More Topics\n\n### TTM TECHNOLOGIES EXPANDS WORKFORCE IN CONNECTICUT\n\nMay 6 2024\n\nStafford, Connecticut, May 6, 2024 – AdvanceCT today announced that TTM Technologies Inc. (TTM), a global manufacturer of technology solutions including radio frequency (“RF”) components, RF microwave/microelectronic assemblies, and advanced printed circuit boards (“PCBs”), is expanding its workforce in its two Stafford locations.TTM was looking to invest in modernization and...Continue Reading [...] Apr 23 2024 \n\nConnecticut was a top 10 destination for remote workers who relocated in 2022, according to a new study.Yardi Kube, a coworking management platform, released the results of its study in February in a report titled, “Remote Workers Leading the Migration Across State Lines.”The study, which is based on data from...Continue Reading\n\n## Contact Us\n\nBen Dwyer headshot\n\nBen Dwyer  \nDirector, Marketing\n\n[S6] N. R. Narayana Murthy\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N._R._Narayana_Murthy\n|  v  t  e |\n\n| People (list) | |  |  |  --- | | Founders |  N. R. Narayana Murthy  Nandan Nilekani  N. S. Raghavan  S. Gopalakrishnan  S. D. Shibulal  K. Dinesh  Ashok Arora | | Board of directors |  Salil Parekh (CEO & MD)  U. B. Pravin Rao (COO)  Carol M. Browner  John Etchemendy  Jeffrey S. Lehman  Kiran Mazumdar-Shaw  Ravi Venkatesan | |\n| Divisions |  Infosys BPM  Infosys Consulting  EdgeVerve Systems |\n| Products |  Finacle  Panaya |\n| Other |  Infosys Foundation  Infosys Prize | [...] In this Indian name, the name Nagavara Ramarao is a patronymic, and the person should be referred to by the given name, Narayana Murthy.\n\nNagavara Ramarao Narayana Murthy (born 20 August 1946) is an Indian billionaire businessman. He is the founder of Infosys, and was the chairman, chief executive officer (CEO), president and chief mentor of the company before retiring and becoming chairman emeritus. As of January 2025, his net worth was estimated at US$5.0 billion, according to Forbes. [...] Murthy mentions that being arrested and expelled for no good reason during the communist era 1974 in a border town near the Yugoslav-Bulgarian border, turned him into a \"compassionate capitalist\" from a \"confused leftist/communist\". In 1981 he, with six software professionals, founded Infosys with an initial capital investment of Rs 10,000, which was provided by his wife Sudha Murty. Murthy was the CEO of Infosys for 21 years from 1981 to 2002 and was succeeded by co-founder Nandan Nilekani. At\n\n[S7] N.R. Narayana Murthy: Founder | Management Profiles\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/narayana-murthy.html\n# N.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nFounder\n\nN.R. Narayana Murthy\n\nMr. Murthy founded Infosys in 1981. Infosys is, today, a highly innovative software services global\ncompany listed on NYSE in the US and on the Bombay Stock Exchange in Mumbai. [...] Under Mr. Murthy’s leadership, Infosys became the leader in innovation - in technical, managerial and\nleadership training, software technology, quality, productivity, customer focus, employee\nsatisfaction, and physical and technological infrastructure. [...] ##### Chat\n\nChat Expand Icon\n\n## Recent\n\nSearch AI icon\n\n##### Ask Leon\n\nSpecial characters are not allowed. Maximum length: 1000 characters.\n\nContent is generated with AI\nassistance\n\nSearch with voice\n\n## Navigate your next\n\nUnlock AI Value\n\nKnow\nMore\n\nTales\nof\ntransformation\n\nKnow\nMore\n\n## Industries\n\n## Services\n\n### Insights\n\n### Innovate\n\n### Assure\n\n### Accelerate\n\n### Experience\n\n### Platforms\n\n### Infosys Knowledge Institute\n\n### Learn\n\n### About Us\n\n### Flagship Brand Partnerships\n\n[S8] Infosys - Nandan M. Nilekani: Co-founder and Chairman of the Board | Management Profiles\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/nandan-nilekani.html\nNandan Nilekani is the Co-Founder and Chairman of Infosys Limited. He was the Founding Chairman of the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) in the rank of a Cabinet Minister from 2009-2014. Nandan has co-founded and is the Chairman of EkStep Foundation, a not-for-profit effort to create a learner centric, technology-based platform to improve basic literacy and numeracy for millions of children. In January 2023, he was appointed as the co-chair of the “G20 Task Force on Digital [...] ### Experience\n\n  + Infosys Aster\n  + Digital Marketing\n  + Digital Commerce\n  + Digital Interactions\n  + Digital Workplace Services\n  + Digital Experience\n  + Infosys Metaverse Foundry\n\n  + Application Development and Maintenance\n  + Business Process Management\n  + Consulting Services\n  + Incubating Emerging Offerings