ipedia.org/wiki/N._R._Narayana_Murthy\nSOURCE PAGE (excerpt; […] marks omitted text):\n\"\"\"\n[Jump to content](#bodyContent)\n\n[![](/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg)  ![Wikipedia](/static/images/mobile/copyright/wikipedia-wordmark-en-25.svg) ![The Free Encyclopedia](/static/images/mobile/copyright/wikipedia-tagline-en-25.svg)](/wiki/Main_Page)\n\n[Search](/wiki/Special:Search \"Search Wikipedia [f]\")\n\n## Contents\n\n* [1 Early life and education](#Early_life_and_education)\n* [2 Career](#Career)\n* [3 Views on working hours](#Views_on_working_hours)\n* [4 Personal life](#Personal_life)\n* [5 Awards and honours](#Awards_and_honours)\n* [6 Bibliography](#Bibliography)\n* [7 References](#References)\n* [8 Further reading](#Further_reading)\n* [9 External links](#External_links)\n\n# N. R. Narayana Murthy\n\n* [العربية](https://ar.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D8%A5%D9%86_%D8%A2%D8%B1_%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%86%D8%A7_%D9%85%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AB%D9%8A \"إن آر نارايانا مورثي – Arabic\")\n* [مصرى](https://arz.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D8%A7%D9%86._%D8%A2%D8%B1._%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%86%D8%A7_%D9%85%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AB%D9%89 \"ان. آر. نارايانا مورثى – Egyptian Arabic\")\n* [অসমীয়া](https://as.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%97%E0%A6%BE%E0%A7%B1%E0%A7%B0%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A7%B0%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%AE%E0%A6%BE%E0%A7%B0%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%93_%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BE%E0%A7%B0%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%BC%E0%A6%A3_%E0%A6%AE%E0%A7%82%E0%A7%B0%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BF \"নাগাৱৰা ৰামাৰাও নাৰায়ণ মূৰ্তি – Assamese\")\n* [বাংলা](https://bn.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%A6%8F%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A6%86%E0%A6%B0_%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%BC%E0%A6%A3_%E0%A6%AE%E0%A7%82%E0%A6%B0%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BF \"এন আর নারায়ণ মূর্তি – Bangla\")\n* [Deutsch](https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/N._R._Narayana_Murthy \"N. R. Narayana Murthy – German\")\n* [فارسی](https://fa.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%B1%D8%A7%DB%8C%D8%A7%D9%86%D8%A7_%D9%85%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AA%DB%8C \"نارایانا مورتی – Persian\")\n* [עברית](https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%A0%D7%A8%D7%90%D7%99%D7%A0%D7%94_%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%A8%D7%98%D7%99 \"נ\n[…]\n Wikidata [g]\")\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian businessman (born 1946)\n\n\"Narayana Murthy\" redirects here. For the actor, director and producer of Telugu films, see [R. Narayana Murthy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R._Narayana_Murthy \"R. Narayana Murthy\").\n\n| N. R. Narayana Murthy |\n| --- |\n| Murthy in 2014 |\n| Born | Nagavara Ramarao Narayana Murthy   (1946-08-20) 20 August 1946 (age 80)[[1]](#cite_note-DOB-1)  [Sidlaghatta](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sidlaghatta \"Sidlaghatta\"), [Kingdom of Mysore](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mysore \"Kingdom of Mysore\"), [British India](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Raj \"British Raj\") (present-day [Karnataka](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karnataka \"Karnataka\"), India) |\n| Education | [National Institute of Engineering](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Institute_of_Engineering \"National Institute of Engineering\"), Mysuru ([BE](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B.E. \"B.E.\")) [IIT Kanpur](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IIT_Kanpur \"IIT Kanpur\") ([MTech](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M.Tech. \"M.Tech.\")) |\n| Known for | Founder and Chairman Emeritus of [Infosys](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infosys \"Infosys\")[[2]](#cite_note-2) |\n| Board member of | [United Nations Foundation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Foundation \"United Nations Foundation\")[[3]](#cite_note-3)  [Ford Foundation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Foundation \"Ford Foundation\")[[4]](#cite_note-4) |\n| Spouse | \n[…]\n Infosys for 21 years from 1981 to 2002[[29]](#cite_note-studyrays-29) and was succeeded by co-founder [Nandan Nilekani](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nandan_Nilekani \"Nandan Nilekani\").[[31]](#cite_note-yentha-31) At Infosys he articulated, designed and implemented a global delivery model for IT services outsourcing from India.[[32]](#cite_note-32) He was the chairman of the board from 2002 to 2006, after which he also became the chief mentor.[[31]](#cite_note-yentha-31)[[33]](#cite_note-33) In August 2011, he retired from the company, taking the title chairman emeritus.[[9]](#cite_note-auto1-9)[[10]](#cite_note-auto-10)\n\n[![](//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/The_Founder%2C_Infosys%2C_Shri_N.R._Narayana_Murthy_calling_on_the_Prime_Minister%2C_Shri_Narendra_Modi%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_December_05%2C_2014.jpg/250px-The_Founder%2C_Infosys%2C_Shri_N.R._Narayana_Murthy_calling_on_the_Prime_Minister%2C_Shri_Narendra_Modi%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_December_05%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:The_Founder,_Infosys,_Shri_N.R._Narayana_Murthy_calling_on_the_Prime_Minister,_Shri_Narendra_Modi,_in_New_Delhi_on_December_05,_2014.jpg)\n\nMurthy with [Narendra Modi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narendra_Modi \"Narendra Modi\") in 2014\n\nMurthy is an independent director on the corporate board of [HSBC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HSBC \"HSBC\") and has been a director on the boards of [DBS Bank](https:/\n[…]\n 1 January 2026. Retrieved 22 January 2026.\n6. [↑](#cite_ref-6) [\"Infosys – Founders of the Company | Management Profiles\"](https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/founders.html). [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20221026110612/https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/founders.html) from the original on 26 October 2022. Retrieved 13 April 2021.\n7. [↑](#cite_ref-7) [\"Murthy to continue as Chief Mentor of Infosys\"](https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/software/murthy-to-continue-as-chief-mentor-of-infosys/articleshow/1736087.cms?from=mdr). [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20221026050717/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/software/murthy-to-continue-as-chief-mentor-of-infosys/articleshow/1736087.cms?from=mdr) from the original on 2