{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:50:36.976Z","session":"4887d3e1-4b42-479b-9fff-0e35560bb652","event":"tool.end","callId":"5137f5a2-521d-44d7-a7c4-6b4fd5da75bc","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2475,"result":[{"title":"K Krithivasan - Indiaspora","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/k-krithivasan","content":"K. Krithivasan (also known as Krithi) is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Tata Consultancy Services (TCS), one of the world’s largest IT services companies. He became the CEO and MD of TCS on June 1, 2023. Krithivasan completed his BTech in Mechanical Engineering from Coimbatore Institute of Technology, under University of Madras, in 1985. Thereafter he pursued Master’s Degree in Industrial and Management Engineering from IIT Kanpur. He graduated from IIT in 1987. [...] Krithivasan has been part of the global technology sector for over 34 years, having joined Tata Consultancy Services in 1989. During his long tenure at TCS, he has held various leadership roles in delivery, customer relationship management, large program management and sales. With more than three decades of experience at TCS, Krithivasan has played a crucial role in digital transformation initiatives, especially within the Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance (BFSI) sectors. [...] He has successfully driven innovation within the company, which employs over 600,000 people across 50 countries. He is recognized as a skilled business strategist with a strong passion for fitness and reading. His extensive experience and strategic vision are credited with propelling TCS’s global expansion. TCS’s success under his direction suggests a focus on data-driven decision making, customer focus, and fostering a strong company culture. Looking to the future, Krithivasan aims to maintain","score":0.86954874},{"title":"K Krithivasan","url":"https://www.tcs.com/who-we-are/leadership/k-krithivasan","content":"K. Krithivasan, also known as Krithi, took over as the CEO & MD of Tata Consultancy Services on June 1, 2023. In his three-decade plus tenure at TCS, he has held various leadership roles in delivery, customer relationship management, large program management and sales and has a strong track record of successfully leading TCS’ largest industry vertical, the Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance business. [...] TCS’ expansion into high-growth markets such as Latin America, Australia and New Zealand. Born in Trichy, Tamil Nadu, Krithi received a bachelor’s degree in mechanical engineering from the University of Madras and a master’s degree in industrial and management engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT), Kanpur. He is a proud father of two daughters and attributes his success to his family. [...] Krithi joined Tata Consultancy Services in 1989 as an assistant system analyst in New Delhi. He moved to North America in 1997, where he was soon promoted to Regional Manager for TCS Florida. In the year 2000, Krithi took over as the e-business delivery head and was promoted in 2004 to head the BFSI Solution Centre. From 2018, he led the unit to achieve double-digit growth driven by strong momentum in all major markets. In his role as the head of the BFSI vertical, Krithi steered TCS’ expansion","score":0.75831425},{"title":"Mr K Krithivasan | IIT Kanpur","url":"https://iitk.ac.in/dora/profile/mr-k-krithivasan","content":"Mr. K. Krithivasan, also known as Krithi, became the CEO and MD of Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) on June 1, 2023. With over three decades of experience in the technology industry, Mr. Krithi has positioned TCS as a leader in the rapidly evolving tech landscape. Under his leadership, TCS gained $2 billion in brand value in 2024, making it the second most valuable IT services brand globally. Mr. Krithi emphasizes customer centricity and employee empathy, and his efforts have been pivotal in TCS [...] Mr. K. Krithivasan, also known as Krithi, became the CEO and MD of Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) on June 1, 2023. With over three decades of experience in the technology industry, Mr. Krithi has positioned TCS as a leader in the rapidly evolving tech landscape. Under his leadership, TCS gained $2 billion in brand value in 2024, making it the second most valuable IT services brand globally. Mr. Krithi emphasizes customer centricity and employee empathy, and his efforts have been pivotal in TCS [...] Born in Trichy, Tamil Nadu, Mr. Krithi holds a bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering from the University of Madras and a master's degree in Industrial and Management Engineering from IIT Kanpur.   \n  \nHonoring his stellar contributions in the field of Technology Leadership, and Emerging Business, IIT Kanpur confers upon Mr. K. Krithivasan the Distinguished Alumnus Award 2024.","score":0.7311551},{"title":"In Conversation with K Krithivasan | Tata group","url":"https://www.tata.com/newsroom/business/krithivasan-tcs-perpetually-adaptive","content":"K Krithivasan, Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, TCS, discusses among other things, the company's long-term vision, its trademark resilience, being perpetually adaptive - and how his role at TCS has tranformed his leadership outlook. Excerpts:\n\nThis is a time of great global disruptions — both technological and geopolitical. What makes TCS resilient even in the face of such turbulence? [...] The CEO and Managing Director of Tata Consultancy Services elaborates on the company's long-term vision, its resilience, and the path ahead.\n\n#### November 2025     |     2064 words     |     9-minute read\n\nShare Share Share Share\n\nCopy link Copy link Copy link Copy Link [...] \"Personally, my journey has reinforced my belief in purpose-driven leadership, that technology must serve clients, societies, and the planet in equal measure.\"\n\nThese are just a few examples of how TCS balances business impact with societal value, using technology responsibly, inclusively, and for the greater good. That alignment between innovation and human progress is something we are deeply proud of.\n\nHow has leading TCS at this pivotal moment shaped you and your leadership approach?","score":0.67063034},{"title":"K Krithivasan","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/in/k-krithivasan-84659325","content":"# K Krithivasan\nTata Consultancy Services\nMumbai, Maharashtra, India, IN  \n500 connections, 150428 followers\n\n## About\nNone\n\n## Experience\nN/A\n\n## Education\n### Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur  \nN/A  \n1986 - 1987  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n1981 - 1985  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n1975 - 1981  \nNone\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nN/A\n\n## Certifications\nN/A\n\n## Volunteering\nN/A\n\n## Languages\nN/A\n\n## Organizations\nN/A [...] - It was a pleasure meeting Nick Bitel, CEO, London Marathon Group, along with my colleague Vinay Singhvi, Head, UK and Ireland, TCS, and…  \nShared by K Krithivasan  \nView Post  \nActivity Image\n\n- 𝐒𝐞𝐭𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐏𝐚𝐜𝐞 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐈𝐧𝐝𝐢𝐚’𝐬 𝐀𝐈 𝐅𝐮𝐭𝐮𝐫𝐞! We have partnered with TPG to strengthen our newly launched, GW-scale…  \nLiked by K Krithivasan  \nView Post  \nActivity Image [...] - Navin Gupta (Datamatics Global Services Limited) - \n- Geetanjali Khatri (GK) (Capgemini Invent) - \n- Arun Menon (Jade Global) - \n- Pinaki Bhattacharya (Engaged Media, LLC) - \n- Srimathi Shivashankar (HCL Technologies) - \n- Maj Deepak C Joshi (Retd.) (TPMGuru) - \n- Manish Israni (Olive Intelligence Pvt. Ltd.,) - \n- Tirthankar Mitra (Sigma-Byte Computers) -","score":0.43510985}]}
