 held various leadership roles in delivery, customer relationship management, large program management and sales and has a strong track record of successfully leading TCS’ largest industry vertical, the Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance business.\n\n## Executive Director – President and Chief Operating Officer","score":0.9006087},{"title":"K Krithivasan - Indiaspora","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/k-krithivasan","content":"K. Krithivasan (also known as Krithi) is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Tata Consultancy Services (TCS), one of the world’s largest IT services companies. He became the CEO and MD of TCS on June 1, 2023. Krithivasan completed his BTech in Mechanical Engineering from Coimbatore Institute of Technology, under University of Madras, in 1985. Thereafter he pursued Master’s Degree in Industrial and Management Engineering from IIT Kanpur. He graduated from IIT in 1987. [...] K Krithivasan\n\n# K Krithivasan\n\n### Managing Director & CEO, Tata Consultancy Services\n\n Residence: Maharashtra\n HQ: India\n Net Income: $5.67 B\n Revenue: $29.76 B\n Market Cap: $144.8 B\n\n# K Krithivasan\n\n### Managing Director & CEO, Tata Consultancy Services [...] He has successfully driven innovation within the company, which employs over 600,000 people across 50 countries. He is recognized as a skilled business strategist with a strong passion for fitness and reading. His extensive experience and strategic vision are credited with propelling TCS’s global expansion. TCS’s success under his direction suggests a focus on data-driven decision making, customer focus, and fostering a strong company culture. Looking to the future, Krithivasan aims to maintain","score":0.8989177},{"title":"Mr K Krithivasan | IIT Kanpur","url":"https://iitk.ac.in/dora/profile/mr-k-krithivasan","content":"Mr. K. Krithivasan, also known as Krithi, became the CEO and MD of Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) on June 1, 2023. With over three decades of experience in the technology industry, Mr. Krithi has positioned TCS as a leader in the rapidly evolving tech landscape. Under his leadership, TCS gained $2 billion in brand value in 2024, making it the second most valuable IT services brand globally. Mr. Krithi emphasizes customer centricity and employee empathy, and his efforts have been pivotal in TCS [...] Mr. K. Krithivasan, also known as Krithi, became the CEO and MD of Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) on June 1, 2023. With over three decades of experience in the technology industry, Mr. Krithi has positioned TCS as a leader in the rapidly evolving tech landscape. Under his leadership, TCS gained $2 billion in brand value in 2024, making it the second most valuable IT services brand globally. Mr. Krithi emphasizes customer centricity and employee empathy, and his efforts have been pivotal in TCS","score":0.8976328}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:50:37.127Z","session":"4887d3e1-4b42-479b-9fff-0e35560bb652","event":"tool.end","callId":"4a51c586-3af1-4661-89f5-3528a1942eec","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2629,"result":[{"title":"TCS paid CEO K Krithivasan Rs 26.5 crore in FY25 - The Economic Times","url":"https://m.economictimes.com/tech/information-tech/tcs-paid-ceo-k-krithivasan-rs-26-5-crore-in-fy25/articleshow/121460506.cms","content":"Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) chief K. Krithivasan’s total compensation increased 4.6% to Rs 26.5 crore in financial year 2025, according to the company’s latest annual report released Wednesday. [...] Krithivasan who assumed the role of chief executive and managing director at TCS in 2023, saw his total pay package increase from Rs 25.45 crore a year earlier. In FY25, his total compensation constituted a base salary of Rs 1.40 crore, benefits and allowances of Rs 2.13 crore and a commission of Rs 23 crore. His pay ratio to the median remuneration of employees is 329.8, data showed. [...] ET reported on May 15 that Infosys released performance bonus letters for eligible employees for the January-March (Q4FY2024-25) quarter. Much of the workforce saw the payout as being significantly lower than the previous one, employees told ET.  \n  \nIn April, Infosys had reported an 11.7% year-on-year fall in net profit to Rs 7,033 crore. The revenue guidance for the year 2025-26 was also in a low-single-digit range.  \n  \nHeadcount","score":0.8190992},{"title":"TCS CEO Krithivasan earned $3 mln in first year at top job | Reuters","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/india/tcs-ceo-krithivasan-earned-3-mln-first-year-top-job-2024-05-09","content":"BENGALURU, May 9 (Reuters) - Tata Consultancy Services (TCS.NS), India's top IT services firm, said its CEO K Krithivasan earned 253.59 million rupees ($3.04 million) in financial year 2024, making him likely the lowest-paid CEO among top the four Indian IT firms.","score":0.7872945},{"title":"Tata Consultancy Services"