 the Tata group. The Tata group comprises over 100 operating companies in seven business sectors: communications and information technology (IT), engineering, materials, services, energy, consumer products and chemicals. The group has operations in more than 100 countries on six continents. Its companies export products and services to 150 countries. Total revenue was $107 billion in 2014-15, with 67% coming from business outside India. Tata [...] outside India. Tata companies employ over 600,000 people worldwide. [...] # Tata Sons\n\n[S16] TATA SONS PRIVATE LIMITED - 2026 Company Profile & Financials - Tracxn\nURL: https://tracxn.com/d/legal-entities/india/tata-sons-private-limited/__vmyAZpz9CXmnZRwsJDnZxhZMKO1DZR5b_nS9yrJ3EEs\nTATA SONS PRIVATE LIMITED is a Private Limited Company and was incorporated on Nov 08, 1917 in India. It is registered at Registrar of Companies, ROC Mumbai I. Its registered address is BOMBAY HOUSE 24 HOMI MODY STREET, FORT, MUMBAI, Maharashtra, India, 400001.  Its corporate identification number is (CIN) U99999MH1917PTC000478 and its current status is Active. It has 4 GST numbers registered across 4 states. These include 07AAACT4060A2ZW in Delhi (active) and 20AAACT4060A1Z9 in Jharkhand [...] TATA SONS PRIVATE LIMITED's last Annual General Meeting (AGM) was held on Aug 14, 2025 as per records from Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA). TATA SONS PRIVATE LIMITED's authorised share capital is ₹5,800Cr and its paid up capital is ₹40.4Cr. The current board of directors of TATA SONS PRIVATE LIMITED comprises . Venu srinivasan, Chandrasekaran Natarajan and 4 more.\n\nTATA SONS PRIVATE LIMITED generated more than ₹1,000 Cr in revenue for the financial year ending on Mar 31, 2025. [...] | Logo for Tata Communications Tata Communications | Provider of managed WiFi, network cloud security interaction, and internet connectivity services | 1986 | India | Public |\n| Logo for Tata Group Tata Group | Diversified conglomerate operating across multiple industries | 1868 | India | Funding Raised |\n| Logo for Tata Nexarc Tata Nexarc | Online B2B marketplace offering digital products | 2020 | India | Unfunded |\n\n[S17] Tata Sons | Tata group\nURL: https://www.tata.com/business/tata-sons\nTata Sons is the principal investment holding company and promoter of Tata companies.\n\n66% of the equity share capital of Tata Sons is held by philanthropic trusts, which support education, health, livelihood generation, and art and culture.\n\nEach Tata company or enterprise operates independently under the guidance and supervision of its own Board of Directors.\n\n## Governance Philosophy [...] # The world looks best in a portrait mode. So does our website :) Please tilt and enjoy the experience.\n\nSearch Search\n\nplus plus Clear Category\n\nDate Range\n\nplus plus Clear Date Range\n\nSearch Results for Trending Tags\n\nClear all\n\nCard Result\n\nCookie whiteCookie \n\nWe use cookies \n\nto give you a better experience. By using our website you agree to our policies.\n\nbanner \n\nAbout us\n\n# Tata Sons\n\nTata Sons Private Limited is the principal holding company of the Tata group [...] Our Governance Philosophy is based on resilience. Globally, organisations are becoming vulnerable as businesses become complex, virtual and interdependent. It is imperative to build a sustainable and resilient enterprise.\n\nTata Sons’ relationship with the group operating companies is governed by:\n\nShareholding in the group companies: Tata Sons is the principal investment holding company and the promoter of its group operating companies.\n\n[S18] TATA SONS LIMITED\nURL: https://in.linkedin.com/company/tata-sons-limited\n# TATA SONS LIMITED\nN/A\nBusiness Consulting and Services • MUMBAI, Maharashtra • 21,716 followers • 51-200 employees\n\n## Overview\nTATA SONS LIMITED is a company based out of BOMBAY HOUSE 24 HOMI MODY STREET, MUMBAI, Maharashtra, India.\n\n### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\nN/A\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nBusiness Consulting and Services\n\n### Company Size\n51-200 employees  \n231 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed TATA SONS LIMITED as their current workplace on their profile) [...] Tata Group (Executive Offices):  (Mumbai, Maharashtra); Agratas – A Tata Enterprise (Renewable Energy Equipment Manufacturing):  (Bengaluru, Karnataka); Tata Trusts (Non-profit Organizations):  (Mumbai, Maharashtra); Tata Consultancy Services (IT Services and IT Consulting):  (Mumbai, Maharashtra); Tata Motors (Motor Vehicle Manufacturing):  (Pune, Maharashtra); TAS Official (Human Resources Services):  (Mumbai, Maharashtra); Goodfellows India (Services for the Elderly and Disabled):  (Mumbai,\n\n[S19] N. Chandrasekaran\nURL: https://www.tcs.com/who-we-are/leadership/n-chandrasekaran\n### \n\ntata.com logo\n\n##### Top Results\n\n# N. Chandrasekaran\n\nChairman (Non-Independent, Non-Executive)\n\nYou have these already downloaded\n\nWe have sent you a copy of the report to your email again.\n\nNatarajan Chandrasekaran (Chandra) is the Chairman of Tata Sons Private Limited (Tata Sons), the holding company and promoter of all Tata group companies. Chandra joined the Board of Tata Sons in October 2016 and was appointed as Chairman in January 2017. [...] He is an avid photographer and a passionate long-distance marathon runner. He is a Six Star Finisher of the World Marathon Majors and continues to champion fitness.\n\nBorn in 1963, Chandra is a Bachelor in Applied Sciences and has Masters in Computer Applications.\n\n## With you for the long run\n\nWhether you are a client, partner, investor, or employee, our promise is to be with you for the long run. Let’s take the first step together. [...] Chandra is on the International Advisory Council of Singapore’s Economic Development Board, Mitsubishi's International Advisory Committee and on the Board of Governors of New York Academy of Sciences. He is the Co-Chair of the India US CEO Forum.\n\n[S20] Tata Group Chairman N Chandrasekaran to step down in February\nURL: https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1512909pgpo\nBefore becoming chairman, Chandrasekaran was the CEO and managing director of the group's high-profile global IT service provider, Tata Consultancy Services. He joined the group in 1987 - a 2017 press release announcing his appointment as chairman described him as a \"Tata lifer\".\n\nAmbareesh Baliga, an independent market analyst, said that when a person with Chandrasekaran's stature stepped down like this, it was inevitable that the markets would react negatively. [...] # Tata Group Chairman N Chandrasekaran to step down in February\n\nGetty Images N Chandrasekaran, wearing a dark suit, white shirt and thick-rimmed glasses, touches his ear in this photo taken at the Bombay Stock Exchange in Mumbai, India, on November 12, 2025.\n\nN Chandrasekaran, the chairman of Tata Group, has said that he will not seek reappointment when his term ends in February. [...] When the proposal for his extension was brought before the board in February, one board member did not support it, Chandrasekaran said in his statement without naming the person.\n\n\"In the absence of unanimous support, I chose to defer the decision,\" he said, adding that there was no resolution even six months later.\n\n[S21] Natarajan Chandrasekaran - NYAS\nURL: https://www.nyas.org/person/natarajan-chandrasekaran\nChandra is an active member of India’s bilateral business forums including USA, UK, Australia and Japan. He served as the chairman of NASSCOM, the apex trade body for IT services firms in India in 2012-13.\n\nHis business leadership has been recognized by several corporate and community organizations, and he has received numerous awards, including: [...] ---\n\n \n  \n\nBio\n\n  \n \n\n# Natarajan Chandrasekaran\n\n### Life Governor\n\n### Chairman of the Board, Tata Sons\n\nNatarajan Chandrasekaran is Chairman of the Board of Tata Sons, the holding company and promoter of more than 100 Tata operating companies with aggregate annual revenues of more than US $100 billion. He joined the Board of Tata Sons in October 2016 and was appointed Chairman in January 2017. [...] Chandra has been awarded several honorary doctorates by leading universities in India and internationally. He attended the Regional Engineering College, Trichy, Tamil Nadu, where he completed a Master’s degree in Computer Applications before joining TCS in 1987.\n\nChandra is an avid photographer, and a passionate long-distance marathon runner.\n\nBorn in 1963, Chandra lives in Mumbai, with his wife Lalitha. They have a son, Pranav, who is currently pursuing undergraduate studies.\n\n[S22] Tata chair N Chandrasekaran’s exit leaves $120 billion spending ambition in limbo - The Economic Times\nURL: https://m.economictimes.com/news/company/corporate-trends/tata-chandrasekaran-exit-noel-tata-faces-120-billion-investment-test-tcs-air-india/articleshow/133196897.cms\nNatarajan Chandrasekaran’s decision to step down in February jeopardizes Tata Sons Pvt.’s $120 billion wager on future growth and brings an abrupt end to nearly a decade of leadership that helped push India into more advanced technologies. Some of the conglomerate’s current and planned projects could slow down, be scaled back or stretch out longer as it awaits new leadership, said people familiar with the matter who asked not to be identified as the details aren’t public [...] Comment\n\nSynopsis\n\nTata Group is facing a leadership and strategy reset after N Chandrasekaran’s decision to step down as Tata Sons chairman, putting the conglomerate’s planned $120 billion investment programme under scrutiny.\n\nListen to this article in summarized format\n\nLoading...\n\n×\n\n×\n\nSubscribe to ETPrime\n\nUnlock AI Briefing and Premium Content\n\nNew Year Offer 24 Hours Left\n\nSubscribe Now\n\nAlready a member? Sign In\n\n### What's Included [...] The project carries an unusual degree of oversight. The fab team is accountable not only to Tata’s leadership but also to the Indian government, one person involved in the project said.",{"json":true,"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"claims":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"citedUrl":{"type":"string"},"supportingUrls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["text","citedUrl","supportingUrls"]}},"entitiesLearned":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"},"facts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fact":{"type":"string"},"sourceUrl":{"type":"string"}},"required":["fact","sourceUrl"]}}},"required":["name","type","facts"]}},"unableToFind":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["answer","claims","entitiesLearned","unableToFind"]}}]}
