{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:56:46.706Z","session":"eea5bf65-e2dc-4a20-b9f2-ea75b0008065","event":"tool.end","callId":"b498e1df-1ec6-4c75-8e8d-405400be0679","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2496,"result":[{"title":"Nikhil Kamath - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikhil_Kamath","content":"Nikhil Kamath (born 5 September 1986) is an Indian entrepreneur and investor. He is the co-founder of Zerodha, a retail stockbroker, and True Beacon, an asset management company. As of December 2025( Kamath is worth $3.3 billion, according to Forbes. He, along with his brother Nithin, is also part of Forbes' list of India’s 100 Richest for 2024.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit source] [...] | Nikhil Kamath |\n\n| Kamath in 2023 |\n| Born | (1986-09-05) 5 September 1986 (age 39)  Shimoga, Karnataka, India |\n| Occupations |  Entrepreneur  Investor |\n| Organization(s) | Zerodha True Beacon Gruhas |\n| Spouse | Amanda Puravankara  ​   ​ (m. 2019; div. 2021)​  |\n| Relatives | Nithin Kamath (brother) | [...] In 2010, Kamath co-founded Zerodha along with his brother Nithin Kamath. Zerodha provides brokerage services for dealing in stocks, currencies, and commodities. Kamath introduced a discount brokerage model with Zerodha which reduces the commission charged for transactions.\n\nKamath also co-founded True Beacon in 2020, an asset management company that manages investments for ultra-high-net-worth individuals in Indian markets through privately pooled investment vehicles.","score":0.7197191},{"title":"Nithin Kamath (@Nithin0dha) / X","url":"https://x.com/Nithin0dha","content":"Log inSign up\n\nNithin Kamath\n\nNithin Kamath profile banner\n\n@Nithin0dha\n\n# Nithin Kamath\n\nFounder & CEO @Zerodha @Rainmatterin Learning at @RainmatterOrg Musings on business & life: nithinkamath.me. Views are personal, Nothing is advice.\n\nBengaluru\n\nzerodha.com\n\nJoined August 2013\n\n189\n\nFollowing1M\n\nFollowers\n\nRepliesRepliesRepostsRepostsMediaMediaArticlesArticles\n\n Pinned\n\n  @Nithin0dha\n\n  Nithin Kamath\n\n  @Nithin0dha\n\n  Aug 26 [...] Aug 26\n\n  Zerodha turned 16 this month. Sweet 16. Every year, I write a letter to all our customers about what’s happening in the business and how we are thinking about the future. The last couple of years have been mixed for brokers. We had to take revenue hits because of regulatory\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  108\n @Nithin0dha\n\n  Nithin Kamath\n\n  @Nithin0dha\n\n  17h [...] 23h\n\n  I just found out that a disloyal member on my team thinks @nikhilkamathcio is much more handsome than me, so I decided to change the photo on the website to just keep Nik under my name.\n\n  \n\n  @dineshpaii\n\n  Dinesh Pai\n\n  @dineshpaii\n\n  Aug 31\n\n  Replying to @anmolm\\_\n\n  Dont tell Nithin I said this, but Nikhil is better looking. Natural choice for these posts 😁\n\n  114\n @Nithin0dha\n\n  Nithin Kamath\n\n  @Nithin0dha\n\n  Aug 28","score":0.5855047},{"title":"Nithin Kamath | Substack","url":"https://nithinkamath.substack.com","content":"# Nithin Kamath\n\nFounder & CEO @Zerodhaonline @Rainmatterin Learnings at @RainmatterOrg Musings on business & life: \n\nOver 133,000 subscribers","score":0.57322514},{"title":"Nithin Kamath","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/in/nithin-kamath-81136242","content":"- Arindam Ghosh (Professional entrepreneur & senior leader in the BFSI segment in India and the Asia Pacific ranging from green fields/ start-ups to large global organizations across , Asset Management, Wealth Management and NBFCs. <br><br>- Currently building ALPHANITI - a Tech enabled & Big Data company with special focus across prominent asset classes in Investment and Finance Domain in India & US. <br><br>- Director on several Corporate Boards <br><br>-Previously, was associated with Mirae [...] # Nithin Kamath\nZerodha\nBengaluru, Karnataka, India, IN  \n500 connections, 1793972 followers\n\n## About\nOver a decade of trading the markets for a living<br><br> Felt the fatigue, and with Zerodha…\n\n## Experience\nN/A\n\n## Education\nN/A\n\n## Publications\nZerodha in news\nN/A • Published on N/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nStartup of the year (Bootstrap) - 2016\nEconomic Times • September 2016\n\n10 Indian businessmen to watch out for in 2016\nEconomic times • January 2016 [...] with Mirae Asset Group - a leading global asset management organization. Initially, as ‘Head of Asia Pacific Business’ and <br>-Subsequently, as 'CEO and Director' of Mirae Asset India , established a strong foundation and built the Mutual Fund organization from inception. <br><br>- Was also associated with Fidelity with responsibilities for building the Asia Pacific Investment Marketing organization covering Japan, Australia, Korea, Taiwan, HongKong & Singapore<br><br>- Also been in senior","score":0.5382315},{"title":"Nithin Kamath's personal homepage - Musings on finance, business, and life","url":"https://nithinkamath.me","content":"2009\n\nAs a Reliance Money franchisee [...] In school, I was a below average student academically. I discovered trading and the markets by accident at the age of 17. I’ve been through the boom and bust journey every good trader experiences. In the early 2000s, I borrowed money and blew up my trading account and then worked in a call center for 4 years trying to make up for the debt, while also trading on the side. I met Seema while working there. I quit my job when I met the first person who asked me to manage their portfolio. [...] After the success of Zerodha, and more recently, the media bestowing on us glamourised labels like “unicorn” and “billionaires”, I felt I should share my personal perspective on business and life, and what success really means to me, beyond the labels. If nothing else, I want to tell people that it is possible to be successful at business by questioning the true cost of revenue, valuations, and growth, instead of continuously chasing them. And that success is relative, impermanent, and a lot of","score":0.434102}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:56:46.743Z","session":"eea5bf65-e2dc-4a20-b9f2-ea75b0008065","event":"tool.end","callId":"dc1c6564-3649-4d7b-be8b-bcbae66d9623","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2533,"result":[{"title":"Nikhil Kamath - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikhil_Kamath","content":"Nikhil Kamath (born 5 September 1986) is an Indian entrepreneur and investor. He is the co-founder of Zerodha, a retail stockbroker, and True Beacon, an asset management company. As of December 2025( Kamath is worth $3.3 billion, according to Forbes. He, along with his brother Nithin, is also part of Forbes' list of India’s 100 Richest for 2024.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit source] [...] ## External links\n\n[edit source]\n\n Profile at Forbes\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| Authority control databases: Academics Edit this at Wikidata |  Google Scholar |\n\nRetrieved from \"\"\n\nCategories:\n\n Living people\n 1986 births\n 21st-century Indian businesspeople\n Indian billionaires\n Indian technology company founders\n Financial company founders\n Indian businesspeople in finance\n Businesspeople from Karnataka\n People from Shimoga\n Indian investors\n Indian podcasters\n\nHidden categories: [...] Kamath was born on September 5, 1986, in Shimoga and was raised in Bengaluru, Karnataka. He was born into a Kannada-Konkani speaking Hindu family. Kamath's father, Raghuram Kamath, was an executive at Canara Bank, while his mother, Revathi Kamath, had her own event management company that managed major events for HP and Bosch \"Bosch (company)\") at venues like Leela Palace and Windsor Manor. Her landscaping work flourished as she completed projects for the Chinnaswamy Stadium and corporate","score":0.8830044},{"title":"Nikhil Kamath","url":"https://www.forbes.com/profile/nikhil-kamath","content":"Nikhil Kamath is the co-founder of Zerodha, India’s biggest stock brokerage company in terms of volume of trade, and of True Beacon, an asset management company (AMC) focused on ultra-high net worth investors. [...] Nikhil Kamath cofounded discount brokerage Zerodha in 2010 with his older brother Nithin Kamath. It went on to disrupt the brokerage market in India.\n\nThe Bangalore-based Zerodha, has more than seven million active clients, making it one of the largest brokerage firms in the country.\n\nTheir venture capital fund and incubator, called Rainmatter, invests in fintech companies and ventures that promote financial inclusion. [...] A look at how a visit to Bristol Motor Speedway as a young boy inspired Josef Newgarden to become a racing champion who got to return as a source of \"Tennessee Pride.\"\n\nNithin and Nikhil Kamath broke barriers to build Zerodha at a blistering pace amid India's rising stock markets. New rules to curb speculation now pose speed limits.","score":0.83549726},{"title":"Nikhil Kamath - Guy Kawasaki","url":"https://guykawasaki.com/nikhil-kamath","content":"Guy Kawasaki:  \n I'm Guy Kawasaki, and this is Remarkable People. Today's remarkable guest is Nikhil Kamath. Nikhil is the co-founder of India's largest stock brokerage firm, Zerodha. If this sort of thing impresses you, he's in his thirties and therefore one of India's youngest billionaires. [...] Skip to content\n\nGuy Kawasaki Logo\n\nPrevious Next\n\n View Larger Image \n\n# Nikhil Kamath\n\nI’m Guy Kawasaki, and this is Remarkable People. Today’s guest is Nikhil Kamath, the co-founder of India’s largest stock brokerage, Zerodha.\n\nFor what it’s worth, he’s in his early thirties and a billionaire based on his stake in the company. [...] Guy Kawasaki is the chief evangelist of Canva, an online graphic design tool. Formerly, he was an advisor to the Motorola business unit of Google and chief evangelist of Apple. He is also the author of The Art of Social Media, The Art of the Start, APE: Author, Publisher, Entrepreneur, Enchantment, and nine other books. Kawasaki has a BA from Stanford University and an MBA from UCLA as well as an honorary doctorate from Babson College.\n\n## Related Posts","score":0.7931224},{"title":"38-year-old billionaire Nikhil Kamath's No. 1 tip for entrepreneurs","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2024/12/30/38-year-old-billionaire-nikhil-kamaths-no-1-tip-for-entrepreneurs.html","content":"But it may be rewarding to do so, especially if you want to start a business or launch a side-hustle. That's according to Nikhil Kamath, a 38-year-old self-made billionaire and co-founder of Zerodha, an online stock brokerage platform. [...] Kamath got his start in business in the ninth grade, buying and reselling cell phones to his classmates before dropping out of high school. He later got a job working at a call center, teaching himself how to trade stocks in his free time, which inspired his career in finance. [...] Kamath co-founded the Bangalore-based Zerodha in 2010 alongside his brother. The trading platform has since grown to more than 10 million users, making it one of the largest in India and helping Kamath reach a $3 billion net worth, according to Forbes.\n\nIn 2021, he co-founded a venture capital firm called Gruhas, which supports entrepreneurs in industries like artificial intelligence and cleantech — both of which are top of mind for younger generations.","score":0.6852132},{"title":"Nikhil Kamath - Investor & Entrepreneur - Gruhas","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/in/nikhilkamathcio","content":"# Nikhil Kamath\nInvestor & Entrepreneur\nBengaluru, Karnataka, India, IN  \n500 connections, 1637824 followers\n\n## About\nNone\n\n## Experience\n### Co-Founder  \nGruhas  \nJun 2021 - Present   \nBengaluru, Karnataka, India  \n\n### Co-Founder  \nZerodha  \nAug 2010 - Present   \nBengaluru Area, India  \nIndia's #1 brokerage platform and trading community.\n\nwww.zerodha.com\n\n### Co-Founder  \nTrue Beacon  \nAug 2019 - Present   \nBengaluru Area, India  \nDisrupting asset management.\n\nwww.truebeacon.com [...] - Most people know Vijay Kedia as a legendary stock picker. What often goes unnoticed is the power of concentration. A large part of his wealth…  \nLiked by Nikhil Kamath  \nView Post  \nActivity Image\n\n- Episode out now:  Why does a tablet I buy in the US feel stronger than the same one in India? That question pulled us into…  \nShared by Nikhil Kamath  \nView Post  \nActivity Image [...] ## People Also Viewed\n- Mukesh Singh (Davos Finservices Pvt Ltd) - \n- Manisha Bansal (i2i Funding) - \n- Niraj Prakash Saxena (TruCard) - \n- Manish Rathi (Finzome Technologies) - \n- Kenneth Serrao (OAKS Asset Management) - \n- Praveen Choudhary (Ambition Services Pvt Ltd) - \n- Alok Arora (Nupay) - \n- Raghavendra Pratap Singh (i2ifunding) - \n- Kapil Mittal (Raghunandan Money) - \n- Himanshu Chandra (YPO) -","score":0.5931622}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T15:56:46.840Z","session":"eea5bf65-e2dc-4a20-b9f2-ea75b0008065","event":"tool.end","callId":"e9bc2916-eb6a-474b-9210-65076c36b0cd","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2634,"result":[{"title":"Zerodha","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zerodha","content":"## History\n\nZerodha was founded in August 2010 by brothers Nithin Kamath and Nikhil Kamath as a discount brokerage firm. The name Zerodha was a combination of words for the company's ideals: zero and rodha, the Sanskrit word for 'barrier'. The company started with six employees and ₹2 crore in seed money drawn from Nithin Kamath's personal savings and contributions from a Singapore-based friend. [...] |  |  |\n --- |\n|  | |\n| Type | Private |\n| Industry | Financial services |\n| Founded | August 2010; 16 years ago (August 2010) |\n| Founders |  Nithin Kamath  Nikhil Kamath |\n| Headquarters | Bengaluru, Karnataka , India |\n| Products |  Kite  Coin  Console  Varsity |\n| Services |  Equity trading  Derivatives trading \"Derivative (finance)\")  Currency trading  Commodity trading  Mutual funds |\n| Revenue | Decrease ₹8,847 crore (US$920 million) (FY25) | [...] Zerodha was founded and bootstrapped \"Bootstrapping (business)\") by brothers Nithin and Nikhil Kamath. As of May 2024, it has 7.5 million active customers registered with the NSE, making it the second-largest stockbroker in India.\n\n## History","score":0.92684203},{"title":"Zerodha Founder Story: The Inspiring Journey of Nithin Kamath","url":"https://www.tvisha.com/blog/zerodha-founder","content":"This firm named Zerodha was founded in the year 2010 with the objective of providing economical services in terms of stock and investment trading. The main motive of this firm was to introduce the concept of discount brokers which makes the trading process less expensive than other brokerage firms. Moreover, the company operates in different spheres, including mutual funds, investor education, portfolio management solutions, and fintech solutions. Currently, millions of clients use the services [...] The founders of Zerodha are Nithin Kamath and Nikhil Kamath. These two brothers founded this firm by using their experience in trading, investments, and business strategies. In the year 2010, these two brothers founded the firm Zerodha. While Nithin is the visionary of the firm, Nikhil takes care of market intelligence.\n\n### When was Zerodha founded? [...] Zerodha Founder\n\nZerodha Founder Story\n\nNithin Kamath\n\nZerodha Founders\n\nZerodha Success Story\n\nHave an Innovative app Idea\n\nGet a Free Quote to Build & Manage your App..!\n\nsubmit\n\nPopular Posts\n\nSarvam AI Success Story: The Journey Behind India’s AI Revolution \n\nPublished August 18,2026 by  Rishika Kuna\n\nSarvam AI Success Story: The Journey Behind India’s AI Revolution\n\nSarvam AI Founders: The Story Behind India’s AI Powerhouse \n\nPublished August 18,2026 by  Rishika Kuna","score":0.9121316},{"title":"Our company, history, and the people behind it","url":"https://zerodha.com/about","content":"And yet, we are always up to something new every day. Catch up on the latest updates on our blog or see what the media is saying about us or learn more about our business and product philosophies.\n\n## People\n\n##### Nithin Kamath\n\nFounder, CEO\n\nNithin bootstrapped and founded Zerodha in 2010 to overcome the hurdles he faced during his decade long stint as a trader. Today, Zerodha has changed the landscape of the Indian broking industry. [...] ## We pioneered the discount broking model in India. Now, we are breaking ground with our technology.\n\nWe kick-started operations on the 15th of August, 2010 with the goal of breaking all barriers that traders and investors face in India in terms of cost, support, and technology. We named the company Zerodha, a combination of Zero and \"Rodha\", the Sanskrit word for barrier.\n\nToday, our disruptive pricing models and in-house technology have made us the biggest stock broker in India.","sc