{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:19:44.819Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.start","callId":"c3b88498-83b2-471c-a8a3-4d20df1a707b","name":"webSearch","args":["Capgemini company"]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:19:47.251Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"e5d7dd5a-b46c-4286-b053-2b61799adec1","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2436,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/salil-parekh","content":"Before joining Infosys, Parekh had a distinguished 25-year career at Capgemini, where he held several key leadership positions. He began his career at Ernst & Young in 1992 when the consultancy arm later merged with Capgemini. During his tenure at Capgemini, he served as a member of the group management board and held leadership roles in Cloud Infrastructure Services and various business clusters, including Application Services. Since taking the helm at Infosys in 2018, Parekh has led the [...] ### CEO, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys Limited, one of India’s leading global IT services companies. Parekh graduated with a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Bombay in 1986. He then pursued higher studies at Cornell University, earning Master of Engineering degrees in both Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering in 1988.","score":0.9247491},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://arisepedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"## Career\n\nBefore joining Infosys, Parekh worked at Ernst & Young’s consulting division, which later merged into Capgemini. At Capgemini, he held multiple leadership roles over his long tenure starting from 2000. He became a member of the group management board and was appointed as Deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing several business units, including Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services. [...] Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is an Indian business executive and the current Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, a global IT services company. He assumed the role on 2 January 2018, succeeding interim CEO U B Pravin Rao. With decades of experience in the consulting and IT services sector, Parekh is known for his leadership in digital transformation and business growth across geographies.\n\n## Early Life and Education [...] Since taking charge, Salil Parekh has led multiple initiatives including:\n\n Strengthening Infosys' digital and cloud-first strategy.\n Deepening focus on client-centric innovation and transformation.\n Expanding global delivery centers and hiring internationally.\n Driving sustainability and ESG initiatives within the company.","score":0.8952393},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"[edit]\n\nSalil Parekh is born into a Gujarati family. He is a graduate from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay (IIT Bombay) in Aeronautical Engineering. Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University.\n\nParekh was member of the group management board at Capgemini, where he had worked since 2000, after Ernst & Young's consultancy division, where he had been working before, was merged into the company. [...] Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit]","score":0.843393},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html","content":"Prior to Infosys, Salil was a member of the management board at Capgemini and a partner at consulting practice Ernst & Young LLP prior to its acquisition by Capgemini. He had different leadership roles there across US, UK, Europe, Asia, over a span of 25 years.\n\nSalil has received several awards as a leading CEO. [...] Salil holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay. [...] Salil has helped transform Infosys into a leading digital, cloud, and AI company. Salil helps set the strategy and nurture a leadership team to drive its execution. Infosys is in the top decile of shareholder return during his tenure, leading in client satisfaction results, and leading in employee engagement scores.\n\nSalil has a strong track record of driving transformations, executing business turnarounds, and managing successful acquisitions.","score":0.8399576},{"title":"Infosys appoints Capgemini's Salil Parekh as MD & CEO","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/infosys-appoints-capgeminis-salil-parekh-as-md-ceo/articleshow/61893756.cms","content":"Parekh, who has an engineering degree in aeronautics from IIT Bombay, has also completed his masters in computer science and mechanical engineering from Cornell University. He was a partner in global tax and audit firm Ernst & Young between 1992 and 2000 in financial services. He joined Capgemini in 2000 as a result of the acquisition of the consulting division of Ernst and Young. [...] Infosys will hope that Parekh’s background in the financial services industry throughout his career will help it garner more deals in the BFSI sector across Europe and North America. BFSI, the bread and butter for all Indian IT services companies, contributed about 33% to the company’s topline for the second quarter ended September 30. [...] Parekh, who has been appointed for five years and will be the second outsider CEO, joins from French IT and consulting company Capgemini where he is the CEO of financial services across Europe, North America and Asia.He has been with the company for 17 years and also a member of its executive committee.","score":0.8380581}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:19:47.278Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"572a3db1-17e5-4df7-a0b3-6b80e85ad740","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2461,"result":[{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/salil-parekh","content":"Before joining Infosys, Parekh had a distinguished 25-year career at Capgemini, where he held several key leadership positions. He began his career at Ernst & Young in 1992 when the consultancy arm later merged with Capgemini. During his tenure at Capgemini, he served as a member of the group management board and held leadership roles in Cloud Infrastructure Services and various business clusters, including Application Services. Since taking the helm at Infosys in 2018, Parekh has led the [...] ### CEO, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys Limited, one of India’s leading global IT services companies. Parekh graduated with a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Bombay in 1986. He then pursued higher studies at Cornell University, earning Master of Engineering degrees in both Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering in 1988. [...] In May 2022, Parekh was reappointed as CEO and Managing Director for a five-year term ending March 2027, reflecting the board’s confidence in his leadership abilities. Parekh has received several awards as a leading CEO in the technology sector. He is a member of The Business Council, where he contributes his expertise to business leadership discussions. His strategic vision have earned him recognition as one of the prominent figures in the global IT services industry. Parekh’s vision for the","score":0.9119436},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh","url":"https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html","content":"Prior to Infosys, Salil was a member of the management board at Capgemini and a partner at consulting practice Ernst & Young LLP prior to its acquisition by Capgemini. He had different leadership roles there across US, UK, Europe, Asia, over a span of 25 years.\n\nSalil has received several awards as a leading CEO. [...] + Healthcare\n  + High Technology\n  + Industrial Manufacturing\n  + Information Services & Publishing\n  + Insurance\n  + Life Sciences\n  + Logistics & Distribution\n  + Media and Entertainment\n  + Mining\n  + Retail\n  + Semiconductor\n  + Travel and Hospitality\n  + Utilities\n  + Waste Management\n ## Services\n\n  ### Insights\n\n  + Infosys Topaz\n  + Applied AI\n  + Infosys Generative AI\n  + Infosys Sustainability Services\n\n  ### Innovate [...] Salil holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.","score":0.9055316},{"title":"Salil Parekh - Managing Director and CEO, Infosys","url":"https://usispf.org/board-of-directors/salil-parekh","content":"Earlier, Salil was a member of the Group Executive Board at Capgemini, where he held several leadership positions for 25 years. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services (North America, UK, Asia), Cloud Infrastructure Services, and Sogeti (Technology & Engineering Services Division). He was responsible for the strategy and execution of these businesses – setting direction and enabling rapid client adoption. He was also the Chairman of Capgemini’s North [...] Salil was also Partner at Ernst & Young and widely credited for bringing scale and value to the Indian operations of the consultancy firm.\n\nHe holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.\n\n###### Subscribe to our\n\n Daily Newsletter   Weekly Newsletter [...] Salil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic direction for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team to drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services industry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing business turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions. He is a member of the National Council of the","score":0.850382},{"title":"Salil Parekh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh","content":"Parekh was member of the group executive board, and was appointed deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services among others. He then ascended as CEO of MD of Infosys in 2018. Under his leadership Infosys underwent a major digital transformation that increased their company's revenue by 35%.\n\n## Whistleblower allegations\n\n[edit] [...] [edit]\n\nSalil Parekh is born into a Gujarati family. He is a graduate from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay (IIT Bombay) in Aeronautical Engineering. Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University.\n\nParekh was member of the group management board at Capgemini, where he had worked since 2000, after Ernst & Young's consultancy division, where he had been working before, was merged into the company. [...] Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit]","score":0.8021998},{"title":"Salil Parekh: I'm making Infosys relevant for future clients: CEO Salil Parekh - Times of India","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/infosys-is-truly-a-thing-of-beauty-its-been-built-with-so-much-love-and-affection-ceo-salil-parekh/articleshow/63805927.cms","content":"Salil Parekh,  , is three months into his new job. The famed corner room he occupies at the company’s head office is bare but for two black-and- white photos of his family. And, that’s the way it will stay, says the quietly firm former Capgemini executive who is in the process of shifting home from Mumbai to Bengaluru.Dressed in regular light-blue shirt, navy pants, striped tie, Parekh sat down for an hour-long chat with TOI, his first exclusive interaction with media, and spoke on the past, [...] Salil Parekh, Infosys’ second non-promoter CEO, is three months into his new job. The famed corner room he occupies at the company’s head office is bare but for two black-and- white photos of his family. And, that’s the way it will stay says the quietly firm former Capgemini executive who is in the process of shifting home from Mumbai to Bengaluru.\n\nCEO Salil Parekh: I'm making Infosys relevant for future clients","score":0.71758664}]}
