{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:19:47.765Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"llm.start","callId":"90e4f401-c50e-46bb-8aa0-975fa3464845","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence. Each fact is one short, self-contained statement (e.g. \"CEO and MD of Infosys since 2 January 2018\") with \"sourceUrl\" set to the URL of the one source that states it. Sources headed \"Previously learned\" are facts from earlier research — cite their URL like any other source.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"facts\": [{\"fact\": string, \"sourceUrl\": string}]}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: What was Salil Parekh's previous role before joining Infosys?\nSub-questions to cover:\n- What is Salil Parekh's career history?\n- What company did Salil Parekh work for before Infosys?\n- When did Salil Parekh join Infosys?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Mr. Salil Parekh - Indian Institute of Technology Bombay\nURL: https://acr.iitbombay.org/awards/mr-salil-parekh\nPrior to Infosys, Mr. Parekh held leadership roles at Capgemini (Member of the Group Management Board) and Ernst & Young LLP (Partner) over the past 25 years.\n\nHe has won many awards over the years. These include the Fortune India Best IT CEO 2022, the BT-PwC India’s Best CEO 2022 –Large Companies, Forbes India Leadership Awards 20-21 – Best CEO in the Private sector, and the Business Standard Annual Awards 2021 – CEO of the Year.\n\nHobbies:  \n “Reading, movies, listening to music.” [...] Give Back\n\nLogo\n\nMr. Salil Parekh\n\nB.Tech., 1986 Aerospace Engineering\n\nMr. Salil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, Infosys. He graduated with a B.Tech. in Aeronautical Engineering from IIT Bombay in 1986 and got his M.S. in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, Ithaca, New York in 1988.\n\n[S2] Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director: Salil Parekh\nURL: https://www.infosys.com/about/management-profiles/salil-parekh.html\nPrior to Infosys, Salil was a member of the management board at Capgemini and a partner at consulting practice Ernst & Young LLP prior to its acquisition by Capgemini. He had different leadership roles there across US, UK, Europe, Asia, over a span of 25 years.\n\nSalil has received several awards as a leading CEO. [...] Salil is on the board of Advance CT, an organization that supports business and innovation in the state of Connecticut. Salil is on the Board of the US-India Strategic Partnership Forum (USISPF) an organization that works towards strengthening the US-India relationship and promoting collaboration in various sectors, including technology.\n\nSalil Parekh is also an Executive Officer for Infosys.\n\n## Request for services [...] + Formula E\n  + Madison Square Garden\n  + The Economist Group\n  + Dow Jones\n  + Financial Times\n  + The Cloud Hub\n  + Handelsblatt\n Investors\n Careers\n Newsroom\n Blogs\n Contact Us\n\nManagement Profiles\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\nChief Executive Officer and Managing Director\n\nSalil Parekh\n\nSalil is the Chief Executive Officer of Infosys and has been in that role since January 2018.\n\n[S3] Salil Parekh\nURL: https://arisepedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh\n## Career\n\nBefore joining Infosys, Parekh worked at Ernst & Young’s consulting division, which later merged into Capgemini. At Capgemini, he held multiple leadership roles over his long tenure starting from 2000. He became a member of the group management board and was appointed as Deputy CEO in March 2015. He was responsible for overseeing several business units, including Application Services and Cloud Infrastructure Services. [...] Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is an Indian business executive and the current Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys, a global IT services company. He assumed the role on 2 January 2018, succeeding interim CEO U B Pravin Rao. With decades of experience in the consulting and IT services sector, Parekh is known for his leadership in digital transformation and business growth across geographies.\n\n## Early Life and Education [...] Jump to content\n\n  Arisepedia \n\nSearch\n\n# Salil Parekh\n\n English\n\nFrom Arisepedia\n\n| Salil Parekh |\n\n|  |\n| Born | 5 June 1964 India |\n| Nationality | Indian |\n| Education | IIT Bombay (BTech, Aeronautical Engineering) Cornell University (MS, Computer Science & Mechanical Engineering) |\n| Occupation | CEO and MD of Infosys |\n| Spouse | Shaleen S. Parekh |\n| Mother | Kokila S. Parekh |\n\n[S4] Salil Parekh\nURL: https://indiaspora.org/business-leader/salil-parekh\nBefore joining Infosys, Parekh had a distinguished 25-year career at Capgemini, where he held several key leadership positions. He began his career at Ernst & Young in 1992 when the consultancy arm later merged with Capgemini. During his tenure at Capgemini, he served as a member of the group management board and held leadership roles in Cloud Infrastructure Services and various business clusters, including Application Services. Since taking the helm at Infosys in 2018, Parekh has led the [...] ### CEO, Infosys\n\nSalil Parekh is the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Infosys Limited, one of India’s leading global IT services companies. Parekh graduated with a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Bombay in 1986. He then pursued higher studies at Cornell University, earning Master of Engineering degrees in both Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering in 1988. [...] In May 2022, Parekh was reappointed as CEO and Managing Director for a five-year term ending March 2027, reflecting the board’s confidence in his leadership abilities. Parekh has received several awards as a leading CEO in the technology sector. He is a member of The Business Council, where he contributes his expertise to business leadership discussions. His strategic vision have earned him recognition as one of the prominent figures in the global IT services industry. Parekh’s vision for the\n\n[S5] Infosys CEO Salil Parekh | Salary, Age, Email & Net Worth\nURL: https://listofceo.com/infosys/infosys-ceo-email-net-worth-salil-parekh\nBefore becoming Infosys CEO, Salil Parekh spent 17 years at Capgemini, where he rose to the position of Deputy CEO and was a member of the Group Executive Board. He was instrumental in building Capgemini’s North American operations and offshoring capabilities. Prior to Capgemini, he was a partner at Ernst & Young (1992–2000), focused on financial services consulting.\n\n### Is Infosys a profitable company? [...] The current CEO and Managing Director of Infosys is Salil Parekh, who was appointed on January 2, 2018. He was reappointed for a second five-year term in May 2022, with his current tenure running through March 31, 2027. Before joining Infosys, he served as Deputy CEO at Capgemini.\n\n### What is Salil Parekh’s net worth in 2026? [...] | Salil Parekh — At a Glance |\n| Full Name | Salil Satish Parekh |\n| Position | Chief Executive Officer & Managing Director |\n| Company | Infosys Limited (NSE: INFY / NYSE: INFY) |\n| Age | 61 years (born June 5, 1964) |\n| Education | B.Tech, IIT Bombay; M.S., Cornell University |\n| Net Worth (2026) | ~$45 Million |\n| Total Compensation | ~$9.4 Million / ₹80.6 Crore (FY2025) |\n| CEO Since | January 2, 2018 |\n| Previous Role | Deputy CEO & Group Executive Board Member, Capgemini |\n\n[S6] Salil Parekh\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salil_Parekh\n[edit]\n\nSalil Parekh is born into a Gujarati family. He is a graduate from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay (IIT Bombay) in Aeronautical Engineering. Master of Engineering degree in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University.\n\nParekh was member of the group management board at Capgemini, where he had worked since 2000, after Ernst & Young's consultancy division, where he had been working before, was merged into the company. [...] Salil Parekh (born 5 June 1964) is the current chief executive officer and managing director of Infosys. Parekh took over from interim CEO U. B. Pravin Rao on 2 January 2018 for a five year term. The Infosys board has announced that Ashiss Kumar Dash will succeed him as CEO in April 2027.\n\nParekh is a member of The Business Council.\n\n## Early life and education\n\n[edit]\n\n[S7] Infosys appoints Capgemini's Salil Parekh as MD & CEO\nURL: https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/infosys-appoints-capgeminis-salil-parekh-as-md-ceo/articleshow/61893756.cms\nParekh, who has an engineering degree in aeronautics from IIT Bombay, has also completed his masters in computer science and mechanical engineering from Cornell University. He was a partner in global tax and audit firm Ernst & Young between 1992 and 2000 in financial services. He joined Capgemini in 2000 as a result of the acquisition of the consulting division of Ernst and Young. [...] Infosys will hope that Parekh’s background in the financial services industry throughout his career will help it garner more deals in the BFSI sector across Europe and North America. BFSI, the bread and butter for all Indian IT services companies, contributed about 33% to the company’s topline for the second quarter ended September 30. [...] Parekh, who has been appointed for five years and will be the second outsider CEO, joins from French IT and consulting company Capgemini where he is the CEO of financial services across Europe, North America and Asia.He has been with the company for 17 years and also a member of its executive committee.\n\n[S8] Salil Parekh - Managing Director and CEO, Infosys\nURL: https://usispf.org/board-of-directors/salil-parekh\nEarlier, Salil was a member of the Group Executive Board at Capgemini, where he held several leadership positions for 25 years. He was responsible for overseeing a business cluster comprising Application Services (North America, UK, Asia), Cloud Infrastructure Services, and Sogeti (Technology & Engineering Services Division). He was responsible for the strategy and execution of these businesses – setting direction and enabling rapid client adoption. He was also the Chairman of Capgemini’s North [...] Salil was also Partner at Ernst & Young and widely credited for bringing scale and value to the Indian operations of the consultancy firm.\n\nHe holds Master of Engineering degrees in Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering from Cornell University, and a Bachelor of Technology degree in Aeronautical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay.\n\n###### Subscribe to our\n\n Daily Newsletter   Weekly Newsletter [...] Salil Parekh, as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director, sets and evolves the strategic direction for the company and its portfolio of offerings, while nurturing a strong leadership team to drive its execution. Salil has nearly three decades of global experience in the IT services industry with a strong track record of driving digital transformation for enterprises, executing business turnarounds and managing successful acquisitions. He is a member of the National Council of the\n\n[S9] Salil Parekh: I'm making Infosys relevant for future clients: CEO Salil Parekh - Times of India\nURL: https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/infosys-is-truly-a-thing-of-beauty-its-been-built-with-so-much-love-and-affection-ceo-salil-parekh/articleshow/63805927.cms\nSalil Parekh,  , is three months into his new job. The famed corner room he occupies at the company’s head office is bare but for two black-and- white photos of his family. And, that’s the way it will stay, says the quietly firm former Capgemini executive who is in the process of shifting home from Mumbai to Bengaluru.Dressed in regular light-blue shirt, navy pants, striped tie, Parekh sat down for an hour-long chat with TOI, his first exclusive interaction with media, and spoke on the past, [...] Salil Parekh, Infosys’ second non-promoter CEO, is three months into his new job. The famed corner room he occupies at the company’s head office is bare but for two black-and- white photos of his family. And, that’s the way it will stay says the quietly firm former Capgemini executive who is in the process of shifting home from Mumbai to Bengaluru.\n\nCEO Salil Parekh: I'm making Infosys relevant for future clients\n\n[S10] Capgemini\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/company/capgemini\nCapgemini is an AI-powered global business and technology transformation partner, delivering tangible business value. We imagine the future of organizations and make it real with AI, technology and people. With our strong heritage of nearly 60 years, we are a responsible and diverse group of 420,000 team members in more than 50 countries. We deliver end-to-end services and solutions with our deep industry expertise and strong partner ecosystem, leveraging our capabilities across strategy, [...] ### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\nN/A\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nIT Services and IT Consulting\n\n### Company Size\n10,001+ employees  \n347656 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed Capgemini as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\nN/A\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: N/A\nLast Round Type: N/A\nTotal Rounds: N/A\nLast Round Raised: N/A\n\n### Investors\nN/A [...] AI ambition into measurable business outcomes. Agentic AI is now at the center of virtually every client conversation, and Capgemini is recognized as the partner of choice for AI-driven, end-to-end business and operations transformation. At the same time, we are ideally positioned to benefit from accelerating investments in technology sovereignty, defense and security, particularly in Europe, where these themes are becoming strategic priorities. With this momentum, we are raising our full year\n\n[S11] Capgemini Information\nURL: https://rocketreach.co/capgemini-profile_b5c47feaf42e0dfc\nCapgemini is an AI-powered global business and technology transformation partner, delivering tangible business value. We imagine the future of organizations and make it real with AI, technology and people. With our strong heritage of nearly 60 years, we are a responsible and diverse group of 420,000 team members in more than 50 countries. We deliver end-to-end services and solutions with our deep industry expertise and strong partner ecosystem, leveraging our capabilities across strategy, [...] across strategy, technology, design, engineering and business operations. The Group reported 2025 global revenues of €22.5 billion. Make it real | www.capgemini.com [...] Image 1: RocketReach logoToggle navigation\n   Log In\n   Sign Up\n\nImage 2: stars 1Image 3: stars 2Image 4: stars 3\n\n   ## Company Information\n   ## Email Format\n   ## Management\n   ## Technology Stack\n   ## Competitors\n\nImage 5: Capgemini\n\n# Capgemini Information\n\nView Top Employees from Capgemini\n\n[S12] Capgemini | Company Profile - Vault\nURL: https://vault.com/company-profiles/management-strategy/capgemini\nEmployersSchools\n\nVault Law\n\nEvents\n\nBlog\n\nCareer Advice\n\nHeader image of Vault logo on grey background.\n\nCapgemini logo\n\n# Capgemini\n\n(212) 314-8000\n\nCapgemini APAC, Capgemini EMEA\n\nVault Verdict\n\nRankings\n\nWhy Work Here\n\n# Overview\n\nVault logo on a grey bac