{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:06.448Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"2dd2389c-29e5-4657-865f-ab004b3b04a9","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2481,"result":[{"title":"kalyan jewellers Employee Directory, Headcount & Staff | LeadIQ","url":"https://leadiq.com/c/kalyan-jewellers/60153c4e411f372b40487952/employee-directory","content":"Kalyan Jewellers is a jewelry retailer founded in 1993 and headquartered in Thrissur, Kerala, with a broad footprint that now spans about 132 showrooms across India and the GCC. It operates in the luxury segment, offering a wide array of designed pieces across gold and diamond jewelry, including several named collections for weddings, heritage, and everyday wear. The product range includes gold jewelry, diamond jewelry, earrings, bangles, and necklaces, among other pieces. The company is based [...] company is based in Thrissur with significant operations in Maharashtra, and supports a mid-sized workforce. In 2026, Kalyan Jewellers expanded its retail footprint with new showrooms in Ambernath, Maharashtra, and Medipally, Hyderabad. The firm is positioned as a major regional player in luxury jewelry, combining a large showroom network with a broad assortment designed to address varied customer preferences for wedding and occasion jewelry. [...] ### What is kalyan jewellers known for?\n\nMinus sign iconPlus sign iconkalyan jewellers was founded in 1993 and operates in the Retail Luxury Goods and Jewelry industry. Explore kalyan jewellers's company overview page for more information.\n\n### What is kalyan jewellers's most common email format?","score":0.92620385},{"title":"Kalyan Jewellers company information, history, management and director details and CEO salary","url":"https://trendlyne.com/equity/about/447071/KALYANKJIL/kalyan-jewellers-india-ltd","content":"Kalyan Jewellers India Ltd. is one of India’s largest jewellery retailers, operating a pan-India network and a significant presence in the Middle East. The company specializes in gold, st, and other precious jewellery, utilizing a hyperlocal strategy to cater to regional consumer preferences. It manages a multi-channel distribution network comprising brick-and-mortar showrooms, a grassroots network of My Kalyan service centers, and an online presence through its subsidiary, Candere. [...] Business Model: Kalyan Jewellers follows a hyperlocal model, customizing product portfolios to match local tastes across different Indian states. It is increasingly shifting toward a capital-light Franchisee Owned Company Operated (FOCO) model to accelerate expansion. Approximately 195 of its Indian Kalyan showrooms and 68 Candere showrooms are now FOCO-based.\n Key Products and Sub-brands:\n  + Wedding Jewellery: Marketed under the Muhurat brand. [...] 1. Kalyan Jewellers India Ltd.\n2. Company Profile\n\n# About Kalyan Jewellers - Company Information, Overview, History and Profile\n\n About\n Gold Prices/Hedging\n\nWebsite: www.kalyanjewellers.net\n\n## About the company - Business Profile","score":0.92491204},{"title":"Kalyan Jewellers India Limited - The Most Trusted Brand","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/kalyan-jewellers-india-pvt-ltd","content":"Kalyan Jewellers is one of the largest jewellery retailers in India, with its headquarters in Thrissur, Kerala. The company draws from its strong roots of over a century in the business of textile trading and distribution. From its modest beginning with a single jewellery showroom in 1993, Kalyan Jewellers has today grown to over 400 showrooms across India, Middle East, USA & UK. Through its long-standing presence in the Indian market for over three decades, Kalyan Jewellers has set industry [...] has set industry benchmarks in quality, transparency, pricing, and innovation. Kalyan offers an array of traditional and contemporary jewellery designs in gold, diamonds and precious stones catering to the distinct needs of different customers. [...] #UKLaunch #InternationalExpansion #JewelleryIndustry #Leicester [Likes: 302, Comments: 12]; Kalyan Jewellers India Limited (10mo): Forbes Asia features T.S. Kalyanaraman, Managing Director of Kalyan Jewellers, in a story that traces how a brand built on trust and tradition has redefined wedding jewellery in India and is now taking that legacy to global markets. A reflection on scale, craftsmanship and the evolving meaning of weddings in modern India. It’s a journey we’re honoured to share.","score":0.9165366},{"title":"Kalyan Jewellers India Ltd share price | About Kalyan Jewellers | Key Insights - Screener","url":"https://www.screener.in/company/KALYANKJIL/consolidated","content":"Key Points\n\nBusiness Profile(  \n Kalyan Jewellers India Limited is one of India’s largest organised jewellery retailers, established in 1993. The company operates a Pan-India, hyperlocal jewellery retail model with scaled presence in India, the Middle East and the USA.\n\nWebsite   BSE   NSE   F&O\n\n Market Cap   ₹ 60,235 Cr.\n Current Price   ₹ 583\n High / Low  ₹ 649 / 327\n Stock P/E   41.2\n Book Value   ₹ 61.1\n Dividend Yield   0.43 %\n ROCE   21.2 %\n ROE   24.8 %\n Face Value   ₹ 10.0 [...] About\n\nKalyan Jewellers India Ltd. designs manufacture and sells a range of gold, studded and other jewellery products across various price points. It is one of the largest jewellery retailers in India based on revenue as of FY20. The co. was founded by the current Chairman, MD and Promoter, Mr T.S. Kalyanaraman (\n\nKey Points","score":0.7760977},{"title":"Gold Jewellery | about-us | Kalyan jewellers","url":"https://www.kalyanjewellers.net/about-us.php","content":"Indian jewellery, its craftsmanship and variety is an amazing showcase of India’s heritage, culture and diversity. With a deep understanding of local tastes and preferences, Kalyan offers an array of traditional and contemporary jewellery designs in gold, diamonds, precious stones and other precious metals. [...] Today, Kalyan Jewellers has 316 retail stores spread across INDIA, MIDDLE EAST AND USA. Pampered by your unbound love and support and with the blessings of the Almighty, we believe we are in the right path towards the accomplishment of our vision to open stores and serve customers across the world.\n\n## ED's Message\n\n#### Rajesh Kalyanaraman - Executive Director [...] We at Kalyan have always believed that the customer needs to be educated and aware, as this is the first step in preventing malpractices in business. As a part of this philosophy we have conducted several campaigns over the years, to educate customers about purity, pricing and other aspects. These efforts of Kalyan have gone a long way in the industry, that is now becoming more transparent towards the customer’s interests. We believe that this is our legacy to the industry.","score":0.7724109}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:06.464Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"ef24e8a3-ea4e-44ce-8fda-49902c53aefb","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2497,"result":[{"title":"Titan Company - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titan_Company","content":"Titan Company Limited is an Indian fashion accessories company that mainly manufactures items such as jewellery, watches and eyewear. Part of the Tata Group and started as a joint venture with TIDCO, the company has its corporate headquarters in Electronic City, Bangalore, and registered office in Hosur, Tamil Nadu. [...] Titan Company commenced operations in 1984 under the name Titan Watches Limited. In 1994, Titan diversified into jewellery with Tanishq and subsequently into eyewear with Titan Eyeplus. In 2005, it launched its youth fashion accessories brand Fastrack \"Fastrack (fashion accessories)\"). Titan is the largest branded jewellery maker in India by value, with a 6% market share as of 2022. More than 80% of its total revenue comes from the jewellery segment. As of 2019, it is also the fifth-largest [...] [edit]\n\nTitan Engineering & Automation Limited is a wholly owned subsidiary of Titan. It was formerly known as Titan-Precision Engineering Division. The company now deals in machine building, automation and component manufacturing.\n\nTitan Company acquired the historic Swiss watch brand Favre-Leuba in November 2011 for US$2.7 million.","score":0.921591},{"title":"Titan Company Limited Information","url":"https://rocketreach.co/titan-company-limited-profile_b5c493e7f42e0dca","content":"Titan Company Ltd is the organization that brought about a paradigm shift in the Indian watch market when it introduced its futuristic quartz technology, complemented by international styling. With India's two most recognized and loved brands Titan and Tanishq to its credit, Titan Company Ltd is the fifth largest integrated own brand watch manufacturer in the world. The success story began in 1984 with a joint venture between the Tata Group and the Tamil Nadu Industrial Development Corporation. [...] Corporation. Presenting Titan quartz watches that sported an international look, Titan Company Ltd transformed the Indian watch market. After Sonata, a value brand of functionally styled watches at affordable prices, Titan Company Ltd reached out to the youth segment with Fastrack, its third brand, trendy and chic. The company has sold 150 million watches world over and manufactures over 15 million watches every year. Backed by over 6,000 employees, two exclusive design studios for watches and [...] for watches and jewellery, 10 manufacturing units, and innumerable admirers’ world over, Titan Company Ltd continues to grow and set new standards for innovation and quality. The organization is all geared to repeat the Titan and Tanishq success story with each new offering.","score":0.8684817},{"title":"Titan Company Limited - A strong portfolio of brands & industry leading capabilities, Titan is driven by the values and ethos of the Tata Group","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/titan-industries","content":"Titan Company Ltd is the organization that brought about a paradigm shift in the Indian watch market when it introduced its futuristic quartz technology, complemented by international styling. With India's two most recognized and loved brands Titan and Tanishq to its credit, Titan Company Ltd is the fifth largest integrated own brand watch manufacturer in the world. The success story began in 1984 with a joint venture between the Tata Group and the Tamil Nadu Industrial Development Corporation. [...] Corporation. Presenting Titan quartz watches that sported an international look, Titan Company Ltd transformed the Indian watch market. After Sonata, a value brand of functionally styled watches at affordable prices, Titan Company Ltd reached out to the youth segment with Fastrack, its third brand, trendy and chic. The company has sold 150 million watches world over and manufactures over 15 million watches every year. Backed by over 6,000 employees, two exclusive design studios for watches and [...] for watches and jewellery, 10 manufacturing units, and innumerable admirers’ world over, Titan Company Ltd continues to grow and set new standards for innovation and quality. The organization is all geared to repeat the Titan and Tanishq success story with each new offering.","score":0.85097736},{"title":"Titan Company Limited (TITAN.NS) Stock Price, News, Quote & History - Yahoo Finance","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TITAN.NS","content":"Titan Company Limited, together with its subsidiaries, manufactures and sells watches, jewelry, eyewear, fragrances, women's bags, and other accessories and products in India and internationally. The company operates through four segments: Watches and Wearables, Jewellery, Eyecare, and Others. The company designs, manufactures, and retails watches and wearables under the Nebula, Titan, Titan Clock, Zoop, Titan Octane, Titan Raga, Xylys, Edge, Fastrack, Sonata, Titan Smart, Fastrack smart, SF, [...] solutions for the aerospace, defense, transportation, electrical and electronics, and medical sectors. Further, it provides automation and precision engineering solutions. It offers its products through owned and franchised retail stores, as well as online. The company was formerly known as Titan Industries Limited and changed its name to Titan Company Limited in August 2013. Titan Company Limited was incorporated in 1984 and is based in Bengaluru, India. [...] Fastrack smart, SF, Titan World, and Helios brands; jewellery products under the Mia, CaratLane, Tanishq, and Zoya brands; and eyecare products under the Titan Glares, Titan Eye+ and Fastrack Eyecare brands. It also offers sarees, dress materials, and ready-to-wear kurtas under the Taneira brand; perfumes under the SKINN brand; belts and wallets under the TITAN brand; and bags under the Fastrack and IRTH brands. In addition, the company provides manufacturing services and automation solutions","score":0.74807674},{"title":"Titan Company Ltd share price | About Titan Company | Key Insights - Screener","url":"https://www.screener.in/company/TITAN/consolidated","content":"About\n\nTitan Company Ltd is among India’s most respected lifestyle companies. It has established leadership positions in the Watches, Jewellery and Eyewear categories led by its trusted brands and differentiated customer experience. It was founded in 1984 as a joint-venture between TATA Group and Tamilnadu Industrial Development Corporation (TIDCO). (\n\nKey Points [...] Key Points\n\nPart of the Tata Group( (   \n The company benefits from its association with the Tata Group, one of India’s most established and diversified business conglomerates. As of FY26, the Tata Group held a 25% stake in the company, including a 21% shareholding through Tata Sons Pvt Ltd., while Tamil Nadu Industrial Development Corporation Limited (TIDCO) held 28%.\n\nWebsite   BSE   NSE","score":0.7348247}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:06.495Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"ec965b08-9a77-47ec-b806-2f3bedfa6cdb","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2529,"result":[{"title":"Jewelry","url":"https://images.assettype.com/bloombergquint/2024-06/ccf461f1-7931-43a1-bd39-7618c2b4aed6/Motilal_Oswal_Jewlery_Thematic_Note.pdf","content":"(in sourcing, studded ratio, youth-centric focus, and reinvestment strategy), has continued to outperform other branded players. The brand recall and business moat are not easily replicable; therefore, Tanishq’s competitive edge will remain strong in the category. The store count reached to 3,035 stores as of Mar’24 and expansion story remains intact.  Titan’s EBITDA margin has been under pressure during FY24 owing to a lower studded mix. It will be critical to monitor the margin outlook amid [...] 107 124 149 217 337 457 FY21 FY22 FY23 FY24 FY25E FY26E No. of Store in India CAGR~34% 30 30 33 36 41 46 FY21 FY22 FY23 FY24 FY25E FY26E No. of Store in ME CAGR~9% Jewelry: Transcending tradition; adorning fashion June 2024 38 Exhibit 35: KALYAN's showroom center presence across India Jewelry: Transcending tradition; adorning fashion June 2024 39 Overview of the India business India is the primary focus and growth market for KALYAN  Since the IPO in 2021, KALYAN has expanded quite aggressively [...] growth for Pan-Indian brands such as KALYAN and Tanishq.  KALYAN’s success in the non-southern markets has boosted its confidence in faster store expansion. Its goal is to capitalize on the popularity of studded jewelry in the non-southern markets.  The studded jewelry share in India is 22% for southern and 35% for non-southern markets. Studded jewelry operates at a higher gross margin of ~35% in India (non-southern > southern margin) vs. plain gold jewelry (at 11-12%). Hyper-local strategies","score":0.93086797},{"title":"Jewelry Market Size, Share & Industry Trends. 2033","url":"https://www.persistencemarketresearch.com/market-research/jewelry-market.asp","content":"March 2024: Tiffany & Co. (LVMH) launched its \"Tiffany Lock\" collection expansion targeting male and gender-neutral consumers, marking a strategic push into the growing men's fine jewelry segment globally.\n November 2024: Titan Company's Tanishq announced plans to expand its retail footprint to over 500 stores in India, reinforcing its leadership in the organized branded jewelry segment as formalization accelerates. [...] India accounts for 12–14% of global jewelry revenues and is growing at one of the highest rates regionally, at an estimated CAGR of 7.2% through 2033, driven by one of the youngest demographic profiles globally and a deeply entrenched culture of gold gifting. The All India Gem and Jewellery Domestic Council (GJC) estimates over 500,000 jewelry retailers operate in India, with branded chains rapidly expanding their share. Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) mandatory hallmarking regulation [...] Signet Jewelers, the world's largest specialty jewelry retailer, operates over 2,700 store locations across North America, UK, and Australia, reflecting the continued commercial viability of physical stores. Local and family-run jewelers continue to dominate in India, China, and the Middle East, supported by trust, craft reputation, and personalized customer service. Point-of-sale financing, trade-in programs, and in-store customization further differentiate physical retail from online","score":0.85008353},{"title":"Jewelry Market Size, Share, Growth & Trends, 2026-2034","url":"https://www.fortunebusinessinsights.com/jewelry-market-102107","content":"September 2022 – Chaulaz Heritage Jewellery, an Indian designer ornament brand, strengthened its bridal portfolio by launching the ‘Basra’ collection — the hand-crafted heritage range includes nose pins, earrings, necklaces, and pendants. The brand also customizes and sells antique ornaments online through its website and social media platforms. [...] January 2023 – Tanishq, a Titan Ltd-owned jewelry brand, entered the U.S. market by opening its first store in New Jersey. The store houses over 6,500 jewels designs in 18 and 22-karat gold and diamond. [...] The advancement of digital media that promotes high fashion through reality shows, movies, music videos, and others has influenced the global population to be more inclined toward fashion goods, including ornament products. Moreover, many companies are extending their distribution network and opening new stores worldwide. In February 2024, Aditya Birla Group, an Indian international corporation, launched its new jewelry business under the brand name ‘Novel Jewels Ltd.’\n\n## RESTRAINING FACTORS","score":0.751375},{"title":"Jewelry market in India- statistics & facts | Statista","url":"https://www.statista.com/topics/5031/jewelry-market-in-india","content":"Share of gems and jewelry market in India in 2023, by material type\n\nShare of gems and jewelry market in India 2023, by material type\n\nShare of gems and jewelry market in India in 2023, by material type\n\nMarket share of jewelry across India as of 2024, by region \n\nMarket share of jewelry in India 2024, by region\n\nMarket share of jewelry across India as of 2024, by region\n\nMarket share of jewelry across India in 2024, by occasion\n\nMarket share of jewelry in India 2024, by occasion [...] Total revenue of Kalyan Jewellers India Limited from 2017 to 2025 (in billion Indian rupees)\n\nRevenue from operation of P. N. Gadgil Jewellers Limited from financial year 2018 to 2025 (in billion Indian rupees)\n\nRevenue from operation of P. N. Gadgil Jewellers FY 2018-2025\n\nRevenue from operation of P. N. Gadgil Jewellers Limited from financial year 2018 to 2025 (in billion Indian rupees)\n\nDomestic revenue of PC Jeweller Limited from financial year 2012 to 2024 (in billion Indian rupees) [...] PC Jeweller's domestic revenue FY 2012-2024\n\nDomestic revenue of PC Jeweller Limited from financial year 2012 to 2024 (in billion Indian rupees)\n\n## Key insights\n\nMarket size of gems and jewelry in India from 2020 to 2024, with estimates until 2029 (in trillion Indian rupees)\n\nDetailed statistics\n\nMarket size of gems and jewelry India 2020-2029\n\nSize of online jewelry market in India for 2020, with projections for 2029 (in billion Indian rupees)\n\nDetailed statistics","score":0.6141863},{"title":"Top 10 Jewellery Brands in India 2026: Proven Best Picks","url":"https://www.globalbrandsmagazine.com/jewellery-brands-in-india","content":"There is no audited brand-by-brand market-share table for Indian jewellery. Published estimates do exist — Motilal Oswal’s June 2024 thematic put Malabar at 8.0% and Titan at 7.1% of the total market in FY24 — but they rest on an estimated denominator, because more than half the market is unorganised. Titan tells investors it holds about 8.5% of the whole market and wants roughly 11% by FY30. Kalyan’s own deck claims about 7% — but of the organised market only, sourced to MOFSL. Those two [...] It is the largest jewellery brand in India by revenue and by store count, and Titan has set out a public target of roughly 11% of the whole Indian market by FY30, against about 8.5% today.\n It itemises the actual making charge in rupees on every product page, so the labour premium is visible before you pay. Among the legacy chains only Senco, Malabar and PC Jeweller match that. [...] Goods 2023 edition, published in February 2024 on FY2022 sales, which put it 19th worldwide.","score":0.6108487}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:06.702Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"1fac9d5e-322b-4691-b145-b8e652651dab","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2734,"result":[{"title":"About us","url":"https://sencogoldanddiamonds.com/about-us","content":"# The History\n\nSenco Gold and Diamonds is a brand owned by Senco Gold Limited (‘the Company’) with a legacy of over 85+ years. Our company was incorporated as Senco Gold Private Limited on August 22, 1994, in Kolkata, West Bengal, under the provisions of the Companies Act, 1956.\n\nLater, in order to expand its activities in the field of jewellery business, the Company was converted to a public limited company in August 2007 with the name, Senco Gold Limited. [...] ##### Art Of Jewellery\n\nAbout Us - Senco Gold and Diamonds\n\nWest Bengal is a prominent jewellery manufacturing hub in east India, reputed for lightweight and handmade jewellery. The karigars of the state are skilled and known for their craftsmanship. Apart from catering to jewellery demand in the state, jewellery manufacturers from this region also cater to neighbouring states and other parts of the country. It is also one of the major gold and diamond jewellery exporting regions in India. [...] Suvankar Sen is the Managing Director and CEO of Senco Gold Limited. He holds a BSc degree in Economics from Calcutta University and a post-graduate diploma in Business Management from the Institute of Management & Technology, Ghaziabad. He has been associated with the Company since 2005. Under his leadership and strategic direction, Senco Gold got listed on NSE, BSE in July 2023. The company’s turnover also reached 4,000 Cr in FY2023. Suvankar Sen is also a member of GJEPC India (Gem &","score":0.8914433},{"title":"SENCO GOLD LIMITED - 2026 Company Profile, Financials & Shareholding - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/legal-entities/india/senco-gold-limited/__cH9OAPulmOjnbPbHZLVt7fKJS4i56z1yuxcso4xHfVg","content":"SENCO GOLD LIMITED