{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:08.097Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"bd6fa5ad-8b45-4231-9e6d-94513bdc2135","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":4132,"result":[{"title":"Kalyan Jewellers targets opening 170 new showrooms in FY2026","url":"https://www.newindianexpress.com/business/2025/Jan/07/kalyan-jewellers-targets-opening-170-new-showrooms-in-fy2026","content":"Other prominent brands in this space include Tata Group's Tanishq, Joyalukkas, Malabar Gold and Diamonds, PC Jeweller, and Senco Gold. Additionally, the Aditya Birla Group entered the jewellery market last year, further intensifying competition.\n\nHealthy growth\n\nKalyan Jewellers said that it recorded revenue growth of 39% in the October-December quarter when compared to the same period in the previous financial year. [...] Pure gold! Even record prices fail to dampen Kerala's grand love affair with the yellow metal\n\nKalyan Jewellers' aggressive expansion comes amid rising competition and an increasing consumer preference for branded players.\n\nAccording to financial services firm Motilal Oswal, the Indian jewellery sector has witnessed a shift of over 14% towards organised players, with their market share growing to 36-38% over the past five years. [...] Its India operations witnessed revenue growth of 41% during Q3 FY2025 as compared to Q3 FY2024, led by strong festive and wedding demand across both gold and studded categories.\n\nIn the Middle East, the company witnessed revenue growth of 22% in Q3FY25.\n\nThe Middle East contributed 11% to Kalyan’s consolidated revenue for the recently concluded quarter.\n\nKalyan also launched its first showroom (Company Owned Company Operated) in the United States of America during the quarter.","score":0.6016175},{"title":"From Kalyan to Malabar, Indian jewellery brands deepen foothold in $14 billion GCC market - Storyboard18","url":"https://www.storyboard18.com/brand-marketing/from-kalyan-to-malabar-indian-jewellery-brands-