{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:21.882Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"76d60ed7-52e7-4402-8d1e-c6d4013405b0","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2421,"result":[{"title":"Quick Commerce Startup Snabbit Funding Soars to $5.5 Million: Revolutionizing 15-Minute Home Services in India","url":"https://sellerrocket.in/quick-commerce-startup-snabbit-funding.html","content":"Mumbai-based quick commerce startup snabbit has successfully raised $5.5 million in Series A funding to revolutionize India's on-demand home services market. Founded in 2024 by former Zepto executive Aayush Agarwal, Snabbit is pioneering a new approach in the quick commerce sector by offering 15-minute home services like cleaning, dishwashing, laundry, and kitchen preparations. [...] The $5.5 million Series A funding round was led by Elevation Capital, with participation from existing investor Nexus Venture Partners. This follows an earlier $1 million seed investment by Nexus Venture Partners in early 2024.\n\nSeveral prominent angel investors also participated in this round, including:\n\n • Vidit Aatrey and Sanjeev Barnwal (Meesho co-founders)\n • Gaurav Munjal (Unacademy co-founder)\n • Niraj Singh (Spinny founder) [...] This funding round comes at a pivotal time when India's quick commerce sector is experiencing explosive growth, with the broader market expected to reach $5 billion by 2025, according to industry projections.","score":0.8974172},{"title":"Indian quick commerce raises Rs 335.32 Crore in 2025, ...","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/debonkar-roymarketing_debcreates-india-strategy-activity-7363066691586592769-L8yk","content":"87 Indian companies have raised Rs 335.32 Crore in 2025 so far for quick commerce! In 2024, quick commerce secured Rs 11,620 crore in funding. The sector is evolving beyond food and grocery delivery, expanding into electronics, household services, and ultra-fast fulfillment promises ranging from 10 minutes to 1 hour. Here are 5 facts about the Indian quick commerce market: 1. Current market value is expected to reach Rs 29,300 crore in 2025. 2. Projected growth for quick commerce space is >4.5% [...] unit economics by leading players. -Expansion beyond metro cities. - Diversification into new product categories. Despite the funding crunch globally, India's venture capital market rebounded in 2024, hitting Rs 1,15,000 crore in funding. Blinkit, Instamart, Zepto, bigbasket, and Dunzo Daily are the major companies operating in this market. With 50+ quick commerce startups, India leads globally, followed by the US with 15 startups, and the UK with 13. The presence of 87 companies in the funding [...] space is >4.5% CAGR to reach Rs 36,500 crore by 2030. 3. It is projected to grow by 16.07% (2025-2029) resulting in a market volume of Rs 8,20,000 crore in 2029. 4. According to Redseer, industry experts predict a 40-45% GMV CAGR for the next 3 years. 5. According to Bain, India's quick commerce market will surge over 40% annually until 2030. The quick commerce sector witnessed a funding boom since 2024 due to: - Investor confidence in the ultra-fast delivery model. - Proven unit economics by","score":0.8865877},{"title":"Quick Commerce - 2026 Market & Investments Trends","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/trending-business-models/startups-in-quick-commerce/__8Em61CsQQeo5EmPsP-wGXgDzh5yotwlRuXpxOVdqw6Y","content":"| Year | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| 2026 | $507M |\n| 2025 | $2.06B |\n| 2024 | $2B |\n| 2023 | $1.08B |\n| 2022 | $3.28B |\n| 2021 | $11.9B |\n| 2020 | $3.64B |\n| 2019 | $3.84B |\n| 2018 | $4.79B |\n| 2017 | $1.79B |\n\n### Total funding across countries in Quick Commerce\n\nIn the last 10 years, Quick Commerce startups in United States have recieved the highest funding among all countries - $10B. India follows with $8.9B and Germany with $2.8B. [...] | Country | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| United States | $10B |\n| India | $8.9B |\n| Germany | $2.8B |\n| United Kingdom | $1.76B |\n| Saudi Arabia | $286M |\n| Indonesia | $148M |\n| Australia | $23M |\n| Philippines | $21.1M |\n| Canada | $9.1M |\n| Italy | $3M |\n\n### Total funding amount raised by stage in Quick Commerce\n\nOver the last 10 years, Quick Commerce have seen $242M into Seed Stage funding rounds, $4.24B into Early Stage funding rounds and $26.2B go into Late Stage funding rounds. [...] | Year | No. of companies |\n --- |\n| 2026 | 6 |\n| 2025 | 29 |\n| 2024 | 32 |\n| 2023 | 16 |\n| 2022 | 17 |\n| 2021 | 41 |\n| 2020 | 38 |\n| 2019 | 13 |\n| 2018 | 9 |\n| 2017 | 6 |\n\n### Companies founded across countries in Quick Commerce\n\nIndia has 126 Quick Commerce startups, the most by any country, followed by United States which has 16 startups and United Kingdom which has 13.","score":0.8464638},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/29/zepto-confidential-ipo-filing-india-quick-commerce-instamart-swiggy-blinkit-zomato-eternal-flipkart-amazon.html?msockid=204eacd0836e69a202fdba03820968af","content":"Walmart-owned Flipkart also launched its quick commerce service in 2024. Indian food delivery companies, Swiggy and Eternal, which owns Zomato and Blinkit, were among the first movers in this space.\n\nOver the last three to five years, several companies have entered the quick commerce market in India and are \" indulging in a price war\" as firms chase a large total addressable market, Taurani said. [...] Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details. [...] Quick commerce, which promises deliveries in as little as 10 minutes, has become one of India's most competitive consumer internet sectors.\n\nWhile e-commerce giant Amazon has long offered same-day delivery services in India through \"Amazon Fresh\", the launch of its 15-minute \"Amazon Now\" service in June marked an aggressive shift into a crowded space.\n\nThe Jeff Bezos-owned U.S. company has started its quick commerce operations across Indian's three major cities—Mumbai, Delhi and Bengaluru.","score":0.798643},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/29/zepto-confidential-ipo-filing-india-quick-commerce-instamart-swiggy-blinkit-zomato-eternal-flipkart-amazon.html?msockid=0a78734812516d9520186599135b6c8a","content":"Walmart-owned Flipkart also launched its quick commerce service in 2024. Indian food delivery companies, Swiggy and Eternal, which owns Zomato and Blinkit, were among the first movers in this space.\n\nOver the last three to five years, several companies have entered the quick commerce market in India and are \" indulging in a price war\" as firms chase a large total addressable market, Taurani said. [...] Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details.","score":0.798643}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:21.884Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"df4ba591-33cb-4c5c-b86d-d98ff3f36978","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2424,"result":[{"title":"Zepto Revenue, Valuation, Funding & Investors | Multiples","url":"https://multiples.vc/private-comps/zepto","content":"and Kaivalya Vohra, it raised $340 million in primary equity capital in August 2024, led by General Catalyst ($250 million) and Mars Growth Capital ($50 million), with participation from Epiq Capital, Dragon Fund, and existing investors like DST Global, Lightspeed, and StepStone. This followed a $665 million June 2024 round at $3.6 billion post-money, bringing two-month total to $1 billion and overall funding to ~$1.6 billion. The August round valued Zepto at $5 billion post-money ($4.6 billion [...] million in a highly oversubscribed Series F round on June 20, 2024, at a post-money valuation of $3.6 billion, more than doubling from $1.4 billion nine months prior. The round was co-led by existing investors Glade Brook Capital Partners, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group, with participation from new investors Avenir, Lightspeed Venture Partners, and Avra, alongside Goodwater Capital, Lachy Groom, Contrary, and DST Global. Zepto operates around 350 dark stores across 10 cities, [...] ($665M in June 2024 led by Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group to prepare for IPO), Series H ($340M in August 2024 led by General Catalyst and Mars Growth Capital to bolster finances pre-IPO), and more recent pre-IPO rounds in 2024-2025 reaching valuations of $5B to $7B. Total funding across all rounds amounts to approximately $2.93 billion as of October 2025. Later developments show Zepto scaling order volume 200% over 18 months by late 2025, achieving store-level","score":0.8987045},{"title":"Zepto raises $350 Mn, surpasses $1.35 Bn in funding for 2024","url":"https://entrackr.com/news/zepto-raises-350-mn-surpasses-135-bn-in-funding-for-2024-7599303","content":"Celebrity investors such as Sachin Tendulkar and Abhishek Bachchan also participated in this round.\n\nWith this, Zepto has raised a total of $1.35 billion in 2024 and $1.85 billion since its inception. In August, it secured $340 million in funding at a $5 billion valuation. However, the latest round did not result in any change to its valuation. [...] Quick commerce company Zepto has raised $350 million in a funding round led by Motilal Oswal Private Wealth, with participation from notable investors, including Raamdeo Agarwal, the Taparia Family Office, Mankind Pharma Family Office, RP Sanjiv Goenka Group, Cello Family Office, Haldiram Snacks Family Office, Sekhsaria Family Office, Kalyan Family Office, Happy Forgings Family Office, and Mothers Recipe Family Office (Desai Brothers). [...] ## With this, Zepto has raised a total of $1.35 billion in 2024 and $1.85 billion since its inception. In August, it secured $340 million in funding at a $5 billion valuation.\n\nauthor-image/entrackr/media/member_avatars/2024/10/21/2024-10-21t083427265z-harsh-sir-768x768.png )\n\n Follow Us\n\nzepto/entrackr/media/post_attachments/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Zepto-funding.jpg)","score":0.8893851},{"title":"How Much Did Zepto Raise? Funding & Key Investors","url":"https://www.clay.com/dossier/zepto-funding","content":"Motivation Behind the Round: To support growth and operational scaling, including expanding dark stores and Zepto Café services.\n8. Series G\n    Amount Raised: USD 340,000,000\n    Date: August 2024\n    Lead Investors: General Catalyst\n    Valuation at Round: USD 5 billion\n    Motivation Behind the Round: To continue scaling operations and expanding services across India.\n9. Series G (Extension)\n    Amount Raised: USD 350,000,000\n    Date: November 2024 [...] Lead Investors: Goodwater Capital, Nexus Venture Partners\n    Valuation at Round: USD 1.4 billion\n    Motivation Behind the Round: To enhance the platform's technology and expand its market reach.\n7. Series F\n    Amount Raised: USD 665,000,000\n    Date: June 2024\n    Lead Investors: Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, StepStone Group\n    Valuation at Round: USD 3.6 billion [...] General Catalyst\n  + Details: General Catalyst is a venture capital firm that invests in early-stage and growth-stage companies globally. It led Zepto's Series G round in August 2024 at a $5 billion valuation.\n  + Investment Focus Areas: Technology, healthcare, consumer services.\n  + Notable Investments: Airbnb, Stripe, Snap.\n Lightspeed Venture Partners","score":0.8886914},{"title":"Zepto - 2026 Funding Rounds & List of Investors - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/zepto/__vOTzafGt-8S4kwYniiZ_yRogd6c_Jsw_vRD0gckHtfE/funding-and-investors","content":"| Nov 07, 2024 | $350M | Series G | $7.12B  Motilal Oswal Private Wealth | Motilal Oswal Asset Management Company, Claypond Capital, Happy Forgings, Mothers Recipe, Raamdeo Ramgopal Agarawal, Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar, Motilal Oswal Financial Services, Ananta Capital, Rajeev Juneja, Pradeep Ghisulal Rathod, Vinila Oswal Family Trust, Raamdeo Agarawal, Jaydev Mukund Mody, Varun Daga, Kemfin Services, Ravi Modi Family Trust, Compact Structure Fund, Baldota Group, Eudora Ventures, SHREE CAPITAL, Big [...] | Aug 29, 2024 | $340M | Series G | $5B | 5.2x | General Catalyst | Epiq Capital, StepStone Group, DST Global, Contrary Capital, Dragon Funds, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Raamdeo Agarawal |\n| Jun 21, 2024 | $665M | Series F | $3.6B | 3.9x | avra, Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, StepStone Group, Goodwater Capital, Avenir Growth Capital, Lightspeed | Lachy Groom | [...] | Date of Funding | Funding Amount | Round Name | Post-Money Valuation | Revenue Multiple | Lead Investors | Other Investors |\n ---  ---  --- \n| Oct 16, 2025 | $300M | Series H | $6.88B  General Catalyst, CalPERS | Goodwater Capital, Glade Brook Capital, Lightspeed Venture Partners, StepStone Group, Avenir Growth Capital, Azo4, Zpt Holdings, Mangum, avra, Contrary, Nexus Venture Partners |\n| Aug 13, 2025 | $45.6M | Series G | $7B | 3.7x  Motilal Oswal Financial Services |","score":0.8858788},{"title":"Zepto raises $450M at $7B valuation as Indian quick-commerce market heats up | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2025/10/16/zepto-raises-450-million-at-7-billion-valuation-as-indian-quick-commerce-market-heats-up","content":"Zepto competes with other quick-commerce players such as Eternal’s (formerly Zomato) Blinkit, Swiggy Instamart, and Tata-owned BigBasket — all part of publicly listed companies. The startup has been on a funding spree as it picked up $1.3 billion in a span of several months last year. Since Zepto’s last funding round in November 2024, Swiggy made its public debut on India’s stock exchange, and Blinkit surpassed Zomato in gross order value (the total value of customer orders) for Q1 2025.","score":0.8051581}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:21.904Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"773f50cd-bf02-43af-be0d-25bcb0b342dd","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2443,"result":[{"title":"Swiggy Funding 2026 – Total Funding, Rounds & Investors","url":"https://inc42.com/company/swiggy/funding","content":"datalabs-logo\n\n### \n\n### \n\nSwiggy-logo\n\nCompany\n\nSwiggy-logo\nSwiggy-logo\n\n# Swiggy - Total Funding, Funding Over Time, Funding By Rounds and More\n\nFounded in 2014, Swiggy is a food delivery aggregator platform. The foodtech company has its subsidiary company to compete with Blinkit, named Swiggy Instamart, with its operations in over 100 cities....View more\n\nFunding stage:\n\nUndisclosed\n\nLast funding:\n\n29/09/2024\n\nTotal funding:\n\n$3.58 Bn+\n\nRevenue:\n\nInvestors\n\nEmployee count:\n\n29,201\n\nLast 90d [...] ## FAQs on Funding of Swiggy\n\n### What is the total funding raised by Swiggy ?\n\n### What is the total funding raised by Swiggy ?\n\nFoodtech Funded Swiggy has raised a total funding of $3.58 billion as of 30 September 2024 across 18 rounds. Find the details around funding rounds, participating investors, and other insights of Swiggy here...\n\n### How many funding rounds does Swiggy have ?\n\n### How many funding rounds does Swiggy have ? [...] Swiggy has raised a total of $3.58 billion across 18 funding rounds and the last round was raised on 30 September 2024.\n\n### Who are the lead investors in Swiggy?\n\n### Who are the lead investors in Swiggy?\n\nSwiggy's key investors include Accel, Prosus Ventures, Elevation Capital and 2 others.\n\n### What was Swiggy's latest funding round?\n\n### What was Swiggy's latest funding round?\n\nSwiggy's latest funding round was an undisclosed amount in Late Stage, raised on 30 September 2024.","score":0.8747745},{"title":"India's Swiggy bets on Instamart model shift, mirroring main rival Blinkit; eyes margin boost","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/india/indias-swiggy-bets-instamart-model-shift-mirroring-main-rival-blinkit-eyes-2026-08-20","content":"Swiggy, which went public in 2024, is yet to turn profitable. Earlier this month, it set a fiscal 2031 target to turn earnings per share positive.\n\n## RISING COSTS\n\nThe shift, however, would result in higher working ​capital to fund purchases and ​manage stock, brokerage Jefferies ⁠said in a note. Eternal said last month that working capital at Blinkit was \"largely driven by inventory ownership\". [...] Swiggy and Eternal have been investing heavily in quick commerce ​to expand beyond groceries into higher-margin categories, jostling for consumer attention alongside deep-pocketed rivals ​such as Amazon ⁠India (AMZN.O), opens new tab , Walmart's Flipkart and Reliance (RELI.NS), opens new tab.\n\nSmaller rival Zepto is looking to raise up to $837 million in a highly anticipated public listing this year. [...] Swiggy has said the transition could add about 80 basis points to Instamart's contribution margin, which measures revenue after variable costs. \"That's about 4-5 rupees an order — about a sixth of the 30 rupees an order it needs ​to break even,\" said Samarth Patel, associate vice president, Equirus Securities.\n\nAdvertisement · Scroll to continue\n\nInstamart's first-quarter contribution margin was negative 0.2%, against negative ​1.8% in the previous quarter.","score":0.81025416},{"title":"zomato swiggy blinkit zepto ola uber news: Latest News & Videos, Photos about zomato swiggy blinkit zepto ola uber news | The Economic Times - Page 1","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/topic/zomato-swiggy-blinkit-zepto-ola-uber-news","content":"How Ather powered past Ola; Apple's first foldable iPhone\n\n  ## How Ather powered past Ola; Apple's first foldable iPhone\n\n  Ather Energy has surpassed Ola Electric in sales and other metrics. This and more in today’s ETtech Top 5.\n\n  Swish raises $24 million funding, bets on repeat orders to scale up 10-minute food delivery\n\n  ## Swish raises $24 million funding, bets on repeat orders to scale up 10-minute food delivery [...] Swish, a 10-minute food delivery startup, has raised $24 million to expand its kitchen network and supply chain. The two-year-old company has crossed one million monthly orders, with 70–75% of revenue coming from repeat users. It operates 250 stock-keeping units (SKUs) across 20 categories in 50 pincodes.\n\n  Flipkart launches standalone Minutes app, rolls out food delivery pilot ahead of BBD sale\n\n  ## Flipkart launches standalone Minutes app, rolls out food delivery pilot ahead of BBD sale [...] Happy Wednesday! Amazon and Flipkart have broadened their bets as quick commerce platforms chip away at their share of user base. This and more in today’s ETtech Morning Dispatch.\n\n  Rapid food delivery startup Swish to raise $20-25 million led by Bertelsmann India: Sources\n\n  ## Rapid food delivery startup Swish to raise $20-25 million led by Bertelsmann India: Sources","score":0.59089786},{"title":"Quick Commerce Profitability: Blinkit, Swiggy & Zepto","url":"https://laffaz.com/blinkit-swiggy-zepto-profitability-quick-commerce","content":"To be fair to Swiggy, it isn’t standing still. The company restructured Instamart into a separate subsidiary, raised ₹10,000 crore through a qualified institutional placement in December 2025, and has been quietly shifting its own model toward first-party inventory — an acknowledgment, as the Blinkit CEO himself noted, that the inventory-led model is inevitable. The pivot is right. The timeline is just slower than investors want.\n\n## Zepto: The IPO That Asks You to Believe in the Future [...] The counterargument from sceptics is harder to dismiss. Zepto’s cash reserves of $600–700 million as of March 2026 compare unfavourably with Blinkit’s $1.9 billion and Swiggy’s $1.7 billion. In a capital war — and this is very much a capital war — that gap is significant. Zepto raised $450 million in October 2025, but the runway tightens if the IPO is delayed, the market stays volatile, or competition forces another round of defensive fee-cutting. [...] Swiggy’s investors haven’t been patient. The stock had fallen 26% in calendar year 2026 by early March, touching an all-time low, as public market shareholders — who watched Swiggy go public in November 2024 — grew increasingly frustrated with the gap between revenue growth and profitability. The company’s share price dropped nearly 8% intraday following the Q3 results.","score":0.5758033},{"title":"SWIGGY INSTAMART PRIVATE LIMITED - 2026 Company Profile - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/legal-entities/india/swiggy-instamart-private-limited/__TKi-aQjuXlJ-YRC_0v-3fDvLnK5_Fd2sbYR49LNH1As","content":"SWIGGY INSTAMART PRIVATE LIMITED is a Private Limited Company and was incorporated on Sep 12, 2025 in India. It is registered at Registrar of Companies, ROC Bangalore. Its registered address is No.55 Sy No.8-14, GF, I&J Block, Embassy Tech, Bellandur, Bangalore, Bangalore South, Karnataka, India, 560103.  Its corporate identification number is (CIN) U47912KA2025PTC208374 and its current status is Active. Its industry classification as per MCA is retail sale via e-commerce. [...] SWIGGY INSTAMART PRIVATE LIMITED's authorised share capital is ₹10L and its paid up capital is ₹1L. The current board of directors of SWIGGY INSTAMART PRIVATE LIMITED comprises Sri Harsha Majety and Nandan Reddy.\n\n## Contact Details for SWIGGY INSTAMART PRIVATE LIMITED\n\n## Documents of SWIGGY INSTAMART PRIVATE LIMITED15 mins\n\n### Recent Filings\n\nBelow are the most recent filings submitted by the company:","score":0.2862595}]}
