{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:21.931Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"ab42f22d-6540-4e15-928b-4f723a14efee","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2471,"result":[{"title":"Quick Commerce Powers India’s US$13.7B Venture Capital Growth","url":"https://www.india-briefing.com/news/quick-commerce-powers-indias-us13-7b-vc-growth-in-2024-36466.html","content":"India’s venture capital landscape experienced a strong resurgence in 2024, signaling renewed investor confidence and a revitalized startup ecosystem. Venture funding surged to US$13.7 billion—marking a 1.4-times jump from 2023—driven by robust economic indicators, regulatory reforms, and a thriving technology sector. As global investors continue to prioritize India as a key growth market, this sets the stage for stronger deal activity in 2025. [...] India’s technology ecosystem continues to thrive, with technology-driven segments such as consumer technology, software and SaaS, and fintech emerging as the primary focus areas for investors. These segments accounted for more than 60 percent of the total VC funding in 2024. The report notes that among these, consumer technology stood out, with funding increasing 2.3 times to US$5.4 billion. This surge was largely attributed to major deals in sub-sectors like business-to-consumer (B2C) [...] Source: Bain & Company; PitchBook; Venture Intelligence; AVCJ; VCCEdge\n\n\\Total funding over different rounds in 2024.\n\n## Trends in deal values and funding stages\n\nThe average deal value remained largely stable across stages. Seed-stage deals grew from 628 in 2023 to 756 in 2024, with average funding rising from US$1.3 million to US$1.6 million.","score":0.8684817},{"title":"Quick Commerce Industry","url":"https://www.chryseum.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Quick-Commerce-Industry.pdf","content":"in millions Source: JM QC Report Zepto: Funding History Date Fund Raise Valuation (in $ Millions) Investors Aug-24 $340 Million 5,000 General Catalyst, Mars Growth Jun-24 $665 Million 3,600 DST Global, Avenir Growth Capital, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Avra Nov-23 $31 million NA GoodWater Capital, Nexus VP, Mangum Aug-23 $200 million 1,400 StepStone Group, GoodWater Capital, Nexus VP, Glade Brook, Lachy Groom May-22 $200 million 900 Y-Combinator, Nexus VP, Glade Brook, Kaiser Permanente, Lachy [...] The Quick Commerce Industry In India Market size is estimated at USD 3.34 billion in 2024, and is expected to reach USD 9.95 billion by 2029, growing at a CAGR of greater than 4.5% during the forecast period (2024-2029).\n~USD 45 bn The quick commerce market in India currently exhibits a penetration rate of only 7% of the potential market, with a total addresable market at $45b, surpassing that of food delivery, indicating that a significant opportunity remains untapped. [...] GMV IN $BILLION ~6 ~6 3.3 81.8% +5 Mn Additional Dark Stores Monthly Transacting Users Monthly Transacting Users The Quick Commerce Industry In India Market size is estimated at USD 3.34 billion in 2024, and is expected to reach USD 9.95 billion by 2029, growing at a CAGR of greater than 4.5% during the forecast period (2024-2029).Source: Redseer Supply Chain - Quick Commerce Source: Zomato presentation Eg:Blinkit QC platforms are partnering with manufacturers for direct sourcing, to bypass the","score":0.8684817},{"title":"Indian quick commerce raises Rs 335.32 Crore in 2025, ...","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/debonkar-roymarketing_debcreates-india-strategy-activity-7363066691586592769-L8yk","content":"87 Indian companies have raised Rs 335.32 Crore in 2025 so far for quick commerce! In 2024, quick commerce secured Rs 11,620 crore in funding. The sector is evolving beyond food and grocery delivery, expanding into electronics, household services, and ultra-fast fulfillment promises ranging from 10 minutes to 1 hour. Here are 5 facts about the Indian quick commerce market: 1. Current market value is expected to reach Rs 29,300 crore in 2025. 2. Projected growth for quick commerce space is >4.5% [...] unit economics by leading players. -Expansion beyond metro cities. - Diversification into new product categories. Despite the funding crunch globally, India's venture capital market rebounded in 2024, hitting Rs 1,15,000 crore in funding. Blinkit, Instamart, Zepto, bigbasket, and Dunzo Daily are the major companies operating in this market. With 50+ quick commerce startups, India leads globally, followed by the US with 15 startups, and the UK with 13. The presence of 87 companies in the funding [...] space is >4.5% CAGR to reach Rs 36,500 crore by 2030. 3. It is projected to grow by 16.07% (2025-2029) resulting in a market volume of Rs 8,20,000 crore in 2029. 4. According to Redseer, industry experts predict a 40-45% GMV CAGR for the next 3 years. 5. According to Bain, India's quick commerce market will surge over 40% annually until 2030. The quick commerce sector witnessed a funding boom since 2024 due to: - Investor confidence in the ultra-fast delivery model. - Proven unit economics by","score":0.85567063},{"title":"Quick Commerce - 2026 Market & Investments Trends","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/trending-business-models/startups-in-quick-commerce/__8Em61CsQQeo5EmPsP-wGXgDzh5yotwlRuXpxOVdqw6Y","content":"| Year | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| 2026 | $507M |\n| 2025 | $2.06B |\n| 2024 | $2B |\n| 2023 | $1.08B |\n| 2022 | $3.28B |\n| 2021 | $11.9B |\n| 2020 | $3.64B |\n| 2019 | $3.84B |\n| 2018 | $4.79B |\n| 2017 | $1.79B |\n\n### Total funding across countries in Quick Commerce\n\nIn the last 10 years, Quick Commerce startups in United States have recieved the highest funding among all countries - $10B. India follows with $8.9B and Germany with $2.8B. [...] | Country | Total Funding |\n --- |\n| United States | $10B |\n| India | $8.9B |\n| Germany | $2.8B |\n| United Kingdom | $1.76B |\n| Saudi Arabia | $286M |\n| Indonesia | $148M |\n| Australia | $23M |\n| Philippines | $21.1M |\n| Canada | $9.1M |\n| Italy | $3M |\n\n### Total funding amount raised by stage in Quick Commerce\n\nOver the last 10 years, Quick Commerce have seen $242M into Seed Stage funding rounds, $4.24B into Early Stage funding rounds and $26.2B go into Late Stage funding rounds. [...] | Company Stage | No. of companies |\n --- |\n| Founded | 256 |\n| Funded | 105 |\n| Series A+ | 55 |\n| Series B+ | 41 |\n| Series C+ | 35 |\n\n## Funding Trends in Quick Commerce\n\n### Total funding year-on-year in Quick Commerce\n\nQuick Commerce saw a total funding of more than $34.9B in the last 10 years. The most amount of funding was in 2021 at more than $11.9B. There has been a total funding of $507M in 2026 till date.","score":0.750937},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/27/indias-zepto-files-for-ipo-as-quick-commerce-race-heats-up.html","content":"Walmart-owned Flipkart also launched its quick commerce service in 2024. Indian food delivery companies, Swiggy and Eternal, which owns Zomato and Blinkit, were among the first movers in this space.\n\nOver the last three to five years, several companies have entered the quick commerce market in India and are \" indulging in a price war\" as firms chase a large total addressable market, Taurani said. [...] Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details.","score":0.66045773}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:22.060Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"ffd9758b-424e-447d-a9ba-89e5263415c3","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2596,"result":[{"title":"Flipkart Minutes quadruples business as quick-commerce battle intensifies","url":"https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/flipkart-minutes-quadruples-business-as-quick-commerce-battle-intensifies-126091001430_1.html","content":"Flipkart Minutes, the quick-commerce arm of e-commerce giant Flipkart, has quadrupled its business over the past year as it marks two years since its launch in August 2024. The service now operates nearly 1,200 micro-fulfilment centres across more than 150 cities, highlighting the rapid expansion of on-demand delivery in one of the world’s fastest-growing digital markets. The expansion comes ahead of Flipkart’s Big Billion Days sale in October, as the company faces intensifying competition from [...] Since August 2024, Flipkart Minutes has built a partner ecosystem of close to 500 direct-to-consumer (D2C) brands, giving them access to hyperlocal demand and new customer segments. Through partnerships with Farmer Producer Organisations (FPOs), the platform has also connected thousands of farmers directly to consumers, helping them reach new markets and improve price realisation. [...] The new developments at Flipkart Minutes highlight the intensifying battle for scale in the country’s rapidly expanding instant-delivery market. According to a recent CLSA report, Blinkit accounted for close to 30 per cent of dark stores across the country’s top 10 cities and more than 34 per cent nationally and had the leading store count in six of them, with Zepto leading in three of the remaining four. Blinkit’s presence in more than 180 cities, CLSA said, positioned it to capture an","score":0.8430832},{"title":"Flipkart Hyperlocal","url":"https://www.flipkart.com/flipkart-minutes-store?marketplace=HYPERLOCAL","content":"Flipkart Minutes is a quick and easy-to-handle assortment of products for everyday needs, making top-ups and unplanned needs from home simple.","score":0.7811474},{"title":"Flipkart","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flipkart","content":"In October 2024, Flipkart was among the initial partners in the launch of YouTube's Shopping affiliate programme in India, allowing eligible video creators to link products from Flipkart and Myntra, in their content.\n\nIn 2025, the company announced that it would shift its domicile from Singapore to India.\n\nOn 11 September 2026, Flipkart Minutes expanded its operational footprint to approximately 1,200 micro-fulfillment centers spanning over 150 cities.\n\n## Business structure\n\n[edit] [...] In March 2024, Flipkart launched its UPI services, Flipkart UPI, in partnership with Axis Bank.\n\n\n\nIn August 2024, Flipkart entered the quick-commerce market with the introduction of Flipkart Minutes. In the same month, Flipkart-backed super.money launched its mobile application offering credit-first UPI services. [...] 104. ↑ Goel, Samiksha (3 March 2024). \"Flipkart launches digital payments service Flipkart UPI\". mint. Retrieved 25 April 2024.\n105. ↑ \"Flipkart's 10-min quick-commerce service 'Minutes' goes live in Bengaluru\". Business Standard. 5 August 2024. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n106. ↑ \"super.money launches new credit-first UPI app, hits 10 million transactions in beta phase\". CNBCTV18. 22 August 2024. Retrieved 4 May 2025.","score":0.6194488},{"title":"Vaibhav Rustagi Email & Phone Number | Flipkart Head of Revenue and Growth @ Flipkart Minutes Contact Information","url":"https://rocketreach.co/vaibhav-rustagi-email_2047361","content":"### products\n\n   Advanced Search\n   Chrome Extension\n   Edge Extension\n   Bulk Lookups\n   API\n   Integrations\n\n### information\n\n   Pricing\n   Help\n   Reviews\n   User Agreement\n   Privacy Policy\n   Cookie Policy\n   Do Not Sell My Info\n\n### teams\n\n   Features\n   Start Team Plan\n   Custom Plan