{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:22.101Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"e57b88ff-c54c-4dec-9754-897605b06a58","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2639,"result":[{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blinkit","content":"Blinkit is an Indian quick-commerce company owned by Eternal Limited. It was founded in December 2013 and is based in Gurgaon.\n\nCustomers of the company use a mobile app to order groceries and essentials online, which are sourced from the company's dark stores and delivered in 10 minutes. Blinkit operates in 153 cities in India, as of March 2025.\n\nIn 2022, Zomato Limited (now Eternal) acquired Blinkit for US$568 million in an all-stock deal.\n\n## History\n\n[edit] [...] Blinkit\n\n| Formerly | Grofers (2013–2021) |\n| Type | Subsidiary |\n| Industry | Q-commerce |\n| Founded | December 2013; 12 years ago (2013-12) |\n| Founders | Albinder Dhindsa Saurabh Kumar |\n| Headquarters | Gurgaon, Haryana, India |\n| Area served | India |\n| Key people | Albinder Dhindsa (CEO) |\n| Products | Bistro |\n| Services | Online grocer |\n| Revenue | Increase ₹5,206 crore (US$540 million) (FY25) |\n| Parent | Eternal Limited |\n| Website | blinkit.com | [...] In June 2022, a Bengaluru-based web development company called Blinkhit filed a trademark infringement lawsuit against Blinkit.\n\nIn April 2023, hundreds of Blinkit delivery partners in Delhi NCR, where about half of the company's dark stores were located, went on strike after a revision in payout structure resulted in lower earnings for them. This led to a temporary closure of many dark stores.","score":0.90692574},{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/letsblinkit","content":"## Overview\nBlinkit (An Eternal Company) is a grocery and e-commerce platform. We pioneered the doorstep delivery model in India with over 10 million Indians shopping on Blinkit, for everything from grocery staples and vegetables to emergency supplies and electronics, and much more. If our mission interests you, send your CV to future@blinkit.com\n\n### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\nN/A\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nTechnology, Information and Internet [...] ### Company Size\n1,001-5,000 employees  \n29232 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed Blinkit as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\n2013\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: N/A\nLast Round Type: N/A\nTotal Rounds: N/A\nLast Round Raised: N/A\n\n### Investors\nN/A\n\n### Specialties\nN/A\n\n## Locations\nPioneer Square, Sector 62, Golf Course Extension, Blinkit Headquarters, Gurgaon, Haryana 122001, IN\n\n### Get Directions\nDirections [...] # Blinkit\nIndia's Last Minute App ✨ Sell your products on Blinkit via seller.blinkit.com\nTechnology, Information and Internet • Gurgaon, Haryana • 1,772,212 followers • 1,001-5,000 employees","score":0.8747745},{"title":"Blinkit Foods Limited - 2026 Company Profile - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/legal-entities/india/blinkit-foods-limited/__djKNSolKqqiifOhCQSY8wrP4ba7ttguUwe7MUea3s2U","content":"Blinkit Foods Limited is a Public Limited Company and was incorporated on Aug 18, 2025 in India. It is registered at Registrar of Companies, ROC Delhi I. Its registered address is T-19, Basement, Green Park Main, Green Park, South West Delhi, New Delhi, Delhi, India, 110016.  Its corporate identification number is (CIN) U47222DL2025PLC453320 and its current status is Active. Its industry classification as per MCA is retail sale of non-alcoholic beverages including icecream not for consumption [...] | Name | Short Description | Founded Year | Location | Current Stage |\n ---  --- \n| Logo for Blinkit Blinkit | Online retailer of groceries, personal care, and household essential products | 2013 | India | Acquired |\n\nLogo for Blinkit\n\n## Documents of Blinkit Foods Limited15 mins\n\n### Latest Financials, Share Allotment and Annual Report\n\nThe latest filed financial documents, annual reports, and share allotment filings are shown below:\n\n### Recent Filings [...] Blinkit Foods Limited's authorised share capital is ₹1Cr and its paid up capital is ₹27.5L. The current board of directors of Blinkit Foods Limited comprises Deepak Ahluwalia, Ali Kausar Siddiqui and 1 more.\n\n## Contact Details for Blinkit Foods Limited\n\n## Brands associated with Blinkit Foods Limited","score":0.87139857},{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://www.zoominfo.com/c/blinkit/359515698","content":"# Blinkit\n\nBlink Commerce Private Limited, d/b/a Blinkit and formerly Grofers, is an Indian instant delivery service. Customers of the company use a mobile application to order groceries and essentials online. Blinkit's employees then secure the items from their warehouse and deliver the items to the consumer within 10 minutes. In 2022, Zomato acquired Blinki... \n\n## Leadership [...] ## Leadership\n\n- Khevender Daga — Quick Commerce Finance Controller (Blinkit & ...\n- Sanchit Bhasin — City Chief Executive Officer - Gujarat\n- Simran Shrivastav — Co-Chief Executive Officer\n\n## Company Details\n\n- Website: \n- Revenue: $94.2 Million\n- Employees: 1K - 5K\n- Industries: Freight & Logistics Services; Retail; Transportation; Grocery Retail\n- Headquarters: Golf Course Road Vipul Tech Sector-43 Sq Fl 4, Gurgaon, Haryana, 122001, India\n\n## Social Media\n\n- \n- \n- \n\n## Tech Stack [...] - blinkit cfo vipin kapooria has exited the quick commerce startup after more than a year moneycontrol reported kapooria could likely rejoin flipkart where he had worked for around seven years in two separate stints he was blinkits first fulltime designated cfo since amit sachdeva who worked at the startup as cfo between 2019 and 2022 left the firm\n- Blinkit-AI, an advanced artificial intelligence-driven platform, has raised $1.2 million in its seed funding round from Foliflex Cables (India).","score":0.84707206},{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://eternal.com/our-businesses/blinkit","content":"Eternal\n\nInstant commerce indistinguishable from magic\n\nLaunched with the ambition of making everyday essentials available at your doorstep, Blinkit has revolutionized how India shops.  \n  \nIt has now evolved into a full-fledged quick commerce company, delivering thousands of products including grocery and daily essentials, electronics, beauty & personal care items, stationery, and emergency supplies.\n\n# Leading the quick commerce evolution [...] Blinkit is powered by a dynamic network of customers, store partners, and delivery partners working together seamlessly.\n\n31 million+ customers use our app monthly\n\n2,400+ stores across 300+ cities\n\n500,000+ delivery partners delivering at your doorstep\n\n# Beyond essentials\n\nBlinkit is constantly innovating to serve the evolving customer needs, the latest being in:\n\nBeauty & personal care\n\nBeauty & personal care [...] Sports\n\nSports\n\nFor training, playing, or just starting out, you can get the right gear delivered to your doorstep.\n\nToys\n\nToys\n\nBrain-boosting games, cuddly companions, and everything in between — toys to match every age and every mood.\n\n# Download the app now\n\nEverything you need, delivered to your doorstep on the Blinkit app.\n\nApp Download LogoApp Download Logo\n\nScan the QR code to download the app\n\ndownload app\n\n# Our other businesses\n\nBringing the world closer, one meal at a time","score":0.77893573}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:22.116Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"4eac74d7-3414-406a-8e55-6666f8fbb1f6","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2654,"result":[{"title":"Zepto (company)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zepto_(company)","content":"Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce company headquartered in Bengaluru.( It was founded in July 2021 by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra.( of August 2024,( the company is valued at over $5 billion( and operates over 250 dark-stores across ten metropolitan areas in India.(\n\n## History\n\n[edit&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: History\")] [...] Indian quick-commerce company\n\nNot to be confused with ZeptoLab.\n\nZeptoImage 4\nFormerly KiranaKart\nTypePrivate\nIndustryQuick-commerce\nFounded July 2021;5 years ago(2021-07) in Mumbai, Maharashtra, India\nHeadquartersBengaluru, Karnataka\n\n, [...] In 2021, the company rebranded to Zepto and verticalized the operation, building a network of dark stores to fulfill orders. In April 2022, Zepto launched Cafe, a division focused on delivery of coffee and ready-to-eat food.( In February 2023, the company launched Bloom, a platform for farmers to manage food production and distribute goods from villages to cities.(","score":0.9108078},{"title":"Zepto Pvt Ltd - Company Profile and News - Bloomberg Markets","url":"https://www.bloomberg.com/profile/company/1858712D:IN","content":"# Zepto Pvt Ltd\n\nZepto Private Limited provides online grocery delivery services. The Company offers instant delivery of groceries and household essentials through a marketplace platform connecting users with sellers and delivery partners. Zepto Pvt Ltd serves consumers seeking fast and convenient grocery delivery across India.","score":0.8306082},{"title":"Zepto Technology Stack | Zepto Technology Profile","url":"https://rocketreach.co/zepto-technology-stack_b5596628f920a666","content":"Salesforce CRM\n\nSalesforce.com, Inc. is an American cloud computing company headquartered in San Francisco, California. Though its revenue comes from a customer relationship management (CRM) product, Salesforce also sells commercial applications of social networking through acquisition and internal development.\n\n View Companies Using Salesforce CRM \n\n## Zepto Platform And Storage Technology\n\nImage 22: Rackspace Email\n\nRackspace Email [...] Python\n\nPython is an interpreted high-level programming language for general-purpose programming. Python features a dynamic type system and automatic memory management. It supports multiple programming paradigms, including object-oriented, imperative, functional and procedural, and has a large and comprehensive standard library.\n\n View Companies Using Python \n\nImage 19: Zepto\n\nZepto\n\nZepto is a minimalist JavaScript library for modern browsers with a largely jQuery-compatible API. [...] View Companies Using Zepto \n\n## Zepto Sales Technology\n\nImage 20: Odoo CRM\n\nOdoo CRM\n\nOdoo CRM is an open source & social CRM that track leads, close opportunities and get accurate forecasts.\n\n View Companies Using Odoo CRM \n\nImage 21: Salesforce CRM\n\nSalesforce CRM","score":0.75809944},{"title":"How Zepto Became India’s Fastest Growing Startup","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aYK0H85E_oU","content":"Posted: 2025-04-18\nImagine ordering groceries and having them show up at your doorstep in just 10 minutes. That’s the promise of Zepto, the fastest growing e-commerce company in India. In this episode of How To Build The Future, Garry sits down with Aadit Palicha, the co-founder and CEO of Zepto, to discuss how they got started in a Whatsapp group, what it’s like going up against incumbents like Amazon and Zomato and how the future of e-commerce is changing in the age of intelligence. [...] [33:20] what are you seeing at Zeppto? So the way that I look at it is you know we're like a very nent internet native company and and we I was actually talking to\n[33:27] someone senior at Microsoft yesterday and he gave us gave me a really good framework which is on the we're basically the application side of of the\n[33:35] AI acceleration right and if I have to figure out what applications I need to prioritize because in the end all the [...] [15:50] some of the um existential moments for Zeppto what are some other moments that uh you know gave you sort of the deepest\n[15:57] lessons into building this company and you know coming up as a CEO in the very early days I think you know we had uh\n[16:04] plenty of existential crises that the YC partners helped us through right there was like like before we got into this whole first party thing we were realizing when we did like an","score":0.7491794},{"title":"Zepto - get everything you forgot, remembered, or craved in mins*","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/zeptonow","content":"Founded in 2021 by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra, Zepto is on a mission to save you time —making every second count towards life's real joys. Our platform has revolutionised rapid commerce in India with cutting-edge technology and strategically optimised delivery hubs. Zepto offers an extensive range of 45,000+ products, from fresh groceries to electronics, beauty essentials, apparels, toys and more, delivering across 50+ cities in minutes Zepto Café extends our commitment to convenience, [...] ### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\n\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nTechnology, Information and Internet\n\n### Company Size\n5,001-10,000 employees  \n18902 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed Zepto as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\n2021\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: 2025-11-16T00:00:00.000Z\nLast Round Type: Series H\nTotal Rounds: 6\nLast Round Raised: US$ 450.0M\n\n### Investors\nCalPERS, + 7 Other investors\n\n### Specialties\nN/A\n\n## Locations\nIndia, IN [...] order possible. You too can stay hydrated, search for “ #Letshydrate ” on Zepto and grab your pack of Electrorush. Halewood Laboratories Private Limited [Likes: 279, Comments: 27]; Zepto (1w): the only competition tougher than the spice challenge? sharing desi chinese 🤭 Tata Consumer Products [Likes: 71, Comments: 17]; Zepto (1w): Back to school season just got a whole lot tastier 😋 We've created this Tic-tac-toe flyer with McCain Foods . Get it with your Zepto order and let us know who's","score":0.7023877}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:22.483Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"28b09ab9-cb2a-452f-ac3f-fce08f72a09e","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":3019,"result":[{"title":"BigBasket - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BigBasket","content":"BigBasket is an Indian online grocer, headquartered in Bengaluru and owned by Tata Digital. The company was set up in 2011 and is registered with the name Supermarket Grocery Supplies Pvt. Ltd. As of January 2023,( it operates in more than 30 cities in India.\n\n## History\n\n[edit]\n\nBigBasket was founded in December 2011 by five entrepreneurs from the dot-com crash era. It received its initial funding of $10 million from Bengaluru-based private equity investor Ascent Capital. [...] In 2015, Bigbasket acquired the hyperlocal delivery company Delyver to build its last-mile \"Last mile (transportation)\") delivery network. By mid-2016, BigBasket was operating in eight large Indian cities and had grown to become India's biggest e-grocer. [...] In other projects\n\n Wikidata item\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian online grocery delivery company\n\nBigBasket","score":0.902687},{"title":"bigbasket","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/bigbasket-com","content":"Starting our journey in 2011, today, bigbasket - a Tata Enterprise is a leading online supermarket with a presence across 60+ cities and towns. We operate through business lines including bigbasket, bbinstant, bbdaily, bbmandi and bbsaathi, while continuing to strengthen our quick commerce capabilities across Tier 1 and Tier 2 cities. As bigbasket scales, we are expanding into categories such as Fashion, Electronics, Food, Pharmacy, and Gold & Silver Coins, creating a more comprehensive and [...] comprehensive and convenient shopping ecosystem. We make everyday shopping seamless while continuously enhancing the customer experience. With a workforce of more than 60,000, we are a proud and growing bigbasket family, constantly looking to work with the best talent in the industry. Every bigbasketeer embodies the 'Spirit of bb' that defines our work ethos. We nurture a people-first environment where employee well-being is prioritised. Guided by our values, we encourage humility, [...] home plums that are naturally sweet, delightfully juicy, and full of pleasant surprises. 💜 #Fresho #bigbasket #Plums #StoneFruits #HimachalPradesh #SeasonalProduce #FromOurFarmers [Likes: 157, Comments: 12]; bigbasket (1mo): We are proud to be part of a significant milestone in strengthening India's agricultural value chain. Hon'ble Union Finance Minister Smt. Nirmala Sitharaman , on 18 July 2026 inaugurated Global Chilli Agro Pvt. Ltd., Farmer Producer Company (FPC) at Virudhunagar, Tamil","score":0.79637206},{"title":"BigBasket - Success Story of India's Largest Online Grocer","url":"https://www.imsrindia.com/single-post/bigbasket-success-story-of-india-s-largest-online-grocer","content":"BigBasket is into delivering everyday cooking essentials like ghee (clarified butter), diced coconut, fragrant basmati rice, and more, amounting to a total of over 40,000 items, along with other household products ranging from bread to laundry detergents for the customers to shop from. The company gets all of them delivered to their doorsteps. The target motive of the company is to enable the ease of grocery shopping online to avoid traffic and the drudgery of supermarket visits. [...] Founded in 2011, by the dot-com bubble survivors - V.S. Sudhakar, Hari Menon, V.S. Ramesh, Vipul Parekh, and Abhinay Choudhari, Supermarket Grocery Supplies Pvt. Ltd., trading as BigBasket, is a household name soon after it came to existence.\n\nHeadquartered in Bengaluru, BigBasket is currently known as India's largest online grocer receives over 150,000 orders per day. [...] To date, BigBasket has raised a total of $1.3B in funding over 19 rounds. The latest funding for the company was raised on June 2, 2022, when BigBasket raised Rs 350 crore ($45.10 mn) from Supermarket Grocery Supplies, the holding company of the grocery unicorn. As per the reports, BigBasket had previously allocated 3.5 crore shares at a value of INR 100 per share to Supermarket Grocery Supplies on May 24, 2022. Supermarket Grocery Supplies is currently a Tata-owned company. Tata Digital owned","score":0.78611463},{"title":"BigBasket Co-founder on 10 Min Delivery, TATA Acquisition, Wealth Creation & More | Neon Show","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=roc8zlAU5FM","content":"Today, companies like BlinkIt and Zepto dominate the space, delivering groceries in 10 minutes using the same model.\nIn 2019, BigBasket hit the big leagues, joining the unicorn club with a valuation of $1.2 billion valuation after raising $150 million, outpacing Amazon and Grofers.\nIn May 2021, Tata Digital, a subsidiary of Tata Sons, acquired a  64% stake in stake in BigBasket for about $1.5-2 billion from major shareholders, including Alibaba and Actis. [...] In 2015, BigBasket pioneered the dark store model, using small, strategically placed warehouses to speed up deliveries and roll out express delivery services. [...] Vipul shares candid insights on the recent disruption in the online grocery space with the rise of quick commerce. He reveals how BigBasket is not just catching up, but evolving to become a formidable player by leveraging the Tata Group's ecosystem and building a culture of innovation and resilience.","score":0.6599319},{"title":"Online Grocery Shopping and Online Supermarket in India - bigbasket","url":"https://www.bigbasket.com","content":"Did you ever imagine that the freshest of fruits and vegetables, top-quality pulses and food grains, dairy products, and hundreds of branded items could be handpicked and delivered to your home, all at the click of a button? In today's fast-paced world, bigbasket.com, India's pioneering online grocery store, continues to bring a staggering array of over 40,000 products from more than 1,000 brands to the doorsteps of over 10 million satisfied customers. From essential household cleaning products","score":0.5760895}]}
