stamart as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\nN/A\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: N/A\nLast Round Type: N/A\nTotal Rounds: N/A\nLast Round Raised: N/A\n\n### Investors\nN/A\n\n### Specialties\nN/A\n\n## Locations\nBengaluru, Karnataka, IN\n\n### Get Directions\nDirections [...] # Instamart\nN/A\nTechnology, Information and Internet • Bengaluru, Karnataka • 112,559 followers • 1,001-5,000 employees\n\n## Overview\nWe’re now live in 120 cities! That’s 120 places where spontaneous plans, unexpected guests, late-night needs, and lazy Sundays are all covered. From mood swings to midnight cravings, we’re built for whatever today throws at you. No waiting. No planning. 🌆 120 cities and growing 📲 20+ categories - from groceries to electronics\n\n### Website\n\n[S33] BigBasket - Wikipedia\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BigBasket\nBigBasket is an Indian online grocer, headquartered in Bengaluru and owned by Tata Digital. The company was set up in 2011 and is registered with the name Supermarket Grocery Supplies Pvt. Ltd. As of January 2023,( it operates in more than 30 cities in India.\n\n## History\n\n[edit]\n\nBigBasket was founded in December 2011 by five entrepreneurs from the dot-com crash era. It received its initial funding of $10 million from Bengaluru-based private equity investor Ascent Capital. [...] In 2015, Bigbasket acquired the hyperlocal delivery company Delyver to build its last-mile \"Last mile (transportation)\") delivery network. By mid-2016, BigBasket was operating in eight large Indian cities and had grown to become India's biggest e-grocer. [...] In other projects\n\n Wikidata item\n\nAppearance\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIndian online grocery delivery company\n\nBigBasket\n\n[S34] bigbasket\nURL: https://in.linkedin.com/company/bigbasket-com\nStarting our journey in 2011, today, bigbasket - a Tata Enterprise is a leading online supermarket with a presence across 60+ cities and towns. We operate through business lines including bigbasket, bbinstant, bbdaily, bbmandi and bbsaathi, while continuing to strengthen our quick commerce capabilities across Tier 1 and Tier 2 cities. As bigbasket scales, we are expanding into categories such as Fashion, Electronics, Food, Pharmacy, and Gold & Silver Coins, creating a more comprehensive and [...] comprehensive and convenient shopping ecosystem. We make everyday shopping seamless while continuously enhancing the customer experience. With a workforce of more than 60,000, we are a proud and growing bigbasket family, constantly looking to work with the best talent in the industry. Every bigbasketeer embodies the 'Spirit of bb' that defines our work ethos. We nurture a people-first environment where employee well-being is prioritised. Guided by our values, we encourage humility, [...] home plums that are naturally sweet, delightfully juicy, and full of pleasant surprises. 💜 #Fresho #bigbasket #Plums #StoneFruits #HimachalPradesh #SeasonalProduce #FromOurFarmers [Likes: 157, Comments: 12]; bigbasket (1mo): We are proud to be part of a significant milestone in strengthening India's agricultural value chain. Hon'ble Union Finance Minister Smt. Nirmala Sitharaman , on 18 July 2026 inaugurated Global Chilli Agro Pvt. Ltd., Farmer Producer Company (FPC) at Virudhunagar, Tamil\n\n[S35] BigBasket - Success Story of India's Largest Online Grocer\nURL: https://www.imsrindia.com/single-post/bigbasket-success-story-of-india-s-largest-online-grocer\nBigBasket is into delivering everyday cooking essentials like ghee (clarified butter), diced coconut, fragrant basmati rice, and more, amounting to a total of over 40,000 items, along with other household products ranging from bread to laundry detergents for the customers to shop from. The company gets all of them delivered to their doorsteps. The target motive of the company is to enable the ease of grocery shopping online to avoid traffic and the drudgery of supermarket visits. [...] Founded in 2011, by the dot-com bubble survivors - V.S. Sudhakar, Hari Menon, V.S. Ramesh, Vipul Parekh, and Abhinay Choudhari, Supermarket Grocery Supplies Pvt. Ltd., trading as BigBasket, is a household name soon after it came to existence.\n\nHeadquartered in Bengaluru, BigBasket is currently known as India's largest online grocer receives over 150,000 orders per day. [...] To date, BigBasket has raised a total of $1.3B in funding over 19 rounds. The latest funding for the company was raised on June 2, 2022, when BigBasket raised Rs 350 crore ($45.10 mn) from Supermarket Grocery Supplies, the holding company of the grocery unicorn. As per the reports, BigBasket had previously allocated 3.5 crore shares at a value of INR 100 per share to Supermarket Grocery Supplies on May 24, 2022. Supermarket Grocery Supplies is currently a Tata-owned company. Tata Digital owned\n\n[S36] BigBasket Co-founder on 10 Min Delivery, TATA Acquisition, Wealth Creation & More | Neon Show\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=roc8zlAU5FM\nToday, companies like BlinkIt and Zepto dominate the space, delivering groceries in 10 minutes using the same model.\nIn 2019, BigBasket hit the big leagues, joining the unicorn club with a valuation of $1.2 billion valuation after raising $150 million, outpacing Amazon and Grofers.\nIn May 2021, Tata Digital, a subsidiary of Tata Sons, acquired a  64% stake in stake in BigBasket for about $1.5-2 billion from major shareholders, including Alibaba and Actis. [...] In 2015, BigBasket pioneered the dark store model, using small, strategically placed warehouses to speed up deliveries and roll out express delivery services. [...] Vipul shares candid insights on the recent disruption in the online grocery space with the rise of quick commerce. He reveals how BigBasket is not just catching up, but evolving to become a formidable player by leveraging the Tata Group's ecosystem and building a culture of innovation and resilience.\n\n[S37] Online Grocery Shopping and Online Supermarket in India - bigbasket\nURL: https://www.bigbasket.com\nDid you ever imagine that the freshest of fruits and vegetables, top-quality pulses and food grains, dairy products, and hundreds of branded items could be handpicked and delivered to your home, all at the click of a button? In today's fast-paced world, bigbasket.com, India's pioneering online grocery store, continues to bring a staggering array of over 40,000 products from more than 1,000 brands to the doorsteps of over 10 million satisfied customers. From essential household cleaning products\n\n[S38] Flipkart Minutes quadruples business as quick-commerce battle intensifies\nURL: https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/flipkart-minutes-quadruples-business-as-quick-commerce-battle-intensifies-126091001430_1.html\nFlipkart Minutes, the quick-commerce arm of e-commerce giant Flipkart, has quadrupled its business over the past year as it marks two years since its launch in August 2024. The service now operates nearly 1,200 micro-fulfilment centres across more than 150 cities, highlighting the rapid expansion of on-demand delivery in one of the world’s fastest-growing digital markets. The expansion comes ahead of Flipkart’s Big Billion Days sale in October, as the company faces intensifying competition from [...] Since August 2024, Flipkart Minutes has built a partner ecosystem of close to 500 direct-to-consumer (D2C) brands, giving them access to hyperlocal demand and new customer segments. Through partnerships with Farmer Producer Organisations (FPOs), the platform has also connected thousands of farmers directly to consumers, helping them reach new markets and improve price realisation. [...] The new developments at Flipkart Minutes highlight the intensifying battle for scale in the country’s rapidly expanding instant-delivery market. According to a recent CLSA report, Blinkit accounted for close to 30 per cent of dark stores across the country’s top 10 cities and more than 34 per cent nationally and had the leading store count in six of them, with Zepto leading in three of the remaining four. Blinkit’s presence in more than 180 cities, CLSA said, positioned it to capture an\n\n[S39] Flipkart Hyperlocal\nURL: https://www.flipkart.com/flipkart-minutes-store?marketplace=HYPERLOCAL\nFlipkart Minutes is a quick and easy-to-handle assortment of products for everyday needs, making top-ups and unplanned needs from home simple.\n\n[S40] Flipkart\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flipkart\nIn October 2024, Flipkart was among the initial partners in the launch of YouTube's Shopping affiliate programme in India, allowing eligible video creators to link products from Flipkart and Myntra, in their content.\n\nIn 2025, the company announced that it would shift its domicile from Singapore to India.\n\nOn 11 September 2026, Flipkart Minutes expanded its operational footprint to approximately 1,200 micro-fulfillment centers spanning over 150 cities.\n\n## Business structure\n\n[edit] [...] In March 2024, Flipkart launched its UPI services, Flipkart UPI, in partnership with Axis Bank.\n\n\n\nIn August 2024, Flipkart entered the quick-commerce market with the introduction of Flipkart Minutes. In the same month, Flipkart-backed super.money launched its mobile application offering credit-first UPI services. [...] 104. ↑ Goel, Samiksha (3 March 2024). \"Flipkart launches digital payments service Flipkart UPI\". mint. Retrieved 25 April 2024.\n105. ↑ \"Flipkart's 10-min quick-commerce service 'Minutes' goes live in Bengaluru\". Business Standard. 5 August 2024. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n106. ↑ \"super.money launches new credit-first UPI app, hits 10 million transactions in beta phase\". CNBCTV18. 22 August 2024. Retrieved 4 May 2025.\n\n[S41] Vaibhav Rustagi Email & Phone Number | Flipkart Head of Revenue and Growth @ Flipkart Minutes Contact Information\nURL: https://rocketreach.co/vaibhav-rustagi-email_2047361\n### products\n\n   Advanced Search\n   Chrome Extension\n   Edge Extension\n   Bulk Lookups\n   API\n   Integrations\n\n### information\n\n   Pricing\n   Help\n   Reviews\n   User Agreement\n   Privacy Policy\n   Cookie Policy\n   Do Not Sell My Info\n\n### teams\n\n   Features\n   Start Team Plan\n   Custom Plan\n   Speak to Sales\n\n### company\n\n   About Us\n   Careers\n   Blog\n   Contact Us\n\n© 2026 RocketReach.co\n\n\n\nImage 21: Company Logo\n\n## Privacy Preference Center [...] These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising.\n\n### Cookie List\n\nClear\n   - [x] checkbox label label \n\nApply Cancel\n\nConsent Leg.Interest [...] E-commerce\n   Category Management\n   Digital Marketing\n   P&L Management\n   Market Research\n   Competitive Analysis\n   Sales Operations\n   Marketing\n   Brand Management\n   FMCG\n   Business Development\n   Marketing Management\n   Trade Marketing\n   Sales Management\n   Key Account Management\n   Market Planning\n   Customer Insight\n   Channel Management\n   Market Analysis\n   Segmentation\n   Business Strategy\n   Business Analysis\n   Analytics\n   Mobile Advertising\n   Product Marketing\n   Strategy\n\n[S42] Sweta Dutta Email & Phone Number | Flipkart Head Brand partnerships - Flipkart minutes Contact Information\nURL: https://rocketreach.co/sweta-dutta-email_243625036\nSweta Dutta, based in Karnataka, India, is currently a Head Brand partnerships - Flipkart minutes at Flipkart. Sweta Dutta brings experience from previous roles at Flipkart, PharmEasy and ICICI Prudential AMC Ltd. Sweta Dutta holds a 2015 - 2017 Master of Business Administration - MBA in Finance and Marketing @ International Management Institute - IMI. Sweta Dutta has 2 emails and 2 mobile phone numbers on RocketReach.\n\n### Looking for a different Sweta Dutta? [...] ### teams\n\n   Features\n   Start Team Plan\n   Custom Plan\n   Speak to Sales\n\n### company\n\n   About Us\n   Careers\n   Blog\n   Contact Us\n\n© 2026 RocketReach.co\n\n\n\nImage 22: Company Logo\n\n## Privacy Preference Center [...] These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising.\n\n### Cookie List\n\nClear\n   - [x] checkbox label label \n\nApply Cancel\n\nConsent Leg.Interest",{"json":true,"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"claims":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"citedUrl":{"type":"string"},"supportingUrls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["text","citedUrl","supportingUrls"]}},"entitiesLearned":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"},"facts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fact":{"type":"string"},"sourceUrl":{"type":"string"}},"required":["fact","sourceUrl"]}}},"required":["name","type","facts"]}},"unableToFind":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["answer","claims","entitiesLearned","unableToFind"]}}]}
