{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:32.534Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"5d75802f-bfaa-476b-b2ef-1a914bd6c185","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":3434,"result":[{"title":"Zepto Revenue, Valuation, Funding & Investors","url":"https://multiples.vc/private-comps/zepto","content":"and Kaivalya Vohra, it raised $340 million in primary equity capital in August 2024, led by General Catalyst ($250 million) and Mars Growth Capital ($50 million), with participation from Epiq Capital, Dragon Fund, and existing investors like DST Global, Lightspeed, and StepStone. This followed a $665 million June 2024 round at $3.6 billion post-money, bringing two-month total to $1 billion and overall funding to ~$1.6 billion. The August round valued Zepto at $5 billion post-money ($4.6 billion [...] | Aug 2024 | Series G | General Catalyst, Mars Growth Capita… +8General Catalyst (lead); Mars Growth Capital (lead); Epiq Capital; Dragon Fund; StepStone; Lightspeed Venture Partners; Avenir; Avra; Contrary; DST Global | $340M | $5B | Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce startup delivering groceri…Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce startup delivering groceries and essentials in minutes via dark stores in urban areas, competing with Blinkit and Swiggy Instamart. Founded by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya [...] ($665M in June 2024 led by Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group to prepare for IPO), Series H ($340M in August 2024 led by General Catalyst and Mars Growth Capital to bolster finances pre-IPO), and more recent pre-IPO rounds in 2024-2025 reaching valuations of $5B to $7B. Total funding across all rounds amounts to approximately $2.93 billion as of October 2025. Later developments show Zepto scaling order volume 200% over 18 months by late 2025, achieving store-level","score":0.9191869},{"title":"Zepto raises $340 Mn at $5 Bn valuation","url":"https://entrackr.com/2024/08/zepto-raises-340-mn-at-5-bn-valuation","content":"author-image/entrackr/media/member_avatars/2024/10/21/2024-10-21t083427265z-harsh-sir-768x768.png )\n\n Follow Us\n\nzepto/entrackr/media/post_attachments/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Zepto-funding.jpg)\n\nQuick commerce company Zepto has raised $340 million in a follow-on financing round led by General Catalyst, with Dragon Fund and Epiq Capital joining as new investors. Existing investors, including StepStone, Lightspeed, DST, and Contrary, also increased their stakes. [...] /entrackr/media/agency_attachments/2024/10/18/XDGqYgwk8PhvKwQWyFWY.png)\n\n0\n\ngoogle\ngoogle\n\nBy clicking the button, I accept the Terms of Use of the service and its Privacy Policy, as well as consent to the processing of personal data.\n\nDon’t have an account? Signup\n\nad_close_btn\n\n# Zepto raises $340 Mn at $5 Bn valuation\n\n## Zepto has raised $340 million in a follow-on round led by General Catalyst with Dragon Fund, and Epiq Capital joining as new investors. [...] With this new funding, Zepto’s valuation has surged by nearly 40%, rising to $5 billion from $3.6 billion in June, when it raised $665 million in its Series F round. The firm has raised over $1 billion in 2024, $1.2 billion in the past 12 months, and more than $1.5 billion since its inception.","score":0.8624794},{"title":"Zepto funding: Zepto bags $340 million in funding, valuation jumps to $5 billion - The Economic Times","url":"https://m.economictimes.com/tech/funding/zepto-bags-340-million-more-from-general-catalyst-mars-growth-and-epiq-capital/articleshow/112901416.cms","content":"Image for Zepto bags $340 million in funding, valuation jumps to $5 billionETtech\n\nZepto has raised $340 million more from General Catalyst, Mars Growth and Epiq Capital [...] Quick commerce firm Zepto has raised another $340 million (Rs 2,850 crore) from new investors General Catalyst, Mars Growth Capital and Epiq Capital, and others, taking the total funds it raised in the past two months to $1 billion. [...] Existing investors such as StepStone, Lightspeed, DST Global, and Contrary have also participated in the latest funding round, the company said in a statement. DST Global is an investor also in Swiggy which runs quick-commerce platform Instamart. The three-year old firm since its June funding has stepped on the gas in terms of expansion even as it sees intense rivalry from existing and new entrants in the red-hot quick-delivery sector.","score":0.8296166},{"title":"Zepto Raises $340 Mn At $5 Bn Valuation, Led By General ...","url":"https://www.bwdisrupt.com/article/zepto-raises-340-mn-at-5-bn-valuation-led-by-general-catalyst-531242","content":"Zepto, a quick commerce Unicorn today secures USD 340 million in a follow-on financing round, placing the company at USD 5 billion in valuation","score":0.7915799},{"title":"Quick commerce unicorn Zepto has raised $340 million in ...","url":"https://www.instagram.com/p/C_RqdoITVSx","content":"Zepto has raised $340 million in follow-on financing at a valuation of $5 billion amid growing competition and consumer traction in the sector.","score":0.74363416}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:33.055Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"644f9e72-d32a-4f2d-a568-4c01d9bff78f","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":3955,"result":[{"title":"Zepto Revenue, Valuation, Funding & Investors","url":"https://multiples.vc/private-comps/zepto","content":"| Date | Revenue \\ | Valuation | Revenue Multiple | Stage |\n| Oct 2025 | $1.2B | $7B | 5.9x | Series H |\n| Aug 2025 | $1.2B | $5.4B | 4.5x | Secondary |\n| Aug 2025 | $477M | $6.1B | 12.8x | Secondary |\n| May 2025 | $1.2B | $7B | 5.9x | Secondary |\n| Nov 2024 | $1.2B | $5B | 4.2x | Series G |\n| Aug 2024 | $1.2B | $5B | 4.2x | Series G |\n| Jun 2024 | $1.2B | $3.6B | 3.0x | Series F |\n| May 2022 | $200M | $900M | 4.5x | Series D | [...] \\ Revenue (or ARR) figures are the values recorded alongside each funding round. Typically run-rate revenue at the time of the deal, or a reported LTM (last 12 months) revenue.\n\n### Zepto Funding History\n\nZepto has raised a total of $2.4B across 12 funding rounds, plus 3 secondary share sales.\n\nZepto's first fundraising round was a $500K seed round in September 2020. The most recent completed round was a $450M Series H in October 2025.\n\n#### Zepto funding rounds\n\nZepto funding rounds [...] | Date | Stage | Valuation | Revenue Multiple |\n| Oct 2025 | Series H | $7B | 5.9x |\n| Aug 2025 | Secondary | $5.4B | 4.5x |\n| Aug 2025 | Secondary | $6.1B | 12.8x |\n| May 2025 | Secondary | $7B | 5.9x |\n| Nov 2024 | Series G | $5B | 4.2x |\n| Aug 2024 | Series G | $5B | 4.2x |\n| Jun 2024 | Series F | $3.6B | 3.0x |\n| Nov 2023 | Series E | $1.4B \n| Aug 2023 | Series E | $1.4B \n| May 2022 | Series D | $900M | 4.5x |\n| Dec 2021 | Series C | $570M \n| Oct 2021 | Series B | $12B \n\n### Zepto Revenue","score":0.80735475},{"title":"Zepto Funding: $1.9B Raised, Series F (2025)","url":"https://startupfundraising.com/companies/zepto","content":"Zepto is an E-commerce company based in Mumbai, India. Zepto has raised $1.9B in total disclosed funding. That places its disclosed total in over $1B. Its most recent disclosed round is a Series F announced in October 2025. The round record for Zepto runs through 2025; nothing later has been disclosed. Investors on record include Y Combinator, Nexus Venture Partners, Glade Brook Capital, Contrary Capital, StepStone Group, Goodwater Capital and 3 others. 9 distinct backers are named across the [...] # Zepto Funding: $1.9B Raised, Series F (2025)\n\nZepto is an E-commerce company based in Mumbai, India. It has raised $1.9B in total funding. Latest round: Series F.\n\n## Zepto funding overview [...] named across the disclosed rounds.","score":0.6742441},{"title":"Zepto raises $340 mn in Series G funding, valuation shoots to $5 bn | News - Business Standard","url":"https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/zepto-raises-340-mn-in-series-g-funding-valuation-shoots-up-to-5-bn-124081401004_1.html","content":"In a Series G funding round, quick commerce start-up Zepto has raised $340 million from a clutch of investors. With this, the company’s valuation has shot up to $5 billion, according to an Outlook Business report.\n\n  \n\nSeries G round is typically used for companies that are on to their next stage of growth, gearing up for an IPO or acquisition, or expansion into a new market. [...] “We are where Amazon was in the late 90s, early 2000s. We are sitting on the right macro and the right business model to create something huge. And if we execute well, we are sitting on a $50-80 billion outcome,” said Aadit Palicha, Zepto co-founder, as reported by MoneyControl.\n\n### Also Read\n\nZepto\n\n## Zepto to raise $310 million, valuing quick-commerce firm at $5 billion\n\nZepto\n\n## Quick commerce unicorn Zepto to shift base from Mumbai to Bengaluru\n\nZepto [...] Of the $340 million that Zepto received, $250 million came from General Catalyst, $50 million from Mars Growth, and the remaining amount was fetched from existing investors.\n\n  \n\nInitially, Zepto wanted to raise $400 million in funding but later, it decided to keep its funding round at $340 million, according to a MoneyControl report. The funding entirely consists of primary capital and will all be in equity.","score":0.6052631},{"title":"Seven Aussie startups that raised $45.6 million this fortnight - SmartCompany","url":"https://www.smartcompany.com.au/startupsmart/seven-aussie-startups-raised-45-6-million-fortnight","content":"“We believe that keeping on top of regulatory change and remaining compliant should and can be effortless by leading on technology, ease of use, and using humans where it’s needed–  and that belief is at the centre of everything that we do and where we will take our solution.”\n\nRead more.\n\n## Monty Compost Co: $1 million\n\nMonty Compost Co founder Ashley Baxter startup \n\nMONTY COMPOST FOUNDER ASHLEY BAXTER. SOURCE: MONTY COMPOST CO [...] The startup, which recently won an iAward in the startup category under its previous name, Gracenote, was founded by a group of lawyers and a computer scientist who were frustrated with inefficient compliance solutions in former roles in financial services companies.\n\n“We have seen and experienced the stress that the constant state of not knowing whether you are in or out of complaint creates,” Simon Quirk, co-founder and CEO of Graceview, told SmartCompany earlier this week. [...] Eyeonic was founded by associate professor Simon Skalicky, an opthalmologist by trade, and is a previous winner of SmartCompany‘s early-stage pitching competition, the Pitch.\n\nThe startup aims to eliminate the need for specialised machines and personnel for glaucoma testing to ensure more patients can be screened accurately and conveniently, and therefore, improve the rates of early detection of the eye disease.","score":0.31050667},{"title":"Applied Digital doubles Series G preferred stock offering to $300 million","url":"https://ng.investing.com/news/sec-filings/applied-digital-doubles-series-g-preferred-stock-offering-to-300-million-93CH-2067633","content":"Title: Applied Digital doubles Series G preferred stock offering to $300 million\n# Applied Digital doubles Series G preferred stock offering to $300 million. Applied Digital doubles Series G preferred stock offering to $300 million. (NASDAQ:APLD), whose stock has surged over 260% in the past year according to InvestingPro data, disclosed Thursday that it amended its preferred equity purchase agreement to increase the aggregate commitment for its Series G Convertible Preferred Stock from $150 million to $300 million. The amendment, signed August 14, 2025, also removes a previous limit that capped the aggregate purchase price for any single issuance at $75 million. The company stated that these changes are intended to provide additional capital for the ongoing construction and development of its Polaris Forge I data center in Ellendale, North Dakota. According to the filing, the offer and sale of the Series G Preferred Stock, as well as the shares of common stock issuable upon conversion, are being made in reliance on an exemption from registration under Section 4(a)(2) of the Securities Act of 1933. In a related move, Applied Digital filed an amendment to the Certificate of Designations for the Series G Convertible Preferred Stock. The amendment increases the initial floor price for conversion to $12.50 from $4.25 and raises the minimum limit below which the floor price may not be reduced to $4.33 from $1.34. The floor price sets the minimum conversion price for the Series G shares, which can only be changed at the company’s discretion. Applied Digital’s common stock is listed on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the ticker APLD. In other recent news, Applied Digital Corp reported its financial results for the fourth quarter of 2025. The data and prices on the website are not necessarily provided by any market or exchange, but may be provided by market makers, and so prices may not be accurate and may differ from the actual price at any given market, meaning prices are indicative and not appropriate for trading purposes.**Fusion Media**and any provider of the data contained in this website will not accept liability for any loss or damage as a result of your trading, or your reliance on the information contained within this website.","score":0.18790671}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:20:33.183Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"2af3526d-4ff2-4cf6-8b21-67b560ff6cc4","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":4084,"result":[{"title":"Zepto Revenue, Valuation, Funding & Investors","url":"https://multiples.vc/private-comps/zepto","content":"| Jun 2024 | Series F | Glade Brook Capita…, Nexus Venture Part… +8Glade Brook Capital Partners (lead); Nexus Venture Partners (lead); StepStone Group (lead); Goodwater Capital; Lightspeed Venture Partners; Avenir; Avra; Lachy Groom; Contrary; DST Global | $665M | $3.6B | Zepto, a Mumbai-based quick commerce startup specializing in…Zepto, a Mumbai-based quick commerce startup specializing in 10-15 minute grocery and essentials delivery via dark stores, raised $665 million in a highly [...] million in a highly oversubscribed Series F round on June 20, 2024, at a post-money valuation of $3.6 billion, more than doubling from $1.4 billion nine months prior. The round was co-led by existing investors Glade Brook Capital Partners, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group, with participation from new investors Avenir, Lightspeed Venture Partners, and Avra, alongside Goodwater Capital, Lachy Groom, Contrary, and DST Global. Zepto operates around 350 dark stores across 10 cities, [...] ($665M in June 2024 led by Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group to prepare for IPO), Series H ($340M in August 2024 led by General Catalyst and Mars Growth Capital to bolster finances pre-IPO), and more recent pre-IPO rounds in 2024-2025 reaching valuations of $5B to $7B. Total funding across all rounds amounts to approximately $2.93 billion as of October 2025. Later developments show Zepto scaling order volume 200% over 18 months by late 2025, achieving store-level","score":0.8993429},{"title":"Zepto Raises $665 Million Series F // Cooley // Global Law Firm","url":"https://www.cooley.com/news/coverage/2024/2024-07-22-zepto-raises-665-million-series-f","content":"Press Release\n\n# Zepto Raises $665 Million Series F\n\nSan Francisco – July 22, 2024 – Cooley advised Zepto, India’s fast-growing quick commerce company, on its $665 million Series F financing, more than doubling its valuation to $3.6 billion in less than a year. The oversubscribed financing round was co-led by Glade Brook, Nexus and StepStone Group, and included participation from Avenir, Lightspeed, Avra, Goodwater, Lachy Groom and Contrary.","score":0.8690161},{"title":"Zepto, a 10-minute delivery app, raises $665M at $3.6B valuation | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2024/06/20/zepto-a-10-minute-delivery-app-raises-665-million-at-3-6-billion-valuation","content":"Glade Brook, Nexus and StepStone Group co-led the “highly-oversubscribed” Series F round, Zepto said. Avenir, Lightspeed and Avra (former YC Continuity exec Anu Hariharan’s new fund) as well as existing backers Goodwater, Lachy Groom and Contrary also invested in the round, the startup said. [...] Zepto has raised a massive $665 million in a new round of funding, more than doubling its valuation to $3.6 billion from $1.4 billion in less than a year, as the Mumbai-based startup doubles down on its efforts to capture the contested quick commerce market in India. [...] DST Global, an early backer of Swiggy, a Zepto rival, also co-led the new funding round, according to two people familiar with the matter. Zepto didn’t disclose DST Global’s participation in the new funding round and declined to comment.\n\nZepto competes with BlinkIt (owned by Zomato) and Swiggy’s Instamart in the quick commerce space.","score":0.8571119},{"title":"2026 Funding Rounds & List of Investors - Zepto","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/zepto/__vOTzafGt-8S4kwYniiZ_yRogd6c_Jsw_vRD0gckHtfE/funding-and-investors","content":"| Aug 29, 2024 | $340M | Series G | $5B | 5.2x | General Catalyst | Epiq Capital, StepStone Group, DST Global, Contrary Capital, Dragon Funds, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Raamdeo Agarawal |\n| Jun 21, 2024 | $665M | Series F | $3.6B | 3.9x | avra, Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, StepStone Group, Goodwater Capital, Avenir Growth Capital, Lightspeed | Lachy Groom | [...] | Date of Funding | Funding Amount | Round Name | Post-Money Valuation | Revenue Multiple | Lead Investors | Other Investors |\n ---  ---  --- \n| Oct 16, 2025 | $300M | Series H | $6.88B  General Catalyst, CalPERS | Goodwater Capital, Glade Brook Capital, Lightspeed Venture Partners, StepStone Group, Avenir Growth Capital, Azo4, Zpt Holdings, Mangum, avra, Contrary, Nexus Venture Partners |\n| Aug 13, 2025 | $45.6M | Series G | $7B | 3.7x  Motilal Oswal Financial Services |","score":0.82795376},{"title":"How Much Did Zepto Raise? Funding & Key Investors","url":"https://www.clay.com/dossier/zepto-funding","content":"Lead Investors: Goodwater Capital, Nexus Venture Partners\n    Valuation at Round: USD 1.4 billion\n    Motivation Behind the Round: To enhance the platform's technology and expand its market reach.\n7. Series F\n    Amount Raised: USD 665,000,000\n    Date: June 2024\n    Lead Investors: Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, StepStone Group\n    Valuation at Round: USD 3.6 billion [...] Motivation Behind the Round: Pre-IPO financing to expand the delivery network and strengthen the balance sheet; existing investors Avenir, Avra, Lightspeed, Glade Brook, StepStone Group, and Nexus Venture Partners also participated.\n11. Growth (Pre-IPO Private Placement)\n     Amount Raised: Not publicly disclosed\n     Date: August 2026\n     Lead Investors: Not publicly disclosed\n     Valuation at Round: USD 4.5 billion (about ₹42,925 crore) [...] Status\n\nVerified\n\nUse Clay's email finder to get anyone's work email in seconds.\n\nZepto has raised substantial funding across multiple rounds backed by prominent investors including CalPERS, General Catalyst, Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, StepStone Group, Y Combinator, and others.\n\nKeep reading to explore Zepto's fundraising journey from seed stage to its August 2026 pre-IPO private placement.\n\n## What Is Zepto?","score":0.8266142}]}
