pStone.\nSOURCE URL: https://multiples.vc/private-comps/zepto\nSOURCE PAGE (excerpt; […] marks omitted text):\n\"\"\"\n[Connect to MCP](/app/authorization/sign-in)\n\n![Claude Desktop](https://assets.multiples.vc/images/claude.png)![Claude Code (CLI)](https://assets.multiples.vc/images/claude-code.png)![ChatGPT](https://assets.multiples.vc/images/chatgpt.png)![Cursor](https://assets.multiples.vc/images/cursor.png)![VS Code](https://assets.multiples.vc/images/vscode.png)\n\n- [Companies](/companies)\n1. Zepto\n\n# Zepto Revenue, Valuation, Funding & Investors\n\n## Zepto is valued at $7B as of October 2025, a 5.9x revenue multiple. Zepto revenue was $1.2B, as disclosed with its latest round.\n\n[See full Zepto profile](/app/companies/9abcf71f-01b3-4f82-ac67-94e929ddadd0)\n\nLast Zepto valuation\n\nSeries H · Oct 2025\n\nLast Zepto funding round\n\nSeries H · Oct 2025\n\nZepto revenue\n\nSeries H · Oct 2025\n\nKey investors in Zepto\n\n* ![](https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nexusvp.com&size=64)Nexus Venture Partners\n* ![](https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&url=http%3A%2F%2Fcontrary.com&size=64)Contrary\n* ![](https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.gladebrookcapital.com&size=64)Glade Brook Capital Partners\n* ![](data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns=)\">Lachy Groom\n* ![](https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.goodwatercap.com&size=64)Goodwater Capital\n* ![](https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&url=http%3A%2F%2Flsvp.com&size=64)Lightspeed Venture Partners\n\n### Zepto Overview\n\n#### About Zepto\n\nZepto is a Mumbai-headquartered quick-commerce platform delivering groceries, fruits, and electronics in 10 minutes via dark stores. Operating 300+ warehouses in 10 cities, Zepto stocks 5,000 SKUs from brands like Nestle and P&G. The app serves urban India with slotless ordering. Valued at $1.4 billion in 2023, it rais\n[…]\nl Partners; StepStone Group; Goodwater Capital; Lightspeed Venture Partners; Avenir; Avra; Nexus Venture Partners | $450M | $7B | Zepto, an Indian quick-commerce startup delivering groceries…Zepto, an Indian quick-commerce startup delivering groceries and essentials in under 10 minutes, closed a $450 million funding round on October 16, 2025, led by CalPERS with participation from existing investors including Avenir, Avra, General Catalyst, Glade Brook Capital Partners, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group. The round, a mix of primary (around $300-380 million) and secondary transactions, valued the company at $7 billion post-money, up 40% from $5 billion in its prior November 2024 round of $350 million. This pre-IPO financing boosted Zepto's cash reserves to nearly $900 million, intended to strengthen its balance sheet, fuel operational expansion, and support path to public listing soon. Zepto's revenue grew 2.5x year-on-year to Rs 11,110 crore in FY2025 (ending March 2025), from Rs 4,455 crore in FY2024 and Rs 2,024 crore in FY2023, reflecting consistent doubling of top-line growth per ROC filings. The company has raised about $3 billion total, with two-thirds in the last 18 months, positioning it strongly amid intensifying competition in India's $7 billion quick-commerce market against Blinkit, Swiggy Instamart, BigBasket, Flipkart Minutes, and Amazon. CEO Aadit Palicha highlighted the round as validation of rapid growth and operating lev\n[…]\nvestors and family offices have significantly increased their ownership stakes in recent months, with domestic ownership reaching approximately 40 percent of the company following secondary transactions and the broader fundraising activity. Zepto had previously raised $340 million at a $5 billion valuation in 2024. The company subsequently closed a larger $450 million primary funding round at a $7 billion valuation led by US pension fund CalPERS and existing investors General Catalyst and Avenir Growth, representing a 40 percent valuation increase from the prior year. |\n| Aug 2025 | Secondary | [CE Info Systems](/public-comps/ce-info-systems-valuation-multiples \"CE Info Systems\")CE Info Systems (lead) | $3M | $6.1B | Zepto is a quick commerce platform founded in 2021, deliveri…Zepto is a quick commerce platform founded in 2021, delivering groceries and essentials rapidly in India. In August 2025, digital navigation firm MapmyIndia, formally C.E. Info Systems Limited, invested Rs 25 crore ($2.9 million) in Zepto by acquiring 75,18,797 compulsorily convertible preference shares (CCPS) at Rs 33.25 each, equating to a 0.049% stake on a fully diluted basis at a $6.1 billion valuation. This cash transaction, expected to complete within three months, aims to expand MapmyIndia's mapping and location-based solutions in quick commerce. The investment marks up from Zepto's prior $5 billion valuation. Shortly before, Zepto secured Rs 7.5 crore from Elcid Investments. This preceded a larg\n[…]\n29%), and Instamart (25%) based on Q1 FY25 data. Motilal Oswal views Zepto as a potential free cash flow powerhouse in digital businesses. Subsequent developments include MapmyIndia's Rs 25 crore investment for 0.049% stake at $5.9 billion valuation, Elcid's Rs 7.5 crore at the same valuation, and Motilal Oswal's additional Rs 400 crore ($45.6 million) for 0.78% stake. Zepto is in talks for $450-500 million at $7 billion valuation. |\n| Aug 2024 | Series G | General Catalyst, Mars Growth Capita… +8General Catalyst (lead); Mars Growth Capital (lead); Epiq Capital; Dragon Fund; StepStone; Lightspeed Venture Partners; Avenir; Avra; Contrary; DST Global | $340M | $5B | Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce startup delivering groceri…Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce startup delivering groceries and essentials in minutes via dark stores in urban areas, competing with Blinkit and Swiggy Instamart. Founded by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra, it raised $340 million in primary equity capital in August 2024, led by General Catalyst ($250 million) and Mars Growth Capital ($50 million), with participation from Epiq Capital, Dragon Fund, and existing investors like DST Global, Lightspeed, and StepStone. This followed a $665 million June 2024 round at $3.6 billion post-money, bringing two-month total to $1 billion and overall funding to ~$1.6 billion. The August round valued Zepto at $5 billion post-money ($4.6 billion pre-money), a 3.5x increase from $1.4 billion in August 2023, reflecting in\n[…]\nvestor confidence in quick-commerce growth amid sector capital influx. Neeraj Arora from General Catalyst joined the board. Funds strengthen balance sheet for expansion to top 40 Indian cities, aiming to surpass DMart's valuation beyond $30 billion long-term. Financials show FY23 operating revenue of Rs 2,024 crore (up 1321.7% YoY from Rs 142.36 crore FY22), but net losses widened to Rs 1,272 crore (up 226.2% YoY); FY24 results pending. India's quick-commerce market projected to reach $7 billion GMV, growing 35%. |\n| Jun 2024 | Series F | Glade Brook Capita…, Nexus Venture Part… +8Glade Brook Capital Partners (lead); Nexus Venture Partners (lead); StepStone Group (lead); Goodwater Capital; Lightspeed Venture Partners; Avenir; Avra; Lachy Groom; Contrary; DST Global | $665M | $3.6B | Zepto, a Mumbai-based quick commerce startup specializing in…Zepto, a Mumbai-based quick commerce startup specializing in 10-15 minute grocery and essentials delivery via dark stores, raised $665 million in a highly oversubscribed Series F round on June 20, 2024, at a post-money valuation of $3.6 billion, more than doubling from $1.4 billion nine months prior. The round was co-led by existing investors Glade Brook Capital Partners, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group, with participation from new investors Avenir, Lightspeed Venture Partners, and Avra, alongside Goodwater Capital, Lachy Groom, Contrary, and DST Global. Zepto operates around 350 dark stores across 10 cities, planning to doub\n[…]\nnd by FY25, revenue reached $1.3 billion, representing 150% year-over-year growth. The company reported losses that improved significantly, with EBITDA margins moving from -60% in FY23 to -27% in FY24, and the company achieved EBITDA breakeven on an adjusted basis by late 2023. Zepto raised multiple funding rounds in 2023, including a Series E round of $200 million at a $1.4 billion valuation in early 2023 and a $665 million round at a $3.6 billion valuation in June 2023. By August 2024, the company was valued at $5 billion after raising $340 million. |\n| Aug 2023 | Series E | [StepStone Group](/public-comps/stepstone-group-valuation-multiples \"StepStone Group\"), Glade Brook Capita… +4StepStone Group (lead); Glade Brook Capital Partners; Goodwater Capital; Lachy Groom; Contrary; Nexus Venture Partners | $231M | $1.4B | Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce startup offering instant g…Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce startup offering instant grocery and essentials delivery through a network of dark stores or micro-warehouses, operating in seven major cities like Mumbai, Delhi, and Bengaluru, with over 220 stores, daily orders exceeding 300,000, and average order value of Rs 430-470. Founded in 2021 by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra, it provides 10-15 minute deliveries and had previously raised about $360-560 million across earlier rounds, reaching $900 million valuation in Series D in May 2022. In August 2023, Zepto raised $200-231 million in its Series E funding round led by St\n[…]\ngistics capabilities. Other investors in earlier or related rounds include Y Combinator, Nexus Venture Partners, and individuals like Lachy Groom, though specific participation in this round is not detailed beyond the lead. This followed initial funding and preceded a Series C of $100 million in December 2021 led by Y Combinator Continuity Fund for technology infrastructure improvements. Zepto continued aggressive fundraising with later rounds such as Series F ($31.3M in November 2023 led by Goodwater Capital and Nexus Venture Partners for operational improvements), Series G ($665M in June 2024 led by Glade Brook Capital, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group to prepare for IPO), Series H ($340M in August 2024 led by General Catalyst and Mars Growth Capital to bolster finances pre-IPO), and more recent pre-IPO rounds in 2024-2025 reaching valuations of $5B to $7B. Total funding across all rounds amounts to approximately $2.93 billion as of October 2025. Later developments show Zepto scaling order volume 200% over 18 months by late 2025, achieving store-level profitability in parts of its network, building nearly $900 million in cash reserves, increasing domestic ownership to 40%, and preparing for a 2026 IPO after moving its base to India. |\n| Mar 2021 | Series A | Nexus Venture Part…Nexus Venture Partners (lead) | $7M | - | - |\n| Sep 2020 | Seed | Contrary, Y Combinator +3Contrary (lead); Y Combinator; Ricardo Schaefer; Global Founders Capital; Unpopular Ventures | $50\n\"\"\"",{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"verdict":{"type":"string","format":"enum","enum":["supported","unsupported","contradicted"]},"evidenceQuote":{"type":"string"},"reasoning":{"type":"string"}},"required":["verdict","evidenceQuote","reasoning"]}}]}
