{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:21:03.517Z","session":"3b9ec3d1-7df0-41f4-8dd1-d503b69c5c7f","event":"tool.end","callId":"4204bf98-216c-4deb-8263-1d53bc309d53","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2462,"result":[{"title":"Medium","url":"https://blog.zepto.com/from-software-engineer-ii-to-engineering-manager-ravi-patels-journey-at-zepto-ed5e065fcdcc","content":"When Ravi Patel joined Zepto in 2021, he was one of the very first frontend engineers at a startup still defining its place in the quick commerce ecosystem. Fast forward to today — Ravi is an Engineering Manager leading the app teams responsible for Shopping experience, Super Saver, and New Category initiatives on Zepto’s consumer platform.\n\n## Get Bhavya Sharma’s stories in your inbox\n\nJoin Medium for free to get updates from this writer. [...] Sitemap\n\nOpen in app\n\nSign in\n\nSearch\n\nSign in\n\n## Zepto TechXPress\n\n·\n\nZepto TechXPress\n\nStories building the fastest growing company in India\n\n# From Software Engineer II to Engineering Manager — Ravi Patel's Journey at Zepto\n\nBhavya Sharma\n\nBhavya Sharma\n\n3 min read\n\n·\n\nJul 4, 2025\n\n--\n\nPress enter or click to view image in full size [...] From building the first version of the consumer web app to mentoring a growing team of developers, Ravi's story is a reflection of what it means to grow with Zepto: move fast, learn faster, and never lose sight of the customer.\n\n> Keep following the Zepto Tech Blog for more stories from the people powering the platform.\n\nZepto TechXPress\n\nZepto TechXPress\n\n## Published in Zepto TechXPress\n\n1.3K followers\n\n·Last published 5 days ago\n\nStories building the fastest growing company in India","score":0.85624856},{"title":"Zepto - Company Profile","url":"https://www.boringbusinessnerd.com/startups/zepto","content":"Nikhil Mittal: VP of Engineering at Zepto. Former VP of Engineering at KiranaKart.‍\n\n Nitesh Sinha: VP of Product at Zepto. Former Senior Director of Product Management at Meesho.\n\n## Press\n\n Forbes India (March 13, 2023): Where is 10-minute grocery delivery headed?\n\n Business Standard (May 31, 2023): Online grocery firm Zepto announces leadership elevation as it eyes IPO\n\n TechCrunch (May 2, 2022): Zepto, a 10-minute grocery delivery app, raises $200 million at $900 million valuation [...] As of May 2022, Zepto was growing 50% MoM with annualized revenue between $200-$400 million. In Q2 2022, Zepto grew its revenue by 800% while slashing expenses by 5x.\n\n Zepto is currently operational in 10 cities across India.\n\n## Leadership Team\n\n Aadit Palicha: Co-Founder & CEO of Zepto. Former Co-Founder & CEO of KiranaKart.\n\n Kaivalya V.:  Co-Founder & CTO of Zepto. Former Co-Founder & CTO of KiranaKart.\n\n Amritansu Nanda: CMO at Zepto. Former Head of Digital Marketing at FACES Cosmetics.","score":0.8443195},{"title":"How Zepto Delivers Groceries in 10 Minutes","url":"https://techresearchonline.com/blog/zepto-10-minute-delivery-business-model","content":"Zepto's success story wouldn't be complete without the vision and leadership of its two founders, Kaivalya Vohra and Aadit Palicha. These Stanford dropouts have disrupted the quick commerce industry in India, through their passion for innovation and a focus on speed and convenience. Let’s take a closer look at each of them.\n\n### Kaivalya Vohra [...] Since childhood, Kaivalya has demonstrated his enthusiasm for both business and technology by studying how systems operate and how performance could be enhanced. At Zepto, Kaivalya concentrates on technical operations that drive business efficiency and scalability while positioning the company for future developments.\n\n### Aadit Palicha [...] ### Kaivalya Vohra\n\nAs co-founder of Zepto, Kaivalya Vohra stands out for his deep expertise in technology and business foundations. After deciding to drop out of Stanford University, Kaivalya pursued building a company that could transform the grocery delivery industry through its innovative business model. He dropped out of college because he knew advanced technology paired with innovation could address critical issues in the real world.","score":0.7009158},{"title":"Zepto (company)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zepto_(company)","content":", \n\n India\nNumber of locations 1000+ stores (2026)\nKey people   Aadit Palicha (CEO)\n   Nikhil Mittal (CTO)\nServicesOnline grocer\nRevenueImage 5: Increase₹9,366 crore (US$970 million)(2025)\nNet incomeImage 6: Positive decrease₹−3,367 crore (US$−350 million) (2024)\nNumber of employees 16,898(March 2026)\nWebsitezepto.com [...] Aadit Palicha started KiranaKart with Kaivalya Vohra in 2020 when they were 17 years old.( Palicha and Vohra skipped college to start Zepto, instead raising capital from Contrary \"Contrary (venture capital firm)\"), which offered to invest if they dropped out of Stanford University.( [...] Palicha and Vohra originally branded the company as KiranaKart and focused on facilitating grocery delivery by partnering with local kirana stores, but that approach did not gain traction.( They also participated in Y Combinator's accelerator program while building out the first version of the platform.(","score":0.5883458},{"title":"Zepto: How Two 17-Year-Olds Built India's Largest Seller Of Fruits and Vegetables","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKZCU0ynEbs&vl=en-US","content":"### Description\n230,356 views\nPosted: 2026-05-19\nAadit Palicha is the co-founder and CEO of Zepto, one of India's largest quick-commerce grocery platforms. What began as a WhatsApp group delivering groceries to neighbors in Mumbai during COVID has grown into a company employing over 200,000 people, processing millions of deliveries per day and operating one of India's largest fruits and vegetables supply chains — all built around a 10-minute delivery model powered by a network of dark stores. [...] [27:28] surrounded us that we've learned from and most of them most of that learning has come from our management team. So 