{"ts":"2026-09-26T16:39:48.787Z","session":"56a111cd-b411-49d9-9130-1b22a5bb316a","event":"tool.end","callId":"0cd70a80-a6eb-411a-b84a-366fb6b0a70a","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":5112,"result":[{"title":"Loblaw Companies Limited Announces Senior Management Changes, Effective by Q1 2024 - Perishable News","url":"https://perishablenews.com/retailfoodservice/loblaw-companies-limited-announces-senior-management-changes-effective-by-q1-2024","content":"“Robert, Richard and I have worked side by side with our management teams to improve Loblaw’s performance. Per is an exceptional executive with a decades-long track record of delivering retail excellence and successful growth – enabling a smooth transition for our teams,” said Weston. “Coming from Salling, he arrives with a clear understanding of what it means to lead a nation’s largest retail network and team, and a family company established more than a century ago to help Canadians live life [...] “Over the past two years, we have strengthened the foundations of the company. Our management team is exceptional, and our 220,000 colleagues continue to deliver for our customers every day,” said Galen G. Weston. “In Per we have found a world-class retail executive to help us build from that position of leadership and strength, and to continue on that journey.” [...] Mr. Bank is a 30-year career retailer with deep expertise in retail operations and supply chain. He is the outgoing Chief Executive Officer of Salling Group A/S, the largest retailer in Denmark, with 1,700 multi-banner supermarkets across three countries, supported by strong e-commerce, loyalty, and private-brand programs, and having one of Denmark’s largest private-sector workforces.","score":0.8958969},{"title":"Walmart Canada announces senior executive team changes, supporting continued momentum as a leading omnichannel retailer","url":"https://www.newswire.ca/news-releases/walmart-canada-announces-senior-executive-team-changes-supporting-continued-momentum-as-a-leading-omnichannel-retailer-839706705.html","content":"Share this article\n\nMISSISSAUGA, ON, March 6, 2024 /CNW/ - As the company begins its new fiscal year, Walmart Canada has announced expanded and new roles for five members of its senior leadership team to support its continued growth as a modern, omnichannel retailer. [...] Laurent Duray has been promoted to the role of Chief Growth Officer. This expanded portfolio will focus on alternate revenue streams, such as Retail Media and Financial Services, digital enablement, eCommerce and customer understanding. Laurent's portfolio also encompasses the Customer Organization, including marketing, and eCommerce leadership teams. Laurent previously held the role of Walmart Canada's Chief eCommerce Officer. [...] # Walmart Canada announces senior executive team changes, supporting continued momentum as a leading omnichannel retailer\n\nWalmart Canada logo / logo de Walmart Canada (CNW Group/Wal-Mart Canada Corp.)\")\n\n## News provided by\n\nMar 06, 2024, 12:31 ET\n\n## Share this article\n\nShare this article","score":0.8706085},{"title":"Changes in Metsä Tissue Management team","url":"https://www.metsagroup.com/metsatissue/news-and-publications/news/2024/changes-in-metsa-tissue-management-team","content":"Title: Changes in Metsä Tissue Management team\n- Management and Board of Directors. - Aiming for fossil-free packaging. - Ensuring high-quality product safety. - Workplace safety and well-being. - We aim for a transparent value chain. + Subscribe our news to your e-mail. * + Future mill in Goole, East Riding of Yorkshire, the UK. - Endorsements for the planned new tissue paper mill in Goole. / News and Publications / News / 2024 / Changes in Metsä Tissue Management team. # Changes in Metsä Tissue Management team. PRESS RELEASE 18 DECEMBER 2024 at 9.15 CET. **Joonas Kukkonen** has been appointed Senior Vice President, Finland and the Baltics, and member of the company’s Management Team. He reports to Metsä Tissue’s CEO **Esa Kaikkonen**. The change will enter into force as of January 1st 2025. Download the image of Joonas Kukkonen here. **For further information**: Joanna Linnermo, Director, Communications, tel. +358 40 5555868 or joanna.linnermo[@]metsagroup.com. Metsä Group’s Tissue and Greaseproof Papers business, or Metsä Tissue, produces hygiene products for households and professionals, and greaseproof papers for food preparation and packaging. Our high-quality locally produced brands ­– Lambi, Serla, Mola, Tento, Katrin and SAGA – make daily life cleaner. We promote a diverse, equal, and inclusive culture. Our 2023 sales were EUR 1.3 billion, and we have approximately 2,500 employees. Metsä Group’s parent company Metsäliitto Cooperative is owned by around 90,000 Finnish forest owners. ## Subscribe our news. ## Latest news. * ### Metsä Tissue renews organisation to accelerate growth. * ### Metsä Tissue Germany recognised as Top Employer for the sixth consecutive year. * ### Metsä Tissue appoints new management team.","score":0.67758125},{"title":"Management changes at Magura USA | Bicycle Retailer and Industry News","url":"https://www.bicycleretailer.com/announcements/2020/01/23/management-changes-magura-usa-0","content":"Title: Management changes at Magura USA | Bicycle Retailer and Industry News\n# Management changes at Magura USA. They are posted as a service to our readers and supporters. Contact us to submit a press release or if you find a posting objectionable. After 20 years as President of Magura USA, Jeff Enlow has retired as of Jan 1st, 2020. During Enlow's time with Magura he guided the German brands U.S. operations to grow OEM and aftermarket business in both the bike and motorcycle categories. Jeff began his career in the cycling industry with Marwi in 1989 before joining Magura USA in 1999. I've accomplished many of my life goals during my tenor and I'm very thankful to Magura for this time together!\". Enlow will continue to support the Magura USA team on overall strategies as an independent consultant. It was a long ride and I ended up with mud on my face, crash and burns and many scars, but it was all worth it.\" said Jeff. Julia Michels has assumed the role of President & CEO of Magura USA from Enlow on January 1, 2020. Jeff Enlow said of Michels, \"Julia has all the leadership qualities needed to be successful in her new role. Michels originally joined the Magura USA team in 2006 as an accountant but grew to fulfill numerous roles within the company including human resources, inventory control & purchasing, supply chain management, logistics, and information technology. In 2018 she was promoted to the Magura USA management team as CFO/Treasurer. Now, as President/CEO Julia hopes to lead the Magura USA team in providing safety for the mobility of tomorrow. Julia graduated Master of Business Administration from Maryville University of Saint Louis in 2000, and also earned a Bachelor of Science in Accountancy with Honors from University of Illinois at Champaign-Urbana in 1997. ## Taiwan bike makers report sales increases in May. Posted in International *6 hours 48 min* ago. Posted in Industry News *11 hours 40 min* ago. Posted in Announcements *13 hours 28 min* ago. ## PeopleForBikes Investor Summit Explores Opportunities to Shape the Future of Bicycling and the Bike Industry. Posted in Announcements *3 days 14 hours* ago. Posted in International *3 days 18 hours* ago.","score":0.33215925},{"title":"Upcoming changes that impact team management - Platform News - Asana Forum","url":"https://forum.asana.com/t/upcoming-changes-that-impact-team-management/226064","content":"Title: Upcoming changes that impact team management - Platform News - Asana Forum\n# Upcoming changes that impact team management. We’re working on changes to the `Teams` resources and endpoints to improve permissions and management. We don’t currently have a clear specification we can share, but we want to give our developer community as much notice as possible. # Current Behavior. # New Behavior. We will clarify the above behavior with more detail once we have finalized our specification. # Impact. # Timeline. Sasha, on behalf of the Asana API Team. I’m actually lookig forward this change. In our company we are extending the usage of the tool from the Single Company (around 2-3k employees) to the whole Group (up to 60k employees). Currently we have 2 separete organizations/Domain in ASANA. 1 with ~300 users and ~10 teams, and another with ~900 users and ~50 teams. Based on your experience I have 2 questions:. Hey folks, just an update that the specification and description for these changes should become available in the next few weeks. This update to team memberships will begin rollout in February. feature is known as `Team Admins`. The documentation has been updated and should reflect the endpoints that may now. return a `403 Forbidden` when a non-admin user attempts to perform an admin. action in workspaces that have Team Admins enabled. changeset *only* affects write endpoints. There is no change header, and this. change is not eligible for `Asana-Enable` or `Asana-Disable` headers. Hey folks, an update that this will become `Generally Available` on 2023-02-02. | [[New] Team admins](https://forum.asana.com/t/new-team-admins/593026)  Changelog api ,  teams-api ,  breaking-change ,  authorization-api | 2 | 587 | 5 December 2023 |. Product Launches | 12 | 3291 | 27 February 2023 |. | [[Halted] Upcoming changes that impact getting and setting memberships and access levels](https://forum.asana.com/t/halted-upcoming-changes-that-impact-getting-and-setting-memberships-and-access-levels/232106)  Platform News | 51 | 7817 | 25 April 2023 |. | [[ Change ] Ability to edit team administrative settings](https://forum.asana.com/t/change-ability-to-edit-team-administrative-settings/986899)  Changelog teams-api | 0 | 217 | 26 November 2024 |. | Failed to add team member with error: You must be a member of the team to add members  Developers & API | 5 | 1648 | 30 May 2025 |. Powered by Discourse, best viewed with JavaScript enabled.","score":0.2920705}]}
