{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:01:19.156Z","session":"bc5ed9c3-17eb-4e53-a2e2-d55c2f33d937","event":"tool.end","callId":"0ec80626-cd90-479c-aa39-3da1cd5e4f2a","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2535,"result":[{"title":"Kalyan Jewellers makes leadership changes","url":"https://www.peoplematters.in/news/leadership/kalyan-jewellers-makes-leadership-changes-26214","content":"Kalyan Jewellers has appointed Sanjay Raghuraman as its new Chief Executive Officer.  Raghuraman has been elevated to the new position of CEO from his earlier position as the Chief Operating Officer. The company has also announced the appointment of Salil Nair joining the company’s board as a non-executive director, and Anil Nair joining as an independent director. [...] ### Leadership\n\n# Kalyan Jewellers makes leadership changes\n\n\n\nAnushree Sharma•Join UsGoogle News\n\nJoin UsGoogle News\n\nArticle cover image\n\nKalyan Jewellers has announced the appointment of its new CEO along with two other appointments on company's board. [...] Speaking about this announcement T S Kalyanaraman, chairman and managing director, Kalyan Jewellers said, “We are extremely delighted to appoint Sanjay Raghuraman as the chief executive officer of the company and warmly welcome Salil Nair and Anil Nair, who bring to the table expertise in the retail and marketing spaces, to the Kalyan Jewellers core team. With an aim to continue expanding the company’s footprint to cater to newer audiences, we are confident that our enhanced team will take us","score":0.8588255},{"title":"Kalyan Jewellers","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalyan_Jewellers","content":"In 2022, the company onboarded Vinod Rai as its chairperson and independent non-executive director. Vinod Rai was the former Comptroller and Auditor General of India (CAG) and the former chair of the United Nations Panel of External Auditors.\n\n## Candere\n\n[edit] [...] 4. ↑ \"Kalyan Jewellers IPO opens today: Everything you need to know\". The Indian Express. 16 March 2021. Retrieved 1 October 2024.\n5. ↑ Stock exchange, Bombay. \"Kalyan Jewellers IPO BSE\" – via BSE Official.\n6. ↑ \"Ex-CAG Vinod Rai appointed as Kalyan Jewellers India chairman\". Business Today. 28 March 2022. Retrieved 1 October 2024.\n7. ↑ \"Kalyan Jewellers acquires remaining 15% stake in Candere for Rs 42 crore - CNBC TV18\". CNBCTV18. 3 June 2024. Retrieved 1 October 2024. [...] Kalyan Jewellers expanded into tier-2 and tier-3 cities in India. It has over 200 stores in India and a presence in the Middle East, with stores in the UAE, Qatar, Oman and Kuwait.\n\nIn 2014, Warburg Pincus picked up a minority stake in Kalyan Jewellers for ₹700 crore and a second tranche of ₹500 crore in 2017. In 2021, Kalyan Jewellers went public with an initial public offering (IPO).","score":0.80442166},{"title":"Kalyan Jewellers to enter U.S. market in FY25 - The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/kalyan-jewellers-to-foray-into-us-market-in-fy25/article68003323.ece","content":", we plan to open at least 80 Kalyan Jewellers showroom in India, at least 50 Candere stores in India and six showrooms overseas,” said Ramesh Kalyanaraman, Executive Director, Kalyan Jewellers India in an interview.\n\n“In FY26 we plan grow 20% more,” he added.\n\nIn the past year, the company had gone for the Franchise Owned Company Operated (FOCO) model and it would take this route to expand its base. [...] “So our expansion is completely fuelled by franchisee partners now. They will invest the money for the inventory and the capex for a store, and Kalyan Jewellers will run the store for them and it’s a margin share, which we do, wherein they get return on investment which they expect and we get the return which we want,” Mr. Kalyanaraman said. [...] He attributed growth in jewellery sales to the sector’s transition to becoming more formalised and the government mandating hallmarking and levying Goods & Services Tax.\n\nPublished - March 28, 2024 10:12 pm IST\n\n Copy link\n Email\n Facebook\n Twitter\n Telegram\n LinkedIn\n WhatsApp\n Reddit\n\nSEE ALL  Remove\n\n### Related Topics\n\njewelry\n\n0 / 0\n\nThe Hindu\n\nSign in to unlock member-only benefits!","score":0.7825466},{"title":"About Kalyan Jewellers - Company Information, ...","url":"https://trendlyne.com/equity/about/447071/KALYANKJIL/kalyan-jewellers-india-ltd","content":"References\n\n1. Annual Report May 2025\n2. Investor Presentation Feb 2026\n3. Annual Report May 2024\n4. Investor Presentation Nov 2025\n\n## Kalyan Jewellers Management structure\n\nAll Gross Remunerations are in INR\n\n##### Jishnu R G\n\n###### Company Secretary, Compliance Officer\n\n-\n\nMar 26\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### Mr. Sanjay Raghuraman\n\n###### Chief Executive Officer\n\n-\n\nMar 26\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### Mr. V Swaminathan\n\n###### Chief Financial Officer\n\n-\n\nMar 26\n\nGross Remuneration [...] Gross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### Mr. Arun Sankar\n\n###### Head(Technology)\n\n-\n\nMar 26\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### Mr. Sanjay Mehrottra\n\n###### Head(Strategy, Corporate Affairs)\n\n-\n\nMar 26\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### Mr. Abraham George\n\n###### Head(Treasury & Investor Relation)\n\n-\n\nMar 26\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n## Kalyan Jewellers Board of directors\n\nAll Gross Remunerations are in INR\n\n##### Trikkur Sitarama Iyer Kalyanaraman\n\n###### ED / MD / Promoter\n\n1127.6 Lac\n\n2025 [...] 1127.6 Lac\n\n2025\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### SEETHARAM KALYANARAMAN TRIKKUR\n\n###### WTD & Executive Director\n\n1127.6 Lac\n\n2025\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### TRIKKUR KALYANARAMAN RAMESH\n\n###### WTD & Executive Director\n\n1127.6 Lac\n\n2025\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### Vinod Rai\n\n###### Chairman & Independent Directo\n\n6 Lac\n\n2025\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### K J Udeshi\n\n###### Independent Non Exe. Director\n\n6 Lac\n\n2025\n\nGross Remuneration\n\nYear\n\n##### A D Murthy Chavali","score":0.68697983},{"title":"Gold Jewellery | about-us | Kalyan jewellers","url":"https://www.kalyanjewellers.net/board-of-directors.php","content":"Vinod Rai was the former comptroller and auditor general of India\n\nMr. Rai was awarded the Padma Bhushan, India’s Third highest civilian award in recognition of his services to the country.\n\nMr. TS Kalyanaraman\n\n###### Mr. TS Kalyanaraman\n\nManaging Director\n\n46 years’ retail experience\n\n26 years in the jewellery industry\n\nWith Kalyan since Inception\n\nMr.TK Seetharam\n\n###### Mr. TK Seetharam\n\nWhole Time Director\n\n23 Years with Kalyan\n\nMr.TK Ramesh\n\n###### Mr. TK Ramesh\n\nWhole Time Director [...] 23 Years with Kalyan\n\n#### Non – Executive Directors: Retail industry experience and financial sponsor Representations\n\nMr. Salil Nair\n\n###### Mr. Salil Nair\n\nNon-Executive Director\n\n24 years’ experience in the retail industry\n\nFormer CEO of Shoppers Stop.\n\nAnish Kumar Saraf\n\n###### Mr. Anish Kumar Saraf\n\nNon-Executive Director\n\nHigh dell Nominee Director\n\nManaging Director at Warburg Pincus, India\n\n#### Independent Directors: Industrial Experience and expertise in key domains [...] Ms. Radhika Ramani\n\n###### Ms. Radhika Ramani\n\nIndependent Director\n\nOver 25 years of global experience in media, communications, and growth operations across the UK, Singapore, and India.\n\nFormer Managing Partner (South) at Motivator (GroupM network). Currently Global Head of Growth Operations at Dentsu, UK.\n\nHolds a Master’s in Data Science from Deakin University and an MBA from Goa Institute of Management.\n\nMr. C. R. Rajagopal\n\n###### Mr. C. R. Rajagopal\n\nIndependent Director","score":0.5243709}]}
