{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:03:41.195Z","session":"f222efe3-750b-436c-b711-11fce1f15687","event":"llm.start","callId":"103836e7-3bdd-4758-9762-e76165259ea9","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence. Each fact is one short, self-contained statement (e.g. \"CEO and MD of Infosys since 2 January 2018\") with \"sourceUrl\" set to the URL of the one source that states it. Sources headed \"Previously learned\" are facts from earlier research — cite their URL like any other source.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"facts\": [{\"fact\": string, \"sourceUrl\": string}]}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: For Zepto, find its current head of engineering, when they joined, and where they worked before.\nSub-questions to cover:\n- Who is the current head of engineering at Zepto?\n- When did Zepto's head of engineering join the company?\n- Where did Zepto's head of engineering work before joining Zepto?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Zepto elevates Jitendra Singh to director of engineering - Indian Television Dot Com\nURL: https://indiantelevision.com/mam/zepto-elevates-jitendra-singh-to-director-of-engineering\nSingh announced the development on LinkedIn, sharing that he has stepped into the new role after serving in a series of increasingly senior leadership positions at the company. As director of engineering, he will continue to oversee engineering excellence, platform scalability, product innovation and broader technology strategy as Zepto expands its footprint across India. [...] His appointment comes at a time when Zepto continues to scale operations in one of India’s most competitive consumer technology sectors. Engineering leadership has become increasingly critical for quick-commerce players as they balance rapid customer growth, operational efficiency and product innovation. [...] Share  Tweet\n\nMUMBAI: Climbing the tech ladder at quick speed, much like the deliveries his company is known for, Jitendra Singh has been promoted to director of engineering at Zepto, marking the latest milestone in his nearly four-year journey with the fast-growing quick-commerce platform.\n\n[S2] From Software Engineer II to Engineering Manager\nURL: https://blog.zepto.com/from-software-engineer-ii-to-engineering-manager-ravi-patels-journey-at-zepto-ed5e065fcdcc\nWhen Ravi Patel joined Zepto in 2021, he was one of the very first frontend engineers at a startup still defining its place in the quick commerce ecosystem. Fast forward to today — Ravi is an Engineering Manager leading the app teams responsible for Shopping experience, Super Saver, and New Category initiatives on Zepto’s consumer platform.\n\n## Get Bhavya Sharma’s stories in your inbox\n\nJoin Medium for free to get updates from this writer. [...] From building the first version of the consumer web app to mentoring a growing team of developers, Ravi's story is a reflection of what it means to grow with Zepto: move fast, learn faster, and never lose sight of the customer.\n\n> Keep following the Zepto Tech Blog for more stories from the people powering the platform.\n\nZepto TechXPress\n\nZepto TechXPress\n\n## Published in Zepto TechXPress\n\n1.3K followers\n\n·Last published 5 days ago\n\nStories building the fastest growing company in India [...] Sitemap\n\nOpen in app\n\nSign in\n\nSearch\n\nSign in\n\n## Zepto TechXPress\n\n·\n\nZepto TechXPress\n\nStories building the fastest growing company in India\n\n# From Software Engineer II to Engineering Manager — Ravi Patel's Journey at Zepto\n\nBhavya Sharma\n\nBhavya Sharma\n\n3 min read\n\n·\n\nJul 4, 2025\n\n--\n\nPress enter or click to view image in full size\n\n[S3] Deepak Jain - Director of Engineering @ Zepto\nURL: https://in.linkedin.com/in/deepcoder\n- One of the things I enjoy the most at Zepto is seeing complex systems take shape from a blank canvas. Over the last few years, we've built products at an incredible pace—not just shipping fast, but continuously evolving them to handle massive scale, changing business models, and ever-growing operational complexity. Every iteration teaches us something new. Our Builder Series is an opportunity to go beyond demos and feature launches. It's where our engineers share the architecture, trade-offs, [...] trade-offs, and engineering decisions behind the systems powering Zepto. These deep dives are so exciting and insightful. Looking forward to many more sessions from our teams! 🚀 Nikhil Mittal Ayush Agrawal Nishant Takkar Sripad Vallabha Sumit Nagariya Deepak Jain srk prasad Rajendra Bera ANUMOD AGARWAL Bhavya Sharma Pallavi M R [...] and a more productive engineering experience. Proud of the team's deep dive and the engineering mindset behind it. Kudos to Vivek Kumar , Madhavi Parmar and Sarthak J. ! 🚀 Zepto Deepak Jain Karthic Somalinga Nikhil Mittal Kaivalya V. #zepto #zeptotech\n\n[S4] Engineering Manager job at Zepto - Instahyre\nURL: https://www.instahyre.com/job-219683-engineering-manager-at-zepto-bangalore\nFounded in 2021 by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra, Zepto is on a mission to save you time making every second count towards life's real joys. Our platform has revolutionized rapid commerce in India with cutting-edge technology and strategically optimized delivery hubs. Zepto offers an extensive range of 45,000+ products, from fresh groceries to electronics, beauty essentials, apparels, toys and more, delivering across 50+ cities in minutes\\. Zepto Caf extends our commitment to convenience, [...] Engineering @ Zepto\n\nBuilding for scale, rapid iterative development, and customer-centric product thinking at each step define every day for a Zepto engineer. If building technology that impacts millions, brainstorming with some of the best minds in the country, executing at lightning speed, product-driven thinking, and owning your work from start to finish excites you, then Zepto is the right place for you.\n\nAbout Company\n\n##  Office and Product Photos [...] ## at Zepto Featured employer Diversity & inclusion focused employer\n\nBangalore8-13 Years\n\nThis job is no longer accepting applications\n\n## Job Description\n\nFunction:  Software Engineering → Mobile Development\n\n \n React Native\n JavaScript\n\n## About About Zepto\n\nOur Story\n\n[S5] Anshuman Srivastava - Engineering @ Zepto | Ex Gojek ...\nURL: https://in.linkedin.com/in/justanshuman\n# Anshuman Srivastava\nZepto\nBengaluru, Karnataka, India, IN  \n500 connections, 4849 followers\n\n## About\nProduct Engineering Leader with experience in leading high performing cross functional…\n\n## Experience\nN/A\n\n## Education\n### ABV-Indian Institute of Information Technology and Management  \nN/A  \n2010 - 2015  \nNone\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nN/A\n\n## Certifications\nBuilding and Leading Effective Teams (Columbia Business School)\n\n## Volunteering\n- Mentor\nScaler Academy\nEducation\nN/A\n\n[S6] Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto | TechGig\nURL: https://cio.techgig.com/my-first-tech-job/gen-zs-should-stay-focus-on-their-goals-and-must-give-their-best-yash-dayal-head-of-engineering-zepto/articleshow_b2b/99206539.cms\n* Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto. # Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto. In an exclusive interaction with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. We got an exclusive chance to interact with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto shared his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. E-Commerce is a challenging space as successful companies need to be best-in-class across many dimensions like operations, customer care, etc. **TechGig: Can you tell us your exclusive learnings from your first tech job?**. **Yash:** Your first tech job needs to be as explorational as possible. **Yash:** Technology evolves at a very rapid pace and one needs to have a dedicated focus to remain updated with the latest innovations in the space. A lot of times, fundamentals and approaches which were industry standards get disrupted by technology and one needs to adapt to learning new ways of doing things. **Yash:** The world today is full of many distractions and it is easy to get influenced and pressured by social media and success stories. The flip side is that the new-gen working cultures, like the hybrid work model, come with a unique set of challenges. 28 Aug 2024, 01:28 PMTechGig Guest Author. 9 Aug 2024, 10:40 AMTechGig Guest Aut\n\n[S7] Zepto elevates Zepto Cafe's business head Shashank Shekhar Sharma as CXO | Company News - Business Standard\nURL: https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/zepto-elevates-zepto-cafe-s-business-head-shashank-shekhar-sharma-as-cxo-124121900993_1.html\n\"After 2 years of deep work, iteration, and disciplined scaling, Zepto Caf is now at 30K+ orders/day and what we believe to be clear customer product-market-fit and solid unit economics.\n\n \n\n\"This excellent execution was only possible because of the leadership of Shashank Shekhar Sharma, who worked tirelessly with his team to turn Zepto Caf from a fringe idea to what could be the next revolution in food QSR in India,\" Zepto co-founder and CEO Aadit Palicha said in a LinkedIn post on Thursday. [...] Sharma, who has been building Zepto Cafe since its inception, will oversee Caf operations, footprint expansion, equipment procurement, quality control, and the end-to-end customer experience of Zepto Caf, a company statement said.\n\nPreviously serving as Business Head at Zepto Cafe, Sharma will continue to report to Zepto President Vinay Dhanani. [...] Thursday, September 24, 2026 | 07:17 AM ISTहिंदी में पढें\n\nNotification Icon\n\nuserprofile IconSearch\n\nHome / Companies / News / Zepto elevates Zepto Cafe's business head Shashank Shekhar Sharma as CXO\n\n# Zepto elevates Zepto Cafe's business head Shashank Shekhar Sharma as CXO\n\n## Sharma, who has been building Zepto Cafe since inception, will oversee Caf operations, footprint expansion, equipment procurement, quality control, and end-to-end customer experience of Zepto Cafe\n\n[S8] Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited - FY 2026\nURL: https://www.thecompanycheck.com/company/zepto-range-customized-engineering-private-limited/U29100MH2021PTC366500\nTitle: Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited - FY 2026\nIndian Legal Entity People Database Charges Regulatory Alerts Litigations Detailed Financials Credit Ratings Global Brands Funding Rounds Acquisitions Investors Database IPO & Listings News Company Report. Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited Company Logo. # Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited - Company Profile. It is a equipment & machinery private limited company based in Vasai, Maharashtra, India, established in 2021. About Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited. **Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited**, a active private limited company, was established on 28 August 2021 in Vasai, Maharashtra, India. It has an authorized capital of ₹0.10 M and a paid-up capital of ₹50.00 K . Explore comprehensive insights into Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited — covering financial performance, compliance records, Competitor, shareholding patterns, directors, key metrics, and litigation history. Who are the key members and board of directors at Zepto Range Customized Engineering Private Limited? Financial Performance of Zepto Range Customized Engineering. What is the Ownership and Shareholding Structure of Zepto Range Customized Engineering? was recorded as a recent event. The activity Raju Narayanath was appointed as a Director was appointed as a Director on 28 Aug 2021 & has been associated with this company since 4 years 9 months . The activity Prave\n\n[S9] Zepto People | Engineering & Technology\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RtmDvKBbqug\n0 subscribers\n3 likes\n456 views\n19 Sep 2024\nOur Engineering & Technology team at Zepto are paramount to the success of Zepto and every day they are innovating, scaling and securing our platform for our enterprise customers.\n\nHear straight from the team about the incredible work they do and why they love Zepto.\n\nKeen to board our mission? Head to www.zepto.com.au/careers/ to explore current job openings or to express your interest.\n\n\n\n[S10] Zepto Head Office\nURL: https://www.instagram.com/popular/zepto-head-office\nLog In\n\nSign Up\n\n# Zepto Head Office\n\nZepto is an Indian quick-commerce company with its corporate office located at Second Floor, 773 Sarjapur Main Road, Kaikondarahalli, Bengaluru, Karnataka, India. The company shifted its headquarters... more\n\n## zepto\n\n## zepto office [...] 89\n\nCREDAI Hyderabad Property Show 2026 Full Walkthrough | HITEX Top Projects & Deals❤️❤️@teja70mm47 #hitex #hitexexhibition #hitexexhibitioncenter #credai\n\nZepto work day --42 .\n#dailyvideo #viralreels #insta #work #zeptoofficial\n\n167\n\nZepto work day --42 . #dailyvideo #viralreels #insta #work #zeptoofficial [...] Get the full experience\n\nSign up for Instagram\n\n[S11] Software Engineers (Front-end & Back-end roles) at Zepto\nURL: https://startup.jobs/software-engineers-front-end-back-end-roles-zepto-8800811\nJoin a Talented Team: Work with world-class talent and leaders who support career growth\n   Flexible Work: A remote-first work culture, with the opportunity to work anywhere in Australia. You’ll also get access to premium co-working spaces and a Byron, Sydney & Melbourne Hub\n   Paid Parental Leave: 12 weeks Paid Parental Leave for primary caregivers and 4 weeks for secondary caregivers [...] Why Zepto?\n\nHeadquartered in beautiful Byron Bay, Zepto has an inspiring founder story and is a customer-focused, culture-first organisation. You’ll be joining a team that champions curiosity and a pioneering perspective, and thrives in a fast-moving sector.\n\nJust some of Zepto’s commitments to our people include: [...] About the Role\n\nZepto’s engineering teams are growing! And we’re currently looking to hire a back-end and a front-end focused Software Engineer. Reporting into an Engineering Manager, these two roles will make a significant impact as we continue scaling a world-class payments platform.\n\n[S12] Zepto Career Growth & Development 2026 | Built In\nURL: https://builtin.com/company/zepto/faq/career-growth-development\nRapid Shift-in-Charge Path — Rider partners (“Zeptons”) are promoted to shift-in-charge within three to four months, with internal moves also into in-store operations and rider call-center support. Visible fast promotions and multi-track mobility increase retention and signal real, near-term leadership opportunities for high performers. [...] View Website\n\n Overview\n Jobs\n Offices\n + Working at Zepto\n  + Culture & Values\n  + Career Growth & Development\n  + Compensation & Benefits\n  + Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing\n  + Leadership & Management\n  + Stability & Growth\n Is This Your Company?  Claim Profile\n\n# Zepto Career Growth & Development\n\nUpdated on April 01, 2026 [...] Pragati Six-Month Mentorship — The Pragati program provides six months of mentoring and observation for graduate-level Zeptons before elevation to bigger roles from the rider level. This structured cadence makes advancement predictable and merit-based, helping early-career employees convert frontline experience into supervisory scope quickly.\n\n[S13] Mohit G. - Associate Director @ Zepto\nURL: https://in.linkedin.com/in/mohit-g-a39abb28\nPlease fill in details in form link mentioned in first comment. Edit: Have received more than 3000 applications in last few hours . Closing the form as of now. Will open it up again, if required. #Hiring #Zepto #Engineering #JoinUs Karthic Somalinga Pallavi M R Nikhil Barge (निखिल बर्गे) ...more [...] # Mohit G.\nZepto\nBengaluru, Karnataka, India, IN  \n500 connections, 7085 followers\n\n## About\nI'm an Engineering Leader with over a decade of experience driving tech/product…\n\n## Experience\nN/A\n\n## Education\nN/A\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nSpot Award\nDirector Enginnering at Spire Technologies • April 2017\n\n## Certifications\nN/A\n\n## Volunteering\nN/A\n\n## Languages\nEnglish (-)\n\n## Organizations\nN/A [...] vested between July 16, 2023, and July 15, 2026. Liquidity Price: Set at Rs 713.4 per option. Payout Timeline: Scheduled for August 2026. \"It is time to share the company's success with employees who have contributed to its growth journey.\" — Kalyan Krishnamurthy, Flipkart Group CEO This follows a highly successful buyback last year that benefited over 7,000 employees across the Flipkart Group. It’s a massive win for employee-centric corporate culture in the ecosystem! #Flipkart #ESOP #Buyback\n\n[S14] Headed for the Exit: the Great Engineering Leader Career Break\nURL: https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/the-great-engineering-leader-career-break\nAlready a paid subscriber? Sign in\n\n© 2026 Gergely Orosz · Privacy ∙ Terms ∙ Collection notice\n\nStart your SubstackGet the app\n\nSubstack is the home for great culture [...] Several engineering leaders are stepping back into IC roles for more stability because engineering teams are smaller now.\n\nKarthik Hariharan, engineering leader at DoorDash, notes: [...] Two engineering leaders – a CTO and a VP of Engineering – mentioned “insane working hours” as a factor that contributed to them finally quitting. But there were other things as well:\n\n The business struggling for growth\n Their equity grant’s value shrinking to nothing before their eyes\n CEO/founder ignoring or overriding efforts to help the business succeed\n\n[S15] Previously learned\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zepto_(company)\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce company headquartered in Bengaluru\n- Zepto: Zepto was founded in July 2021 by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra\n\n[S16] Previously learned\nURL: https://www.boringbusinessnerd.com/startups/zepto\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Nikhil Mittal is the VP of Engineering at Zepto and former VP of Engineering at KiranaKart\n\n[S17] Previously learned\nURL: https://multiples.vc/private-comps/zepto\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Raised $665 million in June 2024 co-led by Glade Brook Capital Partners, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group\n- Zepto: Secured $340 million in August 2024 led by General Catalyst and Mars Growth Capital\n\n[S18] Previously learned\nURL: https://entrackr.com/news/zepto-raises-350-mn-surpasses-135-bn-in-funding-for-2024-7599303\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Raised $350 million in November 2024 led by Motilal Oswal Private Wealth",{"json":true,"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"claims":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"citedUrl":{"type":"string"},"supportingUrls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["text","citedUrl","supportingUrls"]}},"entitiesLearned":{"type":"array","item