excerpt; […] marks omitted text):\n\"\"\"\n[Skip to footer](#baseFooter)\n\n### Infrastructure to Intelligence\n\nNavigate the AI era with confidence. TCS helps you turn AI into a strategic partner that empowers talent, reimagines processes, and accelerates business transformation.\n\n[Unlock enterprise intelligence](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/infrastructure-to-intelligence)\n\n* [Industries](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/infrastructure-to-intelligence)\n* [Services](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/infrastructure-to-intelligence)\n* [Products and Platforms](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/infrastructure-to-intelligence)\n* [Research & Innovation](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/tcs-research-and-innovation)\n* [Alliances](https://www.tcs.com/who-we-are/alliances-partnerships)\n\n* [Banking](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/banking)\n* [Capital Markets](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/capital-markets)\n* [Consumer Packaged Goods and Distribution](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/consumer-packaged-goods-and-distribution)\n* [Communications, Media, and Information Services](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/communications-media-information-services)\n* [Education](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/education)\n* [Energy, Resources, and Utilities](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/energy-resources-utilities)\n* [Healthcare](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/healthcare)\n* [High Tech](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/high-tech)\n* [Insurance](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/insurance)\n* [Life Sciences](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/life-sciences)\n* [Manufacturing](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/manufacturing)\n* [Public Services](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/public-services)\n* [Retail](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/retail)\n* [Travel and Logistics](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/industries/travel-and-logistics)\n\n* [Artificial Intelligence and Data & Analytics](https://www.tcs.com/what-we-do/services/ai-data-and-\n[…]\nnowned professional with over four decades of varied work experience in banking and financial services domain. In 1975, Mr. Mistry began his career with AF Ferguson & Co, a renowned Chartered Accountancy Firm, followed by short stints with Hindustan Unilever Limited and Indian Hotels Company Ltd. In 1981, Mr. Mistry joined Housing Development Finance Corporation Limited (HDFC Ltd.), India's premier housing finance company. Over the years he held several responsibilities, prior to being inducted onto its Board as Executive Director in 1993. He was appointed as the Managing Director in 2000, as the Vice Chairman & Managing Director in October 2007 and was the Vice-Chairman & Chief Executive Officer of the Corporation with effect from January 1, 2010. With the amalgamation of HDFC Ltd. with HDFC Bank, Mr. Mistry superannuated from HDFC Ltd. and has been appointed as a Non-Executive Director on the Board of HDFC Bank from June 30, 2023. Apart from being responsible for the overall functioning of HDFC, Mr. Mistry played a critical role in the successful transformation of HDFC into India's leading Financial Services Conglomerate. He facilitated the formation of companies including HDFC Bank Limited, HDFC Asset Management Company Limited, HDFC Life Insurance Company Limited and HDFC ERGO General Insurance Company Limited. Mr. Mistry is a Senior Advisor to the Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan (OTPP), a Canada based pension fund, a Strategic Advisor for Cyrus Poonawalla Group’s Financia\n[…]\n A renowned professional with over four decades of varied work experience in banking and financial services domain. In 1975, Mr. Mistry began his career with AF Ferguson & Co, a renowned Chartered Accountancy Firm, followed by short stints with Hindustan Unilever Limited and Indian Hotels Company Ltd. In 1981, Mr. Mistry joined Housing Development Finance Corporation Limited (HDFC Ltd.), India's premier housing finance company. Over the years he held several responsibilities, prior to being inducted onto its Board as Executive Director in 1993. He was appointed as the Managing Director in 2000, as the Vice Chairman & Managing Director in October 2007 and was the Vice-Chairman & Chief Executive Officer of the Corporation with effect from January 1, 2010. With the amalgamation of HDFC Ltd. with HDFC Bank, Mr. Mistry superannuated from HDFC Ltd. and has been appointed as a Non-Executive Director on the Board of HDFC Bank from June 30, 2023. Apart from being responsible for the overall functioning of HDFC, Mr. Mistry played a critical role in the successful transformation of HDFC into India's leading Financial Services Conglomerate. He facilitated the formation of companies including HDFC Bank Limited, HDFC Asset Management Company Limited, HDFC Life Insurance Company Limited and HDFC ERGO General Insurance Company Limited. Mr. Mistry is a Senior Advisor to the Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan (OTPP), a Canada based pension fund, a Strategic Advisor for Cyrus Poonawalla Group’s Fin\n[…]\n with ICICI in 1990 and ISec, the joint venture between ICICI and JP Morgan, and then spent two years with Peregrine Capital. He was part of the founding team of Rothschild India in 1998 and played a key role in establishing Rothschild as a well-recognised and respected pure play advisory investment banking firm in India. He led the Rothschild India business from December 2005 to June 2016 when he stepped down from his full-time role. Mr. Bhandarkar's focus at Rothschild was on M&A as well as equity capital market advisory for Indian and international companies. He led the teams that worked closely with the Government of India on the 3G and BWA spectrum auctions, the first e-auctions done in India, and on the restructuring of the Enron and GE owned Dabhol power project, one of the largest and most complex restructurings to date. Mr. Bhandarkar did his Postgraduate Diploma in Management from XLRI, Jamshedpur in 1990. He lives in Mumbai.\n\n## Non Independent, Executive\n\nSwipe Left\n\nSwipe Right\n\n### K. Krithivasan\n\nChief Executive Officer & Managing Director\n\nK. Krithivasan, also known as Krithi, took over as the CEO & MD of Tata Consultancy Services on June 1, 2023. In his three-decade plus tenure at TCS, he has held various leadership roles in delivery, customer relationship management, large program management and sales and has a strong track record of successfully leading TCS’ largest industry vertical, the Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance business. As CEO, Krithi s\n[…]\nharpened the multinational company’s focus on industries by realigning the organisational structure into key business groups. He has steered TCS’ strategy for creating the world’s largest AI ready workforce. His focus has been on two key pillars: customer centricity and employee empathy. Under Krithi’s leadership, TCS continues to be recognized as a Global Top Employer. During his tenure, TCS’ brand value has risen by $2 billion, according to Brand Finance and has been rated as one of the world’s most admired companies by Fortune Magazine. He co-chairs the B20 Digital Transformation Taskforce in Brazil and has served as a member of the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) National Council. He is Chairman of the Board of Directors of Tata Consultancy Services Japan, Ltd. and holds Directorship position in TCS Foundation. Krithi joined Tata Consultancy Services in 1989 as an assistant system analyst in New Delhi. He moved to North America in 1997, where he was soon promoted to Regional Manager for TCS Florida. In the year 2000, Krithi took over as the e-business delivery head and was promoted in 2004 to head the BFSI Solution Centre. From 2018, he led the unit to achieve double-digit growth driven by strong momentum in all major markets. In his role as the head of the BFSI vertical, Krithi steered TCS’ expansion into high-growth markets such as Latin America, Australia and New Zealand. Born in Trichy, Tamil Nadu, Krithi received a bachelor’s degree in mechanical engineering f\n[…]\nrom the University of Madras and a master’s degree in industrial and management engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT), Kanpur. He is a proud father of two daughters and attributes his success to his family.\n\nRead more  About K. Krithivasan Opens in an overlay\n\n## K. Krithivasan\n\n### Chief Executive Officer & Managing Director\n\nK. Krithivasan, also known as Krithi, took over as the CEO & MD of Tata Consultancy Services on June 1, 2023. In his three-decade plus tenure at TCS, he has held various leadership roles in delivery, customer relationship management, large program management and sales and has a strong track record of successfully leading TCS’ largest industry vertical, the Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance business. As CEO, Krithi sharpened the multinational company’s focus on industries by realigning the organisational structure into key business groups. He has steered TCS’ strategy for creating the world’s largest AI ready workforce. His focus has been on two key pillars: customer centricity and employee empathy. Under Krithi’s leadership, TCS continues to be recognized as a Global Top Employer. During his tenure, TCS’ brand value has risen by $2 billion, according to Brand Finance and has been rated as one of the world’s most admired companies by Fortune Magazine. He co-chairs the B20 Digital Transformation Taskforce in Brazil and has served as a member of the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) National Council. He is Chairman of the \n[…]\nBoard of Directors of Tata Consultancy Services Japan, Ltd. and holds Directorship position in TCS Foundation. Krithi joined Tata Consultancy Services in 1989 as an assistant system analyst in New Delhi. He moved to North America in 1997, where he was soon promoted to Regional Manager for TCS Florida. In the year 2000, Krithi took over as the e-business delivery head and was promoted in 2004 to head the BFSI Solution Centre. From 2018, he led the unit to achieve double-digit growth driven by strong momentum in all major markets. In his role as the head of the BFSI vertical, Krithi steered TCS’ expansion into high-growth markets such as Latin America, Australia and New Zealand. Born in Trichy, Tamil Nadu, Krithi received a bachelor’s degree in mechanical engineering from the University of Madras and a master’s degree in industrial and management engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT), Kanpur. He is a proud father of two daughters and attributes his success to his family.\n\n### Aarthi Subramanian\n\nExecutive Director - President and COO\n\nMs. Aarthi Subramanian is the Executive Director – President and Chief Operating Officer of the Company. Prior to the above role, Ms. Aarthi Subramanian was the Group Chief Digital Officer at Tata Sons Private Limited (Tata Sons), the principal investment holding company and promoter of Tata enterprises. In this pivotal role, she led the conglomerate's digital, technology and innovation agenda across a diverse portfolio of indu\n\"\"\"",{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"verdict":{"type":"string","format":"enum","enum":["supported","unsupported","contradicted"]},"evidenceQuote":{"type":"string"},"reasoning":{"type":"string"}},"required":["verdict","evidenceQuote","reasoning"]}}]}
