under the name Instamart in 100 cities. The company was incorporated in 2013.\n\nSwiggy competes primarily with Zomato in food delivery. In quick-commerce, Instamart ranks behind competitors Blinkit and Zepto \"Zepto (company)\") in terms of market share.\n\n## History [...] In May 2020, Swiggy laid off 1,100 employees during the pandemic. The pandemic also resulted in the shut down of more than three-fourths of its cloud kitchens.\n\nIn August 2020, Swiggy launched its instant grocery delivery service called Instamart using a network of dark stores. In early 2021, the company closed Swiggy Stores and expanded its operations under Instamart. [...] | Key people |  Sriharsha Majety (CEO)  Rohit Kapoor (CEO – Food)  Phani Kishan Addepalli (CEO – Instamart)  Rahul Bothra (CFO)  Madhusudhan Rao (CTO) |\n| Services |  Online food ordering  Online grocery |\n| Revenue | Increase ₹163.33 billion (US$1.7 billion) (2025) |\n| Operating income | Decrease ₹−19.1 billion (US$−200 million) (2025) |\n| Net income | Decrease ₹−31.07 billion (US$−320 million) (2025) |","score":0.7978881},{"title":"Swiggy Instamart Business Model & Revenue Strategy","url":"https://www.icoderzsolutions.com/blog/instamart-business-model","content":"Swiggy Instamart is Swiggy’s quick commerce arm that delivers groceries, fresh produce, snacks, and household essentials through a fast, hyperlocal delivery network. You can explore the live platform at Swiggy Instamart. [...] Quick commerce has changed how India shops for groceries, and the Instamart business model sits right at the center of that shift. Swiggy launched Instamart to deliver everyday essentials quickly through a hyperlocal network, and it now competes directly with Blinkit and Zepto for a share of India’s fast-growing quick commerce market. [...] How Instamart has evolved: Instamart started as a grocery add-on within the Swiggy app and grew into a standalone quick commerce business with its own dark store network and app experience.\n Instamart’s role in Swiggy’s ecosystem: It complements Swiggy’s food delivery business, cross-selling to the same customer base while tapping into a new use case — quick, everyday grocery needs.\n\n## How Does the Instamart Business Model Work?","score":0.7498395},{"title":"Instamart - 2026 Company Profile, Funding & Competitors","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/instamart/__D5g1hntOjcAEcbfGgaSCI9-DycJiBD7Z01qDiHLq2hc","content":"Instamart is a funded company. Instamart has 1 institutional investor.\n\n## Instamart's founders and board of directors\n\n### Instamart's employee count trend\n\nEmployee count trend for Instamart\nlock\nchrome_extension_cta_illustration\n\n## Instamart's Competitors and alternates [...] | 18th | Logo for Instamart  Instamart 2005, Denver  (United States), Funding Raised | Online retailer offering ultra-fast grocery delivery  TGV | 48/100 | [...] JavaScript is disabled in your browser. enable it to enjoy the full features of Tracxn.\n\nTracxn.com\nAndroid\nApple\nChrome Web Store\nFirefox Extension\ntracxn ai suite\n\nAI-powered market intelligence across companies, investors, and sectors.\n\nLogo for Instamart\n\n# Instamart - Company Profile\n\nlock\nlock\nlock\nlock\nlock\n\n## Instamart - About the company\n\n### Company Details\n\nX\nFacebook\nPDF Illustration Image\n\n## Instamart's funding and investors","score":0.6932451},{"title":"Instamart","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/swiggy-instamart","content":"### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\nN/A\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nTechnology, Information and Internet\n\n### Company Size\n1,001-5,000 employees  \n5419 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed Instamart as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\nN/A\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: N/A\nLast Round Type: N/A\nTotal Rounds: N/A\nLast Round Raised: N/A\n\n### Investors\nN/A\n\n### Specialties\nN/A\n\n## Locations\nBengaluru, Karnataka, IN\n\n### Get Directions\nDirections","score":0.62742686}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:17:21.760Z","session":"fb606d91-84d8-4449-ae8e-447eaa3b9089","event":"tool.end","callId":"dd02e36e-7783-495c-9df2-561750759d9c","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2526,"result":[{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blinkit","content":"Blinkit is an Indian quick-commerce company owned by Eternal Limited. It was founded in December 2013 and is based in Gurgaon.\n\nCustomers of the company use a mobile app to order groceries and essentials online, which are sourced from the company's dark stores and delivered in 10 minutes. Blinkit operates in 153 cities in India, as of March 2025.\n\nIn 2022, Zomato Limited (now Eternal) acquired Blinkit for US$568 million in an all-stock deal.\n\n## History\n\n[edit] [...] Blinkit\n\n| Formerly | Grofers (2013–2021) |\n| Type | Subsidiary |\n| Industry | Q-commerce |\n| Founded | December 2013; 12 years ago (2013-12) |\n| Founders | Albinder Dhindsa Saurabh Kumar |\n| Headquarters | Gurgaon, Haryana, India |\n| Area served | India |\n| Key people | Albinder Dhindsa (CEO) |\n| Products | Bistro |\n| Services | Online grocer |\n| Revenue | Increase ₹5,206 crore (US$540 million) (FY25) |\n| Parent | Eternal Limited |\n| Website | blinkit.com | [...] In June 2022, a Bengaluru-based web development company called Blinkhit filed a trademark infringement lawsuit against Blinkit.\n\nIn April 2023, hundreds of Blinkit delivery partners in Delhi NCR, where about half of the company's dark stores were located, went on strike after a revision in payout structure resulted in lower earnings for them. This led to a temporary closure of many dark stores.","score":0.90692574},{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://in.linkedin.com/company/letsblinkit","content":"## Overview\nBlinkit (An Eternal Company) is a grocery and e-commerce platform. We pioneered the doorstep delivery model in India with over 10 million Indians shopping on Blinkit, for everything from grocery staples and vegetables to emergency supplies and electronics, and much more. If our mission interests you, send your CV to future@blinkit.com\n\n### Website\n\n### Crunchbase\nN/A\n### LinkedIn\nN/A\n\n### Industry\nTechnology, Information and Internet [...] ### Company Size\n1,001-5,000 employees  \n29232 associated members (LinkedIn members who've listed Blinkit as their current workplace on their profile)\n\n### Founded\n2013\n\n### Funding\nLast Round Date: N/A\nLast Round Type: N/A\nTotal Rounds: N/A\nLast Round Raised: N/A\n\n### Investors\nN/A\n\n### Specialties\nN/A\n\n## Locations\nPioneer Square, Sector 62, Golf Course Extension, Blinkit Headquarters, Gurgaon, Haryana 122001, IN\n\n### Get Directions\nDirections [...] # Blinkit\nIndia's Last Minute App ✨ Sell your products on Blinkit via seller.blinkit.com\nTechnology, Information and Internet • Gurgaon, Haryana • 1,772,212 followers • 1,001-5,000 employees","score":0.8747745},{"title":"Blinkit Foods Limited - 2026 Company Profile - Tracxn","url":"https://tracxn.com/d/legal-entities/india/blinkit-foods-limited/__djKNSolKqqiifOhCQSY8wrP4ba7ttguUwe7MUea3s2U","content":"Blinkit Foods Limited is a Public Limited Company and was incorporated on Aug 18, 2025 in India. It is registered at Registrar of Companies, ROC Delhi I. Its registered address is T-19, Basement, Green Park Main, Green Park, South West Delhi, New Delhi, Delhi, India, 110016.  Its corporate identification number is (CIN) U47222DL2025PLC453320 and its current status is Active. Its industry classification as per MCA is retail sale of non-alcoholic beverages including icecream not for consumption [...] | Name | Short Description | Founded Year | Location | Current Stage |\n ---  --- \n| Logo for Blinkit Blinkit | Online retailer of groceries, personal care, and household essential products | 2013 | India | Acquired |\n\nLogo for Blinkit\n\n## Documents of Blinkit Foods Limited15 mins\n\n### Latest Financials, Share Allotment and Annual Report\n\nThe latest filed financial documents, annual reports, and share allotment filings are shown below:\n\n### Recent Filings [...] Blinkit Foods Limited's authorised share capital is ₹1Cr and its paid up capital is ₹27.5L. The current board of directors of Blinkit Foods Limited comprises Deepak Ahluwalia, Ali Kausar Siddiqui and 1 more.\n\n## Contact Details for Blinkit Foods Limited\n\n## Brands associated with Blinkit Foods Limited","score":0.87139857},{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://www.zoominfo.com/c/blinkit/359515698","content":"# Blinkit\n\nBlink Commerce Private Limited, d/b/a Blinkit and formerly Grofers, is an Indian instant delivery service. Customers of the company use a mobile application to order groceries and essentials online. Blinkit's employees then secure the items from their warehouse and deliver the items to the consumer within 10 minutes. In 2022, Zomato acquired Blinki... \n\n## Leadership [...] ## Leadership\n\n- Khevender Daga — Quick Commerce Finance Controller (Blinkit & ...\n- Sanchit Bhasin — City Chief Executive Officer - Gujarat\n- Simran Shrivastav — Co-Chief Executive Officer\n\n## Company Details\n\n- Website: \n- Revenue: $94.2 Million\n- Employees: 1K - 5K\n- Industries: Freight & Logistics Services; Retail; Transportation; Grocery Retail\n- Headquarters: Golf Course Road Vipul Tech Sector-43 Sq Fl 4, Gurgaon, Haryana, 122001, India\n\n## Social Media\n\n- \n- \n- \n\n## Tech Stack [...] - blinkit cfo vipin kapooria has exited the quick commerce startup after more than a year moneycontrol reported kapooria could likely rejoin flipkart where he had worked for around seven years in two separate stints he was blinkits first fulltime designated cfo since amit sachdeva who worked at the startup as cfo between 2019 and 2022 left the firm\n- Blinkit-AI, an advanced artificial intelligence-driven platform, has raised $1.2 million in its seed funding round from Foliflex Cables (India).","score":0.84707206},{"title":"Blinkit","url":"https://eternal.com/our-businesses/blinkit","content":"Eternal\n\nInstant commerce indistinguishable from magic\n\nLaunched with the ambition of making everyday essentials available at your doorstep, Blinkit has revolutionized how India shops.  \n  \nIt has now evolved into a full-fledged quick commerce company, delivering thousands of products including grocery and daily essentials, electronics, beauty & personal care items, stationery, and emergency supplies.\n\n# Leading the quick commerce evolution [...] Blinkit is powered by a dynamic network of customers, store partners, and delivery partners working together seamlessly.\n\n31 million+ customers use our app monthly\n\n2,400+ stores across 300+ cities\n\n500,000+ delivery partners delivering at your doorstep\n\n# Beyond essentials\n\nBlinkit is constantly innovating to serve the evolving customer needs, the latest being in:\n\nBeauty & personal care\n\nBeauty & personal care [...] Sports\n\nSports\n\nFor training, playing, or just starting out, you can get the right gear delivered to your doorstep.\n\nToys\n\nToys\n\nBrain-boosting games, cuddly companions, and everything in between — toys to match every age and every mood.\n\n# Download the app now\n\nEverything you need, delivered to your doorstep on the Blinkit app.\n\nApp Download LogoApp Download Logo\n\nScan the QR code to download the app\n\ndownload app\n\n# Our other businesses\n\nBringing the world closer, one meal at a time","score":0.77893573}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:17:21.800Z","session":"fb606d91-84d8-4449-ae8e-447eaa3b9089","event":"tool.end","callId":"cc73a47f-85d1-447a-9c37-672a30812e32","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2569,"result":[{"title":"Top 25 Quick commerce platforms based in India","url":"https://revenuebase.ai/companies/quick-commerce-platforms/india","content":"| Strong evidence  “Dukaan is a DIY platform which enables merchants with zero programming skills to set up their e-commerce store using smartphone.”  Source: RevenueBase Database · checked Sep 14, 2026Thanks. The Data Team will review it. |\n| 23 | OOorjaa | Indirect evidence | Mumbai, India✓HQ checked Sep 14, 2026 | 51-200 | 111 contacts → | [...] | Strong evidence  “We are a quick, curated one-stop pan-city delivery platform, offering quality experiences to discerning consumers.”  Source: RevenueBase Database · checked Sep 14, 2026Thanks. The Data Team will review it. |\n| 13 | FFoodpanda India | Partial evidence | Bengaluru, India✓HQ checked Sep 14, 2026 | 1,001-5,000 | 427 contacts → | [...] | # | Company | RevenueBase Smart Search | Headquarters | Employees | Contacts |\n| 1 | SSwiggy | Partial evidence | Bengaluru, India✓HQ checked Sep 14, 2026 | 10001+ | 16,257 contacts → |\n| Partial evidence  “Swiggy is India’s pioneering on-demand convenience platform, catering to millions of consumers each month.”  Source: RevenueBase Database · checked Sep 14, 2026Thanks. The Data Team will review it. |","score":0.7311551},{"title":"Quick commerce targets e-commerce turf in India | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2024/06/17/can-quick-commerce-leapfrog-e-commerce-in-india","content":"Amazon — increasingly scaling down on its investments in e-commerce in India — has so far shown no interest in quick commerce in the country. The company, which offers same-day delivery for some items to Prime members, has questioned the quality of products from firms making “fast” deliveries in some of its marketing campaigns.\n\nA recent India consumer survey by Bank of America (BofA)Image Credits:BofA Global Research (screenshot) [...] Manish Singh\n\nEven as quick commerce startups are retreating, consolidating or shutting down in many parts of the world, the model is showing encouraging signs in India. Consumers in urban cities are embracing the convenience of having groceries delivered to their doorstep in just 10 minutes. The companies making those deliveries — Blinkit, Zepto and Swiggy’s Instamart — are already charting a path to profitability. [...] As brands increasingly focus on quick commerce as their fastest-growing channel and more consumers embrace the convenience and value proposition of 10-minute deliveries, the stage is set for a fierce battle between quick commerce and e-commerce giants in India.\n\nTopics\n\nAmazon, Amazon India, Apps, Asia, Commerce, Exclusive, Flipkart, India, Quick commerce, Swiggy, Swiggy Instamart, Walmart, Zepto, zomato","score":0.7304634},{"title":"Quick Commerce in India: Beyond Groceries and ...","url":"https://entrepreneur.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/funding/quick-commerce-in-india-beyond-groceries-and-the-future-of-instant-delivery/129933106","content":"Plazza is bringing the quick commerce model to the online pharma space dominated by Tata Digital's 1mg and Apollo 24/7. The startup delivers medicines in 10-15 minutes within a 3-4 km radius. \"This hasn't been done before in pharma,\" says founder Aman Priyadarshi. \"If a medicine exists in Bengaluru, you will git from us 24/7, and you will get it fast.\" [...] While some verticals have picked up, others are still navigating demand and funding. Gurugram-based Zing, which offered 10-minute food delivery, shut down in August 2025. Food delivery major Swiggy's 10-minute food delivery arm Snacc also ended operations earlier this year. Rival Swish, launched in 2024, however, has raised $54 million so far. [...] Home\n News\n Funding\n Quick commerce expands beyond groceries with VC funding, but scale questions persist","score":0.59796065},{"title":"World's Fastest Deliveries Ignite an Investment Frenzy in ...","url":"https://www.bloomberg.com/features/2025-India-instant-shopping","content":"India’s top three quick commerce firms have collectively lost more than $1.4 billion (123 billion rupees) over the past four years. This figure does not account for Zepto’s fiscal year 2025 results, which have not yet been disclosed, or Blinkit’s FY22 performance, as it was private until its acquisition.","score":0.5425973},{"title":"How Zepto and Blinkit Make Money: 4 Revenue Streams","url":"https://startupfeed.in/quick-commerce-india-zepto-blinkit-instamart-make-money","content":"Dr. Mayank Raj is Contributing Editor at StartupFeed, writing on incubators, state startup policy and early-stage funding. He has spent more than eight years building India's...\n\nFollow:\n\n- Contributing Editor\n\nShare\n\nBlinkit, Zepto, and Swiggy Instamart logos arranged as a quick commerce India explainer feature with dark store and delivery rider illustration in editorial halftone style. [...] Quick commerce India is a Rs 64,000 Cr ($7.6 Bn) market where Blinkit, Zepto, and Swiggy Instamart deliver everyday items to your door in under 10 minutes from small warehouses called dark stores.These three platforms together control roughly 95% of India’s instant-delivery market. Most people have never stopped to ask how they actually make money when deliveries cost Rs 40 to 55 each to execute. The answer is a four-part revenue model that gets more interesting the deeper you look. [...] Most people assume quick commerce platforms earn the same way an e-commerce site does: sell things at a markup. That is true, but only partly. The real money machine is advertising. Blinkit and Zepto each crossed Rs 1,000 Cr in ad revenue by FY25, and the three platforms combined pulled in Rs 3,000 to 3,500 Cr in ads. For any FMCG (Fast Moving Consumer Goods) brand in India, quick commerce is now a media channel, not just a logistics one. Brands that skip advertising risk being invisible at the","score":0.529337}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:17:21.917Z","session":"fb606d91-84d8-4449-ae8e-447eaa3b9089","event":"tool.end","callId":"d6408c5c-2e1c-47cf-a196-7c7a96fefa24","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2689,"result":[{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/27/indias-zepto-files-for-ipo-as-quick-commerce-race-heats-up.html","content":"Indian quick-commerce startup Zepto has confidentially filed for an initial public offering, according to a public notice issued by the company on Sunday.\n\nThe company plans to raise 110 billion rupees ($1.22 billion) of fresh capital. Zepto was valued at $7 billion during its last funding round in October, data from research firm Tracxn showed.\n\nZepto told CNBC it filed its draft prospectus under the confidential route, which keeps its filings private, and declined to disclose further details. [...] Quick commerce, which promises deliveries in as little as 10 minutes, has become one of India's most competitive consumer internet sectors.\n\nWhile e-commerce giant Amazon has long offered same-day delivery services in India through \"Amazon Fresh\", the launch of its 15-minute \"Amazon Now\" service in June marked an aggressive shift into a crowded space.\n\nThe Jeff Bezos-owned U.S. company has started its quick commerce operations across Indian's three major cities—Mumbai, Delhi and Bengaluru. [...] He told Bloomberg that the quick commerce industry has relied heavily on \"relentless fundraising\" to cover steep losses and that companies would soon face limits on how long they can continue absorbing them.\n\nZepto's losses reportedly widened in fiscal year 2025 to 33.67 billion rupees from 12.15 billion rupees a year ago.","score":0.58976424},{"title":"Indian quick commerce startup Zepto files for $1.2 billion IPO amid warnings of bubble in the sector","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/27/indias-zepto-files-for-ipo-as-quick-commerce-race-heats-