{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:17:41.962Z","session":"fd39e669-0c5b-4ddd-a11a-7edb19299993","event":"tool.end","callId":"ab686d15-40aa-4592-983c-eee18e19c66f","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2224,"result":[{"title":"Yash Dayal quits Zepto to join Wakefit as CTO","url":"https://www.techcircle.in/2023/07/10/yash-dayal-quits-zepto-to-join-wakefit-as-cto","content":"Dayal holds a master’s degree from University of Texas at El Paso. He is currently undergoing an Advanced Management program from IIM Bangalore. In his spare time he likes to watch movies, read books and tinker with Arduino projects, he mentioned in his LinkedIn profile.\n\nLoading... [...] . Dayal stepped down from Zepto, a quick commerce app delivering groceries where he served as head of engineering. He joined the quick commerce company more than a year ago.\n\nIn his new role as CTO at Wakefit, he will execute the brand’s technology vision and strategy.\n\n\"I’m delighted to announce that I have joined as Chief Technology Officer at Wakefit! Looking forward to building exciting and innovative hashtag#technology with the teams here” Dayal posted on LinkedIn.\n\nLoading... [...] Prior to joining Zepto, Dayal had worked as the CTO at Zivame, an Indian lingerie company. He has also headed the Android and iOS app development for the online fashion retailer Myntra and Jabong. He had a five-year stint with the company where he worked as its director of engineering for retail and growth. Dayal has also served as principal research engineer at Yahoo! And prior to that worked at Info Edge India (naukri.com.)","score":0.82117355},{"title":"Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Ya","url":"https://content.techgig.com/my-first-tech-job/gen-zs-should-stay-focus-on-their-goals-and-must-give-their-best-yash-dayal-head-of-engineering-zepto/articleshow/99206539.cms","content":"We got an exclusive chance to interact with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto shared his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. Below are the excerpts.  \n  \nTechGig: Can you give a brief of your early career and what motivated you to choose to be part of this e-commerce industry? [...] Yash: My management style has been deeply inspired by Joel Spolsky. I actively follow his posts and try to adopt his recommendations. Zepto has also been a great learning experience; right from learning how to lead the team, to building and delivering projects in a faced paced environment manner without compromising on perfection and quality. All through my career progressions at the various organizations I have worked at, I have been very fortunate to have had many mentors. [...] 157 Views | 3 Apr 2023, 12:58 PM | Updated on: 3 Apr 2023, 04:38 PM | Shruti Bhattacharya\n\nIn an exclusive interaction with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. Below are the excerpts.\n\nGen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto","score":0.7147281},{"title":"Wakefit.co appoints Yash Dayal as CTO","url":"https://hr.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/wakefit-co-appoints-yash-dayal-as-cto/101730922","content":"Wakefit.co, an Indian home and sleep solutions company, on Thursday announced the appointment of Yash Dayal as its Chief Technology Officer.  \n  \nPrior to joining Wakefit.co, Dayal held key roles, including Head of Engineering at Zepto, CTO at Zivame, and Senior Director at Myntra and Jabong. He has also served at Yahoo! and Info Edge India (naukri.com). [...] Yash Dayal, Chief Technology Officer, Wakefit.co, said, “As a market leader, Wakefit.co has the potential to set new standards in the industry, and I am committed to contributing to the company’s growth. With a focus on omnichannel expansion, my goal is to redefine the customer experience by leveraging advanced technology and data science.”  \n  \nWith a career 