nnections, 5196 followers\n\n## About\nYash Dayal has over a decade experience in working with internet technologies<br><br> Currently,…\n\n## Experience\nN/A\n\n## Education\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n2018 - 2019  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n2012 - 2013  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n2002 - 2005  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n1998 - 2001  \nNone\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nYahoo! Labs Excellence Award\n- • June 2013 [...] ## Certifications\nWorking with an Executive Coach (LinkedIn)\n\n## Volunteering\nN/A\n\n## Languages\nN/A\n\n## Organizations\nN/A\n\n## Activity\n- Delete the French language pack! It will surely free up a lot of disk space 😜 Do evaluate this optimisation if you have a Linux system. If you run it do let me know your experience 😎 ...more  \nYash Dayal shared this  \nView Post  \nActivity Image","score":0.5117904}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:17:42.261Z","session":"fd39e669-0c5b-4ddd-a11a-7edb19299993","event":"tool.end","callId":"73be29b8-6a8e-4cf3-bd80-8bed41ba9fa9","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2527,"result":[{"title":"Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give ...","url":"https://content.techgig.com/my-first-tech-job/gen-zs-should-stay-focus-on-their-goals-and-must-give-their-best-yash-dayal-head-of-engineering-zepto/articleshow/99206539.cms","content":"We got an exclusive chance to interact with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto shared his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. Below are the excerpts.  \n  \nTechGig: Can you give a brief of your early career and what motivated you to choose to be part of this e-commerce industry? [...] 157 Views | 3 Apr 2023, 12:58 PM | Updated on: 3 Apr 2023, 04:38 PM | Shruti Bhattacharya\n\nIn an exclusive interaction with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. Below are the excerpts.\n\nGen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto [...] Follow a work discipline to be successful in career: Dr. Kiran Marri, SVP & Chief Scientist, Movate\n Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto\n\n  My success mantra is to take advice from all but do what you think is best: Monish Darda, CTO & Co-founder, Icertis\n Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto","score":0.7644879},{"title":"Yash Dayal quits Zepto to join Wakefit as CTO","url":"https://www.techcircle.in/2023/07/10/yash-dayal-quits-zepto-to-join-wakefit-as-cto","content":"Prior to joining Zepto, Dayal had worked as the CTO at Zivame, an Indian lingerie company. He has also headed the Android and iOS app development for the online fashion retailer Myntra and Jabong. He had a five-year stint with the company where he worked as its director of engineering for retail and growth. Dayal has also served as principal research engineer at Yahoo! And prior to that worked at Info Edge India (naukri.com.) [...] . Dayal stepped down from Zepto, a quick commerce app delivering groceries where he served as head of engineering. He joined the quick commerce company more than a year ago.\n\nIn his new role as CTO at Wakefit, he will execute the brand’s technology vision and strategy.\n\n\"I’m delighted to announce that I have joined as Chief Technology Officer at Wakefit! Looking forward to building exciting and innovative hashtag#technology with the teams here” Dayal posted on LinkedIn.\n\nLoading... [...] Loading...\n\nDayal has over a decade experience in working with emerging and new technologies. He is passionate about the augmented reality and virtual reality space as well as in the potential of generative AI.","score":0.7498395},{"title":"Wakefit.co appoints Yash Dayal as CTO","url":"https://hr.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/wakefit-co-appoints-yash-dayal-as-cto/101730922","content":"Wakefit.co, an Indian home and sleep solutions company, on Thursday announced the appointment of Yash Dayal as its Chief Technology Officer.  \n  \nPrior to joining Wakefit.co, Dayal held key roles, including Head of Engineering at Zepto, CTO at Zivame, and Senior Director at Myntra and Jabong. He has also served at Yahoo! and Info Edge India (naukri.com). [...] Yash Dayal, Chief Technology Officer, Wakefit.co, said, “As a market leader, Wakefit.co has the potential to set new standards in the industry, and I am committed to contributing to the company’s growth. With a focus on omnichannel expansion, my goal is to redefine the customer experience by leveraging advanced technology and data science.”  \n  \nWith a career spanning over two decades, Dayal holds a Master's degree from the University of Texas at El Paso. [...] HR TV More\n\nBeyond OfficeHRTechEditor's PickHumourAcademiaLegally SpeakingAdvisory BoardInterviews\n\n \n\n Integrated Campaigns\n Bespoke Events\n Advertorial\n Virtual Engagement\n Videos\n Digital Branding & Awareness\n More;)\n\n More;)\n\n Industry\n 1 min read\n\n# Wakefit.co appoints Yash Dayal as CTO\n\nPrior to joining Wakefit.co, Dayal was serving as the Head of Engineering at Zepto.\n\nOnline Desk\n\n Online Desk\n ETHRWorld\n\n Updated On Jul 13, 2023 at 05:41 PM IST\n\n Google Preference icon","score":0.74229145},{"title":"Yash Dayal exits Zepto; joins Wakefit, ETCIO","url":"https://cio.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/corporate-news/yash-dayal-exits-zepto-joins-wakefit/101567456","content":"Dayal’s previous stints include being the CTO at Zivame, the Indian lingerie company. He has also headed Android and iOS app development for the online fashion retailer, Myntra and Jabong. He was also the Director of Engineering for retail and growth at the company, where he was posted for half a decade.  \n  \nDayal has also served as Principal Research Engineer at Yahoo! And has also worked at Info Edge India (naukri.com.) He has a masters degree from the University of Texas at El Paso. [...] Yash Dayal exits Zepto, the quick commerce app delivering groceries, as Head of Engineering after more than a year. In his new role, Dayal will be the Chief Technology Officer at Wakefit, a sleep and home solutions company. [...] Dayal has over a decade of experience in Internet technologies, and is excited about the AR/VR space and recent product launches by Apple and Meta. “These technologies have the potential to disrupt and unlock richer and futuristic consumer experiences for Wakefit.co customers,” he says.","score":0.7279179},{"title":"Join in as Mr. Yash dayal , CTO at Wakefit, discusses his ...","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/et-now-live_join-in-as-mr-yash-dayal-cto-at-wakefit-activity-7209444270913556480-4kAb","content":"In conversation now with Mr. Yash there, He's the CTO at Wakefield. So, Yash, tell us, what makes you so passionate about, you know, customer Internet? Especially given your background, you know, in Zip 2 and Mince Round, what can you tell us? I started programming in those 15 years of age, just stay back after school and then do my own programming. And then my first job was with naukri.com. That was my first stint. And that's when I realized that it's working with visibility companies. You [...] : To send real-time notifications directly to users. - Sportsdata.io API: As the backbone for retrieving accurate, live sports data. 💡 What I Learned: - Deepened my understanding of serverless architecture and event-driven systems. - Enhanced my ability to work with APIs to fetch and manage real-time data. - Gained hands-on experience integrating AWS services for scalable solutions. 📈 Why This Matters: With the growing demand for instant information, this project highlights how cloud technology [...] LikeComment\n\n Share \n       Copy\n       LinkedIn\n       Facebook\n       Twitter\n\nTo view or add a comment, sign in\n\n   \n Account Executive - APAC at Coralogix. Ex-MongoDB, Ex-Salesforce, Ex-IBM\n\n 7mo    \n\n       Report this post","score":0.3617513}]}
