{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:17:43.131Z","session":"fd39e669-0c5b-4ddd-a11a-7edb19299993","event":"llm.start","callId":"77297dd6-2fda-475f-8552-77840b765eaa","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence. Each fact is one short, self-contained statement (e.g. \"CEO and MD of Infosys since 2 January 2018\") with \"sourceUrl\" set to the URL of the one source that states it. Sources headed \"Previously learned\" are facts from earlier research — cite their URL like any other source.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"facts\": [{\"fact\": string, \"sourceUrl\": string}]}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: Yash Dayal was mentioned earlier as Zepto's head of engineering — where did he work before Zepto?\nSub-questions to cover:\n- Who is Yash Dayal, Zepto's head of engineering?\n- What is Yash Dayal's professional career history before joining Zepto?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give ...\nURL: https://content.techgig.com/my-first-tech-job/gen-zs-should-stay-focus-on-their-goals-and-must-give-their-best-yash-dayal-head-of-engineering-zepto/articleshow/99206539.cms\nWe got an exclusive chance to interact with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto shared his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. Below are the excerpts.  \n  \nTechGig: Can you give a brief of your early career and what motivated you to choose to be part of this e-commerce industry? [...] 157 Views | 3 Apr 2023, 12:58 PM | Updated on: 3 Apr 2023, 04:38 PM | Shruti Bhattacharya\n\nIn an exclusive interaction with Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto his learnings and experience at his first job and as a Senior Vice President and CTO. Below are the excerpts.\n\nGen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto [...] Follow a work discipline to be successful in career: Dr. Kiran Marri, SVP & Chief Scientist, Movate\n Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto\n\n  My success mantra is to take advice from all but do what you think is best: Monish Darda, CTO & Co-founder, Icertis\n Gen-Zs should stay focused on their goals and must give their best: Yash Dayal, Head of Engineering, Zepto\n\n[S2] Yash Dayal quits Zepto to join Wakefit as CTO\nURL: https://www.techcircle.in/2023/07/10/yash-dayal-quits-zepto-to-join-wakefit-as-cto\nPrior to joining Zepto, Dayal had worked as the CTO at Zivame, an Indian lingerie company. He has also headed the Android and iOS app development for the online fashion retailer Myntra and Jabong. He had a five-year stint with the company where he worked as its director of engineering for retail and growth. Dayal has also served as principal research engineer at Yahoo! And prior to that worked at Info Edge India (naukri.com.) [...] . Dayal stepped down from Zepto, a quick commerce app delivering groceries where he served as head of engineering. He joined the quick commerce company more than a year ago.\n\nIn his new role as CTO at Wakefit, he will execute the brand’s technology vision and strategy.\n\n\"I’m delighted to announce that I have joined as Chief Technology Officer at Wakefit! Looking forward to building exciting and innovative hashtag#technology with the teams here” Dayal posted on LinkedIn.\n\nLoading... [...] Loading...\n\nDayal has over a decade experience in working with emerging and new technologies. He is passionate about the augmented reality and virtual reality space as well as in the potential of generative AI.\n\n[S3] Wakefit.co appoints Yash Dayal as CTO\nURL: https://hr.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/wakefit-co-appoints-yash-dayal-as-cto/101730922\nWakefit.co, an Indian home and sleep solutions company, on Thursday announced the appointment of Yash Dayal as its Chief Technology Officer.  \n  \nPrior to joining Wakefit.co, Dayal held key roles, including Head of Engineering at Zepto, CTO at Zivame, and Senior Director at Myntra and Jabong. He has also served at Yahoo! and Info Edge India (naukri.com). [...] Yash Dayal, Chief Technology Officer, Wakefit.co, said, “As a market leader, Wakefit.co has the potential to set new standards in the industry, and I am committed to contributing to the company’s growth. With a focus on omnichannel expansion, my goal is to redefine the customer experience by leveraging advanced technology and data science.”  \n  \nWith a career spanning over two decades, Dayal holds a Master's degree from the University of Texas at El Paso. [...] HR TV More\n\nBeyond OfficeHRTechEditor's PickHumourAcademiaLegally SpeakingAdvisory BoardInterviews\n\n \n\n Integrated Campaigns\n Bespoke Events\n Advertorial\n Virtual Engagement\n Videos\n Digital Branding & Awareness\n More;)\n\n More;)\n\n Industry\n 1 min read\n\n# Wakefit.co appoints Yash Dayal as CTO\n\nPrior to joining Wakefit.co, Dayal was serving as the Head of Engineering at Zepto.\n\nOnline Desk\n\n Online Desk\n ETHRWorld\n\n Updated On Jul 13, 2023 at 05:41 PM IST\n\n Google Preference icon\n\n[S4] Yash Dayal exits Zepto; joins Wakefit, ETCIO\nURL: https://cio.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/corporate-news/yash-dayal-exits-zepto-joins-wakefit/101567456\nDayal’s previous stints include being the CTO at Zivame, the Indian lingerie company. He has also headed Android and iOS app development for the online fashion retailer, Myntra and Jabong. He was also the Director of Engineering for retail and growth at the company, where he was posted for half a decade.  \n  \nDayal has also served as Principal Research Engineer at Yahoo! And has also worked at Info Edge India (naukri.com.) He has a masters degree from the University of Texas at El Paso. [...] Yash Dayal exits Zepto, the quick commerce app delivering groceries, as Head of Engineering after more than a year. In his new role, Dayal will be the Chief Technology Officer at Wakefit, a sleep and home solutions company. [...] Dayal has over a decade of experience in Internet technologies, and is excited about the AR/VR space and recent product launches by Apple and Meta. “These technologies have the potential to disrupt and unlock richer and futuristic consumer experiences for Wakefit.co customers,” he says.\n\n[S5] Join in as Mr. Yash dayal , CTO at Wakefit, discusses his ...\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/et-now-live_join-in-as-mr-yash-dayal-cto-at-wakefit-activity-7209444270913556480-4kAb\nIn conversation now with Mr. Yash there, He's the CTO at Wakefield. So, Yash, tell us, what makes you so passionate about, you know, customer Internet? Especially given your background, you know, in Zip 2 and Mince Round, what can you tell us? I started programming in those 15 years of age, just stay back after school and then do my own programming. And then my first job was with naukri.com. That was my first stint. And that's when I realized that it's working with visibility companies. You [...] : To send real-time notifications directly to users. - Sportsdata.io API: As the backbone for retrieving accurate, live sports data. 💡 What I Learned: - Deepened my understanding of serverless architecture and event-driven systems. - Enhanced my ability to work with APIs to fetch and manage real-time data. - Gained hands-on experience integrating AWS services for scalable solutions. 📈 Why This Matters: With the growing demand for instant information, this project highlights how cloud technology [...] LikeComment\n\n Share \n       Copy\n       LinkedIn\n       Facebook\n       Twitter\n\nTo view or add a comment, sign in\n\n   \n Account Executive - APAC at Coralogix. Ex-MongoDB, Ex-Salesforce, Ex-IBM\n\n 7mo    \n\n       Report this post\n\n[S6] Yash Dayal quits Zepto to join Wakefit as CTO\nURL: https://www.techcircle.in/2023/07/21/yash-dayal-quits-zepto-to-join-wakefit-as-cto11\nPrior to joining Zepto, Dayal had worked as the CTO at Zivame, an Indian lingerie company. He has also headed the Android and iOS app\n\n[S7] Yash Dayal - Chief Technology Officer at WakeFit\nURL: https://www.zoominfo.com/p/Yash-Dayal/1676470730\nPrior to this, they served as Head of Engineering at Zepto, an online grocery delivery service, where they focused on team leadership and project delivery\n\n[S8] Frontend Developer job at Zepto - Instahyre | Yash Dayal\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/yashdayal_frontend-developer-job-at-zepto-instahyre-activity-7004383895823544321-92cX\nWe at Zepto are hiring Frontend developers(SDE-2 and SSE). At Zepto, we are building a lot of products from scratch on the Consumer front,\n\n[S9] Looking forward to this session | Yash Dayal\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/yashdayal_looking-forward-to-this-session-activity-7163686388075352065-Mo7B\nPublished Time: 2024-02-15T00:12:09.743Z\n\nLooking forward to this session | Yash Dayal\n\nAgree & Join LinkedIn\n\nBy clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement, Privacy Policy, and Cookie Policy.\n\nSkip to main contentLinkedIn\n   Articles\n   People\n   Learning\n   Jobs\n   Games\n\nJoin nowSign in\n\nYash Dayal’s Post\n\nImage 1: View profile for Yash Dayal\n\nYash Dayal\n\nConsumer Internet Techie, Thought leader in technology, Speaker, Angel Investor\n\n 1y\n\n[S10] Yash Dayal\nURL: https://in.linkedin.com/in/yashdayal\n- My LinkedIn profile says \"Key Account Executive.\" My real life says \"Referee to two boys under 10.\" For a long time, I tried to keep these two worlds completely separate. At Google Cloud, I was the \"Professional.\" Focused on India’s top clients, hitting quotas, and driving revenue. At home, I was \"Mom.\" Focused on my 3-year-old and 8-year-old, managing meltdowns, and finding missing toys. I thought being a leader meant hiding the chaos. I thought I had to be a machine to sustain the pressure [...] # Yash Dayal\nDP World\nBengaluru, Karnataka, India, IN  \n500 connections, 5196 followers\n\n## About\nYash Dayal has over a decade experience in working with internet technologies<br><br> Currently,…\n\n## Experience\nN/A\n\n## Education\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n2018 - 2019  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n2012 - 2013  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n2002 - 2005  \nNone\n\n### N/A  \nN/A  \n1998 - 2001  \nNone\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nYahoo! Labs Excellence Award\n- • June 2013 [...] ## Certifications\nWorking with an Executive Coach (LinkedIn)\n\n## Volunteering\nN/A\n\n## Languages\nN/A\n\n## Organizations\nN/A\n\n## Activity\n- Delete the French language pack! It will surely free up a lot of disk space 😜 Do evaluate this optimisation if you have a Linux system. If you run it do let me know your experience 😎 ...more  \nYash Dayal shared this  \nView Post  \nActivity Image\n\n[S11] Previously learned\nURL: https://cio.techgig.com/my-first-tech-job/gen-zs-should-stay-focus-on-their-goals-and-must-give-their-best-yash-dayal-head-of-engineering-zepto/articleshow_b2b/99206539.cms\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Yash Dayal: Head of Engineering at Zepto\n\n[S12] Previously learned\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zepto_(company)\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Zepto is an Indian quick-commerce company headquartered in Bengaluru\n- Zepto: Zepto was founded in July 2021 by Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra\n\n[S13] Previously learned\nURL: https://www.boringbusinessnerd.com/startups/zepto\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Nikhil Mittal is the VP of Engineering at Zepto and former VP of Engineering at KiranaKart\n\n[S14] Previously learned\nURL: https://multiples.vc/private-comps/zepto\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Raised $665 million in June 2024 co-led by Glade Brook Capital Partners, Nexus Venture Partners, and StepStone Group\n- Zepto: Secured $340 million in August 2024 led by General Catalyst and Mars Growth Capital\n\n[S15] Previously learned\nURL: https://entrackr.com/news/zepto-raises-350-mn-surpasses-135-bn-in-funding-for-2024-7599303\nPreviously learned from this page (2026-09-26):\n- Zepto: Raised $350 million in November 2024 led by Motilal Oswal Private Wealth",{"json":true,"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"claims":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"citedUrl":{"type":"string"},"supportingUrls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["text","citedUrl","supportingUrls"]}},"entitiesLearned":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"},"facts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fact":{"type":"string"},"sourceUrl":{"type":"string"}},"required":["fact","sourceUrl"]}}},"required":["name","type","facts"]}},"unableToFind":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["answer","claims","entitiesLearned","unableToFind"]}}]}
