ceeds Thierry Delaporte, who, after spearheading a significant transformation at Wipro for the last four years, is stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace. [...] Commenting on his appointment, Srini Pallia said, “Wipro is one of those rare companies that combines profit with purpose, and I am truly honored to have been chosen to lead this iconic institution. I am excited to build on the strong foundation established by Thierry and lead Wipro on its next growth trajectory. I have built my entire career at Wipro, and I have a deep appreciation of our 78-year history and our incredible team of more than 240,000 associates. We have the right strategy, and [...] “Srini is an ideal leader to lead Wipro at this pivotal moment for our company and industry. Over the past four years, Wipro has undergone a major transformation under the most challenging external conditions. Srini has been an integral part of this journey. His client-centric approach, growth mindset, strong execution focus, and his commitment to Wipro's values, make him the perfect fit as we enter the next chapter of growth and profitability,” said Rishad Premji, Chairman, Wipro Ltd.\n\n[S2] Wipro CEO Thierry Delaporte Steps Down,  Srinivas Pallia Takes Over As New CEO | N18V | CNBC TV18\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2A0BjqrUs80\n# Wipro CEO Thierry Delaporte Steps Down,  Srinivas Pallia Takes Over As New CEO | N18V | CNBC TV18\n## CNBC-TV18\n5190000 subscribers\n7 likes\n\n### Description\n703 views\nPosted: 8 Apr 2024\nIn a surprise move, Wipro announces the resignation of CEO, Thierry Delaporte & will be replaced by company veteran and insider Srinivas Pallia. Reema Tendulkar gets us a roundup of all the developments, the street view & focus areas for the incoming CEO. [...] thanks so much for that well it comes in as a bit of a surprise whro has announced the resignation of the CEO the delaport with effect from 6th of April 2024 he will be replaced by Wipro veteran and Insider shras Pala as the new CEO and managing director effective immediately that said Theory will stay on till the 31st of May to ensure a smooth transition but he does step down before his 5-year term comes to an end in July 2025 Now who is the new CEO sh IAS Pala he is a whro veteran and an [...] #wipro #wiproceo #thierrydelaporte #srinivaspallia #cnbctv18 #businessnews #businessnewstoday #businessnewsinenglish #sharemarkettoday \n\n🔴CNBC TV18 LIVE TV: \nSUBSCRIBE to our Channel: \n\n👑 Check Out Top CNBC TV18 Playlist Videos: \n   \n🔹CNBC TV18 Budget 2024: \n\n🔹CNBC TV18 Digital Podcast: \n\n🔹Sounding Board:  \n\n🔹International Videos: \n\n🔹CNBC TV18 Market Cafe: \n\n🔹CNBC TV18 Digital: \n\n🔹CNBC TV18 Weekend Special: \n\n🔹CNBC TV18 Next-Gen: \n\n🔹Overdrive Show: \n\n🔹Young Turks: \n\n🔹Startup Streets:\n\n[S3] Wipro MD Thierry Delaporte resigns, Srinivas Pallia to succeed as CEO | Company Business News\nURL: https://www.livemint.com/companies/news/wipro-md-and-ceo-thierry-delaporte-resigns-11712411635730.html\nSrinivas Pallia, who was the CEO for the company's America region, will take over as the new new CEO and MD from April 7, 2024, for a period of five years, said India's fourth-largest tech major in its statement on Saturday. Palia is a Wipro veteran and has spent over three decades at the tech company. [...] ‘’Pursuant to the recommendation of the Nomination and Remuneration Committee, the Board of Directors has approved the appointment of Srinivas Pallia as the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of the Company with effect from April 7, 2024 for a period of five years, subject to approval of shareholders and the Central Government as may be applicable,'' said Wipro in its statement. [...] Delaporte will be relieved from his duties as CEO from May 31,2024. ‘’The Board of Directors noted the resignation of Mr. Thierry Delaporte with effect from April 6, 2024. He will be relieved from the employment of the Company with effect from the close of business hours on May 31, 2024,'' said Wipro.\n\n[S4] Srini Pallia Leads Wipro Limited as CEO & MD\nURL: https://www.wipro.com/leadership/srini-pallia\nSrini has a track record of building cross-functional, cross-regional teams that deliver on clients’ most complex business and digital transformation needs. His focus on client- centricity and ability to lead through major industry transformations have been instrumental in driving ongoing value for clients as well as consistent profitable growth for the businesses he has led. [...] popup-image\n\nSrini Palliais the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Wipro Limited. In his role as the CEO, Srini sets the vision and strategy for Wipro’s business and leads a team of global leaders to drive consistent execution of Wipro’s AI-powered, consulting- led approach across six continents. [...] Prior to assuming the Global CEO role, Srini served as CEO of Wipro’s Americas 1 Strategic Market Unit (SMU), turning it into Wipro’s largest and fastest growing SMU. In his more than three decades at Wipro, Srini has held numerous leadership roles, including President of Wipro’s Consumer Business Unit and Global Head of Business Application Services.\n\n[S5] Wipro Limited Executive Team | Comparably\nURL: https://www.comparably.com/companies/wipro/executive-team\nN. Krishnakumar  VP & Global Head of Service Transformation\nVineet Agrawal  Chief Executive Officer of Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting\nRakesh Taneja  Head of State Government Business\nR. Mohan  Head of Business Application Services, India & Middle East and General Manager\nMohit Lal  Head of Vertical Delivery and Vice President\nGilles Grange  Regional Head of Operations for France\nAlexis Samuel  Global Managing Partner - WCS\nShaji Farooq  President of Banking, Capital Markets & Insurance [...] Srinivas Pallia  President of Consumer Business Unit\nKris Denton  Global Head of Wipro Consulting Services\nAshok Tripathy  Global Head of Public Sector & Higher Education and Vice President\nVinay Narayan Disley  Chief Risk Officer\nR. Velayutham  Head of Account Delivery\nNeeraj Sahdev  Head of Govt & Defence and Vice President\nSriram Tanjore Vaithianatha  Business Head of Telecom Network Service and Vice President\nAngan Arun Guha  Senior Vice President of Banking - Americas [...] Thierry Delaporte  CEO / President\nAzim Hasham Premji  Founder, Executive Chairman & MD\nRishad Azim Hasham Premji  Chief Strategy Officer & Executive Director\nHariprasad Hegde PG Diploma, BTech, B.SC.  Senior Vice President\nRajeev Mendiratta  Head-Work Force Planning & Development and VP\nDevender Malhotra  Chief Quality Officer and Vice President\nRamesh Nagarajan  Chief Operating Officer of GIS & Senior VP\nVipin Nair  Head of Communications\n\n[S6] Wipro Limited (WIT) Leadership & Management Team Analysis - Simply Wall St\nURL: https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nyse-wit/wipro/management\nWipro Limited announced the appointment of Malay Joshi as Chief Executive Officer of Wipro Americas 1 Strategic Market Unit, effective immediately. Malay succeeds Srini Pallia, who was appointed as Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Wipro Limited on April 6, 2024. Malay will also join the Wipro Executive Board. Malay was previously the Senior Vice President and Business Unit Head, leading the Communications, Media, Tech, Retail, Travel, Hospitality and Public Sector industries, [...] Wipro Limited announced resignation of Mr. Jatin Pravinchandra Dalal as Chief Financial Officer of the Company and appointment of Ms. Aparna Iyer as Chief Financial Officer of the Company. Date of appointment /re-appointment /cessation (as applicable) & term of appointment /re-appointment: The Board of Directors has noted the resignation of Mr. Jatin Pravinchandra Dalal and he will be relieved from the services of the Company with effect from November 30, 2023. At their meeting held on [...] Wipro Limited announced that Anne-Marie (“Annie”) Rowland has been appointed to the role of Capco’s Chief Executive Officer. Rowland is currently Managing Partner of Capco’s business in the United Kingdom and Ireland and a member of Capco’s Global Leadership Team. She will take on the CEO role effective April 1, 2024. As CEO of Capco, Rowland will report to Wipro CEO and Managing Director Thierry Delaporte and will become a member of Wipro’s Executive Committee (WEC). Lance Levy, who has led\n\n[S7] Wipro appoints Thierry Delaporte as CEO & Managing Director\nURL: https://www.wipro.com/newsroom/press-releases/2020/wipro-appoints-thierry-delaporte-as-ceo-and-managing-director\nX\n\nmicrosites_play_icon)\n\npopup-image\n\nEast Brunswick, New Jersey, USA and Bangalore, India – May 29, 2020: \n\nWipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading global information technology, consulting and business process services company, today announced the appointment of Thierry Delaporte as the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of the company, effective July 6, 2020. [...] “I want to thank Abid for all that he has done for Wipro and for making this transition as smooth and seamless as possible despite his personal commitments.”\n\nAbidali Neemuchwala will relinquish his position as CEO and MD on June 1. Rishad Premji will oversee the day to day operations of the company until July 5. [...] Commenting on his appointment, Thierry Delaporte said, “I am deeply honored to be invited to lead Wipro, an extraordinary company and an exemplary corporate citizen with a deep technology heritage built on a strong foundation of values. I look forward to working closely with Rishad, the Board, senior leadership and the hugely talented employees of Wipro to turn a new chapter of growth and build a better tomorrow for all our stakeholders.”\n\n[S8] Wipro Appoints Srini Pallia as CEO & Managing Director | WIT Stock News\nURL: https://www.stocktitan.net/news/WIT/wipro-appoints-srini-pallia-as-ceo-amp-managing-0wxw5lwdp7wu.html\nAdd on Google\n\nEAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. & BENGALURU, India--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading technology services and consulting company, today announced the appointment of Srini Pallia as the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of the Company, effective immediately. He succeeds Thierry Delaporte, who, after spearheading a significant transformation at Wipro for the last four years, is stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace. [...] View source version on businesswire.com: \n\nWipro Media Contact:   \nSanuber Grohe   \nsanuber.grohe@wipro.com\n\nSource: Wipro Limited\n\n## Keep reading\n\n### More on WIT\n\n Wipro and CrowdStrike Launch CISO Command Center to Transform Enterprise Cybersecurity Operations Sep 9, 2026\n ABB Extends Engagement with Wipro to Deliver and Enhance Global Digital Workplace Services Sep 2, 2026\n Wipro Partners With Databricks to Enable Enterprises to Modernize Data and Deploy AI at Scale Jul 27, 2026 [...] Commenting on his appointment, Srini Pallia said, “Wipro is one of those rare companies that combines profit with purpose, and I am truly honored to have been chosen to lead this iconic institution. I am excited to build on the strong foundation established by Thierry and lead Wipro on its next growth trajectory. I have built my entire career at Wipro, and I have a deep appreciation of our 78-year history and our incredible team of more than 240,000 associates. We have the right strategy, and\n\n[S9] Abidali Neemuchwala - Wikipedia\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abidali_Neemuchwala\nNeemuchwala, who had been group president and chief operating officer (COO) of Wipro from April 2015, was appointed CEO with effect from 1 February 2016. He previously was the CEO of the BPO division of Tata Consultancy Services Limited.\n\n## Education\n\n[edit] [...] 5. ↑ \"Meet the men behind the success of Tata Consultancy Services\". timesofindia-economictimes. Archived from the original on 10 March 2014. Retrieved 20 