{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:20:36.304Z","session":"13401fe8-664b-49ab-9131-21ab711420eb","event":"tool.end","callId":"c0dc6674-fc40-4a85-88c9-5996b583494b","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2549,"result":[{"title":"Wipro Appoints Srini Pallia as CEO & Managing Director","url":"https://www.wipro.com/newsroom/press-releases/2024/wipro-appoints-srini-pallia-as-ceo-and-managing-director","content":"EAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. | BENGALURU, India – April 6, 2024:  Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading technology services and consulting company, today announced the appointment of Srini Pallia as the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of the Company, effective immediately. He succeeds Thierry Delaporte, who, after spearheading a significant transformation at Wipro for the last four years, is stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace. [...] Srini joined Wipro in 1992 and has held many leadership positions, including President of Wipro’s Consumer Business Unit and Global head of Business Application Services. Srini brings to the CEO role extensive institutional and industry knowledge, as well as a strong track record of leadership through some of the most significant technological shifts the industry has seen. [...] “Srini is an ideal leader to lead Wipro at this pivotal moment for our company and industry. Over the past four years, Wipro has undergone a major transformation under the most challenging external conditions. Srini has been an integral part of this journey. His client-centric approach, growth mindset, strong execution focus, and his commitment to Wipro's values, make him the perfect fit as we enter the next chapter of growth and profitability,” said Rishad Premji, Chairman, Wipro Ltd.","score":0.9183121},{"title":"Srini Pallia's Post - Wipro","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/srini-pallia_i-am-honored-and-humbled-to-assume-the-role-activity-7182579016489476096-tlsM","content":"10,665,560 followers\n\nWipro appoints Srini Pallia as CEO and Managing Director.\n\nSrini has been with Wipro for over three decades and was most recently the CEO of Americas 1, Wipro’s largest and fastest growing market unit. Srini succeeds Thierry Delaporte, who will be stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace.\nSee the full announcement here:","score":0.8939131},{"title":"Wipro","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wipro","content":"62. ↑ \"Wipro appoints T K Kurien as CEO\". Business Today. 21 January 2011. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n63. ↑ \"Wipro Names Abidali Neemuchwala As Its New CEO\". Forbes India. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n64. ↑ Mendonca, Jochelle (1 February 2020). \"Wipro CEO Abidali Neemuchwala steps down\". The Economic Times. ISSN \"ISSN (identifier)\") 0013-0389. Retrieved 28 April 2025. [...] 65. ↑ Suresh, Haripriya; Ishwarbharath B, Sai (6 April 2024). \"Wipro CEO Delaporte resigns; to be replaced by veteran insider\". Reuters. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n66. ↑ \"Wipro Ropes In Srini Pallia As CEO: Who Is He?\". BW Marketing World. Retrieved 17 April 2025.\n67. ↑ \"Infy, Wipro to part-fund Bangalore expressway\". Rediff. Retrieved 18 July 2024.\n68. ↑ \"Wipro to be title sponsor of San Francisco Marathon\". Business Standard. 18 April 2012. Retrieved 18 July 2024. [...] | CEO | Tenure |\n --- |\n| Ashok Narasimhan | 1981–1988 |\n| Ashok Soota | 1991–1999 |\n| Vivek Paul | 1999–2005 |\n| Azim Premji | 2005–2008 |\n| Girish Paranjpe and Suresh Vaswani | 2008–2011 |\n| T. K. Kurien | 2011–2016 |\n| Abidali Neemuchwala | 2016–2020 |\n| Thierry Delaporte | 2020–2024 |\n| Srini Pallia | 2024–present |\n\n## Sponsorships\n\n[edit]","score":0.8803145},{"title":"Srini Pallia Leads Wipro Limited as CEO & MD","url":"https://www.wipro.com/leadership/srini-pallia","content":"popup-image\n\nSrini Palliais the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Wipro Limited. In his role as the CEO, Srini sets the vision and strategy for Wipro’s business and leads a team of global leaders to drive consistent execution of Wipro’s AI-powered, consulting- led approach across six continents. [...] Srini has a track record of building cross-functional, cross-regional teams that deliver on clients’ most complex business and digital transformation needs. His focus on client- centricity and ability to lead through major industry transformations have been instrumental in driving ongoing value for clients as well as consistent profitable growth for the businesses he has led. [...] Prior to assuming the Global CEO role, Srini served as CEO of Wipro’s Americas 1 Strategic Market Unit (SMU), turning it into Wipro’s largest and fastest growing SMU. In his more than three decades at Wipro, Srini has held numerous leadership roles, including President of Wipro’s Consumer Business Unit and Global Head of Business Application Services.","score":0.8732259},{"title":"Leadership - Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting","url":"https://wiproconsumercare.com/leadership","content":"Sriram Iyer brings over 30 years of leadership experience in sales, marketing, and business development within the FMCG sector. He currently serves as Chief Executive – Consumer Lighting & Switches at Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting, where he leads the Consumer Lighting, Switches, and Appliances businesses. In this role, Sriram drives the strategic direction, product development and business growth, with a focus on strengthening Wipro’s presence in these key segments. [...] #### T K Kurien\n\nNon-executive Director – Wipro Enterprises & Chief Executive Officer, Premji Invest\n\nT K Kurien (TK) is the Chief Executive Officer at Premji Invest. PI is the investment office sponsored by Mr Azim Premji,  \nFounder Chairman of Wipro Ltd.\n\nPrior to his current role TK was Vice Chairman & CEO of Wipro Ltd.\n\nIn his career spanning over three decades, TK has held several leadership positions encompassing strategic and operational roles. [...] Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting\n\nHome > Leadership\n\n#### Board of Directors\n\n#### Management\n\n#### Mr. Azim H Premji\n\nFounder Chairman, Wipro\n\n#### Mr. Suresh C Senapaty\n\nNon-Executive Director\n\n#### Mr. Kumar Chander\n\nCEO – Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting & Managing Director, Wipro Enterprises\n\n#### Mr. Pratik Kumar\n\nCEO – Wipro Infrastructure Engineering & Managing Director – Wipro Enterprises\n\n#### Mr. T.K. Kurien","score":0.87113565}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:20:36.414Z","session":"13401fe8-664b-49ab-9131-21ab711420eb","event":"tool.end","callId":"ba85c84f-f530-4fe4-8097-a68ce9904cbc","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2655,"result":[{"title":"Wipro Appoints Srini Pallia as CEO & Managing Director","url":"https://www.wipro.com/newsroom/press-releases/2024/wipro-appoints-srini-pallia-as-ceo-and-managing-director","content":"EAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. | BENGALURU, India – April 6, 2024:  Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading technology services and consulting company, today announced the appointment of Srini Pallia as the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of the Company, effective immediately. He succeeds Thierry Delaporte, who, after spearheading a significant transformation at Wipro for the last four years, is stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace. [...] Commenting on his appointment, Srini Pallia said, “Wipro is one of those rare companies that combines profit with purpose, and I am truly honored to have been chosen to lead this iconic institution. I am excited to build on the strong foundation established by Thierry and lead Wipro on its next growth trajectory. I have built my entire career at Wipro, and I have a deep appreciation of our 78-year history and our incredible team of more than 240,000 associates. We have the right strategy, and [...] “Srini is an ideal leader to lead Wipro at this pivotal moment for our company and industry. Over the past four years, Wipro has undergone a major transformation under the most challenging external conditions. Srini has been an integral part of this journey. His client-centric approach, growth mindset, strong execution focus, and his commitment to Wipro's values, make him the perfect fit as we enter the next chapter of growth and profitability,” said Rishad Premji, Chairman, Wipro Ltd.","score":0.9541759},{"title":"Wipro CEO Thierry Delaporte Steps Down, Srinivas Pallia ...","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2A0BjqrUs80","content":"# Wipro CEO Thierry Delaporte Steps Down,  Srinivas Pallia Takes Over As New CEO | N18V | CNBC TV18\n## CNBC-TV18\n5190000 subscribers\n7 likes\n\n### Description\n703 views\nPosted: 8 Apr 2024\nIn a surprise move, Wipro announces the resignation of CEO, Thierry Delaporte & will be replaced by company veteran and insider Srinivas Pallia. Reema Tendulkar gets us a roundup of all the developments, the street view & focus areas for the incoming CEO. [...] thanks so much for that well it comes in as a bit of a surprise whro has announced the resignation of the CEO the delaport with effect from 6th of April 2024 he will be replaced by Wipro veteran and Insider shras Pala as the new CEO and managing director effective immediately that said Theory will stay on till the 31st of May to ensure a smooth transition but he does step down before his 5-year term comes to an end in July 2025 Now who is the new CEO sh IAS Pala he is a whro veteran and an","score":0.93624437},{"title":"Wipro CEO Steps Down | In a surprise move, Wipro announces the resignation of CEO, Thierry Delaporte & will be replaced by company veteran and insider Srinivas Pallia. Reema Tendulkar gets us a… | CNBC-TV18","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/cnbc-tv18_wipro-ceo-steps-down-in-a-surprise-move-activity-7183049255027167232-vLxW","content":"Thanks so much for that. Well, it comes in as a bit of a surprise. Wipro has announced the resignation of the CEO's theory Delaporte with effect from 6th of April 2024. He will be replaced by Wipro veteran and insider Srinivas Palya as the new CEO and Managing Director effective immediately. That said theory will stay on till the 31st of May to ensure a smooth transition, but he does step down before his five year term comes to an end in July 2025. Now who is the new CEO Srinivas. He is a Wipro [...] just in FY23, but even in the preceding years under the different CEO's. In fact, in FY24 in the 1st 3/4, the company has reported a negative revenue growth. So reviving growth, getting back to industry. Growth rate, the revival of CAPCO which has been hit on account of the macro pressures, the discretionary spending coming down is going to be very crucial and also stemming attrition. The company has seen a slew a spate of high level senior level exits. This list is not exhaustive but you know [...] risk to propel us forward. Together, let's craft the next chapter in Wipro story, building upon the strong foundation led by those who came before us and shaping the future of technology and business for generations to come.","score":0.92359936},{"title":"Who is Srini Pallia, Wipro’s new CEO & MD? All you want to know about him - Times of India","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/who-is-srini-pallia-new-wipro-ceo-and-md-all-you-want-to-know-about-him/articleshow/109092150.cms","content":"Wipro has appointed Srini Pallia as its new Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director from immediate effect. In a company statement, IT giant Wipro said the current CEO Thierry Delaporte will be stepping down from the position, but will continue till May-end, working closely with Srini and Rishad Premji to ensure a smooth transition. [...] January Bank Holidays\n\nBank Holidays\n\n8th Pay Commission\n\nBudget 2025\n\nThis story is from April 6, 2024\n\n# Who is Srini Pallia, Wipro’s new CEO & MD? All you want to know about him\n\nTOI Business Desk / TIMESOFINDIA.COM /  Apr 6, 2024, 20:05 IST\n\nShare\n\nAA\n\nText Size\n\n Small\n Medium\n Large [...] Srini Pallia has been appointed as Wipro's new Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director. Since joining Wipro in 1992, he has held various leadership roles, including President of Wipro’s Consumer Business Unit and Global Head of Business Application Services.\n\nWho is Srini Pallia, Wipro’s new CEO & MD? All you want to know about him\n\nSrini, a veteran of Wipro for over three decades, has recently served as CEO for Americas 1","score":0.8