{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:20:38.533Z","session":"13401fe8-664b-49ab-9131-21ab711420eb","event":"llm.start","callId":"f0edfdb0-6b3a-4e9c-b010-6f17f8988b02","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence. Each fact is one short, self-contained statement (e.g. \"CEO and MD of Infosys since 2 January 2018\") with \"sourceUrl\" set to the URL of the one source that states it. Sources headed \"Previously learned\" are facts from earlier research — cite their URL like any other source.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"facts\": [{\"fact\": string, \"sourceUrl\": string}]}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: Who is the current CEO of Wipro, and when did they take the role?\nSub-questions to cover:\n- Who is the current Chief Executive Officer of Wipro?\n- When did the current CEO of Wipro assume office?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Wipro Appoints Srini Pallia as CEO & Managing Director\nURL: https://www.wipro.com/newsroom/press-releases/2024/wipro-appoints-srini-pallia-as-ceo-and-managing-director\nEAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. | BENGALURU, India – April 6, 2024:  Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading technology services and consulting company, today announced the appointment of Srini Pallia as the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of the Company, effective immediately. He succeeds Thierry Delaporte, who, after spearheading a significant transformation at Wipro for the last four years, is stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace. [...] Srini joined Wipro in 1992 and has held many leadership positions, including President of Wipro’s Consumer Business Unit and Global head of Business Application Services. Srini brings to the CEO role extensive institutional and industry knowledge, as well as a strong track record of leadership through some of the most significant technological shifts the industry has seen. [...] “Srini is an ideal leader to lead Wipro at this pivotal moment for our company and industry. Over the past four years, Wipro has undergone a major transformation under the most challenging external conditions. Srini has been an integral part of this journey. His client-centric approach, growth mindset, strong execution focus, and his commitment to Wipro's values, make him the perfect fit as we enter the next chapter of growth and profitability,” said Rishad Premji, Chairman, Wipro Ltd.\n\n[S2] Srini Pallia's Post - Wipro\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/srini-pallia_i-am-honored-and-humbled-to-assume-the-role-activity-7182579016489476096-tlsM\n10,665,560 followers\n\nWipro appoints Srini Pallia as CEO and Managing Director.\n\nSrini has been with Wipro for over three decades and was most recently the CEO of Americas 1, Wipro’s largest and fastest growing market unit. Srini succeeds Thierry Delaporte, who will be stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace.\nSee the full announcement here:\n\n[S3] Wipro\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wipro\n62. ↑ \"Wipro appoints T K Kurien as CEO\". Business Today. 21 January 2011. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n63. ↑ \"Wipro Names Abidali Neemuchwala As Its New CEO\". Forbes India. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n64. ↑ Mendonca, Jochelle (1 February 2020). \"Wipro CEO Abidali Neemuchwala steps down\". The Economic Times. ISSN \"ISSN (identifier)\") 0013-0389. Retrieved 28 April 2025. [...] 65. ↑ Suresh, Haripriya; Ishwarbharath B, Sai (6 April 2024). \"Wipro CEO Delaporte resigns; to be replaced by veteran insider\". Reuters. Retrieved 28 April 2025.\n66. ↑ \"Wipro Ropes In Srini Pallia As CEO: Who Is He?\". BW Marketing World. Retrieved 17 April 2025.\n67. ↑ \"Infy, Wipro to part-fund Bangalore expressway\". Rediff. Retrieved 18 July 2024.\n68. ↑ \"Wipro to be title sponsor of San Francisco Marathon\". Business Standard. 18 April 2012. Retrieved 18 July 2024. [...] | CEO | Tenure |\n --- |\n| Ashok Narasimhan | 1981–1988 |\n| Ashok Soota | 1991–1999 |\n| Vivek Paul | 1999–2005 |\n| Azim Premji | 2005–2008 |\n| Girish Paranjpe and Suresh Vaswani | 2008–2011 |\n| T. K. Kurien | 2011–2016 |\n| Abidali Neemuchwala | 2016–2020 |\n| Thierry Delaporte | 2020–2024 |\n| Srini Pallia | 2024–present |\n\n## Sponsorships\n\n[edit]\n\n[S4] Srini Pallia Leads Wipro Limited as CEO & MD\nURL: https://www.wipro.com/leadership/srini-pallia\npopup-image\n\nSrini Palliais the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of Wipro Limited. In his role as the CEO, Srini sets the vision and strategy for Wipro’s business and leads a team of global leaders to drive consistent execution of Wipro’s AI-powered, consulting- led approach across six continents. [...] Srini has a track record of building cross-functional, cross-regional teams that deliver on clients’ most complex business and digital transformation needs. His focus on client- centricity and ability to lead through major industry transformations have been instrumental in driving ongoing value for clients as well as consistent profitable growth for the businesses he has led. [...] Prior to assuming the Global CEO role, Srini served as CEO of Wipro’s Americas 1 Strategic Market Unit (SMU), turning it into Wipro’s largest and fastest growing SMU. In his more than three decades at Wipro, Srini has held numerous leadership roles, including President of Wipro’s Consumer Business Unit and Global Head of Business Application Services.\n\n[S5] Leadership - Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting\nURL: https://wiproconsumercare.com/leadership\nSriram Iyer brings over 30 years of leadership experience in sales, marketing, and business development within the FMCG sector. He currently serves as Chief Executive – Consumer Lighting & Switches at Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting, where he leads the Consumer Lighting, Switches, and Appliances businesses. In this role, Sriram drives the strategic direction, product development and business growth, with a focus on strengthening Wipro’s presence in these key segments. [...] #### T K Kurien\n\nNon-executive Director – Wipro Enterprises & Chief Executive Officer, Premji Invest\n\nT K Kurien (TK) is the Chief Executive Officer at Premji Invest. PI is the investment office sponsored by Mr Azim Premji,  \nFounder Chairman of Wipro Ltd.\n\nPrior to his current role TK was Vice Chairman & CEO of Wipro Ltd.\n\nIn his career spanning over three decades, TK has held several leadership positions encompassing strategic and operational roles. [...] Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting\n\nHome > Leadership\n\n#### Board of Directors\n\n#### Management\n\n#### Mr. Azim H Premji\n\nFounder Chairman, Wipro\n\n#### Mr. Suresh C Senapaty\n\nNon-Executive Director\n\n#### Mr. Kumar Chander\n\nCEO – Wipro Consumer Care & Lighting & Managing Director, Wipro Enterprises\n\n#### Mr. Pratik Kumar\n\nCEO – Wipro Infrastructure Engineering & Managing Director – Wipro Enterprises\n\n#### Mr. T.K. Kurien\n\n[S6] Wipro Appoints Srini Pallia as CEO & Managing Director | WIT Stock News\nURL: https://www.stocktitan.net/news/WIT/wipro-appoints-srini-pallia-as-ceo-amp-managing-0wxw5lwdp7wu.html\nAdd on Google\n\nEAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. & BENGALURU, India--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading technology services and consulting company, today announced the appointment of Srini Pallia as the Chief Executive Officer and Managing Director of the Company, effective immediately. He succeeds Thierry Delaporte, who, after spearheading a significant transformation at Wipro for the last four years, is stepping down to pursue passions outside the workplace. [...] View source version on businesswire.com: \n\nWipro Media Contact:   \nSanuber Grohe   \nsanuber.grohe@wipro.com\n\nSource: Wipro Limited\n\n## Keep reading\n\n### More on WIT\n\n Wipro and CrowdStrike Launch CISO Command Center to Transform Enterprise Cybersecurity Operations Sep 9, 2026\n ABB Extends Engagement with Wipro to Deliver and Enhance Global Digital Workplace Services Sep 2, 2026\n Wipro Partners With Databricks to Enable Enterprises to Modernize Data and Deploy AI at Scale Jul 27, 2026 [...] “I’d like to express my gratitude to Thierry for his leadership at Wipro. The changes he implemented have better positioned us for the future. We have optimized our structure, enhanced our leadership, prioritized partnerships, and improved our overall efficiency. This provides a strong foundation for Srini to effectively build upon.”\n\n“Thierry will continue until the end of May, working closely with Srini and me to ensure a smooth transition,” added Rishad Premji.\n\n[S7] We're making 'significant' investments in A.I.: Wipro CEO\nURL: https://www.cnbc.com/video/2023/04/28/were-making-significant-investments-in-ai-wipro-ceo.html\nShare Article via LinkedIn\nShare Article via Email\nStreet Signs Asia\nWe're making 'significant' investments in artificial intelligence, says Indian IT services firm\nThierry Delaporte, CEO of Wipro, says he's very bullish about artificial intelligence.\n03:51\nFri, Apr 28 2023\n2:02 AM EDT\nwatch now\nwatch now\nVIDEO\n01:32\nPresident Trump hosts China's Xi at White House\nwatch now\nwatch now\nVIDEO\n05:27\nDecision Tree Research CEO Gregory Allen on U.S.-China AI talks\nwatch now\nwatch now\nVIDEO\n03:39 [...] Pro News\nJosh Brown\nMike Santoli\nCalls of the Day\nMy Portfolio\nLivestream\nFull Episodes\nStock Screener\nMarke