 succeeded Sridhar Vembu as group CEO, while Vembu transitioned to the role of chief scientist to focus on research and development. In January 2026, Zoho launched Zoho ERP, an enterprise resource planning product developed at its Kumbakonam, Tamil Nadu office. The same month, the company opened its first data centers in the United Arab Emirates, in Dubai and Abu Dhabi.[citation needed]\n\n## Products and services [...] Founded in 1996 as AdventNet, the company initially developed network management software and adopted the Zoho Corporation name in 2009. It is headquartered in Chennai, Tamil Nadu, and remains privately held, having grown without external investment.\n\nIn January 2025, co-founder Shailesh Kumar Davey succeeded Sridhar Vembu as CEO, while Vembu became chief scientist. By February 2026, Zoho had more than one million paying organizations and 150 million users worldwide.\n\n## History","score":0.8655088},{"title":"Sridhar Vembu, Co-Founder and Chief Scientist, Zoho Corp.","url":"https://www.cxotalk.com/bio/sridhar-vembu-ceo-founder-zoho-corporation","content":"Sridhar Vembu is the co-founder and CEO of Zoho Corp. He is known for his unconventional choices. Sridhar started a product company in India when the service sector was all the rage in the IT sector. In 2005, he began the Zoho University programme with six high school students, who were trained for two years in computer science and eventually absorbed in the company. Currently, 15% of Zoho's workforce is made of ZU graduates. Instead of opening new offices in metros, he prefers smaller towns or [...] Sridhar Vembu\n\nCXOTalk Guest\n\n# Sridhar Vembu, Zoho Corp.\n\nCEO and Founder\n\n## Conversations with Sridhar Vembu\n\nSocial Impact: The Philosophy of Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu 01:05:42 \n\n### Social Impact: The Philosophy of Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu\n\nJune 7, 2024 28,521 views\n\n #Leadership\n #Business Impact\n\nZoho CEO: Corporate Social Responsibility and ‘Spiritual Capitalism’ 47:25 \n\n### Zoho CEO: Corporate Social Responsibility and ‘Spiritual Capitalism’\n\nMarch 26, 2021 16,652 views\n\n #Leadership [...] #Leadership\n\nSocial Impact: Zoho CEO on Corporate Responsibility 51:22 \n\n### Social Impact: Zoho CEO on Corporate Responsibility\n\nNovember 6, 2020 21,315 views\n\n #Leadership\n #Startups/Investing\n\nZoho CEO: Building an Enterprise Software Suite 44:38 \n\n### Zoho CEO: Building an Enterprise Software Suite\n\nApril 26, 2019 11,859 views\n\n #Leadership\n\n## Sridhar Vembu Biography","score":0.85157084}]}
{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:42:29.126Z","session":"54fe0cb1-b317-4e7b-ab5b-6e712cf00bdc","event":"tool.end","callId":"a1ac800a-6f5f-43a9-a808-c29c3c4ed132","name":"webSearch","duration_ms":2960,"result":[{"title":"Sridhar Vembu - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sridhar_Vembu","content":"Sridhar Vembu (born 1968) is an Indian billionaire business magnate and the founder and former chief executive officer of the Zoho Corporation. As per the Forbes list of India's 100 richest tycoons, dated October 8, 2025, Vembu and siblings are ranked 51st, with a net worth of US$6 billion.\n\nHe was awarded India's fourth highest civilian award, the Padma Shri, in 2021.\n\n## Personal life [...] | Sridhar Vembu |\n\n| Born | 1968 (age 57–58)  Tanjore, Tamil Nadu, India |\n| Education |  IIT Madras (BTech)  Princeton University (MS, PhD) |\n| Occupation | Businessman |\n| Title | Co-founder and chief scientist of Zoho Corporation |\n| Spouse | Pramila Srinivasan |\n| Relatives | Radha Vembu (sister) |\n| Honours |  Padma Shri (2021) |\n| Scientific career |\n| Thesis | Information Theory without Ergodicity Assumptions: Some New Results (1994) |\n| Doctoral advisor | Sergio Verdú |\n|  |\n|  | [...] ## Personal life\n\nVembu was born in 1968 in a middle class Tamil Hindu family, in a village in Thanjavur district, Tamil Nadu.[citation needed] He graduated with a bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology, Madras in 1989, and earned his MS and PhD in Electrical Engineering from Princeton University in New Jersey.","score":0.8783249},{"title":"Dr Sridhar Vembu","url":"https://www.anu.edu.in/faculty/dr-sridhar-vembu","content":"Dr Sridhar Vembu is the Chief Scientist and Co-founder of Zoho Corporation, one of India’s most successful homegrown technology companies. Dr Vembu completed Electrical Engineering at IIT Madras and went on to complete his Master’s degree and PhD from Princeton University. After a brief stint at Qualcomm in the United States, he co-founded AdventNet in 1996, which later evolved into Zoho Corporation. He was one of the first Indian entrepreneurs to bet big on SaaS, and started the Zoho brand for [...] Dr Sridhar Vembu co-founded Zoho Corporation in 1996 and served as the company’s CEO from 2000 to 2024. In 2025, he assumed the role of Chief Scientist to focus on deep-tech R&D, particularly in AI development. Zoho Corporation has emerged as the largest software product company in India while pursuing a unique set of choices that span hiring, training, product strategy, location and customer satisfaction, all driven by a holistic philosophy that puts contentment and humility as key virtues. [...] Dr Vembu has been a strong proponent of developing deep-tech capabilities in India, especially for critical sectors like healthcare and defence. He has also invested in several companies that are aligned with the same mission of developing this sovereign tech. For his contributions, he was presented with the Padma Shri in 2021. He has previously served on the National Security Advisory Board. Dr Vembu’s leadership blends business success with social purpose, redefining what it means to build","score":0.818055},{"title":"Sridhar Vembu - author at diginomica","url":"https://diginomica.com/author/sridhar-vembu","content":"# Sridhar Vembu\n\nSridhar Vembu is the Co-Founder and Chief Scientist of Zoho Corporation, which he led as CEO until January 2025. One of the world's most prolific software companies, Zoho has been providing apps in nearly every major business category for more than 20 years. Vembu obtained his Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering from Indian Institute of Technology, Madras, and PhD in Electrical Engineering from Princeton University.\n\n## Articles by Sridhar Vembu [...] ### What financial valuations get wrong about businesses This article is sponsored by: Zoho logo 2023 © Zoho\n\nOur system of financial valuation ignores the valuable traits such as culture, loyalty and passion that define a business, writes Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu\n\nRead more  about What financial valuations get wrong about businesses\n\nMiniature people standing on a bar graph © Hyejin Kang - shutterstock\n\n   A grey colored placeholder image [...] Skip to Search   Skip to Subscribe   Skip to main menu   Skip to footer\n\ndiginomica.com     diginomica.com\n\nhuman intelligence   enterprise insights\n\nYour story library\n\nMain content \n\nProfile picture for user Sridhar Vembu\n\n# Sridhar Vembu","score":0.80405265},{"title":"Sridhar Vembu & siblings","url":"https://www.forbes.com/profile/sridhar-vembu-siblings","content":"Sridhar Vembu is the founder and chief scientist of privately held Zoho, a maker of cloud-based business software. He stepped down as CEO in January 2025.\n\nVembu and his two siblings own a majority stake in Zoho. He started the business as AdventNet along with his two siblings and three friends.\n\nZoho co-founder Shailesh Kumar Davey took over as group CEO from Sridhar Vembu in January 2025.\n\nVembu has a Ph.D. in electrical engineering from Princeton and started his career at Qualcomm in 1994.","score":0.77055156},{"title":"Sridhar Vembu, Co-Founder and Chief Scientist, Zoho Corp.","url":"https://www.cxotalk.com/bio/sridhar-vembu-ceo-founder-zoho-corporation","content":"Sridhar Vembu is the co-founder and CEO of Zoho Corp. He is known for his unconventional choices. Sridhar started a product company in India when the service sector was all the rage in the IT sector. In 2005, he began the Zoho University programme with six high school students, who were trained for two years in computer science and eventually absorbed in the company. Currently, 15% of Zoho's workforce is made of ZU graduates. Instead of opening new offices in metros, he prefers smaller towns or [...] Sridhar Vembu has also been instrumental in deepening and broadening the product portfolio of Zoho, stressing on the need for an integrated suite that solves all business problems end-to-end. He also advocates investing more on R&D than marketing. As a result, in 2017, Zoho launched Zoho One, a revolutionary suite that offered 40+ products at just $30 per employee, per month. [...] Sridhar Vembu\n\nCXOTalk Guest\n\n# Sridhar Vembu, Zoho Corp.\n\nCEO and Founder\n\n## Conversations with Sridhar Vembu\n\nSocial Impact: The Philosophy of Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu 01:05:42 \n\n### Social Impact: The Philosophy of Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu\n\nJune 7, 2024 28,521 views\n\n #Leadership\n #Business Impact\n\nZoho CEO: Corporate Social Responsibility and ‘Spiritual Capitalism’ 47:25 \n\n### Zoho CEO: Corporate Social Responsibility and ‘Spiritual Capitalism’\n\nMarch 26, 2021 16,652 views\n\n #Leadership","score":0.7680558}]}
