{"ts":"2026-09-26T17:42:29.131Z","session":"54fe0cb1-b317-4e7b-ab5b-6e712cf00bdc","event":"llm.start","callId":"807b6309-01bc-47bb-96ac-6744a81fb909","name":"gemini.generate","args":["Answer the research question using ONLY the evidence below.\nRules:\n- Every claim must be directly stated by a source. \"citedUrl\" is the URL of the best source for it; \"supportingUrls\" lists EVERY source URL that states it (including citedUrl).\n- If the evidence does not answer something the question asks, put it in \"unableToFind\". Never fill gaps from your own knowledge and never guess.\n- \"entitiesLearned\": named entities with facts established by the evidence. Each fact is one short, self-contained statement (e.g. \"CEO and MD of Infosys since 2 January 2018\") with \"sourceUrl\" set to the URL of the one source that states it. Sources headed \"Previously learned\" are facts from earlier research — cite their URL like any other source.\n- \"answer\" summarises only what the claims support.\n\nReturn JSON exactly in this shape:\n{\"answer\": string, \"claims\": [{\"text\": string, \"citedUrl\": string, \"supportingUrls\": string[]}], \"entitiesLearned\": [{\"name\": string, \"type\": string, \"facts\": [{\"fact\": string, \"sourceUrl\": string}]}], \"unableToFind\": string[]}\n\nQuestion: Who is the current CEO of Zoho?\nSub-questions to cover:\n- Who is the current Chief Executive Officer of Zoho Corporation?\n- When was the current CEO of Zoho appointed?\n\nEvidence:\n[S1] Sridhar Vembu & siblings\nURL: https://www.forbes.com/profile/sridhar-vembu-siblings\nSridhar Vembu is the founder and chief scientist of privately held Zoho, a maker of cloud-based business software. He stepped down as CEO in January 2025.\n\nVembu and his two siblings own a majority stake in Zoho. He started the business as AdventNet along with his two siblings and three friends.\n\nZoho co-founder Shailesh Kumar Davey took over as group CEO from Sridhar Vembu in January 2025.\n\nVembu has a Ph.D. in electrical engineering from Princeton and started his career at Qualcomm in 1994.\n\n[S2] Zoho Corporation Details: Founders, CEO & Headquarters\nURL: https://www.registrationwala.com/knowledge-base/post/business/zoho-company-details-founders-ceo-and-headquarters\nTony Thomas is an entrepreneur and angel investor who began his journey in the startup ecosystem in 1996 with Zoho. He currently serves as the co-founder of Zoho and Vani. He holds a Doctorate degree from Johns Hopkins University.\n\n### 3. Shailesh Kumar Davey: CEO of Zoho\n\nShailesh Davey is an entrepreneur, angel investor and CEO. His startup journey commenced in 1996 with founding of Zoho. He currently serves as CEO of this company. [...] Sridhar Vembu, born in 1968, is the Founder and Former Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of Zoho Corporation. He is an Indian billionaire business magnate, and is the 30th richest person in India with a net worth of $5.85 billion as of 2024 (according to Forbes). In 2021, Vembu was awarded Padma Shri - the fourth highest civilian award in India. At present, Sridhar Vembu is the Chief Scientist at Zoho. [...] Some popular products of Zoho are Zoho Mail, Zoho CRM, Zoho Projects, Zoho Books, Zoho Desk, Zoho Analytics, Zoho Campaigns, Zoho Creator, Zoho Social, Zoho Writer and Zoho WorkDrive. According to Traxn, Zoho has not raised any funding yet and has a current valuation of Rs. 48,900 crore.\n\n## Zoho Founders and CEO Details\n\nThe details of Zoho founders and CEO are provided below:\n\n### 1. Sridhar Vembu: Co-Founder & Former CEO of Zoho\n\n[S3] About Us\nURL: https://www.zoho.com/aboutus.html\nSridhar Vembu transitions to Chief Scientist to focus on R&D, while Shailesh Kumar Davey takes over as CEO of Zoho Corp. Co-founder Tony Thomas now leads Zoho US, Rajesh Ganesan heads ManageEngine, and Manikandan Vembu oversees zoho.com.\n\nNew Position\nZoho Solo\n\nSay hello to Zoho Solo—the all-in-one toolkit for solopreneurs! Manage tasks, track expenses, accept payments, connect with customers, generate invoices, and more.\n\nZoho Start [...] #### Padma Shri\n\nThe Government of India has bestowed the prestigious Padma Shri—India's fourth-highest civilian award—on our CEO, Sridhar Vembu! It's a moment of great honor and pride for all of us here at Zoho Corp.\n\nzoho projects icon \n\n#### Projects\n\nZoho Projects 7—more speed, a complete UI makeover, and new features to help businesses deal with disruptions in their work.\n\nCelebrating 10 years of simplifying accounting with Zoho Books!\n\n[S4] Zoho Corporation - Wikipedia\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoho_Corporation\n| Key people |  Shailesh Kumar Davey (CEO)  Sridhar Vembu (chief scientist)  Tony Thomas (head of Zoho US)  Mani Vembu (CEO, Zoho.com)  Rajesh Ganesan (CEO, ManageEngine)  |\n| Products |  Zoho CRM \"Zoho CRM (application)\")  Zoho One  Zoho Books  Zoho Workplace |\n| Revenue | Increase ₹12,313 crore (FY2025) |\n| Net income | Decrease ₹3,191 crore (FY2025) |\n| Number of employees | 18,000+ (2025) |\n| Divisions \"Division (business)\") |  Zoho.com  ManageEngine  Qntrl  TrainerCentral  | [...] In January 2025, co-founder Shailesh Kumar Davey succeeded Sridhar Vembu as group CEO, while Vembu transitioned to the role of chief scientist to focus on research and development. In January 2026, Zoho launched Zoho ERP, an enterprise resource planning product developed at its Kumbakonam, Tamil Nadu office. The same month, the company opened its first data centers in the United Arab Emirates, in Dubai and Abu Dhabi.[citation needed]\n\n## Products and services [...] Founded in 1996 as AdventNet, the company initially developed network management software and adopted the Zoho Corporation name in 2009. It is headquartered in Chennai, Tamil Nadu, and remains privately held, having grown without external investment.\n\nIn January 2025, co-founder Shailesh Kumar Davey succeeded Sridhar Vembu as CEO, while Vembu became chief scientist. By February 2026, Zoho had more than one million paying organizations and 150 million users worldwide.\n\n## History\n\n[S5] Sridhar Vembu, Co-Founder and Chief Scientist, Zoho Corp.\nURL: https://www.cxotalk.com/bio/sridhar-vembu-ceo-founder-zoho-corporation\nSridhar Vembu is the co-founder and CEO of Zoho Corp. He is known for his unconventional choices. Sridhar started a product company in India when the service sector was all the rage in the IT sector. In 2005, he began the Zoho University programme with six high school students, who were trained for two years in computer science and eventually absorbed in the company. Currently, 15% of Zoho's workforce is made of ZU graduates. Instead of opening new offices in metros, he prefers smaller towns or [...] Sridhar Vembu\n\nCXOTalk Guest\n\n# Sridhar Vembu, Zoho Corp.\n\nCEO and Founder\n\n## Conversations with Sridhar Vembu\n\nSocial Impact: The Philosophy of Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu 01:05:42 \n\n### Social Impact: The Philosophy of Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu\n\nJune 7, 2024 28,521 views\n\n #Leadership\n #Business Impact\n\nZoho CEO: Corporate Social Responsibility and ‘Spiritual Capitalism’ 47:25 \n\n### Zoho CEO: Corporate Social Responsibility and ‘Spiritual Capitalism’\n\nMarch 26, 2021 16,652 views\n\n #Leadership [...] #Leadership\n\nSocial Impact: Zoho CEO on Corporate Responsibility 51:22 \n\n### Social Impact: Zoho CEO on Corporate Responsibility\n\nNovember 6, 2020 21,315 views\n\n #Leadership\n #Startups/Investing\n\nZoho CEO: Building an Enterprise Software Suite 44:38 \n\n### Zoho CEO: Building an Enterprise Software Suite\n\nApril 26, 2019 11,859 views\n\n #Leadership\n\n## Sridhar Vembu Biography\n\n[S6] Dr Sridhar Vembu - Anant National University\nURL: https://www.anu.edu.in/faculty/dr-sridhar-vembu\nDr Sridhar Vembu co-founded Zoho Corporation in 1996 and served as the company’s CEO from 2000 to 2024. In 2025, he assumed the role of Chief Scientist to focus on deep-tech R&D, particularly in AI development. Zoho Corporation has emerged as the largest software product company in India while pursuing a unique set of choices that span hiring, training, product strategy, location and customer satisfaction, all driven by a holistic philosophy that puts contentment and humility as key virtues.\n\n[S7] Sridhar Vembu - Wikipedia\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sridhar_Vembu\n1. ↑ \"Zoho Corporation CEO Sridhar Vembu steps down to focus on R&D as Chief Scientist\". The Hindu. 27 January 2025. Retrieved 29 January 2025.\n2. 1 2 3 Waters, Cara (19 April 2019). \"Barefoot Billionaire: Sridhar Vembu Built a Tech Giant You've Never Heard Of\". The Sydney Morning Herald. Retrieved 24 October 2020.\n3. ↑ \"India's 100 Richest\". India’s 100 Richest. 9 October 2024.[dead link]\n4. ↑ \"PIB Press Release: This Year's Padma Awards announced\". Pib.nic.in. Retrieved 2 February 2011. [...] Sridhar Vembu (born 1968) is an Indian billionaire business magnate and the founder and former chief executive officer of the Zoho Corporation. As per the Forbes list of India's 100 richest tycoons, dated October 8, 2025, Vembu and siblings are ranked 51st, with a net worth of US$6 billion.\n\nHe was awarded India's fourth highest civilian award, the Padma Shri, in 2021.\n\n## Personal life [...] In 1996, Vembu, along with two of his brothers, founded a software development house for network equipment providers called AdventNet. The company was renamed Zoho Corporation in 2009, focusing on providing SaaS support to Customer relationship management services. Vembu moved to Tenkasi, India in 2019. As of 2020, he held an 88 per cent stake in the company. Forbes estimated his net worth at US$2.44 billion. In 2021, Vembu was appointed to the National Security Advisory Board \"National\n\n[S8] Sridhar Vembu steps down as CEO of Zoho Corp, to take ...\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/shamus-mcgillicuddy_a-new-chapter-sridhar-vembu-steps-down-activity-7289690020913795075-u2Ip\nwave in India. The software company crossed $1 billion in annual recurring revenue in November 2022 and has 15,000 employees, mainly in India. 2️⃣ Vembu said Zoho’s growth in FY24 was subdued.He added that the software-as-a-service (SaaS) industry will get consolidated. 3️⃣ Undeterred, Zoho continues to invest in R&D, with as many as 150 active Gen AI models in the company aggregating close to 1 trillion parameters in size. Gen AI needs to be more subtle and less in the users’ faces, he [...] Major leadership shuffle at Chennai-based enterprise software company Zoho. Zoho is the parent company of ManageEngine, an IT management software vendor. Co-founder and CEO Sridhar Vembu is stepping down to take on a chief scientist role. In his statement, Vembu cited the need to devote more resources to R&D in light of rising competitive pressure around AI. Shailesh Kumar Davey will take over as Zoho CEO. This move has triggered several other executive reshuffles, including a new head of [...] leadership has been nothing short of exemplary! He's been an inspiration showing how to stay humble to your roots, persevere through tough times, listen to your customers and invest in employees, the real capital that drives growth. Excited to continue the Zoho journey as a new chapter begins with a leadership team that has been there over these years, only with renewed responsibilities. Congratulations and best wishes to: Shailesh Davey, Group CEO, Zoho Corp Manikandan Vembu, CEO, Zoho\n\n[S9] Our CEO, Sridhar Vembu, recounts the pivotal moment that solidified our decision to steer clear of external funding. Watch his full discussion with Aakash Chaudhry on Josh Talks about the allure of… | Zoho | 37 comments\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/zoho_our-ceo-sridhar-vembu-recounts-the-pivotal-activity-7189235554360651776-L4Jr\nOur CEO, Sridhar Vembu, recounts the pivotal moment that solidified our decision to steer clear of external funding. Watch his full discussion with Aakash Chaudhry on Josh Talks about the allure of unicorn businesses, current tech trends, and more. 👉 \n\n …more \n\nImage 2Image 3Image 4 2,37637 Comments\n\nLikeComment\n\n Share \n   Copy\n   LinkedIn\n   Facebook\n   X\n\nImage 5: Krishnan Sankarasubramanian, graphic\n\nKrishnan Sankarasubramanian 1y \n\n   Report this comment [...] Career\n   Productivity\n   Finance\n   Soft Skills & Emotional Intelligence\n   Project Management\n   Education\n   Technology\n   Leadership\n   Ecommerce\n   User Experience\n\n Show more  Show less [...] Our CEO, Sridhar Vembu, recounts the pivotal moment that solidified our decision to steer clear of external funding. Watch his full discussion with Aakash Chaudhry on Josh Talks about the allure of… | Zoho | 37 comments\n\nAgree & Join LinkedIn\n\nBy clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement, Privacy Policy, and Cookie Policy.\n\nSkip to main contentLinkedIn\n   Top Content\n   People\n   Learning\n   Jobs\n   Games\n\nSign inJoin now for free\n\nPlay Video\n\n[S10] Zoho Information\nURL: https://rocketreach.co/zoho-profile_b5c68c37f42e0c9c\nZoho offers beautifully smart software to help you grow your business. With over 100 million users worldwide, Zoho's 55+ products aid your sales and marketing, support and collaboration, finance, and recruitment needs—letting you focus only on your business. Zoho respects user privacy and does not have an ad-revenue model in any part of its business, including its free products. Zoho Corporation is a privately-held and profitable company headquartered in Austin, Texas with international [...] Website\nRevenue$3.2 billion\nEmployees19,375  (18,813 on RocketReach)\nFounded1996\nAddressZoho Corporation Pvt. Ltd, Estancia IT Park, Plot No. 140 & 151,, GST Road, Kanchipuram Dist, Vallancherry Village, Chennai, Tamil Nadu 603202, IN\nPhone+91 80129 51800\nFax(656) 281-9188\nTechnologiesJavaScript , HTML , PHP+339 more(view full list)\n\n[S11] Zoho\nURL: https://www.disruptiondiaries.in/post/zoho\ntop of page\n\nDisruption Diaries\n\nJinal Sanghavi\n\nAug 15\n\n11 min read\n\nListen to us on your favourite podcast app:\n\nSpotify\n\nApple Podcasts\n\nYoutube\n\nGoogle Drive\n\nToday, Zoho is a fully bootstrapped, family-controlled software company that scaled to ₹12,313 crore, roughly $1.47 billion with 22% year-on-year growth in FY25 and a 25.9% net margin. That gives it a Rule of 40 score of about 43.7, comfortably ahead of venture-backed peers like Freshworks (~17.6) and HubSpot (~19.2). [...] By the mid-2000s, Vembu saw the cloud shift coming. Zoho CRM launched in 2005, followed by productivity tools like Zoho Writer and Zoho Sheet — putting the company in direct competition with Google Apps and Salesforce at a time when neither looked beatable. In 2009, the company officially rebranded from AdventNet to Zoho Corporation.\n\n#### The Zoho Philosophy [...] Here's the tension at the heart of the Zoho story. On one side: a company that has done nearly everything right for 30 years — bootstrapped to $1.5B in revenue, profitable every year, building from rural India, reinvesting 60% into R&D, owning its full technology stack, and holding a digital sovereignty position no competitor can replicate. On the other side: an industry in genuine upheaval, where the SaaSpocalypse wiped hundreds of billions in value, AI-native startups are scaling at\n\n[S12] Zoho - A unique and powerful software suite to transform the way you work; built by a company that values your privacy.\nURL: https://www.linkedin.com/company/zoho\nZoho offers beautifully smart software to help you grow your business. With over 150M+ users worldwide, Zoho's 55+ products aid your sales and marketing, support and collaboration, finance, and recruitment needs—letting you focus only on your business. Zoho respects user privacy and does not have an ad-revenue model in any part of its business, including its free products. Zoho Corporation is privately held and profitable, with its headquarters in Chennai, India, and offices across the globe. [...] ## Locations\nZoho Corporation Pvt. Ltd, Estancia IT Park, Plot No. 140 & 151,, GST Road, Kanchipuram Dist, Vallancherry Village, Chennai, Tamil Nadu 603202, IN, B-1104, 11F, Horizon International Tower, No. 6, ZhiChun Road, HaiDian District, Beijing, 100088, CN, Yokohama Kinkocho building 6F, Kinko-cho 6-3, Kanagawa-ku, Yokohama, 221-0056, JP, 4708 Highway 71 E, Del Valle, Texas 78617, US, Beneluxlaan 4b, Utrecht, 3527 HT, NL [...] # Zoho\nA unique and powerful software suite to transform the way you work; built by a company that values your privacy.\nSoftware Development • Chennai, Tamil Nadu • 2,802,056 followers • 10,001+ employees\n\n[S13] Zoho\nURL: https://www.zoominfo.com/c/zoho-corp/195854549\n- Chennai headquartered Zoho Corporation has launched its Malaysian office to further support its long-standing collaboration with Malaysian partners like Cradle Fund Sdn Bhd in supporting the nation’s startup ecosystem and its digital transformation journey. [...] # Zoho\n\n## Leadership\n\n- Naif Alaskari — Chief Information Security Officer\n- Benny Balaji — Vice President, Solutions Research\n- Sunil Lalvani — Vice President, Enterprise Sales & Business D...\n\n## Company Details\n\n- Website: \n- Revenue: $3.2 Billion\n- Employees: 10K+\n- Industries: Customer Engagement Platforms; Software; Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)\n- Phone: +91 4469656070\n\n## Social Media\n\n- \n- \n- \n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Microsoft IIS\n- Freshservice\n- Zingfit\n- Ember.js\n\n## News & Media [...] - Zoho Day 2026 featured dozens of takeaways and insights from an enterprise software company that has historically been disruptive with great value for the money. And AI is likely to push the SaaS hunger games more into its favor. While we could riff on Zoho-specific takeaways it’s worth highlighting the themes that apply to the broader enterprise software sector including buyers and vendors.\n\n[S14] Sridhar Vembu - author at diginomica\nURL: https://diginomica.com/author/sridhar-vembu\n# Sridhar Vembu\n\nSridhar Vembu is the Co-Founder and Chief Scientist of Zoho Corporation, which he led as CEO until January 2025. One of the world's most prolific software companies, Zoho has been providing apps in nearly every major business category for more than 20 years. Vembu obtained his Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering from Indian Institute of Technology, Madras, and PhD in Electrical Engineering from Princeton University.\n\n## Articles by Sridhar Vembu [...] ### What financial valuations get wrong about businesses This article is sponsored by: Zoho logo 2023 © Zoho\n\nOur system of financial valuation ignores the valuable traits such as culture, loyalty and passion that define a business, writes Zoho CEO Sridhar Vembu\n\nRead more  about What financial valuations get wrong about businesses\n\nMiniature people standing on a bar graph © Hyejin Kang - shutterstock\n\n   A grey colored placeholder image [...] Skip to Search   Skip to Subscribe   Skip to main menu   Skip to footer\n\ndiginomica.com     diginomica.com\n\nhuman intelligence   enterprise insights\n\nYour story library\n\nMain content \n\nProfile picture for user Sridhar Vembu\n\n# Sridhar Vembu",{"json":true,"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"claims":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"citedUrl":{"type":"string"},"supportingUrls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["text","citedUrl","supportingUrls"]}},"entitiesLearned":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"},"facts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fact":{"type":"string"},"sourceUrl":{"type":"string"}},"required":["fact","sourceUrl"]}}},"required":["name","type","facts"]}},"unableToFind":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["answer","claims","entitiesLearned","unableToFind"]}}]}
